window.AKK_THE_LITTLE_DARLING_WIFE_WHO_IS_A_DIVINE_DOCTOR_SAVED_THE_ENTIRE_FAMILY_OF_THE_DUKES_MANSION_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_THE_LITTLE_DARLING_WIFE_WHO_IS_A_DIVINE_DOCTOR_SAVED_THE_ENTIRE_FAMILY_OF_THE_DUKES_MANSION_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":401,"title":"Chapter 401: The Family Reunion Dinner","paragraphs":["Mo Qing saw a moment of stunnedness flash across the face of the person in front of him.","Old Lady Mo quickly introduced, \"Master, this is A'Rui and Madam Mei.\"","She did not directly state Nan Rui and Consort De's true identities, as Nan Rui had previously instructed that from now on, they would no longer be Prince Rui and Imperial Consort De.","Mo Qing probably recognized the two, so Old Lady Mo figured a simple introduction would be enough for him to identify them.","The titles were somewhat unfamiliar to Mo Qing, but he knew his old wife well and understood that she would only introduce people he knew to him.","So Mo Qing took a good look at Nan Rui and his mother. After a long while, he finally had a sense of sudden realization, and also felt incredible disbelief.","If it had been just one familiar face, he could have brushed it off, but with both Nan Rui and his mother - two very familiar people - standing together, Mo Qing had to believe that the people before him were none other than the current Prince Rui and Imperial Consort De.","He just did not understand why the mother and son would appear in such a barren place as the northwest.","No wonder Mo Qing was puzzled. On his way back from the west, he had been drifting in and out of consciousness in the carriage, and his sons did not tell him too much so he could rest properly.","After returning to Xiling Village, the family immediately discussed military affairs, then prepared for the family reunion banquet. So Mo Qing knew nothing about what Nan Rui and the Consort were doing in the northwest.","Seeing his family and two old friends treat Nan Rui and his mother's presence as normal, it was clear that there was nothing odd about them being in Xiling Village.","Even with countless questions in mind, Mo Qing still tried his best to remain calm on the surface.","When introducing them, his wife had addressed them as A'Rui and Madam Mei - there must be some hidden reasons behind this, and he should not pry.","\"Hahaha...welcome, welcome. Today we happen to have a family reunion banquet, please take a seat.\"","He could not stand up, so he simply gestured to invite them to sit.","He did not intend to give up the host's seat to anyone.","The current Mo Qing did not have a very good impression of the Nans. His hospitality was just to avoid spoiling the atmosphere, not true friendliness.","As for how to deal with Nan Rui and his mother in the future, he would have to find out more before deciding.","Nan Rui had always been gentle and refined. Even as a prince, he interacted with others in a down-to-earth way.","Seeing Mo Qing's invitation, he politely took a seat below Mo Qing and Old Lady Mo together with Consort De, showing no discomfort at all with sitting in that position.","At this moment, not only was Mo Qing puzzled by Nan Rui and his mother's situation, Mo Junrui and Mo Jiacheng were also very curious.","But like their father, they tried their best to restrain their curiosity with so many people around, planning to ask the guests after they left.","Unexpectedly, during the meal, Nan Rui took the initiative to tell them about his circumstances.","For a while, Mo Qing could not determine whether Nan Rui was truly tired of power, or had other motives. In any case, he could not completely trust him.","Since the family's situation had been clearly exposed to others, it seemed they would have to speed up the plan of secretly building an army.","In this world, human hearts were unpredictable - who could completely understand another's thoughts?","Of course, in front of Nan Rui and his mother, Mo Qing did not show any abnormality and continued to warmly entertain the guests.","This was the first time Mo Qing, Mo Junrui and Mo Jiacheng tasted such delicious food.","Back in the capital, the Mos had also been a prestigious family with specialized chefs, but the dishes they made could not compare at all to today’s food.","Many ingredients were also things they had never seen before.","And that was not all - after the meal there were many delicious fruits, also novel tastes they had never sampled.","Having just returned home yesterday, they were already experiencing so many fresh foods.","If they had not been stationed in the Western Regions before, they would have certainly thought all these were specialties of the west.","It was Old Lady Mo who noticed the puzzlement of the father and sons and explained where everything came from.","For instance, the delicious watermelon - He Zhiran had intentionally nurtured some seedlings early on in her space ring, hoping to let the family try some fresh ones first. Now, some had ripened.","But the number of ripe watermelons was still small at the moment, not enough to sell externally yet.","After eight years, the Mo family was finally reunited. The atmosphere could not be affected by Nan Rui’s appearance.","Everyone ate, drank and chatted until late into the night before retiring individually.","Due to Nan Rui's presence, Mo Qing inevitably felt some mental pressure.","Seventh Brother had intended to set off south the next day, but was stopped by He Zhiran.","It wasn't that she wasn't anxious to build the army, but she considered that the new compound had been fully constructed with all furniture in place.","If the Mo men had not rushed out to search for their father earlier, they would have moved in already.","For ancient people, moving into a new residence was a big deal - no one hoped for absent family members.","Therefore, He Zhiran decided to delay Seventh Brother's trip for a day - they would move first.","Otherwise, with Seventh Brother only returning in over a month, it would be inconvenient to live in this small courtyard so close to He Zhiran’s due date, especially with the growing household. That was why He Zhiran had specially built those courtyard houses.","Thinking of the large family, and her modern soul also not accustomed to that kind of communal living, she had deliberately constructed ten courtyards, with an eleventh on the far west end later gifted to Mo Hanyue. Each was a siheyuan.","Viewed from afar, the eleven siheyuans stood neatly in an east-west row, with the front and back evenly aligned, looking very orderly.","In front, He Zhiran had specially planted many peach trees in the open spaces surrounding the houses.","Come spring next year, the area would take on a different beauty.","There were not many items in the rented courtyard for the Mo family to move as new furniture had been prepared in the compound, so not much needed to be transported.","The family only had to carry some personal belongings over.","With many helpers from Hu Cong and Tao Ran, moving only took about an hour in the morning.","The sisters-in-law returned to clean up the rented place, checking for any forgotten useful items and giving the rest to villagers. They also thoroughly cleaned the place to return to the landlord.","By afternoon, all was done.","Yu Er prepared another rich feast for the housewarming banquet, after which everyone returned to their own courtyards for the night.","He Zhiran had built so many siheyuans considering the large household, and as someone from the modern age, she was also not accustomed to living in a big traditional family setting. Separate living quarters gave each family privacy while they still worked together in the day."]},{"number":402,"title":"Chapter 402: Better than all the fruits in the palace.","paragraphs":["If it was time to eat, she would have no objection if the two elders did not want to ask to eat alone.","When it was time to eat, just go to the old people's yard together directly.","Living separately like this, not only He Zhiran liked it, but Mo Jiuye also liked it equally.","Ask which man doesn't want to have a place to spend time with his wife alone?","Especially He Zhiran, who had to go in and out of the space every day. Now that she had her own yard, it would be more convenient.","The elder brothers and sisters-in-law felt the same way, they all felt that their own little home was now warm and comfortable.","This night was the most comfortable night since the Mo family came to Xiling Village.","Living in a special large yard, sleeping on a large bed, and most importantly, the whole family was together without losing anyone.","The next morning, the whole family got up early and gathered in the old couple's yard.","On the one hand, the old people did not say they wanted to split up the family and eat alone, on the other hand, it was also to see off the Seventh Elder Brother who was going to the southern border.","Although on the surface Seventh Elder Brother's trip to the southern border did not seem to have any danger, He Zhiran was still careful to prepare a lot of self-defense items for him.","For example, drugs that can quickly take care of enemies when faced with a large number of enemies.","In addition, the antidote pills from when she went to the capital with Mo Jiuye were also essential.","In addition, He Zhiran also prepared some jerky for him, which was easy to eat on the road.","Seventh Elder Brother took the items she had prepared, bid farewell to his family, and rode away without daring to look at his wife's reluctant eyes.","While Seventh Elder Brother went to the south to find his former subordinates, He Zhiran was also not idle on her side.","Since she had already said that she would train a thousand troops, she had to produce gunpowder as soon as possible, otherwise, a thousand soldiers would really be unable to resist the enemy country's army or the people sent by Emperor Shunwu, just as her adoptive father worried.","Seeing her send off Seventh Elder Brother and then return to her own yard, Mo Jiuye hurried to catch up.","\"Ranran, are you going to research grenades?\"","The young couple chatted for a while in the space last night, and He Zhiran told Mo Jiuye about her plans.","No one was more aware of the power of this weapon than Mo Jiuye.","Even though his wife said that the weapon she planned to make was not as powerful as a grenade, and could be called a bomb, it would still be an invincible existence in this era.","Mo Jiuye looked forward to this more than anyone else.","When the two returned to their own yard, they flashed into the space.","Although He Zhiran knew the raw materials needed to make gunpowder, in order to increase the success rate, she still planned to ask the little collector for help in finding the exact formula on Duyu.com, so that she could avoid some detours here.","Nowadays, the little collector catered to He Zhiran's every need, after all, she was his big client.","Soon, he sent the exact formula in the chat box.","He Zhiran got the formula and asked Mo Jiuye to copy it on Xuan paper with a writing brush and give it to Fifth Elder Brother.","Among the several elder brothers at home, Fifth Elder Brother was the most meticulous one, and He Zhiran was most at ease with leaving the production of gunpowder to him.","Of course, Fifth Elder Brother could not do it alone. He called on Eldest Brother, Second Brother and Third Elder Brother to join him.","Fourth Elder Brother also wanted to participate in this matter.","He always felt that he had become a useless person after Ninth Younger Brother saved him.","Although he could walk a few steps when supported now, his legs still felt weak and he had no strength at all.","Fortunately, his hands had recovered seventy to eighty percent, and there was no problem as long as he didn't use too much force.","Thinking that Fifth Brother was going to make weapons, even if he couldn't stand for a long time, he could at least do some work with his hands.","However, the location for making gunpowder was chosen on the mountain to avoid harming the innocent. In addition, He Zhiran also considered the high probability of explosions occurring during the production of gunpowder. If it was too close to the residential area, it would easily damage the buildings.","Because it was on the mountain, Fourth Elder Brother's original plan to participate was no longer feasible either. With his legs, he certainly couldn't let his brothers carry him up and down the mountain!","Helplessly, Fourth Elder Brother had to give up the idea.","On the first day the brothers went up the mountain to research gunpowder, they did not make adequate preparations and came back before dark.","The next day, they gained experience and brought a lot of food to stay on the mountain to continue their research.","He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye knew that it was best not to disturb them while making gunpowder, so Mo Jiuye did not go up the mountain to take a look either.","He had been out for more than a month this time after going out and coming back.","It was now early June, and the vegetables and fruits in the fields were beginning to ripen one after another.","For example, melons. Sixth Elder Brother went to check early in the morning and came back saying that the sweet aroma spread everywhere. He saw one split open and picked it to taste it, and it was as sweet as honey.","Since returning from the Western Regions, He Zhiran had not been to check on the melon field.","After hearing Sixth Elder Brother's description and calculating the planting time, the melons should be ripe now.","Mo Jiuye was currently busy dealing with matters regarding the site for raising poultry and livestock, so He Zhiran called Lan Er to go with her to check on the melon field.","Nowadays, the cultivated land of the Mo family was taken care of by hired help, only those special melon fields were guarded by the dogs, and checking was also done by their own people.","It wasn't that He Zhiran didn't trust those hired people, after all, melons and watermelons were rare treasures in this era, and she planned to sell them for a good price.","Although these villagers were all honest, no one could refrain from touching such edible things placed before their eyes.","Especially the melons, they were not very big. Stealthily tucking two under the arms and taking them away would not be noticed by anyone.","Therefore, the melon fields were managed by their own people.","Supported by Lan Er, He Zhiran was still some distance away from the melon field when a sweet scent rushed up to meet her.","\"Ninth Madam, there was no such fragrance last time I accompanied you here!\" Lan Er was obviously somewhat excited.","She had accompanied the Ninth Madam to check on this melon field countless times, so she had watched these melons grow up.","And she would often go down to the field to do weeding and other chores, so she was naturally happy that the melon field she had carefully tended was now bearing fruit.","When the two came close to the melon field, the sweet scent became even stronger.","Seeing the master, the dogs guarding the field wagged their tails and gathered around.","He Zhiran patted their heads, then took Lan Er into the melon field.","Judging from the appearance of these melons, half of them were already ripe.","He Zhiran picked a nearby one and shared it with Lan Er.","After taking a bite, Lan Er enjoyed it with her eyes closed.","\"Ninth Madam, the melon is really sweet, much more delicious than the fruits in the palace.\"","The Fourth Princess treated her and Yu'er like sisters, and would share any delicacies with them, so Lan Er had tasted the top fruits of this era."]},{"number":403,"title":"Chapter 403: In Search of the Whereabouts of Mohism","paragraphs":["The fruits that Lan Er had eaten before were simply worlds apart compared to this fragrant melon.","He Zhiran knew that Lan Er was a knowledgeable maid.","\"Compared to the fruits you've eaten before, how is this?\"","\"My Lady, the melon is absolutely the king of fruits.\"","As Lan Er spoke, she had already raised her thumb up high.","He Zhiran understood in her heart and had Lan Er pick some more melons to bring back for her family to taste.","At the same time, she sent Liang Hao to the city to look for Tang Mingrui to come to Xiling Village in person to discuss cooperation matters regarding the melons.","He Zhiran only wanted to be a supplier. She currently only trusted Tang Mingrui with the sales issue.","Tang Mingrui's business was now vastly different from before. Relying on the Cold Rabbit Meat from the Mo family shop, he had opened restaurants in several nearby towns that specialized in this Cold Rabbit Meat dish.","Because he opened the restaurants himself, the Cold Rabbit Meat was no longer sold to other restaurants. Moreover, the cooking method for Cold Rabbit Meat was a secret Mo family recipe, and the exclusive sales rights were fully handed over to him.","Even so, the Cold Rabbit Meat was still not enough to meet demands in his several restaurants. At the same time, it also brought his restaurant business to a peak.","Other restaurants were envious of his booming business and tried to get their chefs to make Cold Rabbit Meat as well.","But the taste they made was barely palatable, without even a hint of the original flavor.","Firstly, the most important seasoning for Cold Rabbit Meat, chili peppers, they did not have. So how could they produce a similar taste?","In the end, those who tried to imitate the Cold Rabbit Meat ended in failure.","Yet they did not give up and wanted to obtain the Cold Rabbit Meat through other means.","It was unknown which restaurant owner got wind of the news and found out that the Cold Rabbit Meat at Tang's Restaurant came from the Mo family in Xiling Village. He then secretly sent someone to Xiling Village.","Just as she had sent Liang Hao to look for Tang Mingrui, He Zhiran took Lan Er to her in-laws' courtyard.","Nowadays, Mo Qing was in poor health and always needed someone by his side. Old Lady Mo stayed in her own courtyard every day to take care of him.","As someone who valued filial piety greatly, He Zhiran naturally brought the melons to the elders first for them to taste.","It was scorching hot currently. Mo Qing was moved to rest under the grape trellis in the yard to enjoy the breeze.","Just as a few people were enjoying the delicious melons, they suddenly heard a chorus of barking and hurried footsteps.","These footsteps did not sound very familiar to He Zhiran.","Because they sounded very heavy when running, completely different from the light steps of the Mo men.","Yu Er cleverly walked towards the entrance.","Upon opening the door, she saw a man from the Zhao family standing there panting heavily, together with several dogs.","Before the Zhao man could speak, the dogs barked again the moment they saw He Zhiran and kept looking back towards the village.","He Zhiran knew that something had happened in the village and these dogs came to report it.","But the dogs' ability to communicate was necessarily limited. She first asked the Zhao man.","\"Brother, did something happen?\"","\"Old Nine's family, where are your men? Go check out the village quickly. Some people came looking for the Mo family's whereabouts.","Seeing their malicious intentions, I rushed here to warn you so you can prepare.\"","Seeing the Zhao man's flustered appearance, He Zhiran instantly felt the gravity of the situation.","Coincidentally, Mo Jiuye and Sixth Elder Brother also heard the dogs barking and rushed back.","Tao Ran and others came back together with them.","Judging by their speed, He Zhiran concluded that they must have used Qinggong (lightness skill), otherwise with the distance from the animal farm to their residence, it would not be possible to return this quickly without using Qinggong.","Having just heard the Zhao man's words, Mo Jiuye and the others also understood.","At this time, Mo Qing under the grape trellis also spoke.","\"Jinyean, Jiuye, take some people to the village to see what exactly is going on.\"","It was not that Mo Qing was being paranoid. Since returning to Xiling Village, he had been worried that Emperor Shunwu would make a move.","Now, he did not dare let his guard down whenever anything was amiss.","Mo Jiuye left two people to guard the elders and headed to the village with Sixth Elder Brother and the others.","Just as the group reached the village outskirts, they heard cursing.","\"Get the hell away from me, I'm here for the Mo family. If you continue being obstructionist dogs, don't blame my stick for being merciless.\"","Although afraid, Village Chief Zhao saw the aggressiveness of these people and worried that something might happen to the Mo family. He wanted to buy them as much time as possible to get prepared.","\"Sir, the Mo family are all women... It's not appropriate for you to lead so many people there...\"","Zhao hoped that by emphasizing that the Mo family were originally mostly women when they first arrived, he could dissuade those people with this plea.","But his idea, albeit beautiful, was futile because those looking to make trouble for the Mo family did not care at all whether they were men or women.","Seeing that man becoming impatient and about to push Village Chief Zhao aside, Mo Jiuye dashed forward and fiercely grabbed his wrist.","\"Who are you? What business do you have with the Mo family?\"","Feeling the pain in his wrist, the man turned to look at Mo Jiuye.","\"You dare lay hands on me. Looks like you're tired of living.\"","Mo Jiuye stared at him coldly with no intention of letting go.","This man was dressed in silk but made into casual shorts, which gave off an inconsistent vibe.","Moreover, he had vicious features. Especially with his arm hurting from Mo Jiuye's grip, his distorted expression appeared even more hideous and terrifying to ordinary folks.","Following him were over twenty men, each holding a wooden staff.","Their clothes were made of regular cotton and it was apparent that this man Mo Jiuye grabbed was their ringleader.","Judging by their looks, they resembled local ruffians.","Seeing their boss at a disadvantage, someone immediately pointed his wooden staff at Mo Jiuye.","\"You've got guts grabbing Second Master's arm. Looks like you're tired of living.\"","As he spoke, someone had already swung the staff down towards Mo Jiuye's head.","Seeing this, the villagers who ran over had already closed their eyes in fear.","If that strike really landed on his head, would this man still live?","But what the villagers feared did not happen at all. Mo Jiuye did not show any intention of dodging either.","Only to see Sixth Elder Brother stride forward aggressively. It was unclear how he exactly moved but he sent those ruffians who wanted to harm his younger brother flying several meters away with a kick before anyone even realized it.","The ruffians fell on the ground yelling nonstop. They were used to being arrogant and had never suffered such humiliation before.","Even having witnessed the other party's might, they remained defiant."]},{"number":404,"title":"Chapter 404: Let's Talk.","paragraphs":["\"<Mo Jinnian> did not care who they were. Even if the King of Heaven came, he would not let anyone bully his <Mo Family>.\"","\"I don't care who you are. I advise you today to leave quickly if you don't want to suffer, otherwise...\"","\"Otherwise what? If you make our <Second Master> unhappy, don't expect to live a peaceful life here in the future.\" Before <Mo Jiuye> could finish speaking, the thugs interrupted with threats in their tone.","<Mo Jiuye> snorted coldly and increased the force of his grip.","\"I don't care who you are. If you dare to cause trouble for my <Mo Family>, don't expect to leave here unscathed.\"","The <Second Master> could clearly hear the sound of his own bones breaking, and he screamed in pain, \"Stop...stop quickly...\"","<Mo Jiuye> was not deterred at all by his squeals like a pig being slaughtered. He still firmly gripped the arm that he had crushed.","\"Who exactly are you? Why are you causing trouble for the <Mo Family>?\"","The pain brought tears to the <Second Master's> eyes. He also realized that the person in front of him had a backbone and was not afraid of him at all.","In order not to suffer any more, he softened his tone, but still with a hint of threat.","\"I'm from the provincial government. Go ask anyone there, all the underworld and upper class give <Second Master> me some face.\"","The provincial government?","Clearly, these were just small-time street thugs. <Mo Jiuye> recalled that he had never even left Yuncheng, let alone offend anyone from the provincial government.","\"I'm asking you why you are causing trouble for the <Mo Family>?\"","To make this person more honest, <Mo Jiuye> increased the force again.","The pain brought the <Second Master> to shriek.","\"Ow...ow...\"","Ultimately, he could not withstand the pain and softened.","\"Good sir, spare me. There is room for discussion between us, we can even become friends.\"","<Mo Jiuye> was too lazy to deal more with this kind of person. Impatiently he said, \"Less nonsense, answer my question.\"","The <Second Master> looked at <Mo Jiuye's> cold eyes and broke out in a cold sweat.","He had no trouble believing that if he did not become more honest, he was likely to lose his life.","\"It was Boss <Jin>... it was Boss <Jin> who asked me to come to the <Mo Family> for the recipe for the Cold Rabbit Meat.\"","Although <Mo Jiuye> did not know who Boss <Jin> was, hearing that it was related to the Cold Rabbit Meat, he understood in his heart.","It was nothing more than <Tang Mingrui> using the Cold Rabbit Meat to expand his restaurant business, affecting other restaurants' business.","Even so, he would not sympathize at all with this Boss <Jin>.","Everyone relies on their own ability in business. To use such dirty tactics after losing is not something a good person would do.","<Mo Jiuye> had already figured out the general situation. He ordered <Mo Family's> old unit to tie up all these petty gangsters and threw them at the foot of the mountain for the time being.","<He Zhiran> had originally wanted to follow <Mo Jiuye> and the others to see what was going on. However, Lady <Mo> refused to let her go out no matter what, so she could only anxiously wait for news in Elder <Mo’s> courtyard.","Considering that his parents and <He Zhiran> would worry about the situation here, after resolving those thugs, <Mo Jiuye> went back to explain what happened.","Hearing that these people had come for the Cold Rabbit Meat, <He Zhiran> realized that her family might face similar situations in the future.","The Cold Rabbit Meat business had just started. <Mo Family> would develop other industries in the future. Although they were not afraid of anyone, being eyed like this all the time was quite annoying.","<He Zhiran> felt that it was necessary to communicate this matter with <Tang Mingrui> so that the sources obtained by the <Mo Family> would be kept confidential in the future.","Just as she was thinking about this, <Liang Hao> came with <Tang Mingrui>.","Coincidentally, he had just arrived at the <Tang’s> when he happened to meet <Tang Mingrui> about to go out. After explaining the situation, the two quickly returned to <Xi Ling Village>.","Just walking to the foot of the mountain, they realized something was wrong, especially that <Second Master>. <Tang Mingrui> also recognized him.","Seeing <Tang Mingrui>, the <Second Master> looked as if he saw a lifesaver. While still far away he shouted loudly, \"Boss <Tang>, Boss <Tang> come save me...\"","<Tang Mingrui> was somewhat puzzled by this.","He and this <Second Master> only knew each other, there was no special relationship between them.","There is a saying, don’t challenge the local despot. In order for his business to operate smoothly, <Tang Mingrui> had sent people to contact this person before. But it was limited to his men going to meet the <Second Master>.","\"Why is the <Second Master> here?”","Seeing <Tang Mingrui> respond, the <Second Master> hurriedly said, \"I came here to do business and was caught by them as a bad guy. As long as Boss <Tang> is willing to save me, from now on in the provincial government, you will be my boss.\"","Hearing him say this, the old <Mo Family> unit in charge of guarding these people rushed forward and kicked him violently.","\"Still daring to talk nonsense in front of us, I see you really will not shed tears until you see the coffin.\"","Seeing the old <Mo Family> unit kicking the <Second Master>, <Liang Hao> knew that these people must have come to cause trouble for the <Mo Family>. Otherwise, with the <Mo Family’s> low-key behavior, they would not randomly tie them up and throw them here without reason.","In order not to let <Tang Mingrui> help the wrong side, <Liang Hao> quickly introduced: \"Young Master <Tang>, like me, they are all good brothers who follow the <Mo Family>.\"","Hearing <Liang Hao’s> explanation, even if <Tang Mingrui> did not know exactly what happened, he could confirm one thing, that the <Second Master> had offended the <Mo Family>. Since he was of one heart with the <Mo Family>, how could he possibly help the <Second Master> after understanding the situation?","Therefore, without even glancing at the <Second Master>, he followed <Liang Hao> to Elder <Mo’s> courtyard.","<He Zhiran> did not expect <Tang Mingrui> to come so quickly.","Because she had just heard the purpose of those people coming to the <Mo Family>, she still felt a little unhappy seeing <Tang Mingrui> whose attitude was not very good either.","\"Young Master <Tang>, those people at the foot of the mountain all came to cause trouble for the <Mo Family> because of your business. How do you think this matter should be handled?\"","The <Mo Family> were now just ordinary commoners. Even if the <Second Master> and the others came with unkind intentions, they could not privately dispose of them either.","It would be best if <Tang Mingrui> could resolve this. If that was not possible, they would be sent to the government office.","<Tang Mingrui> had already known that the <Second Master> brought people to cause trouble for the <Mo Family>. He just did not understand how this matter could also be related to himself.","\"What does Ninth Sister-in-Law mean?\"","\"Those people just now were sent by Boss <Jin> from the provincial government to come to my <Mo Family> for the recipe for the Cold Rabbit Meat.\"","\"What did you say?\" Hearing <He Zhiran> say this, <Tang Mingrui> gasped.","It seemed that this matter did arise because of him after all.","And he also knew that Boss <Jin> was the owner of the biggest restaurant in the provincial city. Before he opened the restaurant himself, the Cold Rabbit Meat business had always maintained cooperation with them.","He never expected that they would come to the <Mo Family> for the sake of the Cold Rabbit Meat business, and use such methods too."]},{"number":405,"title":"Chapter 405: This Stuff Is So Good.","paragraphs":["“Ninth Sister-in-law, don't worry. I'll take care of that group of people and guarantee that nothing like this will happen again in the future.”","This was all He Zhiran wanted to hear from him, anything more was unnecessary.","“I asked Brother Tang to come over today because I have something good to show you.” She quickly changed the subject.","Tang Mingrui was just thinking about how to deal with Second Young Master's little gang and how to handle Boss Jin. When he heard He Zhiran say she had something good, his eyes immediately lit up.","“What good stuff does Ninth Sister-in-law have? Quickly show Brother me.” In his mind, anything He Zhiran said was good must be top notch.","He Zhiran asked Lan Er to bring over a plate of washed cantaloupe.","“Brother Tang, try it first.”","Just the smell when the cantaloupe was brought over was irresistible, let alone tasting it.","But he also knew propriety. He first glanced at the two Mo elders.","Although he didn't know who the old man was, he could see that he was sitting with Old Lady Mo. And he also noticed that the Mo men had been coming back one after another, so he guessed that this person was probably the Old Duke.","If Ninth Sister-in-law hadn't mentioned Second Young Master's matter just now, he would have definitely gone to pay his respects to the two elders first.","At this moment, Tang Mingrui was already aware that he had been impolite. Even though he was eager to taste that sweet and fragrant thing, he could not disregard etiquette.","He slowly walked over to the two elders and bowed deeply.","“Greetings, Old Lady Mo.” Tang Mingrui paused for a moment and looked at Mo Qing.","Although he had guessed his identity, they hadn't been formally introduced, so if he got it wrong, it would be embarrassing.","Seeing this, Mo Jiuye quickly introduced, “This is my father.”","Tang Mingrui confirmed his guess and showed even more respect.","Old Duke Mo ah, he was the God of War praised by Great Shun for decades.","“Junior pays respects to the Old Duke.”","In recent days, Old Lady Mo had already told Mo Qing about the Mo family's situation in detail, even introducing who they knew and didn't leave anyone out.","So Mo Qing was not unfamiliar with the name Tang Mingrui.","“No need for such courtesy. Now my Mo family are just commoners, there is no Old Duke. Young Master Tang can just call me Uncle from now on.”","Tang Mingrui was straightforward. He thought his form of address was indeed inappropriate. If someone with ill intentions heard it, it would only bring disaster to the Mo family.","“Uncle.”","Mo Qing liked dealing with frank people. Hearing Tang Mingrui call him Uncle, he immediately burst out laughing.","“Hahaha... You young people have things to attend to, don't mind me, just go about your business.”","Mo Qing had also heard from his wife about Mo Hanyue's intentions towards He Zhiran.","To be honest, he quite liked the character of this young man before him. However, he had heard that Meng Huaining was even more outstanding, so he would have to find time to meet him.","With his daughter's wedding only half a month away, as the father-in-law he didn't even know if the son-in-law was round or square.","This wasn't Meng Huaining's fault either. He had been busy with court affairs recently and overseeing the wedding preparations, so he hadn't come to the Mo family.","When Mo Chuhan took office, he also didn't mention his family members, so Meng Huaining still didn't know that his future father-in-law had returned to Xiling Village.","Tang Mingrui bowed again, then moved closer to He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye.","Lan Er brought the plate of cantaloupe before him again.","This time, Tang Mingrui did not stand on ceremony at all. He took a piece and popped it into his mouth under everyone's gaze.","In the blink of an eye, the piece of cantaloupe entered Tang Mingrui's stomach.","He was expected to make some comment, but instead, Tang Mingrui took another piece and started eating again.","Soon, the plate of cantaloupe Lan Er had brought was cleaned out.","Tang Mingrui looked somewhat embarrassedly at Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran.","“Ninth Brother, Ninth Sister-in-law, please forgive Brother's rudeness. This stuff is too delicious, I couldn't help myself for a moment...”","Seeing him like this, He Zhiran couldn't help but laugh.","“Brother Tang, since you like it, eat more. It's our own produce, so eat as much as you want.”","It wasn't that she was being wastefully generous, not only was the yield of their homegrown cantaloupe high, she also had a lot stocked in her space, waiting for the right time when the cantaloupe outside ripened so she had an excuse to take it out and mix it to sell together.","No matter how much Tang Mingrui liked to eat, how much could he eat by himself?","“Ninth Sister-in-law, you say this is produce from your own home?” Tang Mingrui thought such delicious fruit must have been something the Mo family had procured from somewhere, he didn't expect it was actually homegrown.","It seemed that the good stuff Ninth Sister-in-law mentioned was this.","“Ninth Sister-in-law, is this a fruit? It looks a bit like a melon?”","He Zhiran explained, “This is called cantaloupe, I got the seeds from foreigners and planted them on our land in early spring.”","“Cantaloupe, good name, it really is a fragrant and sweet melon.” Tang Mingrui complimented and quickly got to the point, “Ninth Sister-in-law, does Brother get to cooperate with you on this cantaloupe?”","He Zhiran had a lot of contact with Tang Mingrui and already understood his character. She also didn't intend to make unrealistic demands.","“I asked Brother Tang to come today to discuss cooperation on this cantaloupe.”","What Tang Mingrui was most enthusiastic about was doing business, and he wasn't picky about industry. As long as there was money to be made, he could put his hands in.","“Ninth Sister-in-law, as long as you let me have the exclusive right to sell cantaloupe, you can set any terms.”","Tang Mingrui had always maintained a grateful heart towards the Mo family people. Even if there was no profit for him, as long as they asked for help, he was willing.","Moreover, he was very clear about the character of Mo Jiuye and his wife. They would not do that.","He Zhiran also didn't plan to make unreasonable demands. But she could be certain that with cantaloupe in Tang Mingrui's hands, it would definitely sell for a higher price than she could imagine.","“Brother Tang, this is not our first cooperation, let's stick to the old rules, 50-50 split, what do you think?”","He Zhiran did not have much interest in doing business, moreover, that was not her aspiration.","If it wasn't for wanting the Mo family to live well and for money to come through proper channels, she really couldn't be bothered with such things.","Tang Mingrui was also happy with this. Their previous cooperation had been like this as well.","If he wanted the Mo family to earn more profits, he could work hard to sell the cantaloupe at a high price.","“Good, we'll follow Ninth Sister-in-law's suggestion of a 50-50 split. But the final price the cantaloupe can sell for, I'll only know after trying it out.”","“No problem. The cantaloupes have ripened a lot now. Brother Tang can send people over to transport them tomorrow morning.","Also, the cantaloupes are best picked and transported freshly, so when you come to collect the goods tomorrow, try to come early.”","Next, He Zhiran carefully explained the preservation method and approximate storage time of the cantaloupes to give Tang Mingrui a good idea.","Tang Mingrui made note of everything, not wanting to stay a moment longer. He was prepared to go back and arrange for people to come to Xiling Village to transport cantaloupe.","He also had to deal with Second Young Master's men."]},{"number":406,"title":"Chapter 406: Come Back Full","paragraphs":["That Boss Jin who was always thinking of shady ways to do business also could not be let off.","In short, they could not let their business continue to affect the peaceful lives of the Mo Family People.","Tang Mingrui clasped his hands towards the Mo Family People again.","\"There are still many things to deal with today, so I won't disturb you further.\"","If it was in the past, he would definitely have eaten a delicious meal at the Mo's before leaving.","But now it was not possible, he was in a hurry!","Mo Jiuye knew that when it came to doing business, Tang Mingrui was an impatient man, so he did not try to make him stay.","He Zhiran took the opportunity before Tang Mingrui left to have Lan Er bring a large watermelon for him to take back.","\"Brother Tang, this fruit is also produced by my family. Take it back and try it. I estimate there will be another ten days or so before the ones planted in the fields mature. If you are interested, we can discuss it when the time comes.\"","It was Tang Mingrui's first time seeing such a large fruit.","In fact, even by modern standards, the watermelons grown by He Zhiran were exceptionally outstanding.","After all, they were grown from seeds from the space, so the watermelons were bound to be special in some ways. Huge size was just one trait. More importantly, each one was as sweet as honey.","Moreover, He Zhiran was not worried about her business being snatched away either. She had already tested that only seeds cultivated in the space would not be picky about soil and climate.","The naturally formed seeds planted outside were no different from ordinary seeds.","The land in the northwest was barren, and many crops could not survive at all. Even if those people bought watermelons or cantaloupes, it was unlikely they would have any harvest planting them in the northwest.","Of course, this did not rule out that some smart people might bring the fruit to other regions to plant. Even if they grew successfully, the fruit would be no different from ordinary seeded ones, and could not compare at all to the fruit grown here in terms of either appearance or taste.","Tang Mingrui held the large watermelon, feeling its weight, at least thirty catties.","\"Sister-in-law Nine, this is a fruit?\"","He was almost incredulous. He had seen winter melons produced in Beijing, which were the largest crops in his cognition.","Now, his cognition was completely refreshed by the huge watermelon he was holding, and he had to ask again to convince himself.","He Zhiran had anticipated that the huge watermelon would shock Tang Mingrui. The Mo family people had the same reaction when they first saw it.","She smiled and explained, \"This is a fruit. When you get back, cut it into small pieces with a knife and eat the red flesh inside. It would taste even better if you can store it in a cool place to chill for a while first.\"","The watermelons eaten by the Mo family were usually soaked in the well in advance to cool down, which quenched thirst and cooled off the summer heat.","He Zhiran had also considered using saltpeter to make ice, she just had not had the time for it recently as she was busy with other things.","Tang Mingrui nodded repeatedly as he listened. He was already eagerly looking forward to tasting this large fruit called watermelon.","\"Then I'll have to thank Sister-in-law Nine.\" Then he looked at Mo Jiuye, \"Big brother Nine, you'll have to send some people to help escort Second Master's gang to the prefecture for me.\"","\"No problem, I'll have someone go with you now.\"","Mo Jiuye answered readily. After all, Tang Mingrui had come alone, and it would be difficult for him to escort so many petty thugs on his own.","As for how Tang Mingrui would deal with those people, it was none of his concern. As long as those people stopped causing trouble for the Mo family, things would be fine.","Early the next morning, Tang Mingrui came to transport the cantaloupes, earlier than expected. The sky outside had just brightened.","Fortunately, Mo Jiuye had arranged for people to go pick in the fields in advance. Otherwise, even if they came early, they would have had to wait.","Last night, He Zhiran had quietly placed the cantaloupes stored in the space near the melon fields. With the dogs keeping watch, there was no need to worry at all about them being stolen.","It had been a long time since Tang Mingrui had come to the Mo family in person to take goods. This showed how much importance he attached to the cantaloupe business this time.","On that side, there were people he had brought along with Mo family members responsible for weighing the cantaloupes. Tang Mingrui pulled Mo Jiuye aside and asked excitedly, \"Big Brother Nine, the watermelon you sent yesterday was too delicious. I listened to Sister-in-law Nine and chilled it in the well for a while. It really was crisp and thirst-quenching when eaten.\"","Speaking of this, Tang Mingrui even swallowed subconsciously.","Seeing him like this made Mo Jiuye unable to hold back his laughter.","The relationship between Mo Jiuye and Tang Mingrui was now very close. He put his arm around Tang Mingrui's shoulder and said with a smile,","\"Which do you think would be more popular, watermelon or cantaloupe?\"","\"Both fruits are delicious. If Big Brother insists I make an evaluation, I feel that watermelon tastes slightly better.\"","As Tang Mingrui spoke, his eyes had already started scanning the Mo family's fields.","He knew that the huge watermelons should have also been grown by the Mo family. He wanted to take an early look at what the watermelons looked like in the field.","It was just a pity that as his eyes swept around, he did not catch sight of a single watermelon.","Somewhat disappointed, Tang Mingrui asked, \"Big Brother Nine, aren't the watermelons grown by your family?\"","Yesterday when He Zhiran gave Tang Mingrui a watermelon, it was for the purpose of letting him get an early understanding of future business cooperation. On this point, Mo Jiuye could not possibly conceal anything.","\"The watermelons are also home-grown, it's just that they are not ripe yet at the moment.\"","Hearing this answer, Tang Mingrui was elated.","In his mind, he had already envisioned countless taels of silver flying his way.","Just then, Tang Mingrui excitedly grabbed Mo Jiuye's hand.","\"Big Brother Nine, quick, tell me when the watermelons will ripen?\"","Being grabbed by a grown man felt somewhat strange to Mo Jiuye. He quickly pulled his hand back and took a few steps away.","\"When you've sold all the cantaloupes in the fields, the watermelons will have ripened.\"","This was the timeframe calculated by He Zhiran, because she had discovered a problem.","The watermelon seeds produced by the space would continue to grow in size after maturity even if they were not picked, as long as they remained planted outside.","Of course, the watermelons would not keep growing indefinitely. Once they reached a certain size, growth would stop.","But this timeframe happened to coincide with when the cantaloupes would be almost completely sold off.","Hearing that he still had to wait for some time, Tang Mingrui felt a tinge of disappointment.","It was not for anything else. Nevermind how much profit the watermelons could bring him, at the very least, he and his family would be able to eat their fill of watermelons every day. Just thinking of that feeling made Tang Mingrui incredibly expectant already.","But the watermelons were not yet ripe. It was not something that could be rushed. He could only repress the reluctance in his heart.","\"Alright, the moment the watermelons ripen, Big Brother Nine must immediately send someone to notify me.\"","\"No problem, as soon as the watermelons are ripe, I'll send someone to inform you.\" Detecting Tang Mingrui's thoughts, Mo Jiuye's tone carried a hint of reassurance.","This trip could be considered extremely fruitful for Tang Mingrui. Not knowing just how many cantaloupes the Mo family had for sale, he specifically went to the carriage service to hire several carriage, just to be safe.","Coupled with his own carriage, there was a total of eight carriages.","Unexpectedly, he managed to fill up all eight carriages this trip."]},{"number":407,"title":"Chapter 407: Look who's here.","paragraphs":["This was also thanks to Madam He having made preparations in advance. With her understanding of Tang Mingrui, this guy would definitely bring a lot of carriages over, otherwise there simply wouldn't be enough room for everything.","After sending off Tang Mingrui's group, it wasn't even Chen time yet.","Mo Jiuye had worked up quite a sweat, and was just about to go home to wash up and change, when he saw Song Chao running over.","\"Ninth Master, a carriage has arrived in the village, going around asking about the Mo family's whereabouts.\"","Mo Jiuye wiped the sweat from his forehead, pointed in the direction of the village and said, \"Take me over to take a look.\"","Ever since settling down in Xiling Village, other than becoming familiar with the villagers, there was only Meng Huaining and Tang Mingrui that he could think of having any connection with.","Therefore, he was very curious about the identity of these visitors.","Or rather, he was conspiratorially thinking that it was another person who had come to cause trouble for the Mo family, not knowing better.","With this in mind, Mo Jiuye followed Song Chao into the village.","Ever since the incident where Second Master had brought people to cause trouble for the Mo family, the villagers didn't want any more misfortune to befall them, so when asked about the Mo family's whereabouts, they all avoided answering, with some even directly turning away.","Because he hadn't been able to find out the exact location of the Mo family, the carriage had no clear destination and could only stop on a small road in the village.","The coachman was still asking around, but unfortunately he was asking in vain.","Left with no choice, the coachman could only report back to the carriage.","\"Mistress, the villagers here are all strange, I only asked for directions yet they avoided me as if I were some ferocious beast.\"","Madam He helplessly lifted the carriage curtain to reveal an older female servant helping her down.","She did not blame the coachman. Just now when she had looked out the carriage window, she had already clearly seen the situation.","\"I'll go and ask myself.\"","Mo Jiuye was not very familiar with his mother-in-law.","He had only met her three times. The first time was before he was engaged to He Zhiran, when he went to Minister He's estate to deliver betrothal gifts. Back then it was Minister He and his wife receiving him together, but because of propriety he kept his head lowered while speaking with his father-in-law, and did not look up at his mother-in-law.","The second time was on his wedding day to bring He Zhiran into his household. Minister He and his wife were seeing them off at the door, and Mo Jiuye had only glanced at her for a moment before taking his leave.","The third time was on the day they were exiled. Minister He and his wife had gone to see He Zhiran off. He had also secretly watched from atop the carriage.","And when he went to the capital a few days ago, he had only eavesdropped on the He family's conversation from afar, and did not see his mother-in-law.","Therefore, Mo Jiuye's impression of his mother-in-law was still somewhat vague.","Madam He's outfit today was similar to that of an affluent urban household. The mother-in-law he had seen before was always graceful and elegant, so it was understandable that Mo Jiuye did not recognize her.","However, looking at this woman who, although not dressed very lavishly, still carried an innate grace and virtue that could not be faked, he could determine that she was no ordinary person, and also did not look like someone with ill intentions.","He just found it somewhat confusing what connection the Mo family could have with this woman.","While pondering this in his heart, he had already walked over to Madam He.","As Madam He turned around, she saw two tall figures appear before her.","Although Mo Jiuye did not recognize her as his mother-in-law, Madam He was not a stranger to him.","Back when Mo Jiuye had gone to deliver the betrothal gifts, she had intentionally looked him over a few more times, especially his tall and straight stature which stood out prominently even amongst the crowd.","\"Jiuye,\" seeing Mo Jiuye, Madam He's eyes brimmed with tears, almost spilling over.","Heaven knows how anxious she had been to see her daughter and son-in-law during this trip.","She wanted to see their living environment as soon as possible.","Most importantly, her daughter was about to give birth soon, and she, as her mother, needed to be there for her.","Hearing this call, Mo Jiuye was stunned for a moment, then quickly reacted.","\"Mother-in-law?\"","He tentatively asked. Although he could not recall what his mother-in-law looked like, this voice was familiar, as he had heard it recently in the capital.","As Madam He continuously nodded, tears flowed unchecked down her face.","\"Jiuye, is Ranran well?\" This was her foremost concern right now.","Mo Jiuye stepped forward, \"Mother-in-law, Raran is very well. Seeing you will surely make her very happy. I will take you to see her right away.\"","Song Chao also perceptively realized that the person who had come to Xiling Village looking for the Mo family turned out to be Ninth Master's mother-in-law.","He took the reins from the coachman and walked in front to lead the way.","Madam He was supported by a personal maid as she walked alongside Mo Jiuye.","At this moment, she had no interest in observing her surroundings, only wanting to see her daughter as soon as possible.","He Zhiran was now nearing her due date, and had become lazier than before.","Especially last night, it seemed like the two treasures in her belly were competing, tossing and turning her such that she did not rest well.","Just because of this, He Zhiran had lazed in bed today, only getting up at this time.","Old Lady Mo was worried that it would be inconvenient without anyone by her side to serve her in her advanced pregnancy, hence had thoughtful Lan Er keep her company.","At this time, Lan Er was setting out the specially prepared breakfast for He Zhiran on the stone table in the yard. He Zhiran had just picked up her chopsticks when she heard footsteps and hoofbeats outside the yard.","She found it somewhat strange that someone would be driving a carriage here at this time.","\"Lan Er, go take a look at who's arrived outside.\"","Lan Er responded and opened the yard gate. Mo Jiuye's excited voice floated in.","\"Ranran, come quickly see who's here!\"","He Zhiran put down her chopsticks and got up, looking towards the gate.","The moment she saw Madam He, she froze.","Perhaps it was because she had taken over the original host's body, but this kind of heartfelt intimacy simply could not be faked.","\"Mother?\"","\"Ranran... wuwuwu...\" Seeing her pregnant daughter, Madam He wept torrentially, shaking off her maid's support and rushing towards He Zhiran at top speed.","He Zhiran likewise, with tears flowing down her cheeks like a snapped strand of pearls.","She didn't know why, but the moment she saw Madam He, there wasn't the slightest resentment in her heart, as if it was her own birth mother.","\"Mother... How did you get here?\"","As they spoke, mother and daughter were already weeping bitterly in each other's embrace in full view of everyone.","Mo Jiuye watched from the sidelines, also feeling very awful inside.","If it weren't for the Mo family, Ranran would not have been separated so far from her own mother, not even knowing when they might meet again.","He wanted to step forward and offer comfort, yet did not know what to say, and could only stand stunned on the spot. However, he did not forget to have Song Chao go to Old Lady Mo's courtyard to invite her over.","His mother-in-law had travelled all this way to the northwest, she was an esteemed guest, if his own mother did not promptly show due courtesy, it would reflect badly on them.","It was perceptive Lan Er who saw that the weeping mother and daughter were distressed, and promptly brought over two handkerchiefs for them to dry their tears.","Only then did Madam He realize that her pregnant daughter should avoid such distress for the sake of the child in her belly.","\"Ranran, quickly, stop crying. Let Mother take a look at you.\""]},{"number":408,"title":"Chapter 408: Mother Ran Ran Suffered","paragraphs":["Madam He retreated a few steps, carefully looking over her own daughter.","Although He Zhiran was not wearing the coarse cloth and linen clothes she used to wear, she was also not wearing the previous silks and satins. If it were not for her still stunningly beautiful face, she could easily be ignored in a crowd.","Madam He shook her hands and stroked He Zhiran’s slightly rounder cheeks than before, forcing back her tears and saying:","\"Your mother's Ranan has suffered.\"","Seeing this, He Zhiran hurried to comfort: \"Mother, I'm fine, I didn't suffer at all.\"","Madam He simply did not believe this.","\"There must be suffering on the road to exile, right?\"","Speaking of the exile journey, He Zhiran really did not know how to explain.","She could only evade the subject.","\"Mother, look, my family has built a new house now, and the neighbors on both sides are my sisters-in-law.\"","If it weren't for also building Mo Hanyue a similar quadrangle courtyard as a dowry, He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye’s yard would be in the farthest west position in a row.","Now there was another quadrangle courtyard sent to Mo Hanyue on the west side of their yard, with relatives on both sides as neighbors.","Madam He had already heard from He Yuanming that the Mo men were not dead, but she did not know the specifics.","When He Zhiran mentioned that the neighbors were her sisters-in-law, she asked with concern: \"Is the Mo family situation still good now?\"","For Madam He, every Mo man was tall and mighty, and had made great achievements for the Great Shun. She truly hoped that all the Mo men were alive and well.","He Zhiran could hear the subtext in her mother's words.","\"Mother, not only are all eight elder brothers of the Mo family alive now, but even my father-in-law has been rescued by my husband and them. The Mo family now is reunited without losing a single person.\"","This answer was quite shocking to Madam He.","After all, the news that the Mo men had died in battle one after another was known all over the world at that time.","To say that a few had come back from the dead could already be called a miracle.","As a result, her daughter told her that all the Mo sons were alive, and even the old Duke was alive.","After a long while, Madam He finally nodded with both crying and laughing.","\"Good, good, as long as everyone is alive and the family can be reunited, suffering a little is also good.\"","In Madam He’s heart, how good could life be in a place like this?","Her son-in-law and daughter said they were living well, probably just to reassure their parents!","Thinking of how sensible her daughter and son-in-law were, Madam He's heart ached again.","Seeing that Madam He was showing signs of tears welling up again, He Zhiran quickly changed the subject.","“Mother, let me show you our home in the northwest.”","Madam He wiped the corners of her eyes with a handkerchief, trying hard to hold back the tears. She then reached out and took her daughter's arm.","\"Mother will hold on to you.\"","Madam He had just been preoccupied with reuniting with her daughter after a long absence, and only now noticed that He Zhiran's belly looked rather large.","As someone who had gone through this before, the first thing she thought of was that her little grandson or granddaughter was too big.","When the baby is too big in the mother's womb, it can easily lead to a difficult birth for the expectant mother.","Thinking of this, Madam He instantly broke out in a cold sweat.","She gripped He Zhiran's hand tightly.","\"Ranan, about how much longer until your due date?\"","If there was enough time, she would send someone rushing back to the capital to invite the top obstetrician to come to the northwest, so that her daughter's life would have an extra layer of protection.","The fact that He Zhiran was pregnant with twins was only known to the Mo family, and had not been mentioned to outsiders.","When Mo Jiuye went to the capital, in order not to worry his father-in-law and mother-in-law too much, he did not mention this either.","Now her huge belly was right there, and it was impossible to conceal it even if she wanted to.","Especially when He Zhiran noticed that Madam He's expression had become a little off.","She must have seen that her pregnant belly was too big and was worried about the danger during childbirth.","\"Mother, I'm carrying twins this time, probably due around July.\"","\"What did you say? Twins...\" Madam He's eyes widened, looking incredulous.","Since He Zhiran had chosen to say it, she had anticipated Madam He’s reaction upon hearing it.","She took Madam He’s hand and patted it a few times.","\"Don't worry, Mother. Even though I’m carrying twins, I will definitely be able to give birth smoothly.\"","\"How is that possible?\" Madam He was so anxious that she blurted out what she was thinking.","As far as she knew, she had only heard of two pregnant women carrying twins, and both had died from dystocia in the end.","Her daughter was surely not going to avoid such a fate.","But she quickly realized she had said the wrong thing, and hastily covered her mouth, changing her words: “No, no, no, there’s enough time in a month. Mother will send someone rushing back to the capital right away.","No matter how much money it takes, we must invite the top obstetrician here.","As long as the top obstetrician is here, you and my grandson will not be in danger.\"","After saying this, Madam He didn’t wait for her daughter to react before hurriedly walking towards the gate.","She told Zhang San: “Zhang San, rush back to the capital immediately and have the Master use whatever means necessary to bring the top obstetrician here before early July.\"","Although Madam He was extremely flustered at the moment, she had not completely lost her senses.","While ordering Zhang San to rush back to the capital, she personally took some banknotes out of the luggage in the carriage and handed them to him.","\"Don’t worry about money on the road, change horses when they get tired, you must arrive in the capital at the fastest possible speed.\"","Madam He was so anxious she was about to stretch out her hand and push Zhang San to leave faster.","Seeing this, He Zhiran hurriedly came over to stop her.","\"Mother, don't worry, listen to me.\"","Right now Madam He’s mind was full of how to ensure her daughter’s survival, how could she listen to He Zhiran’s explanation?","She continued urging Zhang San: “Leave now, you can’t delay for a moment on the road.”","“Mother, listen to me, it’s really not as dangerous as you think.”","Seeing that Zhang San had started to unhitch the horses from the carriage, Madam He finally turned to look at He Zhiran again.","\"As someone with experience, your mother knows better than you. Matters of life and death cannot be taken lightly.\"","As she spoke, Madam He cried again, grabbing He Zhiran's hand and choking with sobs:","\"Your father and I only have you as a daughter. If something happens to you, how can we still live?\"","The fact that they let their daughter marry into the exiled Mo family in the northwest already weighed heavily with guilt on their consciences. If their daughter were now to lose her life due to childbirth, she was afraid she would not be able to go on living.","\"Mother, don't assume that just because I’m carrying twins that I haven’t made preparations.\"","The original host stayed inside the house all day when she was at home, and only liked to read those strange medical books.","So He Zhiran felt that her excuse was very convincing.","Seeing that Madam He was listening, He Zhiran went on.","“Have you forgotten, Mother? I read those medical books every day when I was at home. Don't look down on the books I read. There are methods for safely giving birth to twins in them.\""]},{"number":409,"title":"Chapter 409: This gift is too expensive.","paragraphs":["To make her words more persuasive, He Zhiran continued, \"When my husband and I were out, we happened to encounter a pregnant woman expecting twins who was in a critical condition.","I used the techniques I learned to save both her and the babies' lives.\"","Madam He didn't refute when it came to the medical books that He Zhiran had been reading.","Their daughter had always had such limited interests.","Whether it was playing musical instruments, chess, calligraphy, or painting, she merely dabbled in them without putting much effort.","She had no interest at all in learning needlework or embroidery.","But when it came to medicine, she was truly obsessed. Sometimes, when she found a medical book she liked, she would even forget to eat and sleep.","However, Madam He had never known what level of skill their daughter had reached with all those medical books.","After all, they didn't object to He Zhiran reading them and thought it would help pass the time. They had never considered that she would achieve any significant accomplishments in medicine.","But just now, she heard her daughter say that she had actually saved a pregnant woman expecting twins.","This completely exceeded Madam He's understanding.","To put her mother-in-law's mind at ease, Mo Jiuye, who had been silent for a long time, walked over.","\"Mother, what Zhiran said is true. She did help the pregnant woman expecting twins deliver safely.\"","Mo Jiuye had the confidence to speak up. Ever since he learned that his wife was pregnant with twins, he had been studying cesarean section operations in detail whenever he had free time.","Although he hadn't performed one yet, he had already memorized the theory thoroughly.","Not only that, He Zhiran had also helped him purchase instructional videos on Taobao. After watching them and combining the knowledge he had gained, he was confident that he could ensure a successful procedure.","Madam He felt annoyed when she saw Mo Jiuye. It was this troublemaker who caused their daughter to become pregnant with twins.","However, her self-cultivation wouldn't allow her to show her dissatisfaction too clearly.","\"Since you both say so, I will go and see the pregnant woman that Zhiran saved.\"","She knew that her daughter liked reading medical books, but she had never seen her daughter personally treat any patients. So, Madam He was still skeptical even after hearing their words.","Pregnancy with twins was no small matter, and she needed to see it with her own eyes to believe it.","At this moment, Zhang San was already on horseback.","\"Madam, I will hurry to the capital city,\" he said.","He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye didn't stop him.","Especially He Zhiran, she knew Madam He's temper very well from the memories of the original owner of her body.","If they were to prevent Zhang San from going to the capital city to invite the renowned gynecologist, Madam He would be even more restless day and night. It was better to let her hold on to some hope than to see her worried every day.","Madam He felt somewhat relieved as she watched Zhang San ride away. She believed that as long as they could bring the gynecologist, their daughter would have a smooth delivery.","He Zhiran didn't know who the renowned gynecologist that Madam He mentioned was, but she didn't underestimate the medical skills of people from ancient times.","Everyone has their specialized field, and someone who can be called a gynecology expert must have extraordinary medical skills.","If they could really invite that person, it would undoubtedly be a good thing.","Mo Jiuye had initially wanted to come up with an excuse to appease his mother-in-law. However, seeing that she had shifted her attention due to Zhang San's departure, he decided not to explain himself for now and wait until his mother-in-law brought it up.","Just then, Old Lady Mo hurriedly arrived, accompanied by Mo Hanyue.","Old Lady Mo genuinely respected Madam He, knowing that she had raised such a good daughter who married into the Mo family.","Even before she entered the courtyard, her voice could be heard.","\"Has my mother-in-law arrived?\"","When she was in the capital, Madam He had interacted with Old Lady Mo on several occasions, so she was familiar with her voice.","She quickly walked towards the direction of the entrance.","\"Mother-in-law, I miss my daughter so much that I rushed here to accompany her during childbirth. I might trouble you for a while in the future, so please don't be bothered by it.\"","As they spoke, the two of them had already met.","Mo Hanyue also respectfully greeted Madam He.","After all, both of them were aristocrats from the capital, so they were well-versed in etiquette.","Madam He quickly signaled the nanny who had come with her, and soon enough, the nanny took out a purse from the carriage and handed it to Mo Hanyue.","Mo Hanyue was the youngest child of the Mo family and was still unmarried. This was also her first meeting with Madam He, so it was natural that there would be a gift exchange.","As Mo Hanyue was about to decline, Madam He smiled and said, \"Since it's our first meeting, let's consider it as a gift from Aunt He.\"","The moment Mo Hanyue received the purse, she pinched it with her hand. It didn't contain silver or banknotes but small grains.","She was very familiar with this thing—they were gold melon seeds.","Now that she was involved in daily labor, she understood the difficulty of earning money and knew the considerable value of these gold melon seeds.","Such a precious gift, she couldn't accept it.","\"Thank you, Aunt He, for your kindness, but this gift is too valuable. Hanyue feels unworthy of it.\"","Seeing Mo Hanyue's generous demeanor, Madam He felt even more distressed.","Such a good girl, just like her Zhiran, but she had innocently come to this barren place to suffer.","If the prosperity of the Mo family still existed, with the exceptional qualities of the Mo daughters, there would be countless suitors knocking on their door.","Madam He didn't know that Mo Hanyue had already arranged a good marriage, so she sincerely pitied her.","She held Mo Hanyue's hand, which was holding the red envelope, and gently patted it.","\"Good girl, Auntie wants you to keep it. We're all relatives, no need to be so polite.\"","Old Lady Mo could tell that the red envelope from Aunt He had to be given away.","\"Hanyue, this is Aunt He's heartfelt gift. You should accept it.\"","Seeing her mother speak, Mo Hanyue graciously bowed to Madam He.","\"Then, thank you, Auntie.\"","\"That's right,\" Madam He said softly.","As the host, Old Lady Mo gestured once again, inviting Madam He to come inside and sit down.","At this moment, Madam He wasn't as upset as when she had seen He Zhiran. Especially since she had already sent Zhang San to the capital to invite a renowned gynecologist, her mood had improved slightly.","She walked side by side with Old Lady Mo into the courtyard, while also taking in her surroundings.","This glance didn't go unnoticed and actually surprised her.","The courtyard appeared square and neat, with smooth square bricks covering the ground. In the northwest corner of the courtyard, there was a grape trellis with neatly arranged stone tables and chairs underneath.","The structure of the house was quite unique but looked very comfortable.","Most importantly, the windows of their house seemed to be made of glass...","Although glass was a rarity in this era, as the wife of the imperial Grand Minister, she still had some knowledge.","Back when Emperor Shunwu celebrated the Empress Dowager's 60th birthday, she had accompanied those noble ladies to the Longevity Palace where the Empress Dowager resided.","There was a special little house in the Longevity Palace, which was said to be the place where the Empress Dowager watched the snow during winter."]},{"number":410,"title":"Chapter 410: The Big Lady's home is too grand.","paragraphs":["The windows of that small hut were made of glass.","It was said that the glass was brought from the West by foreigners to be presented as a tribute to Emperor Shunwu, and there were only those two small pieces.","In order to show his filial piety, Emperor Shunwu used those two pieces of glass to build a special small hut for the Empress Dowager.","At that time, many people privately discussed the value of those two pieces of glass. Finally, an old eunuch quietly told everyone that those two pieces of glass were worth 10,000 taels of silver.","Now looking at Madam He's house, every window is made of glass, and the windows are several times larger than those in the Empress Dowager's house.","How...how much silver would that cost?!","As Madam He was still in shock, she had already been invited into the main hall by Old Lady Mo.","At this point, her eyes were even more overwhelmed. Accompanying her, her old maid Aunt Li could not help but say, \"Oh my goodness, Madam, isn't the young lady's family residence too luxurious?!\"","Indeed, Mo Jiuye had made the main room into a living room. Although the furnishings were from the hands of ancients, they tended towards some modern styles.","Especially conspicuous was the full-length mirror on the left side of the room.","There were also porcelain tiles with light and elegant patterns on the floor that went perfectly with the furnishings, fully deserving of the word “luxurious”.","Although Old Lady Mo had chosen antique-style furniture for her new residence, she was not unfamiliar with the furnishings in her son's home.","She quickly walked over to point to the sofa in the center of the living room and said,","\"The mother-in-law has traveled a long way by boat and carriage. Please sit down and rest first. You mother and daughter have not seen each other for a long time and can slowly chat.\"","After speaking, she turned her head to Mo Hanyue and said, \"Hanyue, go notify your brother and sister-in-law that we have an esteemed guest. Ask anyone who's free to come greet them, and also have Yu'er prepare dinner.\"","\"Yes, Mother. I'll go now.\"","As Mo Hanyue left, Old Lady Mo had already pulled Madam He to sit on the sofa.","Mo Jiuye supported He Zhiran to sit beside Madam He.","Madam He had now recovered from her shock.","She looked at her daughter and asked,","\"Ranran, are the windows in this house made of glass?","Is that a mirror?","The furnishings in this room?","...","This is simply more luxurious than the imperial palace. In any case, Madam He did not believe that the Mo family would have such financial resources.","Moreover, when they were exiled, the emperor ordered the confiscation of all assets from the Mo family and did not allow them to bring any valuables.","She and He Yuanming had gone to see them off at the outskirts of the capital. She saw with her own eyes that the most valuable thing was the wooden cart that Mo Jiuye was lying on.","This made Madam He very puzzled about where the Mo family's money was coming from.","Her daughter knew that her mother would have countless questions after seeing all this.","\"Mother, what's used for the windows is not glass, but glass brought by foreigners.","As you know, Yancheng is close to the sea. Foreign ships occasionally dock at the pier there. This glass was purchased from the foreigners,\" He Zhiran explained.","\"And these mirrors and tiles are also from the foreigners.”","The excuse of foreigners had been utilized to the fullest extent by Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran. Even they themselves had come to believe it somewhat.","However, Madam He was not clear about the current foundation of the Mo family. No matter how appropriate He Zhiran's explanation was, what she still wondered about in her mind was where the Mo family's money came from.","But she knew better than anyone that even for her own daughter’s in-laws, it would be inappropriate for her to directly inquire about their money.","If she really wanted to understand, she could not ask her daughter about it in front of her mother-in-law.","On the contrary, Old Lady Mo did not feel there was anything about the Mo family's current situation that could not stand the light of day.","She could see Madam He's curiosity underneath.","\"If I have to thank the mother-in-law for the good life the Mo family enjoys today, I really should. If it weren't for you marrying such a good daughter to Jiuye, forget about the Mo family today, I'm afraid we would have died on the road to exile.\"","Old Lady Mo's words made Madam He even more confused.","No one knew her daughter's abilities better than her as the mother.","Even if the mother-in-law wanted to praise her daughter in front of her, there was no need to exaggerate to this extent, right?","At this moment, He Zhiran was indeed a little nervous.","From the memories of the original owner she had received, other than a habitual interest in medical books, there were no other special skills.","But things had already been talked up to this point by the mother-in-law, and she was not lying either.","If it were not for her, not to mention the Mo family living safely in the northwest and reunited, they probably would have died on the road to exile.","As she was thinking about how to smooth things over, Mo Jiuye spoke up.","\"Mother-in-law, Ranan is very clever. She told me that since she was young, she liked to read medical books at home, but never had a chance to demonstrate her skills in the capital. On the road to exile, in order to take care of everyone, she finally revealed her true talents.","My mother said that the Mo family today owes much to Ranan. This is not false at all. Not only is her medical skill superb, she also came up with many money-making ideas.","When we were on the road, she utilized furry fabrics bought from foreigners to make stuffed animals very popular with girls, earning silver that not only covered our travel expenses but also left over to invest in industries here.\"","Mo Jiuye was the only one who knew about He Zhiran's space. He knew that her skills all came from there.","In order not to expose his wife's space, he tried his best to explain.","The original owner was not good at women's needlework. He Zhiran was worried that her mother might be suspicious, so she continued to explain,","\"Mother, don't listen to mother-in-law and my husband exaggerating. It was indeed my idea at the time to make money by producing stuffed toys, but as you know, I am not skilled at needlework. It was done by mother-in-law and my sisters-in-law.”","Madam He had been a little doubtful after hearing Mo Jiuye's words. She knew better than anyone that her daughter was not good at women’s needlework.","Now after hearing He Zhiran say this, she understood.","Just as Madam He was about to say something more, the maid Aunt Li standing behind her spoke up.","\"Young lady, were the stuffed toys you made brightly colored and fluffy?\"","He Zhiran did not dare guarantee that the fluffiness came from the hands of the Mo family. But when it came to bright colors, she certainly did not shy away.","After all, the dyes for the stuffed toys produced by the Mo family came from Taobao Mall, something impossible for the people of this era to imitate even if they wanted to.","He Zhiran nodded, \"What Aunt Li said is correct. The colorful stuffed toys on the market are indeed produced by our family.”","Seeing He Zhiran acknowledge it, Aunt Li smiled, her wrinkles able to trap a mosquito.","\"That’s right.”","Seeing that Madam He was still confused, Aunt Li explained,","“Madam, you don't know that on our way to the northwest, I saw many shops selling colorful fluffy stuffed toys and ornaments that many young ladies were eagerly buying up. What’s more important is that the asking price for the stuffed toys was actually twenty taels of silver each!\""]},{"number":411,"title":"Chapter 411: From Mohism","paragraphs":["On the way to the northwest, Li Auntie took care of Madam He's daily needs, which meant that she would go shopping almost every time they passed through a city.","She noticed that in several cities near the northwest, there were adorable plush dolls being sold.","Having watched He Zhiran grow up since she was a child, Li Auntie's affection for her was no less than that of Madam He, her own mother.","She had been looking forward to seeing the young miss and wanted to bring her a gift.","When she saw those plush dolls, Li Auntie guessed that the young miss would surely like them.","But then she was taken aback when she asked about the price—twenty taels of silver for each doll!","After serving the He family for half a lifetime, it was impossible for her not to have twenty taels of silver.","However, since she was accompanying Madam He on the trip and wouldn't need any expenses along the way, she only brought a few taels of loose silver.","As a result, Li Auntie was deeply impressed by those plush dolls of various colors.","The original host of He Zhiran's soul was also very close to Li Auntie. Just now, He Zhiran was busy catching up with Madam He, and now she finally shifted her attention to Li Auntie.","He Zhiran, who came from the modern world, still held the belief in equality for all in her heart.","Pointing to the single sofas on both sides of the large couch, she said, \"Auntie, you've been working hard all the way. Please have a seat and take a rest.\"","Li Auntie repeatedly waved her hand and said, \"Young Miss, I can't do that. I'm just a servant. How can I dare to sit with the master? It would be disrespectful.\"","He Zhiran felt helpless facing such deeply ingrained beliefs of ancient people.","Just as she was about to say something, Old Lady Mo spoke up.","\"Auntie, listen to our young miss. The Mo family is no longer a prominent household now. We're just an ordinary family, and those old customs no longer apply.\"","She could see that her daughter-in-law valued Li Auntie a lot, so she wanted to help.","Madam He looked at her daughter and then at her mother-in-law. Seeing that they showed no signs of objection, she also understood that the Mo family indeed no longer adhered to so many rules.","She looked at Li Auntie, who was still standing there in an orderly manner.","\"Li Auntie, since the mother-in-law and the young miss allow it, you should sit down!\"","Li Auntie was indeed a bit sore and tired, and when Madam He spoke, she didn't continue to be coy.","\"Then I'll sit.\"","Seeing Li Auntie sitting down, He Zhiran took out a large panda plush toy and a pink long-eared rabbit plush toy from the empty space on the tea table.","\"Auntie, are these the dolls you saw on the way?\"","Li Auntie nodded repeatedly, \"Yes, these are the dolls. They're really expensive, twenty taels of silver each.\"","Madam He was seeing such cute and beautiful dolls for the first time.","She asked in disbelief, \"Ranran, did you say these dolls are made by the Mo family?\"","\"Yes, Mother. These dolls being sold in the market are all made by the Mo family.\"","At this moment, Li Auntie seemed to remember something else.","\"There's another kind made with rabbit fur, and the colors are even more beautiful.\"","\"Mommy, that's called a Long-Eared Rabbit Pendant, also from the Mo Family,\" He Zhiran paused and continued, \"After we arrived at Xi Ling Village, we started raising rabbits. This plush pendant is made from the rabbit fur we produce ourselves. Don't be deceived by the high market price; the actual cost is very low.\"","There was a reason for He Zhiran's explanation.","Currently, the living conditions in the Mo Family are no less than those of wealthy households in the city, or even surpass them. Money must have a reasonable source.","Although selling plush toys and raising rabbits are profitable, it's hard to convince people that they can earn so much money all at once.","Indeed, ever since the Mo Family arrived at Xi Ling Village, their industries have not solely relied on the profits from selling these plush toys. To some extent, they have also benefited from some wealth obtained from the state treasury.","Madam He is not a business person and lacks any economic acumen.","She only heard her daughter say that a doll costs twenty taels of silver, and the beautiful pendant's raw materials are also from the Mo Family. She already firmly believes in the financial strength of the Mo Family.","The Mo Family is not lacking in money, and Madam He is delighted to see them live a comfortable life.","Although she can't see her daughter often, as long as she is doing well, Madam He can be at ease.","Now, seeing Old Lady Mo and her own son-in-law caring for her precious daughter, Madam He finally let go of half of her worries.","Of course, the other half that she hasn't let go of yet is the matter of her carrying two children in her womb. Until Zhang San, the renowned gynecologist, arrives from the capital, she won't be able to stop worrying.","He Zhiran doesn't know what her mother is thinking. Seeing her mother's face no longer filled with worry as when she first arrived, she assumes her mother is relieved to see that she's doing well.","At the same time, she understands that her mother has traveled all the way to the northwest to accompany her during childbirth, so she probably won't leave for a short time.","Old Lady Mo also has the same understanding.","\"Mother-in-law, you must stay in the northwest for a few more days. You just arrived here and don't know that our home has many new and interesting things. I guarantee that once you settle in, you won't want to go back.\"","If these words were spoken when Madam He first entered the village, she would never have believed them.","Now, seeing her daughter's beautiful house and furnishings, she knows that Old Lady Mo wasn't exaggerating.","Away from the hustle and bustle of the city, everything in front and behind the house feels so comfortable, especially the rooms, which are even more comfortable than the palace.","The seats beneath her are made of some unknown material, so soft that sitting on them makes most of the fatigue from the journey dissipate.","It can be said that Madam He has already begun to like it here.","\"Indeed, as you said, I came this time to accompany Ruan Ruan during her delivery. I'm afraid I'll be troubling you for a few days.\"","\"No trouble at all. We are all very happy that you could come.\"","As they exchanged pleasantries, the sisters-in-law who heard the news also arrived one after another.","Not only did they come, but they also brought watermelons and fruits from their own courtyard, which had been cooled in the well.","Madam He's sisters-in-law warmly greeted their ninth sister-in-law and then proceeded to recommend the delicious fruits they had brought along.","Second Sister-in-law was the most enthusiastic among them. She presented a plate of sliced watermelon to Madam He.","\"Madam He, please try this watermelon. It's a unique fruit exclusive to our Mo Family. You won't find it anywhere else,\" Second Sister-in-law said.","Madam He looked at the watermelon, feeling a bit perplexed.","This red fruit, cut into small pieces, was indeed something she had never seen before. What's more, she had no idea how to eat it.","Old Lady Mo, seeing her confusion, explained, \"Dear mother-in-law, you eat the red flesh of this watermelon. It's very refreshing, especially in the hot weather.\"","Madam He was someone who hesitated to try new things. However, due to the excessive enthusiasm of the mother-in-law and daughter-in-law from the Mo Family, she reluctantly accepted it."]},{"number":412,"title":"Chapter 412: Thank God","paragraphs":["He Zhiran inherited all the memories and emotions of the original owner, so she had a good understanding of Madam He and knew that she wasn't very receptive to new things.","However, this watermelon was truly a fantastic treat, and it would be a great loss if her mother didn't give it a try.","\"Mother, what Mother-in-law and Second Sister-in-law said is right. Watermelon is sweet, juicy, and incredibly refreshing. You should try it,\" He Zhiran urged.","Madam He offered a bitter smile to her daughter.","She couldn't help but wonder, \"Is this really my own daughter?\"","In the past, whenever such a situation arose, her daughter would step forward to help her out. But now that she was in her daughter's husband's family, not only did she not help, she was actually persuading her.","Madam He couldn't let her little quirk tarnish her manners, so she forced herself to take a small bite in front of everyone's gaze.","Seeing that she had already swallowed the watermelon in her mouth, He Zhiran smiled and asked, \"Mother, is it delicious?\"","\"It's delicious indeed, just as you all said. It's sweet and juicy,\" Madam He sincerely praised.","Luckily, she listened and gave it a taste; otherwise, she would have missed out on such a delicious fruit.","Seeing that she liked it, Second Sister-in-law brought a few more pieces to her.","\"Aunt He, if you like it, eat more,\" Second Sister-in-law said.","At the same time, He Zhiran also handed a piece to Nanny Li.","Madam He discovered the deliciousness of watermelon, so when the other sisters-in-law offered her other fruits, she didn't refuse anymore.","Apart from watermelon and cantaloupe, which were grown by the Mo family themselves, all the other fruits were brought from the space by He Zhiran, distributed to everyone in the courtyard by Mo Jiuye whenever he went into the city.","The sisters-in-law treasured these delicious fruits dearly. If it weren't for them treating Madam He as an esteemed guest, they definitely wouldn't have brought them out.","As Madam He enjoyed the delicious fruits and chatted with everyone, she couldn't help but feel that her daughter was living a good life.","When Mo's mother, who had traveled a long way, finished her conversation and left with her daughters-in-law, she asked Madam He to rest for a while.","After everyone left, He Zhiran personally arranged a room for her mother and Nanny Li.","When Madam He saw the bedroom in her daughter's house, her perception was once again refreshed.","The bedroom had the same beautiful floor tiles as the living room. The furnishings looked simple but had an elegant charm.","Madam He instantly fell in love with the place, especially the soft, comfortable bed. Sleeping on it would certainly be a great pleasure.","And then there was that thing they called a bathroom, which was like something out of a fairy tale for Madam He.","When she was in the capital, there were servants to attend to her, so although she didn't need to go outside to use the toilet, the smell of the chamber pot was nauseating.","The bathroom in her daughter's house completely resolved this embarrassment. Just by pulling the rope above, the water would automatically flush away the waste.","It was truly miraculous.","At this moment, Madam He felt like Liu Laolao touring the Grand View Garden, finding everything fresh and new, eagerly asking He Zhiran about this and that.","He Zhiran patiently explained everything to her.","Nanny Li looked at her mistress and young mistress with envy, envious that they could enjoy such good things.","Meanwhile, she had already chosen a resting spot for herself, which was a soft area under the window resembling a futon.","In fact, that was a tatami bed specially made by He Zhiran for Hu Cong, with a manually adjustable table in the middle where two people could sit and have tea together.","Li Mammy thought that sleeping there would be sufficient and convenient for taking care of Madam.","Unexpectedly, Miss had also arranged a bedroom like that for her. For Li Mammy, it was simply an overwhelming favor.","However, she also noticed that Miss had many rooms in her courtyard, seemingly occupied only by her and Young Master. Since the rooms were idle, she would take advantage of the opportunity to enjoy them.","He Zhiran thought that after the hard journey, her mother and Li Mammy would rest for a while.","To her surprise, these two still appeared spirited.","Since there was no one around at the moment, He Zhiran decided to inquire about the situation at home.","\"Mother, is Father and Big Brother doing well?\"","When it came to this, Madam He still had some lingering fears.","\"Thanks to Jiuye going to the capital and dealing with Princess Yujun, otherwise our family wouldn't have any peaceful days.\"","These were indeed the issues that He Zhiran was concerned about.","If it weren't for considering the possibility that the matter of the Mo Family's exile might implicate her maternal family, she would have written a letter to inquire long ago.","Seeing her mother now, He Zhiran had a lot of questions to ask.","\"Mother, how is the Ninth Prince's Mansion now?\"","Upon hearing the words \"Ninth Prince's Mansion,\" Madam He's expression turned somewhat grim.","\"I can only say that because of Jiuye's appearance, your father escaped a disaster.\"","Seeing her mother's expression, He Zhiran knew that things were serious.","\"Mother, what exactly happened?\"","\"General Jin, the Grand Academician, and the Left Prime Minister have all been found to be infected with the Puppetry Gu.\"","According to your father, although those people were infected with the Puppetry Gu, they didn't commit any acts against the court. They simply lost their autonomy and even had great difficulty eating.\"","This situation was not surprising to He Zhiran. No one understood better than her that those infected with the Puppetry Gu had no self-awareness and could only eat independently by being controlled by the Gu Keeper.","The Puppetry Gu on these people was planted by the Ninth Prince, and the person providing the Puppetry Gu to the Ninth Prince was Mr. Si Meng.","In other words, the mother Gu of the Puppetry Gu should be in Mr. Si Meng's hands, or rather, it was now in her space.","When they helped their father and brothers dispel the Gu, they discovered that there were several mother Gu present, but they were not clear about where the offspring Gu they bred had gone.","Now it seemed that those mother Gu in her space were very likely the ones controlling several important figures in the capital.","Leaving aside the Grand Academician and the Left Prime Minister, whom He Zhiran had no impression of, she had a great impression of General Jin. Moreover, Mo Jiuye often mentioned that General Jin was upright and had shown kindness to the Mo Family during their exile.","Considering this, it was correct for her and Mo Jiuye not to immediately kill those mother Gu back then. If those mother Gu were really the ones controlling the important figures in the capital, killing the mother Gu would be equivalent to indirectly killing those people.","Madam He was unaware of her daughter's thoughts, assuming that she had been frightened by her own words.","\"Ranran, your father said that the Emperor has already sent people to search for experts who can cure the curse. Although there's currently no one in the capital who can help them, the imperial physicians have been dispatched to find a solution. Their lives are temporarily safe,\" Madam He said.","As she spoke, Madam He clasped her hands together and chanted, \"Amitabha Buddha, thank heavens, it's fortunate that Jiuye came to the capital. That's how your father was spared from harm.\"","Reflecting on it now, Madam He still felt a lingering fear. She had heard from He Yuanming that those afflicted by the curse remained bedridden, resembling lifeless bodies.","He Zhiran noticed her mother's concern and held her hand, saying, \"Mother, as long as Father is safe, you can rest assured.\""]},{"number":413,"title":"Chapter 413: I'm worried about General Kim.","paragraphs":["Although affairs at the royal court had nothing to do with her, He Zhiran was still curious to understand the specific situation.","\"Mother, since the Emperor has already sent people to search for experts who can break curses, does that mean the Ninth Prince has been exposed?\"","Seeing her daughter's interest, Madam He told her what she knew.","\"After Jiu Ye saved your father that day, your father didn't immediately go to court to expose the matter, but first returned home to discuss it with your elder brother.\"","This point, He Zhiran couldn't deny it. In the original owner's memory, this elder brother of hers was extremely talented and even more insightful in analyzing situations than He Yuanming. Thus, it wasn't strange at all that her father returned to discuss it with her elder brother.","Madam He continued.","\"Your elder brother's opinion was that this matter was no small thing. Since the Ninth Prince could do such a big thing, he must have planned his escape route beforehand. Moreover, your father didn't obtain evidence of the Ninth Prince's rebellion when he returned from the Ninth Prince's Mansion.","Therefore, your elder brother suggested that your father should mainly observe and wait.","Of course, this observation didn't mean absolutely hiding at home and not going out. The direction of events still needed to be grasped in real-time to adapt to any changes.","At the same time, your father also thought about his own escape route. He went to the Ninth Prince's Mansion to congratulate him on his birthday and wasn't successfully plotted against by the Ninth Prince. The Ninth Prince would definitely bear a grudge in his heart. If he succeeded in rebellion, he would definitely take revenge on your father.","We had even made preparations to leave the capital city.\"","The more He Zhiran listened, the more interested she became, and she asked, \"Mother, what happened then? How was the Ninth Prince exposed?\"","\"This was thanks to the efforts of Prince Qi. Not long after your father returned, he heard the sound of horse hooves outside. It turned out that Prince Qi had encircled the Ninth Prince's Mansion with his troops before making a report.","I don't know who gave him the idea, but afraid that the Ninth Prince would quietly escape, Prince Qi first led people to enter the mansion and capture him.","It is said that when Prince Qi entered the Ninth Prince's Mansion, General Jin, the Imperial Tutor of the Inner Court, and the Left Prime Minister had already lost consciousness and were sitting motionlessly in chairs, unresponsive to anyone's actions.","As your father said, Jiu Ye told Mr. Fei about this, so Prince Qi also knew these people were cursed, and they became important evidence of the Ninth Prince's rebellion.","With evidence, Prince Qi immediately went to court to report this matter to the Emperor. With one imperial decree, all people inside the Ninth Prince's Mansion were arrested, and the Emperor gave Prince Qi full authority to handle this matter.","How could Prince Qi miss such an opportunity to make contributions?","Moreover, what the Ninth Prince did posed a huge threat to him, so he couldn't easily pardon those involved in this matter.","Later, through severe torture, it was learned that the Ninth Prince had been biding his time for many years, just waiting for the right opportunity to take action. Who would have thought that this matter was unexpectedly resolved by Jiu Ye's timely intervention?\"","At this point, Madam He became even more convinced of her son-in-law's excellence. If it weren't for his appearance, not only would the Da Shun Dynasty be in danger of a change in power, but her He family would likely not have been spared from destruction.","In fact, He Zhiran didn't yet know that because of reporting this matter to Prince Qi, Fei Nanyu had gained even more favor from Prince Qi, and now he was getting closer and closer to his own opportunity to rise.","She continued to ask, \"How did Emperor Shunwu deal with the Ninth Prince?\"","\"After the truth came to light, the Emperor immediately issued an edict to exterminate the entire Ninth Prince's Mansion.\"","As for sparing the Ninth Prince's clan, that wasn't an option, since Emperor Shunwu was also part of the Ninth Prince's clan.","After discussing the Ninth Prince's rebellion, mother and daughter chatted about some other matters. Seeing that her mother appeared tired, knowing it was due to the fatigue of travel and lack of rest, He Zhiran let her rest for a while and went to find Mo Jiuye to tell him what she had learned from her mother.","After hearing this, Mo Jiuye didn't seem as relaxed as He Zhiran appeared to be.","He Zhiran was already very familiar with his temperament and asked, \"Husband, do you feel that something is amiss?\"","Mo Jiuye did indeed feel that something was amiss, but the reason was not due to the situation in the imperial court, but rather because of General Jin.","General Jin had always had an exceptional relationship with the Mo family. In the past, he went through life and death situations together with Mo Jiuye's father many times. If General Jin's curse was known to his father, he would likely not just stand by and do nothing.","\"I'm worried about General Jin. He's my father's good brother.\"","This matter had just occurred to He Zhiran as well. She didn't know about General Jin's friendship with Mo Kun, but she was aware that during their exile, General Jin had not only helped them a great deal but had also given them a substantial sum of money.","He Zhiran was also a grateful person. Just for that reason alone, she didn't wish for anything to happen to General Jin.","\"Husband, why don't you go to the capital city yourself?\"","Upon hearing He Zhiran's words, Mo Jiuye instinctively looked at her large belly.","\"It won't work. You're going to give birth in a little over a month. I can't leave at this time.\"","Although his wife still had more than a month until her due date, if he rode a fast horse to the capital city, he could definitely return within a month.","However, his wife was carrying twins, and when he was learning about cesarean sections, the books mentioned that twins are prone to premature birth.","If his wife went into labor early and he wasn't by her side, and some accident occurred, he wouldn't be able to forgive himself for the rest of his life.","He Zhiran was also aware of her own situation. Allowing Mo Jiuye to leave now would indeed not be wise.","However, aside from using modern medical techniques for surgery, there was only one other way to remove the curse.","That was to use the mother curse to attract the child curse.","Of course, this also required someone skilled in curses to perform the operation; ordinary people couldn't do it.","When the couple discussed this private matter, they habitually did so in the space.","It so happened that at this moment, the puppy was playing and frolicking with Little White in the open area.","\"Husband, can you let Little White go to the capital city to deliver a message to Fei Nanyu, asking him to help keep an eye on General Jin's situation?\"","Mo Jiuye had some difficulty understanding his wife's meaning.","\"There's no problem letting Little White deliver a message, but it won't help with removing General Jin's curse at all.\"","Seeing Mo Jiuye's clueless expression, He Zhiran couldn't help but smile.","\"Have Little White go to the capital, and in the message, make it clear that if General Jin is still alive, Little White should temporarily stay in the capital until Emperor Shunwu summons someone who can remove curses.\"","The reason she wanted Little White to deliver the message to Fei Nanyu instead of to her own father and brothers was also because of something specific.","He Yuanming had been an official for many years and never participated in these intrigues at court. Thus, when the entire Mo family was confiscated and exiled, as the in-laws of the Mo family, He Yuanming was not implicated.","If the message was sent to her father, he would be forced to participate in these matters and might even be suspected by Emperor Shunwu of colluding with the people from the Southern Territory.","After all, when the time came to remove the curses from those people, Mo Jiuye would send Little White to deliver the mother curse.","If He Yuanming held three curse insects in his hands, even if he jumped into the Yellow River, he couldn't wash away this injustice if it aroused Emperor Shunwu's suspicion."]},{"number":414,"title":"Chapter 414: Sending a Letter to the Capital","paragraphs":["But Fei Nanyu was different. He appeared to be from Nan Qi, and now in the capital, aside from Emperor Shunwu, he was already publicly recognized as the next emperor.","He would not do something like using insects to harm people.","Therefore, even if he took out the insects, he would not be suspected by others.","Moreover, Fei Nanyu was currently considered trustworthy, so entrusting this matter to him was equivalent to letting Nan Qi act directly.","This way, Mo Jiuye finally understood.","\"Ran Ran, do you mean Emperor Shunwu asked the powerful insect-taming expert to have Little White come back and take the puppeteer insects?\"","\"Yes, that's what I mean. Currently, only this way can work.\"","She also firmly believed that in this era, even if an insect tamer's skills were high, without the mother insect, they likely could not successfully untame the insects.","\"Good, I will write to Fei Nanyu now and have Little White set off immediately.\" Mo Jiuye said as he walked to the desk and started writing.","Finally, he did not forget to remind Fei Nanyu to treat Little White well with good food and drink while it was with him.","After writing the letter, Mo Jiuye called Little White over and tied the letter to its leg.","Ever since Little White acknowledged Mo Jiuye as its master, the human and bird established a deep bond, especially on the journey to rescue Mo Meng and his father when Little White was almost inseparable from him.","Mo Jiuye stroked Little White's soft feathers reluctantly.","\"Little White, this time I'm afraid it will be hard on you to deliver the letter to the capital...\"","After its master assigned the task, Little White flew high, circling repeatedly above Mo Jiuye's head, clearly reluctant to leave.","Reluctant but with no choice, rescuing people was the priority.","He Zhiran brought Mo Jiuye and Little White out of the space together, fed it some food, and finally let it leave.","Little White's flight speed was extremely fast, taking only about two days to reach the capital from the northwest.","Hopefully everything would develop in a good direction, Older Jin's life would continue, and Emperor Shunwu could quickly find an insect tamer.","Madam He was indeed a little tired on the road and originally planned to listen to her daughter and rest in the room.","However, she did not know if it was because she saw her daughter too excited or had too much on her mind, but she tossed and turned, unable to sleep.","Unable to sleep, she could only get up. When she found He Zhiran, the young couple had just sent Little White off.","Seeing her mother, He Zhiran obviously looked a little surprised.","\"Mother, why don't you sleep a little longer?\"","\"Mother couldn't sleep, so she wanted to come out and look.\"","He Zhiran originally planned to let her mother rest well today and take her around to get familiar with the surroundings tomorrow.","Since her mother couldn't sleep, and there was still some time before dinner, He Zhiran took her for a walk nearby.","Mo Jiuye knew they were mother and daughter and had not seen each other for nearly a year, so they had many private conversations to share. He did not follow them.","With his mother-in-law present in his own territory, he would not worry about He Zhiran's safety either.","Madam He followed He Zhiran out of the courtyard and only then noticed that next to their courtyard residence were many others just like it, roughly counting at least more than ten.","Not only were the structures of those houses the same, but more importantly, the windows were all inlaid with glass.","At this time, Madam He felt that the Empress Dowager was a fool. She cherished the two small pieces of glass like treasures, dispatched maids to guard them every day, afraid someone would inadvertently break them. Yet the treasures the Empress Dowager coveted were ubiquitous here in her daughter's home...","The origins of this glass could not withstand scrutiny, so He Zhiran did not want her mother to dwell on it too much.","\"Mother, let me take you to see the breeding farm.\"","Apart from the Mo family courtyard, Madam He was also attracted by the fruit trees on the hill, so she did not immediately follow He Zhiran to the breeding farm.","When she was in the capital, He Yuanming would also take her out for walks.","The trees on the mountains in the capital were tall and big, completely different from here.","\"Ran Ran, are all the trees on this mountain northwest China's specialties?\"","\"Mother, actually this hill is also the Mo family's property. When my husband and I met Western merchants, their cargo ships carried many fruit tree seedlings not found here, so we bought them all and planted them on the hill.","If you are interested, Mother, I can take you to see.\"","Fortunately, Madam He grew up in a wealthy urban family from a young age and did not understand planting at all.","Otherwise, she would have certainly rambled on about how her daughter and son-in-law did not know how to live, that no matter how good foreign fruit trees were, they could not be successfully planted anywhere, and that they were just wasting silver by buying them.","It was only because she was ignorant that she did not think of all this.","Madam He looked at her daughter's large belly.","\"Let's just walk around the foot of the mountain. Your body is inconvenient, do not go up high.\"","He Zhiran agreed and took her mother to see the fruit trees.","Although these fruit trees were nurtured in the space before being planted outside, the first year after planting could not produce the miracle of bearing fruit that same year.","Therefore, apart from the different appearances, almost all the fruit trees the mother and daughter saw had only green leaves.","Of course, not completely. With her keen eyes, He Zhiran discovered that some nearby cherry trees had sparse fruit.","This was something even she had not expected.","Moreover, the cherries were already ripe, the large red fruits standing out against the green foliage.","With a space available, He Zhiran could usually eat whatever she wanted, so she was not eyeing those few cherries. Rather, she was excited that the planting had succeeded.","\"Mother, look quickly - this is a large cherry, sour and sweet, very delicious.\" He Zhiran did not call it a cherry, feeling that calling it a \"large cherry\" would be more down-to-earth in this era.","There were many wild cherry trees on mountains, so calling it this way would be easier to accept.","Seeing He Zhiran already lifting her dress to walk towards the nearest large cherry tree, Madam He hurried forward to support her.","\"Ran Ran, let Mother go get some. You just wait here.\"","After saying this, Madam He quickly walked past her daughter towards the fruit tree.","He Zhiran knew she could not show off too much, as it would only make her family worry, so she obediently stood and waited.","Madam He thought her daughter was impatient to eat that \"large cherry\" and just wanted to quickly pick some for her.","He Zhiran saw her mother had already picked two and loudly said, \"Mother, this is very delicious. Please try one.\"","Madam He was unmoved by novelties, but since her daughter said so, not wanting to dampen her enthusiasm, she used a handkerchief to wipe one off and put it in her mouth.","He Zhiran smiled as she watched her expression.","She saw Madam He's previously furrowed brow gradually smooth out, then she smiled and said, \"Ran Ran, this large cherry is truly delicious.\"","It tasted even better than the watermelon and other fruits she had eaten before.","After speaking, Madam He continued picking eagerly. Such a delicious fruit, her daughter and little grandson should taste it soon."]},{"number":415,"title":"Chapter 415: I Like to Eat","paragraphs":["Unfortunately, when Madam He and He Zhiran went out, they did not bring anything like a bamboo basket with them. The cherries were too large, and after Madam He picked a few, her hands were too full to hold any more.","With no other choice, she first went back to He Zhiran's side and let her daughter satisfy her craving first.","He Zhiran never cared much for the etiquette of ancient genteel ladies. Seeing her mother come over, she directly lifted up her skirt to make a pouch shape.","\"Mother, just put them here.\"","At first, Madam He was somewhat astonished by her daughter's actions. When they were in the capital, although her daughter did not like learning the skills of proper young ladies, she was no less well-behaved than the other young misses.","Now He Zhiran's actions were worlds apart from those of the original when she was in the capital.","Madam He was astonished for a moment, but quickly found an excuse for her daughter's behavior.","Her daughter must have suffered too much hardship on the road and was now living in the countryside, so the rules of etiquette she had learned were completely useless.","Especially on the exile journey, when they possibly couldn't even eat their fill. Who was she keeping up appearances for?","Thinking of this, Madam He suddenly felt sore in her heart. Thus, she did not have the slightest intention of reminding He Zhiran to mind her manners. Instead, she placed the cherries in her daughter's lifted skirt as she wished.","Not only that, but when Madam He turned back to continue picking cherries, she actually imitated He Zhiran's style and used her skirt as a pouch until she had picked quite a heavy load before heading back.","\"Ranran, do you really like eating these? Look how many your mother picked.\"","Since her old lady was acting so down-to-earth, He Zhiran had to encourage her.","\"Thank you, Mother. I like them.\"","Seeing her daughter say this, Madam He was extremely happy. After almost a year, she could finally do something for her daughter again. Although it was just a helping hand, for a mother it was still blissful.","After picking so many cherries, it was inconvenient for the mother and daughter to go any further, so they folded back home together.","Do not look down on the cherries bundled in Madam He’s clothes - He Zhiran estimated that there were at least seven or eight catties.","Although the yield of large cherries on each tree was not much, there were many fruit trees. Madam He had only picked some nearby trees and already gotten this many.","He Zhiran estimated that if all the cherries on every tree were picked, there would still be several hundred catties.","For now, she did not intend to sell these hundreds of catties of cherries.","First of all, there were many people in the Mo family, plus so many former subordinates who had also come to join them, as well as Meng Huaining and Tang Mingrui and other friends. It would be good for everyone to try them fresh first.","If they wanted to make money, waiting for next year's bumper harvest, they would surely make a fortune. There was no hurry for the time being.","But she and her mother would not be the ones to pick the rest of the cherries.","Upon returning home, He Zhiran immediately ordered Yu Er to call people to pick cherries. She had tasted some earlier and found they were completely ripe and at the peak flavor.","The Mo family did not lack manpower at present. In less than an hour, Yu Er came back leading a group of people carrying several baskets full of large cherries.","He Zhiran took advantage of the freshness of the food to distribute it.","For each Mo family elder branch, she allotted 10 catties.","Liang Hao and several others were currently in a state of being single men with no family, so she gave 5 catties to each person.","Anyway, they had big appetites, and would probably be able to eat it all in one day.","Although the Mo family had not openly divided into branches, everyone was living their separate small families now. Naturally such delicious fruit had to be distributed to each family.","There was also the Fifth Elder Brother and others working on gunpowder research in the mountains. He Zhiran also had Mo Jiuye deliver them a basket.","As for Tang Mingrui and Meng Huaining's groups, Liang Hao was responsible for delivering some over, 10 catties each to sample the fresh cherries.","In addition, shares were allotted to Nan Rui, Hu Cong, the Fang family and the Xie family.","Even several Mo family-adjacent village households received some, which He Zhiran sent over through Yu Er.","Seeing her daughter’s generosity, Madam He quickly distributed most of the cherries. She suddenly felt a bit heartbroken.","She had attended palace banquets before as well, and knew that with the deliciousness of these cherries, they would be top-tier even in the palace.","Yet her precious daughter had given away almost all of them in just a few words...","He Zhiran was unaware her mother was distressed over her large donations. She sat there eating cherries and chatting happily with everyone.","Suddenly, a series of muffled booms came from the mountainside direction.","He Zhiran immediately stood up and strode towards the outside of the house.","She was all too familiar with this sound - it was the sound of an explosion.","The elder brothers had been up the mountain researching gunpowder for many days without coming down. Mo Jiuye had been busy with domestic affairs and also hadn't gone up the mountain to check the progress. So currently she was unclear on how the gunpowder research was going.","However, based on this sound, He Zhiran could determine that the gunpowder should have been successfully developed, it was just that the elder brothers had not yet fully grasped the proper measurements, resulting in the explosion.","What was more important was that gunpowder had extremely strong destructive power. She didn't know if the elder brothers were injured.","The sound was not small. Although Madam He didn’t know the origin of the sound, that didn’t prevent her from being frightened.","She thought that He Zhiran had suddenly stood up because she was also scared. Not minding her own quickening heartbeat, she hurriedly went up to comfort her daughter.","Madam He gently patted He Zhiran's shoulder, \"Ranran, don't be afraid, Mother is here.\"","Of course He Zhiran was not afraid, she was worried. But currently there was no possibility of her going up the mountain to check things out.","Fortunately, Mo Jiuye had just delivered a basket of cherries over, so he must have heard the explosion and would head over at top speed to go investigate.","Sure enough, Mo Jiuye had just walked halfway up the mountain when he heard the series of loud booms.","He considered the same possibilities as He Zhiran, and was mainly worried about the safety of the elder brothers.","He had personally experienced the might of his wife's hand grenades. Although this explosive was not as powerful as the grenades, it still should not be underestimated.","The more Mo Jiuye thought about it, the more afraid he became. He pushed his lightness skill speed to the maximum.","After about an hour, he appeared at the entrance of the mountain cave where Fifth Elder Brother and the others were researching gunpowder.","The scene before him stunned him speechless.","The entrance of the gunpowder research cave was in a mess, and not only that, the ground had also become scorched black, with countless craters of various sizes around it.","Mo Jiuye put down the bamboo basket in his hand, intending to go take a look around, when he heard someone shouting at him from behind.","\"Ninth younger brother, hurry and pull Fifth Elder Brother up!\"","The voice not only sounded weak, it was even somewhat miserable.","Mo Jiuye turned around to see a person currently crawling out from a deep pit not far behind him.","Fifth Elder Brother’s hair was messy and disheveled, looking thoroughly “exploded”.","Apart from flashing a mouthful of pearly white teeth when he spoke, his face was basically pitch black all over.","Not only that, but Fifth Elder Brother’s clothes had also become tattered and torn, comparable to Big Elder Brother and Second Elder Brother’s states when they were at the sixth hillock.","Seeing Mo Jiuye still standing there in a daze, Fifth Elder Brother became somewhat anxious.","\"Ninth younger brother, hurry and pull me up!\""]},{"number":416,"title":"Chapter 416: What's Wrong with Your body","paragraphs":["<Mo Jiuye> ran over quickly, reaching out to grab <Fifth Elder Brother> and pull him up.","When <Fifth Elder Brother> reached the ground, he collapsed and sat on the ground.","He was pitch black all over, <Mo Jiuye> couldn't see where he was injured at all, so he could only ask: \"Fifth Elder Brother, how are you?\"","<Fifth Elder Brother> shook his head and pointed to the deep pit behind him and said, \"I'm fine, <Eldest Brother> and <Second Brother> are still down there, think of a way to pull them up.\"","<Mo Jiuye> took a look down the deep pit, if it wasn't for his good eyesight, he wouldn't have seen two people lying down there at all.","<Mo Jiuye> jumped in, the two elders couldn't even be distinguished from each other at the moment, not only were they disheveled and black-faced, but there was also a lot of soil buried on them.","He strode forward to one elder brother, carried him on his back and jumped up again.","<Mo Jiuye> repeated the same action twice, and finally rescued the two elder brothers.","At this time, the two elder brothers were not in very good condition. Although they were pitch black all over, bloodstains could be vaguely seen.","Fortunately, the two were still breathing steadily.","Just as <Mo Jiuye> was about to try to wake them up, he heard a thud as something heavy fell to the ground nearby.","The person who had already passed out woke up from this fall.","Third Elder Brother was so painful that he almost passed out, plus he was so dizzy that he fainted again after waking up for just a moment.","Seeing this scene, <Mo Jiuye> had one big and two small heads.","Among the brothers, <Fifth Elder Brother> was the one in the best condition. Although his head was a little dizzy, he was better off in that his body was not seriously injured.","The others were not so optimistic. <Mo Jiuye> had just checked their breaths, and although it looked like none of them were in mortal danger, they also had varying degrees of injury.","Most importantly, according to <Fifth Elder Brother>'s account, when the explosion happened, the brothers were completely focused on researching, without any precautions at all.","This explosion caught the brothers completely off guard.","Even if they were prepared, I'm afraid they still couldn't resist the power of the gunpowder explosion.","The brothers were blown up in an instant, not even knowing what their heads hit, and then fell heavily into the deep pit.","<Third Older Brother> was blown directly into a tree...","<Fifth Elder Brother> had now recovered a lot. Although there was still some pain in his body and head, for someone who had been on countless battlefields, how could he care about such minor injuries.","He struggled to stand up.","\"Ninth younger brother, let's take our injured brothers back to see Ninth younger sister now?\"","<Mo Jiuye> was thinking the same thing. Currently, it looked like the elder brothers only had some superficial wounds, but judging by their unconscious state, they must already have internal injuries, it was just that he and <Fifth Elder Brother> were unable to specifically determine where the injuries were.","\"Fifth Brother, can you make it?\"","With <Third Older Brother> unconscious, it would be impossible for <Mo Jiuye> alone to get him down the mountain.","Even if <Fifth Elder Brother> could make it, at most each of them could carry one person.","So one elder brother would have to be left here to wait.","The one waiting had to be the one with the lightest injuries.","Although <Mo Jiuye> had learned some medical knowledge from following <He Zhiran>, he was not at the level to judge who was more or less injured in this situation.","As a last resort, he could only try gently shaking the elder brothers to see if they could wake up and ask them.","In fact, the three elder brothers were not completely unconscious at this point, they just couldn't open their eyes because their heads were too dizzy.","When <Mo Jiuye> shook them, they all reacted somewhat.","Eldest Brother weakly said, \"Ninth younger brother, I'm fine, take your second and third brother down the mountain first.\"","\"Eldest Brother, feel yourself and tell me exactly where you are uncomfortable?\" Leaving Eldest Brother here for the time being was no problem, but <Mo Jiuye> had to confirm his condition first.","\"I just feel dizzy and want to vomit, and my whole body hurts.\"","After getting Eldest Brother's answer, <Mo Jiuye> looked at <Fifth Elder Brother>.","\"Fifth Brother, let's take Second Brother and Third Brother down the mountain first.\"","\"Okay.\" <Fifth Elder Brother> agreed with a sound, and was about to carry <Third Older Brother> first.","<Mo Jiuye> carried <Second Brother> on his back, and the two brothers were about to go down the mountain when they heard the sound of footsteps coming from afar.","Since the Mo family bought this mountain, there were dogs at the foot of the mountain guarding it, and no outsiders had ever come here before.","Therefore, <Mo Jiuye> was not too worried, but he maintained the posture of carrying <Second Brother> on his back, intending to see who was coming.","<Sixth elder brother> looked somewhat red because he had rushed up the mountain too quickly.","He had also come up the mountain to inquire about the situation after hearing the noise and asking about it in Ninth Younger Brother's yard. <He Zhiran> was worried that something big had happened on the mountain and <Mo Jiuye> wouldn't be able to handle it alone, so he urged him to rush up the mountain to assist.","As for the others, because making gunpowder on the mountain was a big secret, <He Zhiran> did not intend to let more people know, so even though she was anxious, she did not think to notify anyone else.","When <Sixth elder brother> came to <Mo Jiuye>, besides the mess in front of him, what caught his eye was <Fifth Elder Brother> and Ninth Younger Brother each carrying a \"piece of charcoal\".","\"Fifth Brother, Ninth Younger Brother, what on earth happened?\"","Seeing that it was his own brother, <Mo Jiuye> had no time to explain too much.","\"Sixth Brother, you're just in time, hurry up and carry Eldest Brother, let's go down the mountain to find Ruan Ruan.\"","Although <Sixth elder brother> didn't get the answer he wanted, from the slightly urgent tone in Ninth Younger Brother's voice, he knew that something big must have happened.","Besides, he also knew clearly what the brothers were doing on the mountain. He had heard Ninth Younger Brother mention before that making such weapons carried great risks, and an explosion could put their lives in jeopardy.","<Sixth elder brother> didn't hesitate for a moment, went forward to carry Eldest Brother, and followed <Mo Jiuye> and the others down the mountain at a fast pace.","On the way, <Sixth elder brother> took the opportunity to ask, \"Ninth Younger Brother, what exactly happened?\"","<Mo Jiuye> couldn't give a detailed answer to this question either, so he had to refer it to <Fifth Elder Brother>.","<Fifth Elder Brother> was obviously somewhat ashamed.","\"It was all my fault for not stopping Second Brother in time.","The research was going very smoothly today. When I saw what was made looked similar to what was in your diagram, I got excited and said it should be successful.\"","Now <Mo Jiuye> understood somewhat, because his wife had said before that once gunpowder was successfully produced, it would be ignited when exposed to fire.","\"Fifth Brother, did you verify whether it was successful by lighting it?\"","\"It was Second Brother. As soon as Second Brother heard me say that, he immediately lit the match. I wanted to stop him but it was too late...\"","<Fifth Elder Brother> felt somewhat annoyed. From that explosion just now, it could indeed prove that the gunpowder research was successful.","But all at once, all the successfully produced gunpowder exploded, without even giving him a chance to conduct further research.","Fortunately, he had memorized all the ingredients and ratios in his mind, so producing it again would not be difficult.","The brothers not only walked down the mountain quickly, but also used qinggong, and arrived at the foot of the mountain in no time.","<Mo Jiuye> had originally wanted to take the injured elder brothers directly to his home, but he was worried that the miserable state of the elder brothers would frighten his mother-in-law, so he chose to send them to the yard of <Fifth Elder Brother>'s house."]},{"number":417,"title":"Chapter 417: I'm not Dead","paragraphs":["After settling his elder brothers, Mo Jiuye went back to fetch He Zhiran.","He Zhiran was anxiously waiting for news, and when he saw Mo Jiuye return, he quickly asked, \"How are my elder brothers? Were they injured?\"","Mo Jiuye's expression became solemn. \"Zhiran, come with me to Fifth Brother's house.\"","In front of their mother-in-law, Mo Jiuye couldn't explain too clearly. He just greeted Madam He and pulled He Zhiran away.","Madam He didn't know what had happened in the Mo family, but seeing her son-in-law's anxious look, she knew it must be something serious.","However, she understood boundaries and wouldn't inquire about matters that others didn't want to discuss.","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran arrived at Fifth Brother's house. Fifth and Sixth Brother were just about to help clean up their bodies. When they saw them coming, they stopped their actions and willingly made way for He Zhiran.","Although Fifth and Seventh Brother had already started cleaning them up, it was still not as effective as not doing anything at all.","The faces of the elder brothers were covered in black and white marks, which looked amusing.","Helplessly, He Zhiran held back her laughter and approached them to check their pulses.","Seeing her stop, Fifth Brother anxiously asked, \"Ninth Younger Sister-in-Law, how are they doing?\"","\"Fifth Brother, don't worry. It seems that they suffered head injuries, but they just need a few days of rest to recover.\"","In modern terms, this would be diagnosed as a concussion.","Of course, concussions can vary in severity, but He Zhiran was certain that the elder brothers had only experienced mild to moderate concussions and would be fine.","Moreover, their current state of unconsciousness was normal, and they would wake up soon enough.","As for the injuries on their bodies, they were mostly superficial scrapes and bruises, which could be cleaned and treated with some medicine after their bodies were cleaned.","\"Ninth Younger Sister-in-Law, are you sure they're fine?\" After all, all of them were in a comatose state, and Fifth Brother found it hard to believe.","\"They are not in any life-threatening danger, but someone should be by their side when they wake up. They might experience vomiting and dizziness.\"","Saying so, He Zhiran took a step towards the exit, with Mo Jiuye following closely behind, because he knew his wife intended to find a secluded place in the space to retrieve some medicine.","Indeed, that was the reason He Zhiran left. Besides, the three elder brothers were extremely dirty, and their clothes were probably torn. If they weren't covered with a blanket, they wouldn't be presentable.","While she was away, Fifth Brother and the others took the opportunity to clean them up.","As He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye left Fifth Brother's house and prepared to take a walk down the foot of the mountain, they saw Old Lady Mo and several sisters-in-law walking towards them.","\"Jiuye, what happened?\"","They had also heard the explosion just now. However, they didn't know the power of explosives, let alone that their own sons had an accident.","It was because Mo Jiuye and the others were carrying their unconscious elder brothers down the mountain when they happened to be noticed by Yu Er, who then went to inform them.","\"Mother, there's nothing to worry about. Big Brother and the others had a minor accident on the mountain, and Ruirui and I were just about to go back and get some medicine.\"","The mother and the sisters-in-law would soon go to Fifth Brother's house to check on the situation. Mo Jiuye didn't want them to worry, but he couldn't evade the truth. He could only tell them what had happened without exaggerating.","Even so, the sisters-in-law were still quite frightened.","Especially Second Sister-in-law, who had always had a loud voice.","\"Jiudie, how is your Second Brother? He won't die, will he?\"","As soon as she said this, even the usually dignified Eldest Sister-in-law couldn't remain calm, because her husband had been on the mountain these past few days.","Third Sister-in-law and Fifth Sister-in-law also felt that asking questions would only waste time. They bypassed Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran and ran straight into Fifth Brother's courtyard.","Seeing that they had all gone in, Second Sister-in-law quickly realized what was happening and followed them inside.","Old Lady Mo, on the other hand, remained calm and composed. She believed her ninth son's words. If something truly dangerous had happened to those brothers, he wouldn't be able to remain so calm.","Therefore, the old lady walked in calmly. Just as she reached the door, she heard a burst of crying and wailing coming from inside the house...","\"Husband, wake up quickly, you can't die... Open your eyes and look at me... If you die again this time, I won't live either... Sob, sob, sob...\"","Everyone stood there dumbfounded, watching Second Sister-in-law who was crying hysterically.","Although the other sisters-in-law who had rushed in were not as exaggerated as her, they were all shedding tears around their own husbands. Only Fifth Sister-in-law was better off. Although her husband looked pale, he was standing there just fine.","Fifth Sister-in-law didn't mind getting dirty. She held onto Fifth Brother's arm and watched the other sisters-in-law cry, wiping her own tears as well.","Old Lady Mo was observant and could read people's expressions. Seeing her fifth and sixth sons standing there without much sadness on their faces, she knew that those daughters-in-law had made a mistake.","\"Alright, all of you stop crying. Didn't Jiuye say that they just had a minor accident? If something had really happened, how could your Ninth Brother and Ninth Sister-in-law leave?\"","Although the sisters-in-law usually listened to their mother-in-law, at this moment, with their husbands having lost their lives, they couldn't take in her words.","When Old Lady Mo saw that her words had no effect, she slammed the table next to her with anger.","\"Didn't any of you hear what I said?\"","This time, her voice was raised, and the sisters-in-law finally reacted.","Second Sister-in-law choked and said, \"Mother, my husband has lost his life. Can't I cry?\"","When Old Lady Mo saw Second Daughter-in-law in this state, she was about to say something, but at that moment, Second Brother, who was lying on the bed, let out a slight cough.","Then he murmured, \"I'm not dead...\"","Although his voice was weak, right after Old Lady Mo scolded them, the room fell silent, and everyone could hear it.","Everyone looked towards Second Brother.","At this moment, Second Sister-in-law had already thrown herself onto him and was shaking him vigorously.","\"Husband, you really didn't die... Sob, sob, sob... It's great that you're still alive... Sob, sob, sob...\"","\"Mm...\" Second Brother groaned as he was being shaken, and then he said, \"I'm not dead, but you're nearly shaking me to death.\"","Only then did Second Sister-in-law realize that she had been a bit rough and quickly straightened up.","\"Darling, I'm sorry. I didn't mean it. I thought you were dead, that's why I acted this way...\"","Upon seeing that Mo Jiacheng had already awakened, Eldest Sister-in-law and Third Sister-in-law assumed that their own husbands would be fine, and half of the gloom in their hearts instantly dissipated.","At this moment, Sixth Elder Brother placed a basin of clean water in the room, along with freshly washed face towels.","The sisters-in-law immediately understood what was going on and approached to help their respective husbands wipe their faces with the towels.","While wiping, the elder brothers gradually woke up one after another, experiencing the nausea and dizziness as described by He Zhiran."]},{"number":418,"title":"Chapter 418: Caught the Attention of Millions","paragraphs":["The sister-in-laws were busy taking care of everything, having experienced the loss of a husband once before, none of them wanted to go through it again. They only hoped to wholeheartedly serve their own husbands and help them recover as soon as possible.","He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye didn't go far. She asked about what had happened on the mountain.","Mo Jiuye recounted in detail what he had witnessed.","While He Zhiran was relieved, she also felt somewhat guilty.","After all, it was her suggestion to develop gunpowder, and she knew better than anyone the risks involved in its production.","Although she had repeatedly reminded Fifth Elder Brother and the others to be careful, such accidents could not be completely avoided.","Fortunately, her brothers only suffered minor injuries, and based on Mo Jiuye's description, she confirmed that the gunpowder's ratio had been successfully completed. From now on, they just needed to follow this ratio for production.","The most important thing now was to take care of her brothers' health.","The men of the Mo family were all strong and healthy, so these injuries shouldn't pose a major problem for them.","After clarifying the situation and realizing that enough time had passed, He Zhiran took out some medicine from her spatial storage and the two of them returned to Fifth Elder Brother's courtyard.","She didn't need to personally apply the medicine, as she entrusted everything to Mo Jiuye.","By the time they finished, it was already evening. Except for the sister-in-laws who stayed behind to take care of their injured husbands, everyone else had prepared dinner.","The dinner was set up in Old Lady Mo's courtyard, mainly to welcome Madam He's arrival.","Mo Junrui and his brothers had already improved significantly after using the medicine given by He Zhiran, but they were still unable to join everyone for the meal.","Madam He had come today, thinking that she would see all the men of the Mo family during dinner. However, she only saw Mo Chongyuan, Mo Yuance, Mo Chuhan, and Mo Xiuyan, who was still sitting in a wheelchair.","Mo Qing was carried to the dining table.","Seeing Madam He, Mo Qing felt somewhat embarrassed, not because of their in-law relationship, but because of his current miserable state.","Back then, he commanded thousands of troops with an imposing manner, and anyone in the capital would respectfully address him as Duke Mo.","But now, he had become a useless person who was taken care of all day long.","The feeling of meeting an old acquaintance was not pleasant, but when Mo Qing thought about Madam He traveling all the way from afar to visit her daughter, he tried to appear more natural.","Madam He, on the other hand, didn't think too much about it. Seeing the long-deceased Duke Mo still alive, she genuinely felt happy for the Mo family.","During the meal, Old Lady Mo occasionally made some remarks to lighten the atmosphere, so it didn't feel too awkward.","What surprised Madam He the most was that the dishes from the Mo family were even more delicious than those in the famous restaurants in the capital.","Madam He encountered many ingredients she had never seen before. At first, she tried to maintain her composure and dignity. However, as she observed the Mo family members being less reserved, she decided to follow suit and adapt to the local customs.","He Zhiran noticed that his mother had a good appetite today. He continuously served her dishes and quietly introduced their names.","During this meal, Madam He ate heartily. Since He Zhiran and the Mo family were exiled to the northwest, she had lost her appetite and had become noticeably thinner.","Today, seeing her daughter happy was one aspect, but the delicious food from the Mo family was also a reason why Madam He shamelessly overate.","Not only that, when she followed her daughter back to their courtyard, she ate a lot of cherries. Finally, Li Auntie accompanied her for half an hour of walking in the courtyard to aid digestion before she could finally fall asleep peacefully.","Several elder brothers were injured while researching gunpowder and couldn't go up the mountain temporarily. However, Fifth Elder Brother didn't want to pause.","He had just found inspiration for making it and didn't want to stop there.","Therefore, early the next day, Fifth Elder Brother planned to continue researching on the mountain.","Seeing this, Sixth Elder Brother took the initiative to accompany him. It was such a dangerous matter, and being alone there without any support would be risky.","Fifth Elder Brother didn't object to this either. The current scene of making gunpowder was a mess, and it would be quite laborious for him to clean it up alone.","The two brothers went up the mountain, but Mo Jiuye didn't go with them.","The main reason was that he considered He Zhiran's condition. She was getting closer to her due date, and it wouldn't be good if something happened and he wasn't by her side.","Also, during his time in the capital, the area for raising poultry and livestock had already been prepared. He was just waiting for an opportunity to bring the poultry and livestock from the space he had prepared for his wife.","With Mo Jiuye's mindset, he didn't want his wife to go out, fearing that something might happen to her.","But with so many poultry and livestock in her space, it was useless for him to go to the city alone.","If they waited for the children to be born, He Zhiran wouldn't be able to leave for a month. Considering this, the constructed area for raising animals would be idle for over two months.","He Zhiran was already a bit anxious about this matter. If Mo Jiuye hadn't gone to the capital to search for his father and brothers, she would have started raising them when the area was ready.","Today happened to be a day when there wasn't much going on at home, so He Zhiran didn't inform her mother before leaving.","Because she knew that no matter what excuse she gave to go to the city, her mother would accompany her.","What she had to do couldn't be seen in the light, so she had to quietly leave without Madam He's knowledge.","The two of them hurriedly took a carriage to the large rented courtyard in Yuncheng. They released all the cattle, sheep, pigs, chickens, ducks, and geese from the space.","In order to quickly expand the scale of animal husbandry at home, these poultry and livestock were all in the adult state and could reproduce at any time.","Only in this way could the scale of the livestock farm at home grow rapidly.","After releasing them, Mo Jiuye quietly sent He Zhiran back home. He then called Liang Hao and others to follow him into the city.","Transporting adult cattle, sheep, and pigs using a cart would be too labor-intensive since their size was too large. A single cart couldn't carry many of them. The best solution was to have people drive them back.","He Zhiran had already trained these guys in advance, and they were all very obedient, so there was no need to worry about them running away on the way.","Although the chickens, ducks, and geese couldn't be driven back like the cows and sheep, they weren't kept in cages either. They had also been trained by He Zhiran and were very well-behaved.","As long as some ox carts were hired, they wouldn't make any mischief on the carts.","As expected, when Mo Jiuye and his men brought these poultry and livestock back home, it caused quite a stir.","First, the villagers from Xiling Village, who were driving groups of cows, sheep, and pigs, attracted the attention of countless people.","For the rural people who were born and raised here, these animals were like fixed assets in their homes."]},{"number":419,"title":"Chapter 419: It's Only Part of It","paragraphs":["In ordinary people's families, those who could have an ox for plowing, or raise one or two fat pigs, would definitely be considered a wealthy family.","When the Cui family in Xilin Village was so wealthy, there were only oxen raised in Ligui's family for plowing.","It was used to plow the fields during the busy farming seasons, and earned quite some silver pulling the cart during other times.","But what did they see now?","The Mo family actually drove hundreds of cattle into the village, with only a dozen or so of the yellow cattle that they were familiar with, the rest were black and white mottled, completely different from what plow oxen should look like in their mind, plus hundreds of sheep, and hundreds of fat pigs...","In fact, the villagers didn't know that the black and white mottled ones were dairy cows.","This was because the Da Shun Dynasty had very strict control over cattle. For any peasant family that had plow oxen, they must be registered with the government, in other words, plow oxen had household registration in Da Shun, slaughtering them randomly was like murdering people.","He Zhiran didn't want to challenge national policies for money, it wasn't that she was timid, but she felt it wasn't worth violating the law for that bit of not so much money.","Therefore, the cows raised on the Mo family farm were mainly dairy cows.","The dairy cows produced in her space had much higher milk yields than normal dairy cows, and milk was also very valuable at this time. Plus it could also be further processed into other delicious foods.","Calculated this way, the profits from raising dairy cows would be no less than beef cattle.","The herds of cattle, sheep and pigs had just been driven towards the foot of the mountain, followed by dozens of ox carts, loaded with chickens, ducks and geese.","The villagers had never seen such a spectacular scene before, and they all gathered around Mo Jiuye.","Zhao Ligui walked at the forefront of the crowd.","\"Old Nine, you got rich? Bought so many livestock.\"","The village was on Mo Jiuye’s way home, he had anticipated that passing by would surely cause a sensation with the villagers.","After all, they didn't intend to hide these poultry and livestock, let alone the necessity.","The farm was built at the foot of the mountain, adjacent to their home fields.","The fields were all being taken care of by hired hands, and everyone knew that the Mo family farm was next door.","\"Uncle Zhao, these are just a fraction, we country folks, don't we rely on land and these to make a living?\"","Mo Jiuye said so, also to let Zhao Ligui and the villagers recognize the Mo family's identity as soon as possible.","Now they, the Mo family, were no longer some nobles, but farmers who made a living by working like them.","At the same time, he also hoped that the next time he transported these poultry and livestock back, it would not cause such a sensation.","At the same time, he also considered that he might further expand the scale of farming in the future, and transport more poultry and livestock into the village, hoping that the villagers could stay calm about it.","Unfortunately, Mo Jiuye still overestimated the villagers' receptivity.","They didn't consider the issue of the Mo family's current status at all. To them, the Mo family was just a big rich family, an out and out big rich family.","There is a saying, a skinny dead camel is bigger than a horse, and the Mo family interpreted this very perfectly.","Although they had been exiled here, they still lived a rich life as before.","Just think about it, how much were so many poultry and livestock worth?","Not to mention so many, even giving them an ox or a sheep would make them considered the most affluent family in the village.","\"What? You said this...this is just a fraction?\"","When Zhao Ligui spoke, his expression was particularly exaggerated, his mouth kept open for a long time, unable to close for a long time.","The other villagers were the same, their focus was on Mo Jiuye's sentence \"This is just a fraction.\" After Zhao Ligui asked, they all stared at Mo Jiuye, waiting for his reply.","Facing these simple villagers, Mo Jiuye was also very helpless. It wasn't that he wanted to be high-profile, but that he couldn't avoid the villagers' sight when transporting poultry and livestock back again, thinking that saying it out beforehand could give them some mental preparation, but it seemed to be counterproductive.","However, he still nodded, \"Yes, this is just a small fraction, there may be a large number of poultry and livestock transported back in the future.\"","The farm was very large, and these current poultry and livestock were far from enough.","Moreover, not only did the Mo family now have many family members who needed support, but people like Tao Ran and their families were now also settling down in Xilin Village. Although they also got some of the Cui family's farmland, it could only feed them, and it was basically impossible to improve their living standards.","What’s more, people like Tao Ran all had backbone, and were unwilling to accept the Mo family's relief in vain.","Now in Xilin Village they were not as simple as ordinary villagers. The incident of the invasion by the barbarians that happened before reminded the Mo family not to let their guard down, and to always be prepared.","People like Tao Ran now assumed this responsibility. In addition to helping their own families with some work every day, they had already taken on the task of patrolling and guarding.","For this reason, Mo Jiuye intended to give them monthly allowances as before when they were at the frontier, but Tao Ran and the others refused to accept it anyway.","In Tao Ran's words, their lives were given by Young Master Nine, and they would not have any complaints even if they worked like oxen and horses for the Mo family in this life, how could they possibly let Young Master Nine pay them allowances from his own pocket?","No matter how Mo Jiuye tried to reason with them, saying that their families also needed a good life, they refused to accept it.","With Tao Ran at the lead, those old subordinates said that the Mo family had provided them with places to live, and gave them farmland, which was already a lot.","Especially now the situation of the Mo family was not very good, they had been ordered by Emperor Shunwu to be exiled, how much better could their life be than them?","They were willing to follow the Mo family because of the comradeship back then between life and death, and did not want to do things that would drag down the Mo family.","But this matter had a different meaning to Mo Jiuye.","Tao Ran and the others were loyal to him and his elders, especially after the experience of escaping death as human medicine, Mo Jiuye cherished the friendship between them even more.","Forget about giving them houses and farmland, even if he had to support their younger generation for life, he would be more than willing.","Mo Jiuye's behavior was not showing off, the treasuries of the Da Shun Dynasty and the Southern Frontier were all in his wife's space, let alone supporting them for life, even supporting the people of a city would be nothing.","It’s just that he couldn’t say this kind of thing clearly, and could only find other ways to aid them.","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran agreed that raising these poultry and livestock was the best way to help them.","Tao Ran and the others all had martial arts skills and would surely join the secret army in the future, but they had many family members.","Raising livestock was not difficult, half-grown children could herd cattle and sheep, women could also raise chickens, ducks and geese, and older people with good health were no exception.","Therefore, regarding the farm, Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran discussed and decided to have it handled by the families of those old subordinates like Tao Ran."]},{"number":420,"title":"Chapter 420: Breeding","paragraphs":["Thus, they would have no excuse for not paying wages anymore.","No matter ancient or modern times, labor deserves reward. This is an unchanging principle everywhere.","By then, they can pay more wages to the families, which also helps resolve the family environment issue.","Village Chief Zhao did not know about Mo Jiuye's arrangement. After calming down, the first thing that came to his mind was that the Mo family raised so many poultry and livestock, they must hire people to take care of them like farming.","\"Old Nine, there are quite some villagers here. Don't you think it's better to hire those familiar faces rather than some strangers?\"","The words were blunt, without any euphemism.","Since arrangements had been made for the poultry and livestock, Mo Jiuye could not agree to Village Chief Zhao's request.","\"Chief Zhao, proper candidates have been selected for the breeding.\"","After a pause, Mo Jiuye looked to the villagers and said loudly, \"But don't worry, my wife and I have discussed that the poultry and livestock will give birth to offspring soon. You can purchase them from my family at low prices then.","Moreover, we can provide the know-how of raising dairy cattle.\"","The villagers were a little disappointed by Mo Jiuye's rejection at first. But soon they got attracted by what he said next.","Especially when Mo Jiuye mentioned dairy cows, it was a very novel concept to them.","Village Chief Zhao asked on behalf of everyone.","\"Old Nine, are you referring to this one?\" He pointed at the black and white patched cow and asked.","Mo Jiuye asked Liang Hao and others to take the poultry and livestock away first. He stayed to patiently explain to everyone.","\"The cow Chief Zhao referred to is a dairy cow...\"","He told them what he knew about dairy cows.","Although the villagers had never heard of dairy cows, they were not unfamiliar with milk.","Back then, the Cui Family raised a cow. When it gave birth, the surplus milk would be sold at high prices in the city to rich families for money.","However, the milk yield of the cow raised by Cui Family was not high. Even if there was surplus milk, there would be very little, precious amount.","But Mo Jiuye just said dairy cows could produce tens of catties of milk every day if raised properly. The number was mind-blowing.","If it was true that so much milk could be produced, even if dairy cows were more expensive, it would be worth pooling money to buy one.","Village Chief Zhao had this idea, and so did other villagers.","Everyone gathered around Mo Jiuye.","\"Old Nine, is what you said true?\"","\"Old Nine, how much does a dairy calf cost? I'll sell my harvest this autumn and buy one from you.\"","\"Old Nine, you didn't lie to us, right?\"","Mo Jiuye knew they were eager to earn more money.","\"Don't worry, I keep my word. The price of calves will absolutely be fair. Also, when the pigs and sheep reproduce, you can purchase from my place if you want to raise them too.\"","That was all he would say. He had decided to let the families of Liang Hao and others be in charge of the breeding. There would be no change.","As for the villagers, they could start small-scale breeding to make money. As long as they took good care of the animals and didn't let them die, they would definitely earn money.","The villagers were all honest and simple people. Seeing Mo Jiuye say so, no one insisted anymore.","Moreover, it would probably be more profitable to learn breeding themselves rather than working for others.","It was just that they needed to find ways to pool money together, because livestock was expensive. Otherwise they would have started raising them already.","\"Since Old Nine has made it clear, let's think of ways to save up money these days. Then we can also raise a dairy cow like the Mo family.\" Village Chief Zhao said one sentence to silence those who still wanted to say something. Then he waved his hand to disperse the crowd.","It took some explanation for Mo Jiuye to bring back so much poultry and livestock. But he was used to doing this kind of thing without any pressure.","The cattle and sheep were directly sent to the pasture where fences had been set up around the grassland in advance.","The sheepdogs that had been prepared early on were already guarding there. Now with the cattle and sheep inside, not a single one tried to escape.","The families hired by Tao Ran only needed to feed and clean up manure.","The pigpen was also built by He Zhiran in the modern breeding style with ventilation and drainage facilities.","The chicken farm spread from the hillside.","It was also He Zhiran's reference to the past world's free-range farming style. Free-range chickens were very popular.","In free-range farming, chickens can roam freely within a confined area to forage by themselves.","When selecting the location, He Zhiran found there were many earthworms, which reproduced quickly enough to feed the chickens.","It was said that chickens often eating worms would have tighter meat texture. The eggs they lay would also have darker egg yolks and more fragrant taste than ordinary eggs.","Ducks and geese liked places with water sources. So their farms were built near a streamlet discovered when they bought the wasteland.","The streamlet was originally going to be excluded from the land area by the officials. But it was acquired together with the wasteland by He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye for the purpose of raising ducks and geese in the future.","The breeding farms built by Mo Family were large in scale. With so much poultry and livestock brought back today, they still looked empty.","Mo Jiuye intended to quickly settle these matters before his wife gave birth, so that he could wholeheartedly accompany her during her confinement.","Therefore, he went to the city for three consecutive days, transporting poultry and livestock back home the same way every day.","After a few busy days, the number of poultry and livestock in the breeding farms finally took shape and temporarily reached their ideal quantity.","Meanwhile, Mo Jiuye also hired the families of Tao Ran and others to work here as originally planned.","Hearing that it was a job in exchange for due remuneration, Tao Ran and others no longer declined.","In five days, Mo Jiuye finally arranged the breeding farms properly.","In the same five days, the fifth and sixth uncles also accomplished a major task up in the mountains.","Gunpowder was finally successfully invented. Moreover, following He Zhiran's method, the fifth uncle packed the gunpowder into a bamboo tube, lit it and threw it into the distance to explode as envisioned.","It was another afternoon again when He Zhiran and Madam He were resting under the grape trellis in the yard and heard several bangs. But this time, the explosions were very different from last time’s."]},{"number":421,"title":"Chapter 421: It Made It","paragraphs":["The previous sound had no discernible pattern; it was continuous.","But this time, it appeared at intervals.","He Zhiran could roughly determine from the interval between the sounds that Fifth Elder Brother had likely successfully made gunpowder and ignited it inside a bamboo tube.","In other words, the bomb was most likely successfully developed.","Madam He had no idea what the sound she heard a few days ago was, and when she heard it again today, she simply thought someone was setting off firecrackers.","However, this time the firecrackers didn't last as long as the previous time.","\"Ranran, is there any local custom here to set off firecrackers for no apparent reason? It's not a festival or holiday, after all,\" Madam He couldn't help but ask curiously.","He Zhiran couldn't explain this question clearly and said vaguely, \"There's no special custom. Maybe it's just some child from a family playing around.\"","Madam He didn't really care about this matter in the first place. It was just a casual question, and after He Zhiran explained, she didn't dwell on it any further.","At this moment, He Zhiran couldn't sit still anymore and slowly stood up.","\"Mother, I'm going to see what my husband is busy with.\"","When Madam He heard that her daughter was going to find her son-in-law, she understood and didn't follow along. It wouldn't be appropriate for her, as the mother-in-law, to intrude on the private time of the young couple.","\"Alright, let Lan Er accompany you, and be careful on the way.\"","Mo Jiuye had been taking time to visit the breeding farm recently, so he was probably there now.","The small path up the mountain was just behind He Zhiran's courtyard. She didn't walk towards the direction of the breeding farm but headed straight to the backyard.","The loud noise just now had stirred things up, and Mo Jiuye planned to go up the mountain to investigate. As soon as he reached the foot of the mountain, he bumped into He Zhiran.","He Zhiran asked Lan Er to step aside and walked towards Mo Jiuye.","\"Husband, I heard the sound just now, and it seems that the bomb has been successfully made.\"","Mo Jiuye also had the same feeling, but he didn't know as much about bombs as He Zhiran did. Now, hearing her say this, his excitement was written all over his face.","\"If you say it's successful, then it must be. I'll go up the mountain to take a look.\"","In fact, He Zhiran came out to find Mo Jiuye for this purpose. After all, she also relied on her experience to judge whether it was really successful. Only seeing it with her own eyes would count.","After He Zhiran had explained the matter about the bomb just now, she had already sent Lan Er away. Even though Mo Jiuye was anxious, he still had to make sure He Zhiran returned home safely before leaving.","He Zhiran returned home and waited while Mo Jiuye quickly went up the mountain.","This time, the scene that greeted him was completely different from the previous one.","Fifth Elder Brother and Sixth Elder Brother were standing a few hundred meters away from the cave, examining several deep pits.","When they heard footsteps approaching, they turned their heads and saw Ninth Younger Brother. Both of them smiled brightly.","\"You came just at the right time, Ninth Younger Brother. These are the results of our experiment today. The craters from the explosion are much deeper than the last time.\" Fifth Elder Brother couldn't hide his excitement in his words.","Sixth Elder Brother added, \"And compared to the craters from the last explosion, these have also expanded a lot, which means the power has increased.\"","Mo Jiuye listened to the words of his two elder brothers and strode over to the deep pit to inspect it.","As they had described, the pit that had been blasted today was indeed deep and wide. Although its power was not as strong as the grenades he used when attacking the people of Southern Xinjiang, the destructive force was not to be underestimated.","Moreover, his wife had made it clear that the bombs made from the gunpowder he developed would not have the same power as grenades. If they could achieve thirty percent of the lethality of a grenade, it would be considered a success.","Mo Jiuye silently compared the power of the two weapons in his mind and was certain that the bombs made by his fifth brother and sixth brother could achieve more than forty percent of the power of a grenade.","\"Fifth Elder Brother, Sixth Elder Brother, we have succeeded.\"","As soon as he finished speaking, a faint rustling sound came from the distance.","Being martial artists, the brothers had exceptional hearing. Without even looking, they could tell that the sound was not made by humans.","Especially Fifth Elder Brother, who had many years of hunting experience.","\"It's wild boars.\"","It was not surprising to find wild boars in the deep mountains.","In the past, if they encountered wild boars, the brothers would undoubtedly hunt them down and bring them home for everyone to taste.","However, in Mo Jiuye's eyes, the wild boars today had a greater purpose.","\"Fifth Elder Brother, Seventh Elder Brother, do you still have the bombs you made?\"","Seeing his ninth brother asking this, the two elder brothers realized his intention.","Fifth Elder Brother quickly took out a small bamboo tube from his waist and held it in his hand.","\"I have one left. I planned to bring it back to show you the power, and now it comes in handy.\"","Using a bomb to blow up a wild boar would yield much better results than throwing it into an open area.","After reaching a unanimous decision, the brothers silently retreated dozens of meters.","As soon as they settled into position, two enormous wild boars emerged from the jungle.","Without hesitation, Fifth Elder Brother lit the fuse of the bamboo tube with a match and threw it in the direction of the two wild boars.","In an instant, a deafening explosion erupted.","In the brothers' line of sight, the wild boar closest to the bomb was blasted high into the air, its body torn apart. Flesh and blood mingled with dust as they all fell into the deep pit.","The other wild boar, which was farther away from the bomb, was also reduced to a bloody mess in the pit, devoid of any signs of life.","It should be noted that the skin of a wild boar is quite tough. If it can be blown up like this by a bomb, one can imagine how devastating it would be if it were to hit a person.","The brothers looked at the scene before them, unable to hide their joy.","Especially Fifth Elder Brother, no one knew better than him how much effort he had put into developing this weapon.","The three brothers embraced each other in excitement.","\"Sixth Brother, Ninth Brother, did you see that? We did it, the weapon research was successful.\"","Sixth Elder Brother was also thrilled. \"Yes, with such a weapon, we no longer have to worry about anyone threatening our Mo family.\"","At the same time, he had already confirmed one fact: why Ninth Sister was so confident in saying that only a thousand soldiers were needed to raise an army.","With such weapons, let alone a thousand soldiers, even if it was just the nine brothers of the Mo family, they would be able to repel any attacker.","The brothers quickly cleaned up the traces left by the experimental bomb and descended the mountain together.","With such a significant event, it was only natural to inform their father and older brothers as soon as possible.","This time, the fourth elder brother also took part.","Ever since the fifth elder brother and the others started researching weapons on the mountain, he had been anxious at home, always wishing to be of some help.","Although he hadn't contributed anything so far, he still cared deeply about it. Therefore, when he heard that all the male members of the family were going to their father to discuss matters, the fourth elder brother insisted on being supported by his wife to come along."]},{"number":422,"title":"Chapter 422: Lucky but not Humiliated","paragraphs":["Mo Si's legs have now recovered to a considerable extent, but after all, they suffered such severe injuries, so it's impossible for them to fully recover all at once.","He can now stand for a long period of time, but when walking, he still feels a bit weak in his legs and needs someone to support him to avoid falling.","In this regard, Mo Si is content. After all, he knows his own body best, and he believes in the exceptional medical skills of his ninth younger sister. As long as he keeps exercising, he knows that the day of complete recovery will come sooner or later.","However, ever since Mo Zhongyuan took the brothers up the mountain to develop weapons, his state of mind hasn't been as good. He always feels that his body is recovering too slowly and that he can't share the burden with his brothers.","Today, he asked his wife to bring him here, hoping to find something within his capabilities to do, even if it involves some danger.","Although First Brother, Second Brother, and Third Brother still feel a little dizzy, it doesn't affect their movements. As long as they move more slowly, there won't be any problems. Mo Xiuyan took the first step and arrived at his parents' courtyard.","Inside Mo Qing's room, the Mo family men sat upright, just as serious as when they used to discuss military affairs with the commander on the border.","Although Mo Qing's appearance has become haggard, after a few days of rest at home, his spirit has recovered considerably. That terrifying aura that makes people shudder still exists.","After glancing at his father, Mo Zhongyuan spoke, \"Father, fortunately, we have successfully researched that powerful weapon, and I have mastered the detailed production methods.\"","Pausing for a moment, he looked at Mo Qing, who was sitting on the bed.","\"Father, I think starting from tomorrow, we can begin making bombs.\"","Mo Qing nodded, \"Yes, those who threaten our Mo family may appear at any time, so the sooner we make the bombs, the better. In about twenty days, Seventh Brother should be back from the southern border with his men. By then, we need to integrate our forces quickly and be prepared for any potential danger.\"","\"Good. Starting tomorrow, we will begin production, aiming to make enough before Seventh Brother returns,\" Mo Zhongyuan replied.","\"Zhongyuan, although Mo Si's mobility is still limited, my hands have fully recovered now, and I can help,\" Mo Xiuyan said, determined to not be refused. He even deliberately waved his arms in front of his family.","First Brother, Second Brother, and Third Brother also expressed that they can contribute.","After all, the production of these weapons is confidential and cannot be entrusted to others. The few brothers can only overcome their physical discomfort and try their best to participate.","Mo Chuhan, who had just returned from work, heard that the bomb development was successful and that they needed to start production urgently. He also became anxious.","\"Tomorrow, I'll go to the yamen and resign from my official position, so I can stay at home and help.\"","\"No, Eighth Brother, you became a constable not just to earn a meager monthly salary, but to provide an additional layer of security for our Mo family,\" Mo Jiuye firmly opposed Mo Chuhan's resignation as a constable.","For the common people, he is an official by working in the yamen every day.","Mo Family's industries were growing by the day. Once those insignificant people had any ideas of targeting the Mo Family, they would have to think twice, considering that there was a constable in the family. Although Mo Jiuye was not afraid of those small-time troublemakers, nobody wanted to live a life filled with constant troubles.","With Mo Chuhan, the constable, around, at least there would be a deterrent effect. Moreover, Mo Chuhan patrolled the city every day, so he had more knowledge of what was happening. In case there was any suspicious activity, he would be the first to know.","As soon as Mo Jiuye finished speaking, Mo Qing followed, saying, \"That's right. Chuhan cannot resign from his position. With so many brothers in the family busy with their own tasks, we can't afford to lose one more person.\"","Mo Chuhan looked at his brothers, who were busy every day, and he genuinely wanted to quit his position as constable and come back to help. However, his greatest virtue was obedience, especially when both his youngest brother and father spoke up. Despite his reluctance, he could only nod obediently.","\"Since that's the case, we'll listen to Dad and the ninth brother.\"","After discussing for a while, the father and sons decided that everyone would participate in the making of bombs the next day. This included Mo Qing and Mo Xiuyan.","The father and sons could be considered to be in the same boat now. Although both of them had limited mobility, they didn't want to miss the opportunity to contribute this time.","At the insistence of the two, they were given the bamboo tubes used for making explosives. It wasn't a very difficult task, but it did take some time.","The next morning, Mo Jiuye took his brothers up the mountain to make gunpowder. As for the bamboo tubes used for making them, the bamboo that was grown by Rice Ball in the space multiplied rapidly and had reached a flooding level. It could be said that there was as much as they needed.","Of course, since Rice Ball could appear here, it meant that there were bamboo trees nearby.","Mo Jiuye had checked before and indeed found a small bamboo forest. Perhaps due to the climate, the bamboo here grew much thinner compared to the bamboo in the south.","The bamboo tubes used for making bombs had to be of the same size from top to bottom, and the more uniform, the better.","Such standard bamboo tubes were difficult to find in that bamboo forest.","Mo Jiuye took the bamboo cut by Rice Ball and stacked them in a corner of the bamboo forest under the pretext of taking a walk. As usual, he safely sent Rice Ball back home and then called some people to transport the bamboo back.","Now, Mo Qing and Mo Xiuyan finally had something to do.","Since Mo Jiuye brought the bamboo back with people, they had been sitting under the grape arbor, splitting the bamboo all along.","Mo Xiuyan held a piece of split bamboo and made a throwing gesture.","Seeing his son like this, Mo Qing asked, \"What's the matter? Are you eager to join the army, my fourth son?\"","Mo Xiuyan shook his head. \"With my legs like this, I'm afraid I won't be able to join in the short term. I just feel that the bamboo tube I'm holding is too light, and it won't throw very far.\"","\"You have a point. When we were in the barracks, we used to add some iron to the arrowheads to increase the range. That way, they could be shot farther,\" Mo Qing agreed, stroking his graying beard.","\"Dad, that's exactly what I meant. Do you think if we add some iron to the outside of the bamboo tube, it will have the same effect as the arrows?\"","Father and son were discussing when Mo Jiuye entered the courtyard carrying a bundle of bamboo.","\"Jiuye, you've come at the right time. Your father and I were discussing wrapping the bamboo tubes with a layer of iron skin, which would increase the throwing distance of the bombs.\"","Speaking of iron skin, Mo Jiuye immediately thought of the extremely powerful grenades in his wife's space.","The appearance of the grenades was indeed made of iron, and their weight was several times heavier than the bombs they made with bamboo tubes.","Not only that, after the grenades exploded, numerous small iron pellets would be ejected. With the force of the explosion, these iron pellets could be even sharper than swords and sabers."]},{"number":423,"title":"Chapter 423: The Blacksmith","paragraphs":["Mo Jiuye's mind was opened up to a whole new perspective by Fourth Brother's suggestion. However, currently, the work of making bombs was not entrusted to others; it was all done by their own brothers, with their own hands.","Their brothers were skilled in handling knives and guns, and Fifth Brother was intelligent and meticulous enough to handle the formulation and production of gunpowder. Learning together to make bamboo tube bombs was not a difficult task. But the problem lay in the blacksmithing aspect, which truly puzzled Mo Jiuye.","Seeing Mo Jiuye's delayed response, Mo Qing asked, \"Jiuye, don't you think Fourth Brother makes a valid point?\"","\"Not at all, Father. Fourth Brother's proposal is excellent. It's just that adding an iron casing to the bomb requires the assistance of a blacksmith. The fewer people who know about bomb-making, the better.\"","For Mo Jiuye, the matter of making bombs was of utmost importance. The Mo Family was already on thin ice, and if this matter were leaked, it would undoubtedly invite significant trouble. He would rather have shorter-range and less powerful bombs, with no risks involved.","In this regard, Mo Qing was thinking further ahead than he had expected.","\"While it's true that currently only you brothers are involved in making bombs, these bombs will eventually be distributed to the soldiers. Do you think the bombs will remain a secret for long?\"","Mo Jiuye was indeed not worried about this. The Mo Family's soldiers were loyal, and he would only feel at ease if the finished bombs were entrusted to them. His caution stemmed from not wanting the bomb-making methods to be revealed.","Thus, even if there were traitors among their privately trained soldiers in the future, they would only be able to take away a few finished bombs. This would lessen the threat to the Mo Family compared to the leakage of the formulation.","However, the thought of being able to make bombs with a longer throwing distance, and his father's clear intention to find a reliable person who could forge an iron casing for the bamboo tubes, crossed his mind.","\"Father, this matter involves the bomb-making methods. If anyone among Tao Ran and the others is capable, then there is no problem at all. After all, their loyalty to the Mo Family is beyond doubt. But if it comes to outsiders, I would rather have our bombs with a shorter throwing distance.\"","In Mo Jiuye's heart, even Hu Cong wouldn't be completely trusted.","Since returning to the Mo Family, Mo Qing had realized that this ninth son of his was extraordinary. Not only was he highly skilled in martial arts, but he also had a keen mind.","\"Your concerns are not without reason. That group of people, including Tao Ran, were trained by me personally. I know them well. Now that the Mo Family has been exiled here, their unwavering loyalty is beyond question.\"","\"Father, are you suggesting that among them, there is someone who can forge iron?\"","Mo Jiuye immediately understood his father's meaning.","\"If my memory serves me right, Lin Hong is the person I saved in a small town not far from the western border.\"","He was working as an apprentice in a blacksmith shop at that time. Because he stole a steamed bun from the boss's house, he was beaten half to death on the street. When I saw how pitiful he was, I stepped in and saved him. So, I thought it would be fine to call him over and ask him. Mo Qing didn't understand blacksmithing, but he knew a little bit about it. Working with iron sheets wasn't a highly skilled job, and he believed Lin Hong could do it. Tao Ran, the group of old comrades, was someone Mo Jiuye still trusted.","\"Dad, I'll go find Lin Hong and bring him here right away.\"","Mo Jiuye didn't take long to go out and came back with Lin Hong.","On the way, he had already inquired and found out that Lin Hong had been an apprentice for a long time and had learned a lot because he had been sent to the blacksmith shop from a young age. However, his master was harsh and bullied him because of his young age, always treating him as an apprentice, even though he was doing the work that only skilled masters could do.","With that said, there was no problem with him working with iron sheets.","But during this era, iron was strictly controlled by the government. Those who wanted to open a blacksmith shop in the city had to apply to the authorities and get approval before they could open their shops. Not only that, the amount of iron materials used by the blacksmith shops was fixed every month, and once it was used up, there was none left.","If the business at the shop was good, they would basically rest for half a month.","Therefore, the source of iron materials was a crucial issue for the Mo Family at present.","But this didn't pose a problem for Mo Jiuye. The Taobao online store in his wife's space had iron materials for sale. He just needed to find an excuse to take them out.","Since he had already decided to use iron sheets to wrap the bamboo tubes, Mo Jiuye planned to put small iron beads inside as well.","He didn't know if this would work, but he was unwilling to give up without trying.","Once it succeeded, the power of the bomb would increase significantly.","With everything settled, Mo Jiuye spent three consecutive days preparing the iron materials, tools, and the location for blacksmithing.","On the other hand, Madam He didn't plan to idle either. It was already early June, and the day Mo Hanyue and Meng Huaining would get married, June 12th, was approaching.","Madam He, being an experienced person, understood well that carrying twins made early delivery more likely.","She didn't know if it would be successful to invite the renowned gynecologist from the capital, Zhang San, to come here. Even if it was successful, considering the distance from the capital to the northwest, it probably wouldn't arrive too early.","Although her son-in-law repeatedly assured her that He Zhiran and the unborn child would be safe, she, as a mother, still worried.","It would be different if the renowned gynecologist was here. He and her son-in-law would each display their expertise, which would provide an additional safeguard for the safety of He Zhiran and the child in her belly.","Therefore, Madam He did nothing all day but stay by He Zhiran's side when Mo Jiuye was not around, fearing that she might make a careless move and harm her health.","With Madam He watching over her all the time, it was a bit inconvenient for He Zhiran to prepare something for Mo Hanyue.","There was no other way; a mother is a mother, and everything she did was for her own good. He Zhiran couldn't just push her away with a gloomy face.","She had already discussed with Mo Jiuye and prepared dowries for Mo Hanyue.","The courtyard that was built can be considered part of the dowry. Originally, He Zhiran intended to pay for it himself, but later his mother-in-law and sisters-in-law felt it was inappropriate.","After calculating the cost of the courtyard, it was divided into ten shares. The nine brothers of the Mo Family each contributed a share of money, and Old Lady Mo also contributed one share.","In other words, this courtyard was the dowry prepared for Mo Hanyue by the whole family.","He Zhiran had already stated in front of his family that it was up to him to arrange Mo Hanyue's dowry.","She had many valuable items in her space, but these possessions were all from the palaces of Da Shun and Nanjiang. She could sell them as antiques on Taobao, but if she took them out as Mo Hanyue's dowry, there was a risk of someone with ill intentions noticing something amiss, and the cost would outweigh the benefits.","Therefore, He Zhiran had planned from the beginning to purchase Mo Hanyue's dowry from the Taobao Mall."]},{"number":424,"title":"Chapter 424: I Can't Stay if I want to.","paragraphs":["Recently when He Zhiran was free, she has already prepared a good dowry for Mo Hanyue in the shopping mall.","The maternal family gave a siheyuan house, although it was in the countryside, this kind of house was not something anyone could live in, especially those imitating modern facilities.","For example, flush toilets, underfloor heating, glass windows, beautiful and practical furniture, etc.","In addition, the few acres of medicinal fields that Mo Hanyue planted herself were also given to her as part of the dowry.","He Zhiran was also very thoughtful. The beddings in the siheyuan given to Mo Hanyue were all complete.","Moreover, the fabrics all came from Taobao Mall.","Ancient silks were extremely rare and expensive.","It was different in Taobao Mall. There were all kinds of imitation ancient silks. She picked some that matched the style of this era and bought them. The cotton for making quilts was also indispensable.","Not long ago, He Zhiran had sent these well prepared things to her sister-in-law and asked her to help make new quilts for the wedding with several sisters-in-law.","Of course, with such beautiful fabrics, they were naturally praised by the sisters-in-law, but no one felt too surprised.","When they were in the capital, such high-end goods would occasionally go on sale in the fabric shops, but the prices were extremely expensive, and ordinary families simply could not afford them.","The sisters-in-law were already used to Mo Jiuye's generosity and unexpected actions. Seeing her take out so much fabric for Mo Hanyue's new house to make quilts, they were only envious for a moment.","As the only daughter of the Mo family going to get married, quilts alone were not enough. Recently, the little girl has been hiding in her room embroidering her wedding dress, which saved He Zhiran from having to prepare it.","But jewelry was also indispensable.","This was no problem at all. In ancient times, the jewelry worn by wealthy ladies was mainly made of gold and silver. For better workmanship, some gems would be added as embellishments.","There were plenty of such jewelry in Taobao Mall, and the styles and craftsmanship were much better than those of this era.","If it was up to He Zhiran's aesthetic taste, she did not like this kind.","However, she would follow the local customs here and could not make the dowry for Mo Hanyue too unconventional.","He Zhiran had already prepared these long ago, just waiting for Mo Jiuye to find time to pretend to go to the city or prefecture to get them. She would give the jewelry to Mo Jiuye, as if he had bought them back from his trip.","After waiting for two days, Mo Jiuye finally became free while bringing back good news.","The good news was that the tinplate and tin beads had been successfully produced. Fourth brother and father had tightly wrapped the tinplate around the bamboo tubes with their own hands.","Fifth brother and the others used the bamboo tubes wrapped in tinplate to make several experimental bombs. The effect was even better than imagined.","The experiment was on the mountain. Some passing birds just happened to be there when the bomb exploded. The birds did not even escape.","With such power, how could the enemy possibly get any benefits from them?","Seeing the power of the bombs, the brothers were very motivated. They produced dozens of bombs using the same method that day.","Their speed was fast. Mo Qing and Mo Xiuyan did not dare to delay one bit. They started making bamboo tubes early every morning.","Unknowingly, the two felt that their bodies had recovered a lot of strength.","Especially Mo Xiuyan, after his hand tendons were reconnected by He Zhiran, he hadn't dared to overexert himself.","Now he didn't even feel it took much effort to wrap the tinplate around the bamboo tubes.","Especially when thinking that they could contribute to the family, father and son worked tirelessly when busy.","Seeing that the production of bombs was gradually on track, Mo Jiuye chose a day to get up early, and took the jewelry and other items prepared by He Zhiran for Mo Hanyue's dowry to go to town by carriage.","His ostensible purpose for going to town was to buy dowry for his sister, but he actually had another important thing to do.","That was he planned to go see Meng Huaining.","Recently Meng Huaining had been too busy preparing for his wedding, so he hadn't come to visit for a long time.","The silly boy didn't even know that his future father-in-law had returned, otherwise how could he have lost his manners?","That was his future father-in-law, yet he had completely missed the best opportunity to show his face.","It was also because Mo Qing was stubborn. After learning that his precious daughter would marry soon, he felt very uncomfortable.","The girl he had doted on and raised with his own hands had reached the age of marriage. To be honest, Mo Qing felt very guilty that Mo Hanyue had lost so many years of fatherly love.","Especially since Mo Qing had lost all his memories of the past eight years. In his impression, his precious daughter was still an obedient and lovely little girl. How could he have returned home to her getting married?","This was something Mo Qing was unwilling to accept from the bottom of his heart, yet he had no choice but to accept it. After all, it was the eternal truth that men should marry and women should be married off when they came of age.","When a girl reached marriageable age, he could not make her stay even if he wanted to.","Although Mo Qing understood these principles, he still felt uncomfortable about meeting the man who would take his precious daughter away.","Therefore, he specifically told Mo Chuhan not to reveal the news of his return to Meng Huaining when going to take office.","He wanted to wait for the family snatcher to come to the door himself and give him a surprise.","The main reason Mo Jiuye went to find Meng Huaining was that he was worried about the situation in the capital. Naturally he had to follow his father's will and not reveal the news of his return.","Xiaobai had left for the capital with the letter more than ten days ago. Reasonably, it should have already delivered the letter.","If Emperor Shunwu had successfully found the gu raiser master, Fei Nanyu would have let Xiaobai come back with a message as soon as he received the news.","But Xiaobai still hadn't returned. Mo Jiuye was worried that the old general Jin's health couldn't hold on.","He knew Meng Huaining was in touch with Fei Nanyu, so he thought he could get some news from the capital through him.","It happened that when Mo Jiuye arrived, Meng Huaining had just finished hearing a case in the court hall and was stepping out.","\"Ninth brother, when did you come over?\" Seeing Mo Jiuye, Meng Huaining's face changed from his usual sternness to a smile as he walked up to greet him.","Mo Jiuye threw the reins of the horse on the wooden post in front of the yamen gate. Facing his future brother-in-law, he did not intend to beat around the bush.","\"I came to ask Brother Meng about some things.\"","Meng Huaining knew that Mo Jiuye was always busy at home. He would not come to find him for no reason. He quickly gestured for Mo Jiuye to come to the study used as his office.","After not seeing him for a while, Mo Jiuye noticed that Meng Huaining looked much thinner.","\"Brother Meng, you seem to have lost weight?\"","He was not a gossip, only asking out of concern because Meng Huaining had clearly lost a noticeable amount of weight.","Being cared for by his future uncle, Meng Huaining's face turned red.","He smiled awkwardly, \"Just been busy recently.\"","When he said he was busy, Mo Jiuye did not doubt it. As a parent official, especially one as clean as Meng Huaining, there must be endless trivial matters to deal with every day.","Plus his wedding with Mo Jiuye's sister was approaching, being busy was understandable."]},{"number":425,"title":"Chapter 425: How did Brother Nine Know about It","paragraphs":["Seeing that nothing had happened, Mo Jiuye was relieved.","He stated the purpose of his visit this time.","\"Brother Meng, I've come this time because I wanted to inquire about some things.\"","\"Brother Jiu, please feel free to ask me anything.\" Meng Huaining had long regarded Mo Jiuye as one of his own family.","Especially after he was engaged to Mo Hanyue, he felt even closer to her few elder brothers.","\"I heard that the Ninth Prince in the capital city colluded with the Gu Masters from the Southern Border to frame several important court ministers.\"","Meng Huaining was quite surprised that Mo Jiuye knew about this matter.","Based on his understanding of the Mo family, they had already lost confidence in the imperial court, and didn't even want to care about it at all.","\"How did Brother Jiu come to know about this?\" Meng Huaining was not trying to pry anything from Mo Jiuye, he was just simply asking.","Since his mother-in-law had come to accompany Lady Ran in the northwest for the impending childbirth, it was impossible for this to be a secret from Meng Huaining who was about to marry Mo Hanyue, so Mo Jiuye did not intend to conceal it either.","\"It was because my mother-in-law came from the capital city and mentioned this matter a few days ago.\"","\"I see.\" Meng Huaining glanced outside the door and saw no one approaching before saying in a low voice, \"I also only received the news a few days ago. Indeed it is as Brother Jiu said, several important ministers have been poisoned by Gu.\"","\"I heard that Emperor Shunwu has already sent people to look for Gu masters to undo the poison, may I ask if there has been any progress on this matter?\" This was what Mo Jiuye cared about the most.","Since his mother-in-law came from the capital city, what she knew was the situation from at least twenty days ago. No one could say clearly what was happening now.","He knew that there were carrier pigeons transmitting letters between Meng Huaining and Fei Nanyu. Although pigeon speed was not as fast as his little white bird, they still had a travel time of three to four days.","That meant the news Meng Huaining received was from the last five or six days, which showed that Emperor Shunwu still had not found the Gu masters to undo the poison yet.","Mo Jiuye had told his family that he went out this time to purchase dowries for Mo Hanyue, so it was still a bit early to return now.","He simply took a stroll around the city before rushing back in the carriage in the afternoon.","After dinner, Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran together handed over the dowry gifts packed neatly in a small wooden box to Mo Hanyue.","\"Hanyue, this is the dowry the family has prepared for you. Take a look and see if you like it,\" He Zhiran pushed the small wooden box in front of Mo Hanyue.","When Mo Hanyue saw the courtyard and land her family had given her, she felt somewhat guilty.","The present Mo family was no longer like when they were in the capital city. Participating in farm work every day made her truly understand that it was not easy for the family to earn money.","For her wedding, all family members had donated money to build her a courtyard residence as dowry. Even the furnishings and beddings inside were the best quality.","The specifications were no less than those of distinguished noble families in the capital city, but rather were of an even higher class.","\"Sister-in-law, this really won't do. You all have given me more than enough. I cannot accept these anymore,\" Mo Hanyue sincerely spoke from her heart. She did not want her family to spend more money for her sake.","As she spoke, she pushed the small wooden box back in front of He Zhiran.","\"Sister-in-law, I really can't accept these. Keep them for when my little nephews get married in the future.\"","This made He Zhiran laugh, \"How do you know they will be nephews and not nieces?\"","\"That's fine too. Keep them for their dowries when they get married in the future.\" In Mo Hanyue's mind, no matter whether Sister-in-law gives birth to boys or girls, she would love them all the same.","At this time, Old Lady Mo also spoke up.","\"Hanyue already has such a large residence for her dowry, which is presentable enough. It's better not to give her these jewelries.\"","Speaking of which, Old Lady Mo also felt somewhat guilty.","Back when she married Mo Qing, she also brought a good dowry with her.","It was a pity that the Mo men were always away on military campaigns. All the wealth they obtained were used to provide relief for the dead and injured soldiers as well as their families, leaving nothing in the family home, let alone giving an outward appearance of deep financial resources.","Later, as news came of the successive deaths in battle of the Mo men, Old Lady Mo didn't wish for her widowed daughters-in-law to live in hardship, so she gradually drew from her own dowry to supplement the family funds.","The sisters-in-law were sensible. Seeing that mother-in-law took out her own dowry for the sake of their livelihood, they were unwilling to fall behind and also contributed their own dowries to the family.","At that time, Mo Jiuye was constantly away at war and did not know the situation at home. He allocated all war spoils obtained to the soldiers who fought alongside him through life and death.","This resulted in He Zhiran not salvaging many valuable items when ransacking the Mo residence before they were exiled.","These were also the reasons behind Old Lady Mo's guilt.","As a mother, it was incumbent on her to prepare the dowry for her daughter's wedding.","Yet now, not to mention dowry, if not for the hard work of her daughter-in-law all this while, it was likely the whole family could not even afford meals.","And now her daughter-in-law had prepared a box of jewelry for her daughter. How could she as the mother feel at ease accepting this?","\"These were originally things that I as her mother should have prepared. Now lacking the means to do so myself, yet needing you as sister-in-law to make these preparations, this pains my heart.\"","Seeing this, the sisters-in-law also gathered around to show their support, concurring with mother-in-law's words only halfway.","Before He Zhiran married into the family, the sisters-in-law always deferred to Eldest Sister-in-law's words. So this time, Eldest Sister-in-law took the lead to speak up first.","\"Hanyue is the only daughter in our Mo family. Not only must her wedding be celebrated in splendor, but her dowry must not wrong her either.","Since little sister is willing to arrange the jewelry for Hanyue, why don't we sisters contribute the silver for it together?","This way, we married-in sisters can also feel more at ease.\"","Second Sister-in-Law also stepped forward to show her support, \"Little sister, just listen to Eldest Sister's suggestion. I am also willing to contribute a share of silver for the jewelry.\"","\"I am also willing...\"","\"And I am willing too...\"","Without exception, all eight sisters-in-law voiced their willingness to share the costs. Moreover, they spoke with utmost sincerity, showing not the slightest reluctance.","Although not wealthy, the solidarity of the nine sisters-in-law was what He Zhiran loved most about the Mo family. Regardless of their great number, the sisters always cooperated seamlessly together, never dissenting over trivial matters.","She understood that her sisters-in-law were speaking genuinely, yet she did not wish for them to share the burden.","The jewelry was all purchased on Taobao Mall. For the wealthy He Zhiran, it was a drop in the ocean.","If converted to silver liang of this era, the value of the jewelry would easily amount to several thousand liang.","While it was true she distributed the due wages to her sisters-in-law on time every month, and the sums were not inconsiderable, those incomes were still outstanding compared to the earnings of common folk in the northwest. Even if the sisters exhausted all their family savings, it was doubtful they could contribute an equal share of silver for the jewelry.","Of course, only He Zhiran knew the true value of the jewelry. She would not allow her sisters-in-law to share costs for it.","\"Sisters, I understand your kind intentions, but do not forget - presently the Mo family affairs are all managed by me. Other than the monthly wages I distribute to you, all remaining income is under my administration.\""]},{"number":426,"title":"Chapter 426: Han Yue's Dowry is Too Expensive","paragraphs":["Speaking of this, He Zhiran really didn't have anything like bills.","She was not good at doing business or managing money. The reason she was able to develop some money-making businesses in this era was simply that she took advantage of her soul crossing over.","In the past when sending money home to her family, she would only roughly keep track of the household income and then distribute a portion to each person, keeping the rest as the public account for the household.","She didn't have an exact number for this public account, after all, recent expenses were greater than income.","For example, she had built eleven siheyuan and breeding farms, and invested in many other things. There were a lot more, she was just too lazy to keep records since that space money could cover it all.","When the sisters-in-law heard He Zhiran's meaning that the jewelry prepared for Mo Hanyue came from the household public account, they no longer competed to chip in.","If He Zhiran said this, it could make the sisters-in-law believe it, but it couldn't fool Old Lady Mo.","Although the Guogong fu didn't have a lot of money and valuables in the past, the old lady had been running the household for many years. Now she had a rough idea in her heart of the profits from the various businesses in the household, even without detailed numbers.","He Zhiran was determined to give these pieces of jewelry to Mo Hanyue as her dowry, leaving no room for objection as she opened the box.","She said it was a small box, but it was actually the size of a modern shoebox.","Inside was full of various gold and silver jewelry.","Things made with modern techniques, whether in quality or appearance, could dazzle anyone's eyes.","He Zhiran took out a solid style peony flower pendant yellow gold necklace, and tried it in front of Mo Hanyue's neck.","\"This will look very good worn outside the wedding dress.\"","Right after, she also took out a pair of peony flower earrings in the same style as the pendant on the necklace.","\"These earrings match the necklace perfectly. Hanyue will be able to entrance her husband on her wedding day wearing these.\"","Although He Zhiran's words were a bit exaggerated, there was some truth to them.","The style of the necklace and earrings was simply shocking to all the women. Even Old Lady Mo who had just tried to stop her was wide-eyed.","\"Jiuye, did you buy these jewelry pieces in the city?\"","Old Lady Mo knew her son had gone into the city today to purchase them, thus the question.","In her understanding, not to mention in the barren northwest, even in the best jewelry store in the capital city, it would be impossible to find such high quality jewelry with such beautiful styles.","These pieces were all selected by He Zhiran. She intentionally didn't choose anything too unusual, precisely because she didn't want others to question them.","She didn't expect that these things would still astonish her mother-in-law.","Seeing Mo Jiuye at a loss for how to explain for the moment, she took the initiative to say, \"Mother, I drew the designs for these jewelry pieces during my free time, and had my husband go commission them from a jewelry shop in the city recently.\"","Saying it this way, Old Lady Mo actually believed it somewhat.","This ninth daughter-in-law of hers had an exceptionally good mind, and could come up with novel ideas from time to time. It was not too surprising that she could draw such beautiful jewelry designs.","However, she still could not accept a whole box full of gold and silver jewelry.","\"Hanyue's dowry is too valuable. Even using the silver from our public accounts is not acceptable.\"","If it were in the past, He Zhiran would also have listened to her mother-in-law's words, but since these things were already prepared, how could she not give them out?","Moreover, she had been in the ancient era for so long, and this was the first time she had the opportunity to splurge on the money from her space. How could she let it end in failure?","He Zhiran didn't say anything, but continued taking pieces of jewelry out of the box to try in front of Mo Hanyue.","At this time, the sisters-in-law had already been attracted by the beautiful jewelry He Zhiran took out. Even Mo Hanyue, the main character herself, was not immune.","But deep down, she still maintained her original intention that no matter how much she liked the jewelry, she could not let the family spend so much on her account.","The sisters-in-law kept praising how beautiful Mo Hanyue looked wearing these jewelry pieces, to the point they had already overlooked the value.","\"Hanyue, this red gemstone bracelet is so pretty.\"","\"Our Hanyue's skin is fair, she looks good wearing anything.\"","\"Hanyue, look at this one. Although it's made of silver, it shines brighter than the clumsy hairpin on Second Sister-in-law's head.\"","\"Are the stones on this ring yellow gold with inlaid jade?\"","\"Quick, look, this little jade frog is so cute, with gemstones dotted on it too.\"","\"...\"","In that moment, the room of the elder couple was filled with the sisters-in-law's praises for how beautiful the jewelry was.","He Zhiran had expected women would like these things, but didn't think they would cause such a sensation when they appeared.","Old Lady Mo watched as her daughters-in-law went back and forth, and didn't know what to say anymore.","Mo Qing kept signalling to his old wife with his eyes for her to hurry up and get control of the situation.","Old Lady Mo took a deep breath. \"Alright, you married-in sisters need to stop urging this on.\"","The sisters-in-law were happily fiddling with the beautiful jewelry at this time. When they heard Mother-in-law speak, Second Sister-in-law laughingly responded.","\"Mother, jewelry like this isn't something ordinary people can own. Having these as her dowry is not just for Hanyue's dignity, but also our Mo family's dignity.","Since Ninth Younger Sister has already said the money to buy the jewelry came from our public accounts, why not just fulfill Ninth Younger Sister's good intentions, and also let Hanyue leave home for marriage in glory with these pieces.\"","Second Sister-in-law opened the conversation, and Eldest Sister-in-law also agreed, \"Mother, what Second Sister-in-law said is right. I have no objections to using the public account silver. \"","Seeing this, the other women also voiced their approval of using the household public funds to prepare the dowry jewelry for Mo Hanyue.","At worst, they could just work harder later to earn back the amount. Right now, the business selling cold rabbit meat and long-eared rabbit pendants were very stable.","Not only so, the rabbits bred extremely quickly at home, so there was no need to worry about running out of materials.","Seeing the sisters-in-law finally take her side, He Zhiran seized the chance to say, \"Mother, you see the sisters-in-law have no objections. Please don't worry yourself over this. I guarantee I will earn back the money for these jewelry pieces as quickly as possible.\"","Having seen the sisters-in-law's enthusiasm for the jewelry just now, He Zhiran already had new ideas to make money.","There were molds for making gold and silver jewelry for sale on Taobao Mall. She remembered when she was little, taking shelter from the rain in a shop that processed gold and silver jewelry. At that time the owner happened to be helping a customer make a bracelet.","The bracelet had beautiful engraved patterns on it. While not too unique if placed in modern times, it would be different in ancient times.","The effect would be the same as the pieces she gave Mo Hanyue today as dowry, very eye-catching.","She was bored waiting for the rain to stop and watched the owner make jewelry the whole time. She still roughly remembered the process. If she purchased various molds on Taobao Mall, and made beautiful jewelry, it would definitely create more profits.","Especially since the family would be raising an army soon, expenses would surely not be small.","Just feeding a thousand-some men was already a considerable expenditure."]},{"number":427,"title":"Chapter 427: How Can I Part","paragraphs":["He Zhiran had been thinking about what kind of business she could do recently that would allow her family to openly see that the money to raise troops was earned.","She immediately decided that she would go into the jewelry business.","She did not need to worry about materials, as there was endless gold and silver from the treasuries of Da Shun and the Southern Frontier Country that she had secretly obtained from her storage space. She just needed to use tools to melt them into gold and silver materials.","This would also save her from having those gold and silver sit uselessly in her storage space. It was simply killing two birds with one stone.","Of course, she would also have Mo Jiuye pretend to go out and purchase some materials on the surface to avoid arousing suspicion.","He Zhiran sank into thought. Seeing that she had not spoken for some time, her sister-in-law gently patted her arm.","\"Sister-in-law, what are you thinking so intensely about? Could it be that you still can't bear to give these to Hanyue?\"","He Zhiran knew that her sister-in-law was teasing her.","\"Sister-in-law, what are you talking about? These were originally meant to be Hanyue's dowry. How could I be reluctant to part with them?\"","Seeing that her daughters-in-law had taken over the floor with their chattering, Old Lady Mo knew that any further refusal on her part would seem powerless.","\"Hanyue, since all nine of your sisters-in-law have said this, just accept them. You must remember everyone's generosity today and find an opportunity to repay them in the future.\"","Since leaving the Capital City, Mo Hanyue had grown more sensible by the day.","She was initially unwilling to accept such a valuable dowry, as she truly did not want her family to spend so much on her marriage.","But now that her mother had spoken, and she did actually like the jewelry, her face flushed red as she said:","\"Hanyue thanks her sisters-in-law for their kindness. Rest assured, sisters-in-law, Hanyue will not forget what you have done for me today.\"","Though addressing everyone as \"sisters-in-law\", Mo Hanyue's gaze remained fixed on He Zhiran.","She knew clearly in her heart that all of this was arranged by Ninth Sister-in-Law, and without Ninth Sister-in-Law there would be no today's Mo Hanyue.","He Zhiran felt very gratified that in just one short year, Mo Hanyue had transformed from a pampered child into a sensible and hardworking young woman.","\"Just look at our Hanyue, growing more sensible by the day. Sisters-in-law will remember what you said. In the future if Lord Meng gets promoted and becomes wealthy, don't forget your maternal family!\"","Although her sister-in-law's words were sometimes blunt, they often hit home for the women.","This time was no exception. They all felt that the Mo Family's current commoner status was lowly enough, and if their exiled status was revealed, they would be even lower than commoners.","With a relative who was an official to rely on, many things could go more smoothly.","He Zhiran didn't care how others thought. She felt at ease after the jewelry was given away.","With matters occupying her mind, she was someone who immediately wanted to take action. After some small talk with everyone, she pleaded tiredness and asked Mo Jiuye to accompany her back.","Madam He had now grown accustomed to life here.","What she hadn't expected was that her daughter's life was not as awful as she had imagined. In fact, it was even more comfortable than life in the Capital City.","This put her much more at ease. Her only worry now was He Zhiran's health, so she would stay at her daughter's side whenever possible.","If her son-in-law was there, Madam He would tactfully take her leave to give the young couple private time together.","Now that Mo Jiuye was accompanying He Zhiran, Madam He naturally did not intrude. Behind closed doors, He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye could freely enter the storage space without reservation.","Seeing his wife in such a hurry to bring him into the storage space, Mo Jiuye knew she must have something she wanted to do.","\"Ranran, what are you going to do?\"","\"Husband, when Father first proposed raising troops, I already said that I could bear the costs of maintaining the soldiers.\"","At that time when He Zhiran had proposed paying the costs, Mo Jiuye did not think too much of it. After all, no one knew better than him just how much wealth was inside the storage space.","\"With so many treasures in the storage space, let alone feeding an army of a thousand troops, we could even support ten thousand!\" The more Mo Jiuye thought about it, the more confused he became. Could it be his wife was having second thoughts and didn't want to use the space's money to raise soldiers?","He Zhiran knew Mo Jiuye was oversimplifying things.","\"Have you ever thought that supporting a thousand cavalry is no meager expense? Although our family currently has some small money-making industries publicly, the amounts earned are still paltry.","If this goes on for some time, Mother's shrewdness is sure to grow suspicious at some point.\"","Hearing He Zhiran explain this, Mo Jiuye instantly understood.","\"Ranran, you've thought of some livelihood to earn money?\"","\"Don't you think that we're perfectly suited for the jewelry business?\"","When the jewelry was given out in the elders' room to Mo Hanyue, Mo Jiuye had been watching nearby at the time too. If he hadn't worried about revealing anything abnormal that might attract suspicion, this grown man would have loved to step forward and take a closer look too.","Originally he thought jewelry was something only women would be interested in. When his wife bought items on Taobao Mall, he had no interest or intention of helping select anything either, so he didn't get to see the true appearances of these jewelry pieces until they were opened from their boxes.","Mo Jiuye's impression at that moment was summed up in two words: \"Beautiful!\" Three words: \"Truly beautiful!\"...","So when his female relations were arranging the jewelry, his own mind was busy imagining that his wife would look even lovelier than the girls when dressed up in these pieces. That night when returning, he ordered He Zhiran to buy some for himself too.","Now hearing his wife propose starting a jewelry business, his eyes unconsciously drifted towards the gold and silver they had secretly taken from state treasuries. His thinking mirrored He Zhiran's - they had the raw materials for making gold and silver jewelry, the only thing they were worried about was skill.","\"Ranran, as far as I know, there are no craftsmen in Da Shun who can make such beautiful jewelry.\" Mo Jiuye frowned.","Seeing Mo Jiuye furrow his brow, He Zhiran simply laughed even more gleefully.","\"If someone in Da Shun could make jewelry like this, how would we make big money?\"","Mo Jiuye was increasingly perplexed.","\"Ranran, stop keeping me in suspense. Tell me, how should we do this?\"","Instead of answering Mo Jiuye's question immediately, He Zhiran randomly purchased a mold template for a pendant necklace in the shape of a prancing foo lion on Taobao Mall.","The style was quite novel for Da Shun's tastes. However, before seeing the final product come out, all Mo Jiuye could see was a white object with no discernible shape.","He Zhiran paid no mind to Mo Jiuye's curious gaze and continued buying some tools to process gold and silver jewelry from Taobao.","Next, she used her mental powers to call over a gold ingot.","Seeing his wife grab the blowtorch and ready herself to do something, Mo Jiuye hastily took it from her.","\"Ranran, your pregnancy makes this unsuited work for you. Just instruct me on what to do.\"","He Zhiran was not being coy either; she directed Mo Jiuye on first using the blowtorch to melt the gold ingot.","The blowtorch gave off strong heat. Before long, the fist-sized gold ingot had liquefied into molten form.","Next, He Zhiran instructed Mo Jiuye to carefully pour the melted liquid into the mold and let it cool before removing it.","In Mo Jiuye's hand was a shiny golden prancing foo lion pendant. His eyes shone with pleasant surprise."]},{"number":428,"title":"Chapter 428: Is This a Viable Business","paragraphs":["Ran Ran had never seen anything like this before. It looked a bit like a toad, but it was much more beautiful and exotic than a toad.","\"Ran Ran, I didn't expect that making such a beautiful piece of jewelry could be so simple,\" Mo Jiuye said.","As He Zhiran told Mo Jiuye the auspicious legend about the pi xiu, explaining its meaning of good fortune, she took out the tools for grinding and polishing and started working on the pi xiu pendant she had made in the mold.","Of course she wasn't a professional jewelry maker, and she was relying completely on the faint memories from her previous life.","Even so, once it was finished, the pi xiu pendant looked just as good as the jewelry bought online, with no difference in luster or delicacy of detail.","After hearing about the auspicious meaning of the pi xiu and seeing the finished pendant his wife had made, Mo Jiuye couldn't help praising her.","\"Ran Ran, I didn't expect this strange little creature to have such a good meaning. Businesspeople will surely like it.","And the jewelry you've made here can definitely be considered top-tier in our place.\"","He Zhiran smiled even more proudly. \"What do you think, will this business work?\"","\"It'll work, it'll work. Ran Ran, you're so clever, I really don't know what other things I don't know about are still in your little head.\"","As he spoke, Mo Jiuye affectionately stroked her smooth hair, his face showing an expression of pride in his wife.","Right after, He Zhiran bought several more kinds of jewelry molds and had Mo Jiuye make them.","Before long, Mo Jiuye had produced several beautiful gold rings, bracelets, and other pieces.","He Zhiran inspected the workmanship, then gathered them into a pile.","\"Husband, when you have time, take these to show Tang Mingrui and ask if he's willing to partner with us in the jewelry business.\"","Pausing a moment, He Zhiran added, \"You can tell him that besides these, we can also make inlaid gemstone and jade jewelry.\"","He Zhiran hadn't actually seen the process of inlaying gems and jade in her previous life.","But when buying the molds, she had noticed there were types for inlaying, so she figured with a little research she could figure it out.","There was no rush for all that. First they had to see if Tang Mingrui was willing to partner. If he wasn't, He Zhiran would have to find someone else.","After all, the situation of the Mo Family was special now, and it wouldn't draw much attention for them to run some farming and animal husbandry businesses on the surface in Xi Ling Village. But if they started this kind of jewelry business, it would likely attract more notice.","Besides, she firmly believed that once this kind of jewelry made using molds came out, it would definitely set off a buying frenzy, and the boss wouldn't be able to keep a low profile even if he wanted to.","Of course, the capital needed for this gold and silver business was different from their other home industries. No matter what kind of profit split Tang Mingrui proposed, they would need to have fixed costs.","This was real gold and silver, with high inherent value. Added to that her special production technique and novel styles, they probably couldn't continue the 50-50 split with Tang Mingrui.","Of course, these were just He Zhiran's initial plans. They'd have to see if Tang Mingrui was willing to partner first before researching the specifics.","Mo Jiuye also thought his wife's idea for making money was good.","\"Alright, tomorrow I'll go find Brother Tang and ask if he's interested in partnering.\"","With the matter settled, after breakfast the next day Mo Jiuye was about to head into town with Ba Ge when he suddenly heard a familiar cheerful chirp overhead.","Little White was back.","Mo Jiuye knew he probably wouldn't make it into town today. He gestured for Ba Ge to go first as he held out his arm.","Before long, Little White landed steadily on it.","Mo Jiuye stroked its head. \"Little White, thanks for your hard work. You must have good news for me?\"","As he spoke, he glanced at its legs.","Little White had landed with its legs tucked in so Mo Jiuye couldn't see. It seemed to sense its master's eagerness and fluttered its wings, standing up and sticking out its right leg.","Sure enough, there was a little paper scroll tied to it.","Mo Jiuye untied the scroll, then took Little White to He Zhiran and let it relax in the space. Right in front of He Zhiran he unrolled the note.","There weren't many words on the little piece of paper, and the tiny writing was packed densely together.","General Jin still has his life for now, but the situation isn't good. A master who can dispel Gu poison has been found, but without the mother Gu worm, he can't dispel it.","Hearing that General Jin was still alive and Emperor Shunwu had found someone who could dispel Gu poison meant there was still hope.","\"Husband, let Little White rest in the space for a day. Tomorrow it can set off for the capital with the Gu worms,\" He Zhiran suggested.","\"Mm, that's what I was thinking too. But with Little White's size, carrying three porcelain bottles with mother Gu worms will be hard for it to fly.\" This was Mo Jiuye's biggest headache.","After all, neither he nor He Zhiran could tell which bottle had the Gu worm controlling the child worms inside General Jin's body.","He Zhiran really couldn't distinguish them either. The bottles weren't light, and Little White truly wouldn't be able to carry them with its strength.","After thinking it over, He Zhiran could only reveal some modern items.","She took out her phone and bought several thin, lightweight plastic containers on Taobao.","Calling them containers was a stretch. They were really just the smallest size of transparent little boxes that takeout places often used for sauces, with almost no weight when held.","Not only that, the little boxes had sealed lids, so putting the mother Gu worms inside also prevented any chance of them escaping.","Mo Jiuye knew his wife was going all out to save General Jin's life, getting out these odd little boxes.","But he already had an excuse for them prepared. The Gu worms had come from Mr. Si Meng anyway, so no one would think that the two of them had repackaged the worms.","Even if someone was suspicious, they could only suspect Mr. Si Meng had gotten the strange boxes from somewhere.","He Zhiran hadn't considered any of this. She was used to her husband finding ways to gloss over the strange things she brought out, so this time would be no different.","The couple carefully put the three Gu worms into the new plastic boxes, then Mo Jiuye tied them to Little White's legs.","On the surface they looked a little clumsy, but to Little White they had almost no weight and wouldn't impede its flight, as long as it flew high enough.","In addition, Mo Jiuye wrote a note to Fei Nanyu, saying these were the Gu worms controlling the important ministers at court.","As for how to handle them, Emperor Shunwu's summoned Gu dispelling master would know better than anyone."]},{"number":429,"title":"Chapter 429: Something's Happened to the Tang Brothers","paragraphs":["Little White's business was arranged, and the couple planned to let Little White rest in the space for a day before leaving.","Moreover, they also discovered that although Little White and Rice Ball were two species, the two little ones had unknowingly established a deep friendship in the space.","When they were together, although they often seemed to fight with each other and neither yielded to the other, after a long time if they didn't see each other they would miss each other.","Just like now, Mo Jiuye had just taken off the box tied to Little White's leg, and the little guy fluttered his wings and ran to play with Rice Ball.","Little White landed on top of Rice Ball's head, and would even peck at its furry cat head from time to time.","Rice Ball would let out a few meows, and then reach out to pat it.","Little White flew away to escape, and Rice Ball strode with its little short legs to chase it. The scene of the two little ones chasing each other, looked extremely harmonious in the eyes of the couple.","It was still early now, and Mo Jiuye planned to continue going to the city to look for Tang Mingrui.","He was in a hurry to find Tang Mingrui, not entirely because of the jewelry business, but because the watermelons at home had gradually ripened, and it was time for harvesting.","In the past few days, Tang Mingrui's muskmelon business had done very well, earning tens of thousands of taels of silver for both himself and the Mo Family.","He should know that these days were the season when the Mo Family’s watermelons were ripe. With Tang Mingrui’s temperament, he would have brought people to transport the goods early.","Mo Jiuye waited for two days without seeing any movement from Tang Mingrui at all.","If it were in the past, with this kind of money-making business, even if Tang Mingrui himself was too busy to get away, he would still send someone to transport the goods.","As a result, this time was unusually abnormal. Not only did he not come in person, but his men did not come either.","Out of concern for his friend, Mo Jiuye also felt it necessary to go there and take a look.","He had just entered Yun City when he saw Eighth Brother leading a group of people, including officials, and a middle-aged man tied up. The group walked quickly towards an alley.","Eighth Brother was the catcher of the yamen. It was normal for him to handle cases with people. It was just that the middle-aged man being escorted by the officials looked a little familiar to Mo Jiuye.","He thought about it carefully and instantly remembered who this person was - one of the subordinates of that Second Young Master hired by Boss Jin last time.","It was normal for a group of small gangsters to commit crimes, but Mo Jiuye had just seen that Eighth Brother's expression was not as indifferent as usual. He instinctively felt that this matter was more or less related to his Mo Family, or involved someone related to the Mo Family.","Thinking of this, Mo Jiuye strode to catch up.","At this time, an official was forcibly smashing the door of a commoner's house.","\"Official handling a case, open the door quickly...\"","Mo Jiuye walked over, \"Eighth Brother, what happened?\"","Mo Chuhan frowned and whispered, \"Brother Tang is in trouble.\"","Hearing Eighth Brother say this, Mo Jiuye suddenly had a bad premonition.","\"Did someone die?\"","Eighth Brother nodded, \"Yeah, Boss Jin was killed this morning.\"","Although Eighth Brother didn't explain much, Mo Jiuye could grasp the general idea from it.","Boss Jin was dead, Brother Tang was in trouble, and the officials took the gangster to catch someone - it was nothing more than Tang Mingrui having a grudge against Boss Jin for coveting his muskmelon business, so he hired someone to kill him.","It had to be said that Mo Jiuye had completely analyzed the superficial meaning.","However, no matter what, he absolutely did not believe that Tang Mingrui would do such a thing.","With that guy's shrewdness, it was impossible for him to do something so easily caught. There must be someone framing him.","Seeing that Eighth Brother was handling the case here, it was not good for him to inquire in detail.","At this moment, with a bang, the courtyard door was forcibly pushed open by several officials, who immediately rushed in with sabers in their hands.","Mo Chuhan handed the gangster to a subordinate to watch, and greeted Mo Jiuye.","\"Ninth brother, come with me.\"","The two brothers had martial arts skills and quickly walked to the front of the yard.","Almost at the same time, the two leapt up onto the west wall.","Immediately after, a scream was heard: \"Ouch!\"","A burly sturdy man fell heavily from the top of the wall to the ground.","Mo Chuhan shouted at the officials: \"Come on, tie him up for me.\"","Soon, several officials came over with ropes and tied the man up neatly.","With the wanted man captured, Mo Chuhan would certainly take him back to the yamen.","On the way, Mo Jiuye took the opportunity to ask, \"Eighth Brother, what exactly happened to Brother Tang?\"","Although he had already guessed seven or eight points in his heart, he still had to get confirmation from Eighth Brother.","\"When I first arrived at the yamen this morning, Magistrate Meng gave me an official document sent from the prefect. It ordered us to immediately arrest Tang Mingrui of Yun City.","When I heard it was Brother Tang, I specifically took a close look at the official document. It stated that last night before the hour of zi, Boss Jin was murdered in the street.","The perpetrator was a subordinate of the provincial hoodlum Second Young Master.","That guy was unlucky. After committing the murder, he was caught on the spot by patrolling officials passing by. After overnight interrogation, he confessed that he was hired by Tang Mingrui to kill Boss Jin.\"","Mo Chuhan pointed to the middle-aged gangster escorted by the officials and said, \"This is the guy. The prefect sent him to our Yun City together, meaning that since Brother Tang is from Yun City, Magistrate Meng should handle this case.","The prefect pushing the case outward this time is also good for Brother Tang. Lord Meng is upright and honest. He will surely find the real murderer and give him justice.\"","\"Eighth Brother means that Brother Tang is now in the county yamen?\"","\"Yes, when Magistrate Meng received the official document, he sent someone to invite Brother Tang to the yamen.\"","Mo Jiuye knew that even though Eighth Brother said Meng Huaining sent someone to invite Tang Mingrui to the yamen, he probably would not let him leave before the case was closed.","Seeing Eighth Brother's appearance, he did not seem to have figured out the specific situation either, so Mo Jiuye could not ask anything useful out of him.","He followed Eighth Brother to the county yamen. Meng Huaining was in the study, but Tang Mingrui was nowhere to be seen.","Mo Jiuye entered the study and asked, \"Brother Meng, what exactly is going on with Brother Tang?\"","Meng Huaining did not treat Mo Jiuye as an outsider. He casually picked up an official document from the desk and handed it to him.","\"Someone accused Tang Mingrui of hiring a killer. Look at the specifics yourself.\"","Mo Jiuye took the official document and read it.","The beginning was consistent with what Eighth Brother said, that Boss Jin was killed on the street last night, and the murderer was caught red-handed by patrolling officials passing by.","At the same time, the murderer also insisted that it was Tang Mingrui who paid him to do it, because Boss Jin had coveted his muskmelon business, so Tang Mingrui held a grudge and hired someone to kill him.","Mo Jiuye skimmed through it quickly, then put the official document back on the table.","\"Brother Tang would never do such a thing.\"","His tone was very certain."]},{"number":430,"title":"Chapter 430: Bring People Up","paragraphs":["Although Meng Huaining did not understand Tang Mingrui's character as well as Mo Jiuye did, he also felt that Tang Mingrui would not take such a big risk to hire someone to commit murder over such a trivial matter.","Meng Huaining knew that Elder Brother Ba had just caught the man, so he might as well interrogate him first while they had the chance.","\"Ninth Brother, if you're free, you can come listen to the trial.\"","Mo Jiuye had come to the city to look for Tang Mingrui. Thinking that he was in some kind of trouble, Mo Jiuye would definitely want to find out more about it.","\"If it's convenient, I do want to listen in on it.\"","With that said, the two men arrived at the courtroom.","For a case that had not yet been investigated clearly, the initial interrogation of the suspect would not be conducted publicly.","Therefore, the doors of the courtroom remained tightly shut.","Meng Huaining sat upright and dignified in the chief magistrate's seat.","\"Bring the prisoner in.\"","At his command, the officers soon brought in the burly man.","As soon as he entered the courtroom, the burly man knelt in the center.","\"Your Honor, I've confessed everything I should, it's true that Master Tang gave us the silver to kill Boss Jin.\"","Meng Huaining slammed the gavel furiously: \"I did not ask you any questions, who allowed you to speak?\"","By doing so, he did seem to be protecting Tang Mingrui.","Because he knew that Tang Mingrui was a business partner of the Mo Family. Although this guy had once liked his young fiancée as well, Meng Huaining had won her over in the end.","For the sake of the Yue Family's business in the future, he had to do his best to find out the truth and help absolve Tang Mingrui.","As he spoke, Meng Huaining's gaze had already fallen upon Chen Wu, who had just been caught and brought back by Mo Chuhany and the others.","\"Are you Chen Wu?\"","Chen Wu knew everything was over since he had failed to escape.","He was also a man who could grasp the situation. When questioned by Meng Huaining, he kowtowed respectfully.","\"This peasant is indeed Chen Wu.\"","Meng Huaining banged the gavel again.","\"Wang Lin confessed that Master Tang hired you to kill Boss Jin and handed you the silver personally, is this true?\"","When asked about this, Chen Wu's eyes became somewhat evasive.","Meng Huaining noticed that he inadvertently glanced at Wang Lin next to him before replying vaguely:","\"This peasant does not know what Your Honor is talking about.\"","Meng Huaining had been a county magistrate for a long time and had seen many stubborn criminals. He did not need to waste words with Chen Wu.","\"Men, Chen Wu is not being honest. Give this official twenty heavy strokes of the rod.\"","The officers who had been with Meng Huaining for a long time also understood his temper. They did not wait for Chen Wu to beg for mercy and immediately blocked his mouth and dragged him out of the courtroom.","The twenty heavy strokes were administered quickly, and Chen Wu was dragged back in.","Meng Huaining did not interrogate him immediately, but instead ordered the officers to fetch a basin of salt water and place it next to Chen Wu.","\"Chen Wu, salt water on open wounds hurts dozens of times more than twenty strokes of the rod. I hope you think carefully before answering the questions I ask you next.\"","Chen Wu took a hard look at the salt water beside him, then gasped heavily a few times.","\"Your Honor, it's true someone gave this peasant silver, but they did not say to kill Boss Jin, only to teach him a lesson.\"","\"Who gave you the silver?\" Meng Huaining pressed.","\"It was Master Tang who gave it to me.\"","\"Well then, tell us, where and when exactly did Master Tang give you the silver?\"","\"It was three days ago. Master Tang came to this peasant's home in Yun City alone and personally gave me five hundred taels of silver, telling me to teach Boss Jin a lesson.\"","Just then, Tang Mingrui's voice rang out from behind the courtroom.","\"Nonsense. I was still at the provincial capital three days ago. I only returned to Yun City yesterday, how could I have given you silver?\"","Tang Mingrui had been arranged by Meng Huaining to listen to the trial from the back of the courtroom. In principle, he should not have spoken, but Chen Wu's lies provoked him to blurt out a retort.","He was fully aware that it was disrespectful to the county magistrate to suddenly speak up from the back. He had just been unable to restrain himself for a moment.","Therefore, although Tang Mingrui had retorted indignantly, he did not show his face.","Meng Huaining did not blame Tang Mingrui for the sudden interruption. After all, he was trying to establish Tang Mingrui's innocence.","He banged the gavel again.","\"Chen Wu, it seems you really won't shed tears until you see the coffin. Since you refuse to tell the truth...\"","As he spoke, his gaze fell upon the basin of salt water.","Before Meng Huaining could give the order, Chen Wu was already begging for mercy loudly.","\"Your Honor, I did not lie! It really was Master Tang who personally brought this peasant five hundred taels of silver three days ago and told me to do this. If you don't believe me, please summon Master Tang to come confront me face to face.\"","Meng Huaining frowned. \"Who was the person speaking from the back just now? Do you recognize that voice?\"","Chen Wu shook his head vigorously. \"He was supposed to be speaking in Master Tang's voice to me, but I'm not familiar with that voice.\"","Hearing this, Meng Huaining looked to Wang Lin, who was scared stiff beside them.","\"Tell me, who ordered you to kill Boss Jin?\"","\"Your Honor, it was Chen Wu who told me to kill Boss Jin.\"","\"Nonsense, I only told you to teach Boss Jin a lesson. When did I ever tell you to kill him?\" Chen Wu was anxious. A matter as grave as taking a life, he could not afford to be wrongly accused.","Wang Lin refused to back down either: \"It was you who told me to kill Boss Jin. You also said you'd give me two hundred taels to escape after the deed was done. I didn't expect you'd keep the entire three hundred taels for yourself.\"","Wang Lin felt more aggrieved the more he spoke. He kowtowed to Meng Huaining several times.","\"Your Honor is wise. This peasant had no enmity with Boss Jin. If Chen Wu had not said he would give me two hundred taels after the deed was done, I would never have dared to do something so wicked.\"","The more aggrieved Wang Lin felt, the more he cried in front of all those people.","In contrast, Chen Wu was extremely indignant.","\"Wang Lin, don't spit blood from your mouth. I promised to give you two hundred taels afterward, but I never said to kill Boss Jin.\"","\"It was you who said to kill Boss Jin...\"","For a time, the only sounds in the silent courtroom were the two men's arguments.","Meng Huaining did not stop them, but observed their expressions as they spoke.","From his observations, he noticed Wang Lin's eyes occasionally dodging, but only when they met Chen Wu's gaze.","With this, Meng Huaining already had a rough guess in mind.","\"Silence. Do you want me to charge you with contempt of court?\"","At his words, the courtroom instantly quieted down.","\"Summon Master Tang.\"","At Meng Huaining's order, Tang Mingrui in the back swiftly came to the front of the courtroom.","Before he could bow, Meng Huaining asked Chen Wu, \"Do you recognize this man before you?\"","Chen Wu looked Tang Mingrui up and down, then shook his head.","\"Replying to Your Honor, this peasant does not recognize him.\"","\"Slap!\"","Meng Huaining slammed the gavel heavily.","\"You don't recognize him, yet you dare to say it was Master Tang who personally gave you five hundred taels?\"","Tang Mingrui was also furious. He walked up to Chen Wu and demanded, \"Take a good look, I am Tang Mingrui. When did I ever give you five hundred taels?\""]},{"number":431,"title":"Chapter 431: I Believe in Lord Meng","paragraphs":["Chen Wu had already been dumbfounded. He really did not recognize the person in front of him.","However, just because he did not recognize this person did not mean that the county magistrate also did not. It was apparent that this was the real Boss Tang.","Who exactly was the person who had given him the silver notes three days ago?","Seeing that Chen Wu had not spoken for a long time, Meng Huaining pressed further: “Chen Wu, speak, who exactly gave you the silver?”","Sweat had already begun beading on Chen Wu's forehead.","“Your honor, this peasant really has not lied. Three days ago a rich young master came to my door and personally handed me five hundred silver notes, telling me to go and teach Boss Jin a lesson.","I had seen Boss Jin a few times before with the Second Young Master. Afraid of being recognized if I took action personally, I found Wang Lin and had him handle this matter.”","As he spoke, Chen Wu desperately kowtowed several times towards Meng Huaining.","“Your honor, this peasant has already endured twenty heavy beatings. I dare not speak another lie, please discern the truth, your honor.”","Not only Meng Huaining, even the observing Mo Jiuye could tell what was going on.","In order to uncover the truth behind this incident, they would have to start with Wang Lin.","Meng Huaining did indeed notice something. He ordered Chen Wu to first be imprisoned, then looked towards Wang Lin.","“Wang Lin, if you do not wish to suffer physical torment, then confess the full truth.”","“Your honor, what this peasant has said is true. I did kill Boss Jin, and it was under Chen Wu's orders. Otherwise, Boss Jin and I had no grievances, how could I have possibly killed him?”","Meng Huaining did not want to say much more to someone so stubborn. He directly ordered that Wang Lin be taken away and given twenty heavy beatings.","After the beating, when asked again, Wang Lin stuck to the same story, though his darting eyes revealed his increased unease.","In any case, based on Chen Wu’s testimony, the idea that Tang Mingrui had hired someone to commit murder could not stand. However, until the true mastermind was found, he could not completely detach himself from this case.","“Boss Tang can return for now. Without this official's order during this period, you cannot leave Yun City and must make yourself available when summoned.”","Having gotten caught up in this matter, Tang Mingrui was also quite helpless. Fortunately, the county magistrate was not muddleheaded, otherwise he would not have been able to leave the government office so quickly.","What was bothering him was that business at the provincial office had been very busy recently. Without him there to oversee things, he worried his subordinates would struggle after some time had passed.","In any case, just being able to temporarily return home was the biggest courtesy Meng Huaining could show him at present, and he would have to accept that favor.","Tang Mingrui respectfully saluted Meng Huaining: “Many thanks for your excellency’s consideration. Tang guarantees he will not leave Yun City before this case is closed.”","Meng Huaining waved his hand to indicate he could leave.","What remained was carefully interrogating Wang Lin himself. Relying on his many years of experience handling cases, to find a breakthrough in this case they would have to start with Wang Lin.","It was just that Wang Lin was extremely stubborn, and it would require more effort to get him to speak out.","Mo Jiuye had come to find Tang Mingrui, so he naturally followed along to ask about the situation. If suitable, he would then consider discussing business matters with the other party.","The two walked shoulder to shoulder out of the government office. Tang Mingrui revealed a bitter smile.","“Ninth brother, I really must have let you see a joke. I just wanted to run my business fairly, yet this kind of thing still happened to me.”","Mo Jiuye knew he felt uncomfortable and lightly patted Tang Mingrui on the shoulder.","“Believe in Magistrate Meng. He will certainly give you justice.”","Tang Mingrui nodded. “Yes, I believe in Magistrate Meng.”","After a short pause, he asked in return, “How did Ninth Brother have free time to come to the city today?”","“I came specifically looking for you. I hadn’t expected to hear as soon as I entered the city that you were caught up in something.”","“Does Ninth Brother have some lucrative business for finding me?” In Tang Mingrui’s eyes, if Mo Jiuye was finding him, it must be because there was some new business to collaborate on.","He had originally planned to go to Xi Ling Village today to strike it rich with the Mo family’s watermelon business. It was now the right time for the Mo family’s watermelons to ripen.","If he went and confirmed the watermelons were ripe, he would immediately arrange transportation into the city.","It was known that the Tang family had always believed watermelons were more delicious than cantaloupes. Especially in this hot summer weather, taking a bite of a nice cold watermelon was simply too refreshing.","Mo Jiuye found it somewhat amusing that the Tang brothers really could only think about business. Even caught up in a government case, the first thought in their minds was still profit.","Since the other party did not mind, he had no reservations about proposing his ideas at this time either.","“Indeed, I have a business deal I wanted to partner with Brother Tang on.”","Speaking, Mo Jiuye took out the several gold and silver accessories made with molds from his bosom last night with his wife.","Tang Mingrui was someone who had seen fine goods before. With just a glance, he could see the intricate quality of the workmanship of the accessories.","Especially that pendant whose form he could not discern. The patterns were so finely carved it seemed lifelike.","And that small ring that should have been quite nondescript. Its shine was dazzling, quite different from the kind sold in the city’s jewelry shops.","He could hardly tear his gaze from the exquisite patterns.","“Ninth Brother, where did you buy these gold and silver accessories from? Da Shun’s jewelry stores definitely don’t have such finely-crafted goods.”","In his impatience to know what kind of new business Mo Jiuye wanted to partner on, Tang Mingrui had not even thought more deeply about these intricate accessories at all.","“Ninth Sister is truly fortunate to have met such a considerate husband as Ninth Brother. Ninth Brother must have gone through great effort to obtain these accessories, right?”","In Tang Mingrui’s mind, Ninth Brother doted on his wife.","From the profits of their recent joint ventures that had been split fifty-fifty, he knew very clearly just how much the other party had earned.","It must be that Ninth Brother had excess silver and bought some accessories for his wife.","Mo Jiuye already knew Tang Mingrui’s reaction to seeing these accessories would be like this.","He was in no rush to put the accessories away.","“I wonder if Brother Tang might be interested in the jewelry accessory business?”","Upon hearing this statement, Tang Mingrui froze for a brief moment before revealing an expression of pleasant surprise.","“Does Ninth Brother mean you can provide accessories of this quality to me?” Tang Mingrui pointed at the accessories, eyes shining, having already forgotten the gloom from earlier.","It was known that Da Shun’s most lucrative businesses were the jewelry stores and money houses. If he hadn’t been unable to find a suitable supplier, he would have opened a proper jewelry store long ago.","Looking at the accessories with special intricacy before him, he already envisioned endless silver pouring towards him.","Tang Mingrui grabbed Mo Jiuye’s arm. “Let’s go, Ninth Brother, find a tea house and discuss properly!”","Mo Jiuye had not come over this time intending to discuss cooperation details with Tang Mingrui. His main purpose was to understand if Tang Mingrui had any intention of partnering up.","As for details of cooperation, that would still have to be left for his wife at home to discuss. After all, his wife was more knowledgeable in such matters than him.","Moreover, they had only made samples of several accessories currently. They were still quite far off from being able to open a store."]},{"number":432,"title":"Chapter 432: Jing Xian Lou","paragraphs":["Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran's original plan was that he would come to the city to inquire about Tang Mingrui's intentions. If the other party was willing to cooperate, Mo Jiuye would go to the dental clinic in the city to buy several suitable people.","He Zhiran's soul came from the modern times and did not support such human trafficking in ancient times.","But after all, she had come and could no longer go back. Following local customs was inevitable.","Using molds to make jewelry was a secret and it was impossible to casually find a few craftsmen to do it.","In order to prevent such secrets from being spread, the best way was to buy people.","In Da Shun, selling personal bonds was equivalent to the lives of those people. Their lives were in the hands of the master. Unless something unexpected happened, they would not betray the family.","Mo Jiuye was not in a hurry, but Tang Mingrui did not want to wait long.","Seeing that Mo Jiuye still did not respond, he said anxiously:","\"Brother Jiu, I know the price of such jewelry must be higher. You are not doing business with me for the first time. Please trust me that I can definitely create the highest profit from this kind of jewelry.\"","Mo Jiuye knew Tang Mingrui was enthusiastic about doing business, but he had never seen him so anxious before, which made him couldn’t help laughing.","\"There are only so many pieces of jewelry I have shown you for now. I came here this time to ask about your willingness to cooperate. Also, the watermelons at my home have partially ripened and can be harvested now.\"","Hearing Mo Jiuye's words, Tang Mingrui was somewhat disappointed at first, and then became excited again.","As he had expected, the watermelons were ripe. He and his family could not only eat the delicious and refreshing watermelons, but also make a lot of money.","\"That's great, Brother Jiu. I will arrange for someone to transport the watermelons immediately.\"","As for his inability to leave Yuncheng, it had been thrown to the back of his mind for now.","Mo Jiuye also believed in Tang Mingrui's ability. Even if he did not leave Yuncheng, he had a way to sell the watermelons.","He had achieved his goal of finding Tang Mingrui. Before they parted, he had to ask:","\"Brother Tang, have you encountered anything strange recently while doing business, or has anyone suspicious appeared?\"","Mo Jiuye asked this for a reason.","He had just listened to the entire trial process in the court.","He guessed that someone must have instigated Wang Lin, but that person was definitely not Chen Wu.","Also, he observed Wang Lin had been avoiding eye contact all the time, especially after Tang Mingrui appeared, it became more serious.","All these little actions of his could explain that there was something big going on in this matter.","And Chen Wu was just a pawn being used. He only knew less than Wang Lin.","In addition, there was another possibility that Wang Lin had some handle that had fallen into someone else's hands, so he had no choice but to do this.","Besides, people don't kill like this in the street and get caught by passing government officials!","This was clearly a trap set for Tang Mingrui.","If it wasn't for Meng Huaining's wisdom, Wang Lin and Chen Wu's confessions would have been enough to convict him of hiring someone to commit murder.","When asked, Tang Mingrui's previous excitement disappeared in a flash. He immediately fell into deep thought, recalling what had happened recently.","After pondering for a long time, Tang Mingrui spoke up:","\"After taking away those little gangsters from Xiling Village last time, in order to teach them a lesson, I directly sent them to the state government yamen and gave some benefits to Prefect.","The prefect had each of those little gangsters severely beaten twenty times, and then fined them some silver before letting them leave.","Since then, I have rarely seen those people wandering on the streets, and it has been much quieter.","Until five days ago, two restaurants named Jingxian Building opened on the two main streets of the state government. That gang leader who had not shown his face for a long time appeared with several of his men.\"","Hearing this, Mo Jiuye interjected, \"Did you say the restaurant was called Jingxian Building?\"","\"That's right, Jingxian Building. As far as I know, Jingxian Building has many branches in Da Shun dynasty and belongs to a high-end consumer restaurant. Ordinary common people simply cannot afford to eat there.","Moreover, Jingxian Building's branches are all located in prosperous cities. Even as a state capital, I'm afraid this place does not meet its criteria for opening a branch.\" Tang Mingrui continued to explain.","Although Tang Mingrui knew about Jingxian Building, he had never thought that such a big restaurant would open in the northwest, let alone know who the real boss behind it was.","However, judging from his experience in business, the person who could open such a luxurious restaurant and had businesses all over the place must have a background. He just didn’t know what kind of background the boss had and what status he was.","Tang Mingrui didn't know, but Mo Jiuye did.","\"The boss behind Jingxian Building is a collateral branch of the maternal family of the current queen. The father of the queen is Left Prime Minister Xue Qing of the current dynasty. In addition, she also has several brothers serving as officials in the imperial court.","It can be said that the queen's maternal family is a huge family in Da Shun.","Such a family not only needs people in power, but also huge financial resources behind it.","The source of the Xue family's finances is supported by the Jingxian boss, Xue Jinchuan.\"","This was not a secret among the aristocratic circles in the imperial capital, especially when Nan Qi fought fiercely with Nan Heng in the past. They would investigate their opponent's background and resources clearly.","Back then, he was as close as brothers with Nan Qi, so Nan Qi would definitely mention it to him after finding out about something like this.","The reason why the Xue family only had a catering business to support their finances was because Jingxian Building had four specialties.","The first specialty - Lion's Head.","The second specialty - Roast Duck.","The third specialty - Red Braised Pork.","The fourth specialty - Steamed Pomfret.","Anyone who had tasted these four dishes would praise them endlessly. The roast duck was crispy on the outside and tender on the inside, and oozed rich oil with every bite.","Although some people could imitate the Lion’s Head and Red Braised Pork, they couldn’t produce the palatable taste of Jingxian’s.","The Steamed Pomfret was even more highly acclaimed.","It should be known that with the lack of seasonings in ancient times, it was not easy to handle the fishy smell well.","But this steamed pomfret was cooked just right, with no fishy smell at all, and tasted particularly delicious when eating.","Therefore, no matter where Jingxian Building opened, it would be sought after by the nobles.","Speaking of these four dishes, Mo Jiuye had tasted them when he was in the imperial capital.","If he hadn't eaten the delicious dishes made by his wife, he might have thought it was sublime cuisine.","But Mo Jiuye, who had tasted many different delicacies, no longer valued Jingxian's four specialties.","Let alone Renren, even with his current cooking skills and his wife's unique seasonings from her space, the dishes produced would definitely overwhelm Jingxian's.","Moreover, Jingxian's dishes were expensive, only making money from the rich. Because the price of each dish there was beyond what ordinary commoners could afford.","That is to say, Jingxian only did business with the rich. It was not that there were no rich people in the northwest, but compared with other regions, there were far fewer."]},{"number":433,"title":"Chapter 433: Do you Have a Family","paragraphs":["Xue Jinchuan opened two restaurants in this place, which obviously could not earn much money in the eyes of observant people. Therefore, this could only mean that the Xue family had some purpose.","Logically speaking, the death or disappearance of Nan Heng in Dashun was no longer a secret, and if it were not for the Empress and Prime Minister Xue Qing that the Xue family still had, they would probably not be far from decline.","Especially the Empress, with Nan Heng dead, she no longer had the bargaining chip to seize power, and at this time the Xue family still arranged Xue Jinchuan to come to the northwest to open restaurants. Mo Jiuye had to think about his own family.","Not only did Mo Jiuye realize this, but after listening to his words, Tang Mingrui also had to consider things from this perspective.","After all, he had been in contact with the Mo family for a long time and understood some things.","\"Ninth Brother, could it be that the people from Jingxian Building are making trouble?","They must have come to the northwest to prepare in advance when they opened restaurants here, and they would have inquired about each other among their peers.","I'm also in the restaurant business, Boss Jin could investigate my cooperation with the Mo family, so it's not difficult for Jingxian Building to find out too.","And the one who impersonated Boss Tang to hire a killer to commit murder is from Jingxian Building. The purpose is to block the Mo family's income.\"","He knew the Mo family's long-term income came only from selling dolls and cold rabbit meat.","Tang Mingrui's words conveyed what Mo Jiuye was thinking.","It's just that he knew a little more than Tang Mingrui.","The Empress was shrewd, and his father Xue Qing was able to take the position of Prime Minister. He had a lot of thoughts.","The bizarre disappearance of Nan Heng upstream of the Salt Lake happened to coincide with their exile there.","Although no one knew at that time that they were exiled there, after such a long investigation, Peng Wang had already returned to the capital with the escort officer for a long time.","When there were many people talking, it was hard to guarantee that they would not ask some useful clues from them. It was just that there was no conclusive evidence.","Jingxian Building opened in the northwest, presumably it was the Xue family looking for clues about Nan Heng, or they had already guessed something and wanted to avenge Nan Heng, which was also possible.","Anyway, no matter what the reason was, the opening of Jingxian Building in the northwest was something that Mo Jiuye had to take seriously.","Especially since the return of all the Mo men was no longer a secret in Xi Ling Village, interested people only need to inquire a little to understand the general idea.","According to Tang Mingrui, Jingxian Building had opened in the prefecture for a few days. They must have started acting.","On the one hand, they framed Tang Mingrui to cut off the Mo family's source of income. On the other hand, they sent people to Xi Ling Village to investigate the Mo family’s news.","Regarding this, Mo Jiuye was not worried at all. After all, things like this would come sooner or later.","Even if it was not the maternal family of the Empress, there would be others.","In short, if the Mo family wanted to live a peaceful life in the northwest in the future, it would probably not be too easy.","Fortunately, several elder brothers had already made many bombs. They just waited for the Seventh Elder Brother to bring those subordinates from the south to come back and organize the Mo Family's own army.","By then, he didn't mind a doomed struggle with those who didn't want the Mo family to live a peaceful life.","Of course, now that the Mo family had reunited, and he was about to become the father of two children, it was impossible for him to take risks with his life.","This was just a bottom line for Mo Jiuye. As long as those short-sighted people did not provoke his Mo family, he would rather spend his whole life farming and living a regular life.","To verify whether his analysis was correct, Mo Jiuye said a few words to Tang Mingrui and then went back to the yamen.","Tang Mingrui was anxious about the watermelon business and did not return home immediately. Instead, he called several cars and went to Xi Ling Village.","Anyway, Meng Huaining only asked him not to leave Yun City, and Xi Ling Village was also within the scope of Yun City, so it was not against the order for him to go there in person.","He didn’t need to worry about selling watermelons either. He had already paved the way when he first sold cantaloupes. As long as he set a price and let his men sell them, it would be fine.","What Mo Jiuye was thinking about was that in order to find a breakthrough in this matter, first Wang Lin had to tell the truth, and second, he wanted to ask Chen Wu what the person who pretended to be Boss Tang looked like.","The officers all knew that Mo Jiuye was the uncle of their county magistrate in the future, so his arrival was naturally not hindered.","Mo Jiuye easily arrived at the public hall.","At this time, Wang Lin was being tortured. His hands were clamped by racks, and he screamed in pain.","In Mo Jiuye’s opinion, unless it was a person with special and tough temperament, it would be difficult to grit one’s teeth so hard.","But no matter how he looked at Wang Lin, he did not seem like a person with a particularly strong will.","So there was only one possibility—this Wang Lin must have some handle that others grasped.","To verify his idea, Mo Jiuye came to stand in front of him.","\"Wang Lin, do you have family?\"","Hearing the two words \"family\" instantly changed Wang Lin's expression. The previous painful grimace also became tense and wooden.","Seeing his expression, Mo Jiuye knew he had asked the right thing.","\"Your family is now in my hands. If you still want to conceal anything for that person, not only will you suffer, but your family will not end up well either.","You endure torture yourself, but you still can't die happily. Such pain from being tortured slowly is probably unbearable for ordinary people, right?\"","In the end, Mo Jiuye couldn't help but threaten him.","Meng Huaining and Mo Chuhan didn't know what medicine Mo Jiuye was selling in his gourd, but they both clearly saw the change in Wang Lin's expression and knew that what Mo Jiuye said had worked.","Therefore, the two just maintained a stance of onlookers and let Mo Jiuye take the lead.","Mo Jiuye just wanted to test to see if there was any handle being grasped by others.","The most common one was that family members were being held hostage as a threat.","He followed up aggressively: \"If you really don't care about whether they live or die, I can leave here now.\"","As he spoke, Mo Jiuye had already turned around and made a gesture as if he was going to leave.","Seeing this, Wang Lin became anxious. He dragged his battered body and kowtowed desperately to Mo Jiuye.","\"Sir, please be kind and spare my old mother and daughter. They have never done anything to harm others or break the law. As long as you let them go, I will tell you everything I know.\""]},{"number":434,"title":"Chapter 434: I'll spare your mother and daughter.","paragraphs":["Mo Jiuye stopped abruptly and turned to look at him.","\"As long as you tell the truth, I will spare your old mother and daughter.\"","\"Three days ago, Chen Wu found me and paid me two hundred taels of silver to teach Gold Boss a lesson. He said that I had been working under Second Master for a short time and Gold Boss did not recognize me, so I was the most suitable person for this task.","After completing the task, he would give me two hundred taels of silver to let my old mother and daughter escape far away.","At that time, I thought that two hundred taels of silver was not a small sum. With this money, I could take them to other places to buy property and live the life of a rich man.","On the day I was about to take action, when I returned home, I found that my old mother and young daughter had disappeared. There was a note left on the table. I had attended a private school for two years when I was young, so I could recognize some words.","The note said that if I wanted my old mother and daughter to live, I had to kill Gold Boss before the end of the day and frame Chen Wu.","In addition, after killing, I had to draw the attention of the officials. If I did not follow the requirements on the note, they would be ready to collect the corpses of my old mother and daughter early tomorrow morning...\"","As he spoke, Wang Lin was already crying bitterly. He kowtowed to Mo Jiuye again.","\"Sir, I did this because I was forced to. Now I have told you everything. I just beg you to spare my old mother and young daughter.\"","Wang Lin spoke in tears. Meng Huaining and Mo Jiuye observed his expression and actions carefully.","They could determine that Wang Lin was probably not lying.","If he was not lying and just went to do things after seeing the note, it would be impossible to find out the person behind the scenes from his mouth.","Mo Jiuye did not pay attention to Wang Lin’s plea. After all, his old mother and daughter were not in his own hands. He had just lied to him earlier.","Therefore, he turned to look at Meng Huaining. Aside from his relationship with Meng Huaining, his actions in the court earlier were indeed a bit presumptuous. Moreover, Meng Huaining was not a fool. Now that he had asked to this point, if Mo Jiuye still did not know what to do next, he might as well stop being the county magistrate.","Meng Huaining nodded slightly to Mo Jiuye and ordered: \"Come, bring Chen Wu here.\"","Chen Wu was escorted back into the court again.","\"Chen Wu, this official asks you, what did the person who gave you five hundred taels of silver to pretend to be Boss Tang look like? Tell me in detail.\"","Chen Wu was more honest than Wang Lin. Besides, he had always believed that he did not kill anyone himself, so the problem was not too serious. Seeing the county magistrate inquire, he recounted in detail what he saw.","\"The person who gave me five hundred taels of silver was about the same age as the real Boss Tang just now, both around twenty years old.","Only he was a little fatter than Boss Tang, wearing a vermilion purple robe, slightly darker skin, thick eyebrows and big eyes, and his accent was a bit like people from Beijing.","Oh yes, after he gave me the silver bill, he left. Judging from his back view when he walked away, he walked with a bit of a limp, but it was not easy to notice if you did not look carefully.\"","After a pause, as if remembering something else, Chen Wu added: \"When that fake Boss Tang gave me the silver bill, he specifically told me to find someone I don't know to do this.","Among Second Master’s men, Wang Lin had arrived the latest, and he often used family affairs as an excuse not to report to Second Master. So I thought it would be most suitable to let him do this.\"","So far, these were the only clues they could get from these two people.","If this matter was really related to the Xue family, they had gone around such a big circle to frame Tang Mingrui in order to indirectly cut off the Mo family's income. The purpose was nothing more than not wanting people to know that they were making trouble.","This was Mo Jiuye’s own analysis and speculation. Even if it was really done by Xue Jinchuan, evidence had to be found.","Although Mo Chuhan was a bit straightforward, he was not completely ignorant.","When he heard Mo Jiuye mention Jingxian Building, he guessed what was going on.","\"Ninth brother, have you discovered something?\"","\"Well, I just heard Brother Tang say that the prefecture has opened two Jingxian Buildings.\"","Mo Chuhan was a little surprised. \"Jingxian Building? Isn't that Xue's property?\"","\"Yes, I suspect that the Xue family did not have a simple purpose in coming to the northwest to open Jingxian Buildings.\" Mo Jiuye felt it necessary to explain things clearly to his brother.","Mo Chuhan had an impatient temper. He turned to Meng Huaining and said, \"Sir, let me take some time off. I want to go to the prefecture.\"","Meng Huaining also heard Mo Jiuye mention Jingxian Building earlier.","Although he did not know what Jingxian Building was and what the Xue family Mo Jiuye mentioned was about, seeing the tight expressions on the Mo brothers, he knew that the matter might be related to them.","\"Eighth Brother, go ahead with your business. You don't need to worry about the yamen these days.\"","With Meng Huaining’s words, Mo Chuhan left with Mo Jiuye without hesitation.","After leaving the court, Mo Chuhan did not forget to change out of his catcher uniform.","Mo Jiuye did have the idea to go to Jingxian Building to investigate. The two brothers raced to the prefecture on fast horses.","Unlike Mo Chuhan, Mo Jiuye was on the list of people exiled by Emperor Wu's edict, so according to the law he was not allowed to leave Yun City.","Fortunately, Meng Huaining was his future brother-in-law. Those officials also knew this fact. Even if he openly left Yun City, those people would only turn a blind eye.","The two brothers rode fast horses and arrived at the prefecture right at noon.","In principle, this was when the restaurants were the busiest. However, there were barely any customers in this Jingxian Building in front of them.","The front door was open with two people standing at the entrance.","On the surface, they were dressed as waiters, standing at the door to solicit customers.","On closer inspection, both of these people were burly. One was even taller than the Mo brothers.","The two stood ramrod straight at the door. Just then, two customers walked in.","The waiters should have enthusiastically come forward to greet them and take them to their seats.","However, these two did not move at all and continued standing there. They looked more like guards than waiters.","In addition, as the brothers observed the interior of Jingxian Building from outside, the furnishings were also very different from Jingxian Buildings in other cities.","The Jingxian Buildings in other cities were decorated magnificently. Even the stone steps at the entrance were made of white marble.","The Jingxian Building here not only lacked luxurious decorations, but even the tables and chairs looked old.","Just as the brothers were pondering the reason, they suddenly heard an unhappy shout from a customer inside the hall.","\"Is this what you call Lion's Head worth five taels of silver a plate? There were so many bones in it and the taste was very ordinary too. This is a black shop.","Get your boss out here and refund my money, or else...\"","Before the customer could finish speaking, the brothers suddenly saw a man fall to the ground in front of them.","It was the customer who had asked to see the boss for a refund just now.","A burly waiter stood behind him with his hands behind his back, yelling at the customer.","\"I see you're here just to cause trouble. Jingxian Building is known nationally as a big restaurant. You don't have any taste yourself yet you dare say Jingxian Building’s food is no good. Who gave you the nerve to cause trouble here?\""]},{"number":435,"title":"Chapter 435: How is it private","paragraphs":["Originally, two burly men were standing at the entrance, and they leaned forward slightly, clearly poised to take action if that customer dared to say anything more.","Seeing their stance, the customer did cower, realizing that the few people in front of him were not those he could afford to provoke. With effort, he got up, dusted himself off, and left dispiritedly.","Then those helpers swiftly returned to their original positions.","Mo Jiuye and Mo Chuhan exchanged a glance.","\"Eighth brother, let's go check out another Jingxian Building.\"","Mo Chuhan nodded, and the two leapt onto their horses and left.","The other Jingxian Building was slightly better, but only in the attitude of the helpers. The decor was almost identical to the first one they saw.","There were similarly few customers inside, and judging from their expressions as they ate, they did not seem very happy.","Mo Jiuye beckoned Mo Chuhan, \"Eighth brother, let's go in and sit for a bit.\"","The two brothers walked into the lobby, and it was a long while before a helper came to greet them.","Mo Jiuye chose a seat by the window and casually ordered two dishes.","As martial artists, their hearing was naturally sharp.","While the brothers were waiting for their food, they heard over a dozen synchronized footsteps coming from the direction of the back kitchen.","Mo Jiuye could even judge that these footsteps belonged to martial artists.","In order not to stir up trouble prematurely, the brothers showed no visible reaction and continued waiting for their dishes as if nothing had happened.","Nonetheless, they kept listening intently to the sounds coming from the back.","When the helpers brought out their dishes, the footsteps had gradually faded away.","Having lost their appetite, the brothers imitated the other customers by taking a couple bites and feigning dissatisfaction before asking for the bill and leaving.","Once outside, they headed straight for the backyard of Jingxian Building, as that was where the kitchen was located and also the direction from where those earlier sounds came.","This property was a stand-alone building that opened onto the main street, so its facade could be considered one of the courtyard walls.","The other three sides were surrounded by 10-foot high enclosing walls, with a side door on the west side.","As soon as the brothers circled around to the west side of the courtyard, a man dressed like those helpers came up to block their way.","\"This is private property. Loiterers please go around.\"","Mo Jiuye deliberately played dumb.","\"But this is clearly an alley. How has it become private property? We want to pass through here. So you're telling us we have to take a detour?\"","Seeing his words had no effect, that man was visibly impatient.","\"I already told you this is Jingxian Building territory. Now scram!\"","The more he talked like that, the more determined the brothers were to get to the bottom of this.","Mo Chuhan had already walked around to the front of Mo Jiuye and strode purposefully toward the inside of the alley.","\"I insist on passing through here. What can you do about it?\"","As they spoke, the brothers had already advanced a dozen or so steps, now barely an arm's length away from that helper who was trying to drive them away.","Seeing the two were impervious to persuasion, that helper instantly lost his temper.","\"I'm telling you to get the hell out of here! This isn't a place you should be. Take one more step forward and don't blame me for getting rough with you.\"","Within two sentences, that helper had revealed his true nature.","As he spoke, from out of nowhere he pulled out a short leather whip and pointed at the brothers, yelling","\"Leave this instant!\"","Mo Chuhan had always had a fiery temper. Especially when dealing with people possibly opposed to his family, how could he possibly compromise?","Before he even had a chance to react, three or four men dressed like that helper suddenly burst out from behind the courtyard gate, surrounding the brothers.","Without further ado, they were poised to attack.","The brothers were even faster to react than them. As those men swung their fists at them, Mo Jiuye and Mo Chuhan almost simultaneously struck back.","The brothers' four hands securely caught the four fists swinging their way.","Four cracking sounds ensued as the wrists of those four helpers were snapped.","Perhaps those four had underestimated them, seeing what looked like ordinary commoners before them. They thought intimidation alone would be enough to scare them off. Little did they expect these two men to actually be martial artists, as evidenced by the mere move of breaking their wrists.","If they had been regular people, having their wrists snapped would surely elicit blood-curdling shrieks.","Yet those helpers made no sound. Exchanging glances with each other, they proceeded to use their uninjured hands to pull out daggers from their waists and hold them up against Mo Jiuye and Mo Chuhan.","At the same time, the commotion outside seemed to have also alerted those inside the courtyard. People started jumping out one after another to check things out.","Unlike the helpers, those emerging from the courtyard were dressed uniformly in grey, looking more like guards of wealthy households.","Gripping obvious broadswords, they raised their weapons towards Mo Jiuye and Mo Chuhan as soon as they grasped the situation.","The brothers had witnessed such a spectacle countless times and were not the least bit intimidated.","In a flash, those broadswords hacked at them in unison.","Unhurried, Mo Jiuye and Mo Chuhan dodged backwards before leaping behind that group of people. Within the blink of an eye and a few somersaults, they had kicked the entire group to the ground.","Seeing this, the helper who had ordered them to leave earlier yelled loudly towards the courtyard,","\"Come help! There's troublemakers here!\"","Right after, over ten people jumped out from behind the courtyard wall charging at the brothers in attack.","From their moves, Mo Jiuye and Mo Chuhan instantly recognized that these people's martial arts were no trivial matter and absolutely incomparable to those earlier men with blades.","Still, the Mo brothers defeated them swiftly all the same.","Admittedly, facing such experts made combat not as effortless as imagined.","From their lethal moves, it was evident those men were akin to the deathsworn nurtured by the wealthy and powerful families of the capital.","Moreover, with Jingxian Buildings being a Xue Family property, their ulterior motives in the northwest were only to be expected, including the stationing of deathsworn.","While the brothers were lost in thought, some of those deathsworn they had restrained had already broken the poison pills in their mouths, bleeding from all seven apertures as they died a swift death.","\"This is bad! Quick Eighth Brother, capture them alive!\"","Mo Chuhan also realized instantly. The two dashed forth, each grabbing hold of one deathsworn by the cheeks with the intention of preventing them from crushing the poison pellets.","With perfect coordination, the brothers finally preserved the lives of two deathsworn.","That helper who had been so arrogant with them earlier was now scared stiff, continuously shuffling backward.","Those family guards were equally dazed, staring blankly at the brothers, completely at a loss on what to do next.","Mo Chuhan stepped forward nimbly, using their belts to tie up those guards along with the dead deathsworn bodies before chucking the lot out the side door into the courtyard.","After all, this was an alley along the bustling main avenue. Any prolonged activity risked attracting public attention.","While the situation in the backyard of Jingxian Building remained unclear, they certainly couldn't interrogate them openly there and then."]},{"number":436,"title":"Chapter 436: I am the man from Jing Xian Lou","paragraphs":["The two brothers finally entered the backyard of the Jingxian Building and casually closed the yard door behind them.","They were in no hurry to ask those people anything, but looked around instead.","The backyard of a restaurant should basically be used as a warehouse and dormitory for the waiters.","Mo Jiuye scanned around but did not see any warehouse at all.","Without even preparing ingredients, how could this be a restaurant?","Especially for such a famous high-end restaurant like the Jingxian Building, not only were there no prepared ingredients, even the food that was served was so perfunctory, which showed how impure their purpose was in opening this place.","Mo Jiuye only took a rough look around and did not check each room.","Just as he turned around, about to interrogate those people, he suddenly heard a faint sob coming from the woodshed.","Mo Chuhan also heard it.","\"Younger brother, you stay here and watch them. I'll go take a look,\" said Mo Chuhan.","As he opened the door of the woodshed, a pungent stench instantly filled the air. Mo Chuhan instinctively covered his nose and mouth.","The woodshed was very messy inside. What caught their eyes the most were two people, one elderly and one young, lying on the ground.","The stench came from these two. It could be determined that they had been locked up here for some time.","Mo Jiuye had witnessed Wang Lin deceiving the king with a scam, and Mo Chuhan was also present then. Seeing the elderly woman in her fifties and the young girl of seven or eight years old, they should be Wang Lin's old mother and daughter.","Wang Lin had committed murder, but his family were innocent. As a government official, Mo Chuhan had the duty to rescue them.","Moreover, after seeing these two, he also believed that Wang Lin had killed Boss Jin out of desperation, otherwise who would deliberately let the officials discover the body after committing murder?","The two were very weak right now, with dry, cracked lips, clearly due to lack of food over the past days.","Mo Chuhan went to the kitchen.","The kitchen was some distance away from the alley where the fight had occurred. The two chefs inside did not know what was happening outside. With little business in the restaurant, the two chefs were casually chatting.","Seeing a stranger enter, they immediately asked, \"Who are you? Don't wander around in the kitchen.\"","With one glance, Mo Chuhan could tell that they were in the same group as those two waiters.","Therefore, without saying anything further, he went forward to knock them down and truss them up in the backyard. Then he took two bowls of water to Wang Lin's family.","The old woman seemed to have been in poor health already. Her eyes were closed now, not knowing if she had lost consciousness. The young girl's condition was slightly better. The voice from earlier came from her.","People of this era valued propriety between men and women. Although the one lying on the ground was an old woman, Mo Chuhan still did not feel proper to go up and help her. He could only let the young girl drink some water first before finding a way to feed the old woman.","The old woman appeared unconscious but had not completely lost awareness, as she could swallow when the girl fed her water.","After a few sips of water, the old woman finally opened her eyes.","She looked at Mo Chuhan, then tears flowed down as she said weakly, \"Thank you, Young Master, for saving us.\"","As she spoke, it was as if she suddenly recalled something. Her expression became terrified.","\"Young Master, everyone here is vicious. You should leave quickly!\"","She and her granddaughter had been locked up here for several days. Although no one came to torment them, no one gave them a bite of food or a sip of water either.","Moreover, she could hear the sounds outside. These were clearly not proper business people, as she sometimes heard them talk about killing people.","Thinking of this, the old woman was worried that her lifesaver would be endangered and thus reminded him.","Instead of leaving as she said, Mo Chuhan asked, \"What is Wang Lin's relationship to you?\"","Hearing the name, the old woman struggled to sit up.","\"Young Master, do you know my son? Where is he now? Is he still alive?\"","Wang Lin was imprisoned in the county prison for murder, and it was indeed as he said - because his old mother and young daughter were being held hostage, he was forced to kill.","Seeing the feeble state of the old woman, Mo Chuhan worried that telling her the truth would be too much for her to handle. If he really needed to inform her, it would be better to wait until she recovered somewhat.","Mo Chuhan's eyes flickered uneasily for a moment as he stood up.","\"Wang Lin is still alive. You need not worry about him.\"","To prevent further questioning from the old woman, Mo Chuhan chose to leave the woodshed.","Even if not to evade the issue, he still had to go out - there were so many people outside that still needed interrogating.","Although Mo Jiuye did not follow Mo Chuhan into the woodshed, he could hear the conversation inside clearly. Hence when Eighth Brother returned, there was not much he needed to ask.","The two brothers exchanged a look and went up to the waiter who had obstructed them earlier.","The waiter had been beaten up severely by the two brothers and was still wincing in pain.","Mo Jiuye did not show mercy at all. He grabbed the waiter by the collar and lifted him up.","\"Speak, who are you people?\"","The waiter had already been deterred by the brothers' prowess earlier. Knowing he had kicked an iron plate, now being lifted up like a little chick, he was so frightened that he felt half of his soul had departed.","\"I... I'm just a waiter of the Jingxian Building...\"","With how these people acted, Mo Jiuye would have to be a fool to believe his nonsense.","Before the waiter could react, Mo Jiuye had already broken his other wrist.","The agony almost caused the waiter to faint, but Mo Jiuye would certainly not give him that chance.","He released the waiter's collar and grabbed his hair instead, forcing him awake.","The waiter had completely lost his previous bluster in the alley. He tearfully pleaded for mercy.","\"Sir, please stop... I'm indeed from the Jingxian Building, but not an ordinary waiter... I'm a specially trained fighter...\"","It would not surprise the Mo brothers one bit that the Jingxian Building had specially trained fighters.","After all, such a big restaurant would need some brawny men to maintain order and prevent troublemakers.","But it was questionable for a fighter to be acting as a waiter.","Furthermore, from this person's words, Mo Jiuye could ascertain that the other waiter dressed identical to him and those attendants in guard uniforms were all the restaurant's fighters.","For the Jingxian Building to open two branches in such a desolate location, and have no customers at all, was already suspicious enough. Add the fact that these fighters were acting as waiters - it showed how impure the purpose was for them to open a restaurant here.","Mo Jiuye continued his interrogation: \"Why did the Jingxian Building open two branches in such a poor place like Northwest China? Why make you fighters act as waiters? Also, where is your manager?\"","With such an extensive network laid out by the Xue family in Northwest China, it was impossible they only had a few fighters and desperados stationed here. Even if the head of the family Xue Jinchuan did not come personally, he would have sent a capable subordinate to oversee things here."]},{"number":437,"title":"Chapter 437: I'll only make you miserable.","paragraphs":["Mo Jiuye shook his head vigorously: \"I'm just here to run this restaurant, I've never seen any steward.\"","In order to prove that he was not lying, the buddy added: \"Even the two cooks were brought in by our brothers, if you don't believe me you can go ask them.\"","Mo Jiuye did not go to ask those two cooks, but pointed in the direction of the woodshed and asked: \"Were that old man and child caught by you?\"","The buddy shook his head again, then looked at the two dead men who had been removed from the poison sacs in their mouths by the Mo brothers.","\"It was them...they put those people there.\"","\"Initially there were only two of them who brought the people here and then left. It wasn't until today that they reappeared with many more people.\"","The other thugs, afraid that they would also suffer physically, hurried to help prove it.","\"Sir, what he said is true...\"","Mo Jiuye did not pay any attention to those people, but walked towards the two dead men.","It had to be said that the dead men were trained rigorously and did not fear life and death.","Seeing Mo Jiuye approaching, the two showed no sign of fear on their faces. Instead, they continued to maintain eye contact with Mo Jiuye.","Mo Jiuye knew clearly that it would not be easy to get any useful information from these two men. He regretted not bringing some of the itching powder made by his wife when he went out.","That stuff was most suitable for interrogation. Even the toughest mouths could be pried open with it.","But now he didn’t have any itching powder on hand. He could only try the usual methods first.","Mo Chuhan saw that his ninth brother had come to the two dead men but had not moved. He took out a dagger from his waist and walked over. \"Ninth brother, let me do it.\"","As he spoke, Mo Chuhan’s dagger had already cut off one of the dead man's ears.","The dead man didn't even react before he felt a cool sensation where his ear used to be, followed quickly by a piercing pain.","Looking at the ground in front of him, his ear was lying quietly there.","\"Just kill me, I won't say anything.\"","His words had just fallen when Mo Chuhan's dagger moved again, cutting off his other ear, then placing the knife tip on his nose bridge.","\"I want to know what you haven't said yet. I won't let you die, I will only let you live painfully.\"","Mo Chuhan also knew the minds of these dead men. Although they were fearless of life and death, they did not want to be tortured. Therefore, the dead men would carry poison sacs in their mouths. In order to protect their master’s secrets and prevent themselves from being tortured, they would choose to break the poison sacs and commit suicide at the first opportunity.","It was unlucky that today they met the Mo brothers. They did not even have a chance to break their poison sacs and commit suicide.","Let's not talk about the person involved. The other dead man also saw this scene and was terrified, afraid that he would be the next one to lose his ears.","However, their ideology had always been loyal to their master. Even in the face of torture, it was impossible for them to confess any information.","The dead man with the knife tip against his nose had already resigned himself to death. In order not to continue being tortured, he suddenly raised his head when Mo Chuhan was not paying attention and thrust his body forward with great force.","His throat was aligned directly with the knife tip.","Mo Chuhan realized it was too late to dodge. The dagger pierced the dead man’s throat and he died instantly.","There were only two people left alive that could provide some information, and one of them died so easily. As for the one left, neither brother dared to be careless, otherwise their lead could be cut off entirely.","To be safe, Mo Jiuye did not dare to be negligent again.","Especially when trying to get useful information out of this kind of fearless dead man, it was not a simple matter.","\"Eighth brother, I saw a dilapidated civilian house nearby just now. Take him there and wait for me. I’ll take care of things here and then meet up with you.\"","Mo Chuhan had also seen the dilapidated house. From the outside it looked pitch black, probably because water damage made it temporarily uninhabitable.","\"Okay, I’ll take him over now.\"","He had just accidentally let a dead man die so easily. This time Mo Chuhan didn’t dare to be careless at all.","He also did not intend to interrogate anymore. As long as he could keep this man alive, there was still hope of getting some useful information out of him.","\"Ninth brother, don't worry, I guarantee I won't let him die again this time.\"","It was really his fault that he had let a live source die just like that.","After Mo Chuhan finished speaking, he picked up the dead man and leapt high into the air.","After all, it was broad daylight. Carrying a live person around would definitely draw attention, so he had to take the high road to avoid people.","Watching his older brother's figure disappear, Mo Jiuye came to the group again.","According to reason, after finding Wang Lin's family in the woodshed, there was no doubt that Boss Jin's death was absolutely related to this gang.","If this matter did not involve the Mo Family, Mo Jiuye would have undoubtedly brought these people to the government for processing.","But he considered that those who could deal with the Mo Family would not be ordinary people. The prefectural magistrate in Yun City was newly appointed after their arrival in Yun City, and Mo Jiuye was unfamiliar with his character and background.","Therefore, Mo Jiuye felt that turning these people over to the magistrate's office was not feasible. Besides, it was not until he and Eighth Brother arrived at the second Jingxian Building that they discovered so many hints. As for whether the situation was the same in the first Jingxian Building, that was still unknown.","The best approach would be for Meng Huaining to take these people away and conduct the interrogation personally.","Moreover, it was reasonable for Meng Huaining to handle this case. After all, he had already received the official document issued by the prefectural magistrate, instructing him to handle the matter. Even if the officials from Yun City came to the prefecture to arrest people, the prefect would not say anything once he knew.","Unfortunately, both he and Eighth Brother had unavoidable reasons to be absent at the moment, which put Mo Jiuye in an awkward situation.","They had finally discovered some clues and captured these people, so there was no reason to quit halfway.","Thinking of these things, Mo Jiuye paced around the yard.","On the surface he was wandering around the yard, but he was actually looking for a place to temporarily hide these people.","As long as he was given a few hours to investigate the inside story of the other Jingxian Building, then he would return to Yun City at the fastest speed to notify Meng Huaining to collect the people.","The elderly grandmother and little granddaughter in the woodshed were feeling a little better after drinking the water Mo Chuhan had given them.","The old woman struggled to stand up, supported by her little granddaughter as they left the woodshed.","Mo Jiuye turned his head when he heard the sound. Seeing that although the old woman was weak, she was not completely immobile. An idea suddenly came to his mind.","\"Auntie, you still remember how you were brought here right?\"","The Mo brothers had not intended to hide things from the old woman when interrogating those people just now. After all, she was also a victim and must harbor immense hatred towards them."]},{"number":438,"title":"Chapter 438: This is what nine brothers and sisters told me to give you.","paragraphs":["The facts were indeed as Mo Jiuye had thought.","The old woman did not care about the identities of these people. She only hated them.","It was those family servants who had grabbed her and her little granddaughter and brought them here, not giving them a sip of water or a bite of food for several days, trying to starve the two of them alive.","\"Of course I remember it was these people who grabbed me and my little granddaughter and brought us here. I'm going to report to the officials.\"","Mo Jiuye had also intended to let the old woman report to the officials. As for the details of her and her little granddaughter being grabbed, he had no time to ask more at the moment.","He took out a piece of broken silver from his arms and gave it to the old woman.","\"Auntie, take this silver. Go out and hire a carriage to rush to Yun City and report to the officials there, because Magistrate Mo has already handed over this case to the Yun City Chief for trial.\"","Mo Jiuye did not explain much more, as long as the old woman could see Meng Huaining and make clear her identity and experience, with Meng Huaining's wisdom, he would definitely send someone to the prefecture to catch people at the first moment.","That way, he wouldn't have to worry about these people escaping after he left.","He wanted to find out more, and it was enough to have the dead warrior taken away by Eighth Brother.","The old woman also had insight. She could feel that the other party did not intend to explain more. Moreover, she was scared to death when she saw those sinister thugs.","After thanking Mo Jiuye profusely, the old woman cautiously led her little granddaughter away together.","Mo Jiuye was in a hurry to meet up with Eighth Brother, and he also wanted to check out the interior of the first Jingxian Building. He couldn't take his eyes off these people in front of him either.","Just as he was at a loss for a good strategy, several people jumped over the wall into the yard.","Mo Jiuye turned his head vigilantly and saw the arrivals. His heart suddenly relaxed.","\"Sixth elder brother, Liang Hao, you guys came just in time. Leave two people here to keep an eye on them, let's go to Eighth Brother.\"","Sixth elder brother, Liang Hao and the other five didn't ask any questions. They voluntarily stayed behind two people and all the rest followed Mo Jiuye quickly to the first Jingxian Building.","The reason he did not interrogate the dead warrior first was that he was worried that if the wind leaked here, it would startle the people behind the scenes. Therefore, he decided to take care of the other Jingxian Building first before anything else.","On the way, Mo Jiuye asked,","\"Sixth elder brother, how did you guys get here?\"","\"Brother Tang went to Xiling Village and saw Ninth Younger Sister-in-Law. He explained the situation in Yun City. Ninth Younger Sister-in-Law guessed that you might come to the prefecture to investigate Jingxian Building, so she asked us to come over and help.","We went to see Brother Meng first. We were told that you and Eighth Younger Brother had already rushed to the prefecture. To save time, we used our lightness martial arts and chased you all the way here.","When we arrived at the prefecture, we kept asking around about Jingxian Building until we found something wrong when we reached the front door. Then we searched towards the backyard and found you here.\"","After listening to Sixth elder brother's explanation, Mo Jiuye felt warmth in his heart.","His wife was thoughtful and could think of things ahead of time.","It was also fortunate that she sent Sixth elder brother and his men to help, otherwise it would be just him and Eighth Younger Brother here, and they really couldn't handle it alone.","Then, Sixth elder brother took out several small paper packs from his arms and handed them to Mo Jiuye.","\"Ninth Younger Sister-in-Law asked me to give these to you, saying you might need them.\"","Seeing those small paper packs, Mo Jiuye suddenly had the confidence to interrogate the dead warrior.","As they spoke, the group had arrived at the other Jingxian Building.","He saw that the two thugs dressed as waiters were still standing at the door, so he knew that the incident at the other Jingxian Building had not reached here yet.","With experience, Mo Jiuye did not enter through the front door this time either, but led everyone around to the backyard instead.","The layout of this Jingxian Building was somewhat different from the previous one. The backyard was also surrounded by walls, but the door was on the north side, a pure back door.","Mo Jiuye leapt onto the top of the wall and observed the inside.","The backyard here was more tidy, but there was no one moving around, so Mo Jiuye couldn't determine the specific situation for the time being.","Sixth elder brother and his men followed closely behind and jumped onto the courtyard wall, asking softly, \"Ninth Younger Brother, should we go in and take a look?\"","Just as Mo Jiuye was about to respond, he saw the kitchen door open.","A young master who looked to be in his early twenties walked out from inside.","Mo Jiuye recalled what Chen Wu had said about the fake Boss Tang, who was fatter than Tang Mingrui, wearing a purple robe, slightly darker skin, thick eyebrows and big eyes...","These matched perfectly. And upon closer look, this person did walk with a limp.","Not only that, Mo Jiuye could also see that this person walked very lightly, clearly a martial artist.","He didn't dare to underestimate him at all, and appeared in front of the man in the fastest speed, immediately attacking to try to subdue him.","As Mo Jiuye had guessed, the man was a martial artist with a very quick reaction.","Seeing his opponent's hand was about to grab his throat, the man dodged back a few meters quickly. If there hadn't been an obstruction behind him, he would probably have dodged even farther.","At the same time, Sixth elder brother and his men who were observing also rushed forward, surrounding the man in purple together.","Unable to defeat the enemy in one move, Mo Jiuye was already prepared to fight him if he called for help.","Unexpectedly, the man in purple had no intention of calling for reinforcements at all. Instead, he kept looking up and down at Mo Jiuye and the others.","\"Who exactly are you people? Why are you here to cause me trouble?\"","Including Mo Jiuye, none of them wanted to talk to him.","Especially Mo Jiuye, who knew this man was the key to the case and an important lead to finding out why Jingxian Building opened shops in the northwest.","Therefore, before the man in purple could make his next move, Mo Jiuye had already attacked again, intending to capture him.","Seeing this, Sixth elder brother and the others also rushed to attack the man in purple.","Although the man in purple was not weak in martial arts, he was still no match for Mo Jiuye, not to mention Mo Jiuye had a lot of help today. In the blink of an eye, Mo Jiuye kicked him to the ground.","Liang Hao came over with some men to hold him down.","To prevent accidents, Mo Jiuye took out the anesthetic his wife had given him and sprinkled it on the man in purple.","Sensing something wrong, the man in purple tried to dodge but it was too late. He immediately lost consciousness.","Seeing that this person could no longer escape, Sixth elder brother searched the entire backyard with his men, but did not find anything unusual or dead warriors like in the other Jingxian Building.","Then, Mo Jiuye asked Sixth elder brother to also take care of those fake waiters in the lobby.","Jingxian Building didn't have a good reputation in the northwest, and the food didn't taste good either. At this moment, there wasn't a single customer in the lobby, which made it convenient for the brothers to take action.","After Sixth elder brother brought those thugs and cooks to the backyard and tied them up tightly, Mo Jiuye sprinkled anesthetics on them again, knocking them unconscious, before throwing them into a carriage in the backyard."]},{"number":439,"title":"Chapter 439: He is the eldest son of our Beijing Xianlou","paragraphs":["Liang Hao was responsible for taking all these people to another Jingxian Building to be detained together, while Mo Jiuye and Sixth Elder Brother took the unconscious man in purple clothes with them to meet Mo Chuhan at that abandoned courtyard.","Mo Jiuye still couldn't confirm whether there were still people from Jingxian Building in the government office. All he could find now was this many. He could only hope to get some useful information soon.","He hoped their purpose here had nothing to do with the Mo Family. It would be best if he was just being paranoid. But if they really came for the Mo Family, he had to take precautions in advance.","When he met up with Eighth Brother, the warrior's eyes immediately fell upon Mo Jiuye and the others carrying the purple-clothed man like a chicken.","Mo Jiuye clearly sensed a fleeting astonishment in the warrior's eyes when he saw the purple-clothed man.","\"Is this your master?\"","In fact, Mo Jiuye didn't know the identity of the purple-clothed man either. He only asked this question to test the waters.","The warrior gritted his teeth, \"I don't know him.\"","\"You don't know him?\" As he spoke, he had already approached the warrior and sprinkled itch powder on him.","The effects of the itch powder took hold quickly. Soon, the warrior began writhing all over.","\"You...what did you give me?\"","This feeling made the warrior very uneasy.","Mo Jiuye stood with his arms crossed, watching him coldly.","\"Let me ask you again, is that man your master or not?\"","\"Just kill me. I won't say anything...\" The warrior was now rolling on the ground, hoping to alleviate the discomfort through friction.","But the more he struggled, the more intense the itchiness became.","This was not Mo Jiuye's first time using itch powder. Minister Si Meng had planned for so long and was much tougher than this warrior, yet even he couldn't withstand the itch powder. This warrior before him was even less worth mentioning.","Sure enough, after struggling for a while, the warrior began begging for mercy.","\"Please...just end it for me.\"","At this point, Mo Jiuye felt the warrior had no reason to lie.","\"Tell me, who exactly is that man?\"","Mo Chuhan had disliked the look of the warrior from the start. Without waiting for Mo Jiuye to speak, he stepped forward and viciously kicked the warrior.","\"Speak. Who is that man? Give me a satisfactory answer and I'll consider ending it quickly for you.\"","No one else could understand the agony of being tormented by itch powder. The warrior now only wanted a quick death.","\"You mean it?\"","\"Of course.\" Mo Chuhan said disdainfully.","\"He is the eldest young master of our Jingxian Building, Xue Fan.\"","Mo Jiuye had assumed the man in purple was just a subordinate cultivated by the Xue family, albeit one of higher status than the thugs and warriors. He didn't expect him to be the eldest young master of Jingxian Building.","Mo Jiuye had heard of Xue Fan from Nan Qi before, but he didn't investigate him extensively and wasn't very familiar with the details. Judging by the sharpness this man had shown in combat earlier, he was likely a master as well.","Unfortunately for Xue Fan, he had the misfortune of running into Mo Jiuye. If he had encountered someone less skilled, perhaps even they wouldn't have been a match for him.","This showed that the Xue family's presence in the northwest under the guise of opening Jingxian Buildings, plus sending a martial arts expert to oversee things, clearly indicated ulterior motives.","Mo Jiuye continued questioning the warrior, \"What exactly is your purpose coming to the northwest?\"","The warrior answered, \"I don't know. The family master only said that after we arrived in the northwest, we were to follow Young Master's arrangements in everything.\"","At this point, Mo Jiuye felt the warrior had no reason to lie.","\"How long have you been in the northwest?\"","\"We came with Young Master, it's been over ten days now.\"","\"What have you been doing these past ten-odd days?\" This was what Mo Jiuye cared about most.","\"We've been following Young Master to set up the shops, then opened two Jingxian Buildings.\"","Mo Jiuye asked, \"Did Xue Fan give you any other tasks to do during this time?\"","The warrior replied, \"Originally Young Master said there might be some action tonight, though he didn't say what. We were just standing by.\"","Mo Jiuye: \"How many people did you bring to the northwest in total?\"","Warrior: \"There were ten warriors like me. Then there were five thugs to help run the buildings. \"","After listening to him, Mo Jiuye calculated the number of people they had captured. It matched up, which reassured him quite a bit. At least there were no loose ends.","He could also confirm that this was likely all the warrior knew. In his current state, desperately seeking death, he would have gladly revealed more if he knew more, for a quicker end.","Mo Jiuye glanced at Eighth Brother, signaling that this man was of no more use.","As the captain, Mo Chuhan's first thoughts were of his family's safety. He also hoped to have a witness who could speak at the trial.","Therefore, he had no intention of immediately executing the warrior. He stepped forward, pulled out a dagger, and severed the tendons in the warrior's hands and feet. This was to prevent him from escaping.","Having his tendons severed caught the warrior off guard. He painfully suppressed the itchiness and angrily cried, \"You despicable people! I've told you everything yet you still won't end it quickly for me.\"","At this point, the warrior only felt it would be better to die. The unbearable itchiness wracked his entire body, and his hands and feet were in unimaginable pain...","Mo Chuhan paid him no mind and simply picked up the man and threw him to Liang Hao nearby.","\"Take this man to the other Jingxian Building and keep him there along with the others to be taken away later by the authorities.\"","\"Understood, I'm on my way.\" Liang Hao acknowledged and left with the man.","Although Mo Jiuye wanted to find out the real reason the Xue family had come to the northwest to open Jingxian Buildings, he couldn't delay things at the government office either.","Especially after interrogating the warrior just now, he understood clearly that Xue Fan was a key figure in this case.","Otherwise, he could have brought Xue Fan back to Xi Ling Village for a thorough interrogation at his leisure. Of course, he wouldn't have let Xue Fan leave alive.","Considering the government office's efforts to clear Tang Mingrui's name, they really couldn't take Xue Fan back for slow interrogation.","Mo Jiuye fetched a basin of cold water and poured it on Xue Fan's face. Xue Fan soon regained consciousness, though his head was still groggy. This didn't stop him from recognizing the danger he was in.","\"Who exactly are you people? Why are you making an enemy of my Jingxian Building?\"","Xue Fan wasn't stupid. After exchanging moves with them earlier, even if it were just one person instead of a group, he probably wouldn't stand a chance.","All he could do was invoke the name Jingxian Building, hoping they would retreat upon hearing of Jingxian Building's background, whether they were jianghu folk or influential officials.","This Xue Fan really had been badly frightened, with his mind in disorder. They were right in the backyard of Jingxian Building. How could they not know of their ties to Jingxian Building?","\"And what can Jingxian Building do about it?\" Mo Jiuye couldn't help but laugh.","Xue Fan had only mentioned Jingxian Building in anxious desperation just now. Seeing they clearly didn't care at all about Jingxian Building, he could only think of another way to escape.","\"I don't know who you people are. I just arrived in the northwest and haven't offended anyone. Isn't treating me like this contrary to reason?\""]},{"number":440,"title":"Chapter 440: Which one of you is Mo Jiuye","paragraphs":["After listening to the few sentences Xue Fan said, Mo Jiuye could determine that this person was definitely a crafty villain, completely different from his somewhat proper appearance.","Facing this kind of person, Mo Jiuye was too lazy to beat around the bush with him.","\"Why did you pretend to be Boss Tang?\"","Upon hearing this question, Xue Fan was stunned for a moment, but he quickly concealed it.","\"What are you talking about? I don't understand at all.\"","Mo Jiuye stepped forward, stepping on the hand Xue Fan had placed near the ground, then ruthlessly ground it a few more times.","\"Don't understand? Haha...\" As he spoke, he ground down forcefully a few more times.","Forget about whether this person had come to the northwest with aims related to the Mo family, just based on his impersonating Tang Mingrui to hire killers and murder, he deserved death.","Xue Fan had been drugged so his body still felt weak and powerless. Being stepped on and ground by Mo Jiuye, he also lacked the strength to struggle, but from his twisted expression one could see how much pain his hand was in.","This guy had quite some endurance. Even though he was in pain, he showed no intention to beg for mercy.","\"You are abusing your power with unlawful punishment, I will report this to officials.\"","Mo Jiuye judged that this guy was definitely the stubborn type who wouldn't cry until he saw the coffin.","He didn't have so much time to waste here. Raising a dagger he ruthlessly stabbed it into Xue Fan's thigh repeatedly several times before stopping.","Blood had already soaked through Xue Fan's pants.","Mo Jiuye showed not an ounce of softness, instead stepping forward to tear open one of his pant legs, revealing the still bleeding wound underneath.","At this moment Xue Fan also saw clearly, the person in front of him was not only vicious and ruthless, but extremely cruel.","Just as he was contemplating how to deal with this, Mo Jiuye had already taken out a small paper package and poured out the white powder inside onto his wound.","Before Xue Fan's eyes his wound started decaying at a speed visible to the naked eye, soon exposing white bone underneath...","Excruciating pain spread throughout Xue Fan's whole body, but that wasn't even the most important thing.","The decay of his flesh had completely shattered Xue Fan's mind, at this moment he had been scared witless, staring at Mo Jiuye in horror.","\"You...just what are you trying to do?\"","Mo Jiuye coldly snorted, his hand already grasping that small paper package containing the medicinal powder.","\"Naturally I want you to obediently answer my questions.\"","Xue Fan stared at the pus-oozing bloody hole on his leg now thicker than a finger, already nearing his limit of collapse.","Even so, he still didn't want to say anything out.","He strenuously took a breath, making a show of trying to smash his head towards the nearest wall.","Seeing this, the three Mo brothers almost simultaneously moved to control him.","Mo Chuhang lacked patience more, angered most by seeing such stubborn and tough people.","After throwing the guy back to the ground he stepped forward and fiercely kicked him several times: \"You do bad things then want to get off easy with death? That would be letting you off too lightly!\"","As he spoke his dagger was already out, neatly severing the tendons in his hands and feet.","Just as Xue Fan was about to cry out loudly in pain, Sixth Brother reacted quickly to find something to plug up his mouth.","Mo Jiuye stared at him.","\"If you don't want to suffer torment, then obediently answer my questions and I will consider giving you a quick death.\"","Xue Fan closed his eyes, still not indicating he would offer up anything.","He was carefully contemplating his current situation, considering if there was still any hope he could escape alive, as well as just who exactly these people in front of him were.","As he thought this over, he seemed to realize something.","To speak of in the northwest, he had not heard there were any masters at all.","The several people who had fought with him just now all had higher martial arts than him.","With such exceptional martial skill, not to mention just in the northwest, even considering the whole of Da Shun it would be a rarely seen existence.","Suddenly, Xue Fan seemed to think of something.","Mo Jiuye could tell there was intent for him to speak, so he stepped forward and ripped away the rag stuffing his mouth.","\"Which one of you is Mo Jiuye?\" Xue Fan stared at the few people in front of him in horror.","According to reason, Mo Jiuye was the former Duke Who Protects The Country, an exceedingly prestigious figure of note in the capital city. As a son of the Xue household it was improbable he wouldn't recognize him.","But Xue Fan was rather special. Due to his exceptional martial arts and status as the Xue house's chosen successor, ever since he was very little he had been sent out wandering to train.","All these years he had been away running taverns in outside lands, very rarely appearing in the capital city. And so he had merely heard of this youngest Duke Who Protects The Country Mo Jiuye, but had never seen the man himself before.","Now having encountered people with martial skill far exceeding his own by countless bounds in the northwest, and the people before him were not bad looking, around the age he had heard of Mo Jiuye, he couldn't help but suspect the man to be Mo Jiuye.","The reason he didn't have this suspicion from the start was because in his awareness, in the present Mo family there was only Mo Jiuye as a male descendant. The possibility many top masters could appear by his side was practically zero.","But after thinking it over, he couldn't come up with any possibilities for high level masters to exist in the northwest other than Mo Jiuye. Therefore, his asking was also just probing.","Right now Mo Jiuye didn't want to conceal anything, because in his eyes this Xue Fan was already a dead man.","\"That's right, I am Mo Jiuye.\"","As Mo Jiuye spoke, his gaze closely watched Xue Fan's change in expression.","Sure enough, when Xue Fan heard he was Mo Jiuye his eyes narrowed ever so slightly for a moment, but his movement was very quick, basically undetectable if one didn't pay close attention.","It had to be said, Xue Fan's composure was still quite good. He quickly collected himself again.","\"Since you are Mo Jiuye, you should even less make things difficult for me. Which of the nobles in the capital doesn't know the powerful backer behind Jingxian Building is? Offending Jingxian Building is equal to offending the current Empress. My Xue family has always been without enmity or grudge against the Mo family. Why must you treat me like this? Aren't you afraid this will bring disaster upon the Mo family?\"","Disaster? Haha...what disasters had the Mo family not endured enough of already?","While mockingly laughing coldly to himself in his heart, Mo Jiuye once again poured medicinal powder onto another one of Xue Fan's wounds.","Seeing his actions, Xue Fan had no way to dodge, only able stare helplessly as his other wound also transformed into a pus-oozing bloody hole.","He was frantic!","\"Mo Jiuye, why must you oppose against the Xue family?\"","\"Stop beating around the bush with me. Just like Eighth Brother already said very clearly earlier, if you don't want to suffer torment then obediently answer my questions. If you continue being dishonest, I have even more methods to torment you wishing you were dead.\"","Mo Jiuye wasn't exaggerating threats at all with these words. The medicinal powders his wife had brought him that tormented people were exceptionally cruel.","Actually, Xue Fan was already terrified to an extreme degree in his heart. If it wasn't for him still thinking of the Xue family and not wanting to drag them out, he wished he could just say everything he knew for a quick relief from this ordeal.","\"I've said it already. I truly don't know anything about this Boss Tang you speak of. I've only been in the northwest a few days and haven't contacted any outsiders.\"","Mo Jiuye hadn't expected this guy's backbone to be so stubbornly tough.","But he already knew Xue Fan was extremely fearful of the decaying wounds over his own body. His current stubborn denial was purely him barely managing to hold himself together.","Thus, he once again poured medicinal powder onto another one of Xue Fan's wounds."]},{"number":441,"title":"Chapter 441: Can't I be honest","paragraphs":["Xue Fan was really scared. When Mo Jiuye sprinkled medicine powder on his wound, he had already collapsed.","\"No... don't torture me anymore. I know who Boss Tang is...\"","Mo Jiuye stopped what he was doing.","\"Why did you frame Boss Tang?\"","Xue Fan gasped for air a few times, trying his best to make his breathing calm.","\"I did pretend to be Boss Tang. That was because Boss Jin's restaurant business was too good, the number one competitor of my Jingxian Building, in order to make Jingxian Building earn more money in the northwest, I came up with this method to deal with him.\"","No matter how perfunctory this story was, not to mention Mo Jiuye didn't believe it, even the subordinates who were listening didn't believe it.","Mo Jiuye took out the small paper bag again, deliberately shook it in front of Xue Fan before sprinkling it on his wound.","\"I already told you, why are you still doing this?\" Xue Fan was in a hurry.","\"This is the consequence of you not being honest.\" Mo Jiuye said, without stopping his actions, sprinkling the powder little by little on Xue Fan's wound.","\"Your assassin subordinate has already said that you have been in the northwest for more than ten days, but you said it's only been a few days.","Also, as far as I know, the best business in the northwest region is currently Tang's Restaurant. I'm afraid your intention is not on the wine, isn't it?","Since you are not frank, I can only use some means to make you frank.\"","This time Xue Fan was really scared. That bloody hole was not just painful, it was simply devastating.","It was indeed the case. When Xue Fan saw the new bloody hole on his leg again, he had completely collapsed.","\"I beg you... don't torture me anymore... isn't being frank okay?\"","Mo Jiuye didn't say anything because his patience was also almost worn out by this sly Xue Fan. He just stared coldly at the other party, waiting for him to speak up.","Xue Fan also knew that he would not escape today, but he really could not bear such mentally devastating torture.","He silently said in his heart: Father, Empress Aunt, I have let you down.","Xue Fan made up his mind and finally spoke up.","\"After I arrived in the northwest, I had dealings with Boss Jin a few times. I heard from him that the cold rabbit of Tang's Restaurant came from a Mo family.","He also said that the Mo family was ransacked by the imperial edict and exiled here. So I can be sure that the Mo family Boss Jin was referring to was the former Duke Mansion Mo Family.","In my understanding, before the Mo Family was exiled, their home was ransacked when they left Beijing and they didn't have a penny left.","So I can be sure that the cold rabbit is the capital for the Mo Family to make a living.\"","Just as Xue Fan was about to say something more, Mo Chuhan angrily interrupted him.","\"Do you mean that your purpose in doing this is to cut off the source of livelihood for my Mo family?\"","Xue Fan nodded, \"That's right. When the Mo family was in the capital, they had no less enemies with Prince Heng. You also know that the Xue family is the one who protects Prince Heng. How can we not resent the Mo family?\"","Although Xue Fan was trapped, it did not affect his thinking.","Just now, that person said cut off the source of livelihood of my Mo family.","Those who can call themselves my Mo family must also be from the Mo family.","In his cognition, there was only Mo Jiuye left of the Mo family men, no one else was possible.","\"Are you also from the Mo family?\"","Mo Chuhan didn't pay attention to him at all, but looked at Mo Jiuye, wanting to see what his next move would be.","If someone who didn't know about this had heard Xue Fan's words, they would all think it made sense.","But the Mo brothers would not believe it at all.","Mo Jiuye sneered coldly.","\"It's fake that you came to the northwest to cut off the source of livelihood for my Mo family. The real purpose is to find out information about my Mo family, right? If possible, would you take action to dispose of me too?\"","Mo Jiuye's mind was delicate. He could hear from Xue Fan's words that after arriving in the northwest, Xue Fan had been busy with the Jingxian Building all the time and had no time to investigate the Mo family yet.","\"On the surface, you made a move against Boss Tang to cut off my Mo family's source of income, but the real purpose was to force me to show up, right?\"","Mo Jiuye pressed step by step, every sentence hit the sore spot in Xue Fan's heart.","Xue Fan instantly broke into a cold sweat, because everything Mo Jiuye said was right.","Then he looked at Mo Chuhan again. This man was burly in stature, and his appearance was no less handsome than Mo Jiuye's.","According to his knowledge, Mo family men were all handsome in appearance and extraordinary in temperament. No matter from any aspect, this person was no less outstanding than Mo Jiuye at all.","Could it be that he is also a Mo family man?","This is impossible. Except for Mo Jiuye, all Mo family men died on the battlefield, this is a fact known to the whole world.","Just as Xue Fan was wondering, Mo Jiuye spoke again.","\"I don't have much patience to linger here with you. If you think there should be a few more bloody holes on your body, I don't mind dirtying my hands again.\"","As Mo Jiuye spoke, the small paper bag in his hand was already opened, pretending to sprinkle it on Xue Fan's wound.","Because he deliberately slowed down this time, it gave Xue Fan a chance to react.","\"Don't... don't... I'll tell.\"","Mo Jiuye stopped his movements.","\"Then say something that can make me believe.\"","\"It was my Empress Aunt. She has always believed that the disappearance of Prince Heng is related to you. So she discussed with the Prime Minister to send someone to the northwest to catch you alive and ask about the whereabouts of Prince Heng.","On the one hand, she hopes I can find out the whereabouts of Prince Heng from you, and on the other hand, she is worried that Prince Qi will find a way to redress the Mo Family one day. Once that day comes, with your support, even if Prince Heng comes back, it would still be very difficult for him to stand firm.","Therefore, my Empress Aunt also hopes that I can dispose of you unknowingly...\"","Speaking to this point, Xue Fan couldn't help but glanced at Mo Jiuye's expression. Seeing that there was no anomaly, he continued:","\"The main purpose of me opening two Jingxian Buildings in the northwest is to cover people’s eyes.","Today I was just waiting for the news from the government side. Once Boss Tang gets convicted, I believe it won’t take many days for your Mo family to think of other ways to sell the cold rabbit.","By then, I can take the opportunity when the Mo family's attention is all on their livelihood to send someone to catch you alive.\"","Mo Jiuye asked with interest: \"Oh? According to what you said, after you arrived in the northwest, you still have not gone to investigate any news about my Mo family?\""]},{"number":442,"title":"Chapter 442: This person can also be directly handed over to the Yamen","paragraphs":["Mo Jiuye appeared calm on the surface, but he was actually nervous.","From Xue Fan's account, it was clear that his purpose in coming to the northwest was indeed related to the Mo Family, which was almost entirely different from what he had speculated.","What worried him now was that before the Mo Family had fully prepared to deal with external threats, Xue Fan had already gathered some information about the Mo Family.","Once this information reached the capital and was known to Emperor Shunwu, there was no guarantee that he wouldn't take any actions detrimental to the Mo Family.","Xue Fan shook his head vigorously, \"After I arrived in the northwest, I was busy with the opening of Jingxian Building. I just freed up some time to think about using Boss Tang's hiring of a killer to force you to show up voluntarily. Before the matter had any results, you found out about it. I can only count myself unlucky.\"","His words were not untrue at all.","Xue Fan was accustomed to being self-righteous in his actions, and everyone in the capital knew that Mo Jiuye was the only male descendant of the Mo Family.","He also understood Mo Jiuye's martial arts skills well; if they were to truly face each other, he would definitely not be his opponent.","Therefore, after arriving in the northwest, he did not immediately send someone to take action but instead opened Jingxian Building.","In this way, having a place for himself and his men was one aspect; the most important thing was for his true purpose in coming to the northwest.","At the same time, he hoped that Mo Jiuye wouldn't overthink things and assume that he was simply doing business.","After all, Jingxian Building had branches all over the north and south of the Great River, so it wasn't unreasonable to open one in the northwest.","Unexpectedly, he underestimated Mo Jiuye's intelligence, thinking that as a mere martial artist, he wouldn't have so many thoughts.","Never in a million years did he expect that despite his best efforts, he would be discovered so quickly.","Not only that, but he might even lose his life here.","The more Xue Fan thought about it, the more he regretted it. He shouldn't have tried to show off in front of the Empress just to get this job.","If Mo Jiuye knew what he was thinking, he would probably laugh for a while.","Was there no one left in the Xue Family? They actually sent someone so brainless and self-righteous to deal with the Mo Family.","Indeed, they treated the Mo Family like fools...","But this was also good; it was better than if the Xue Family had sent a cunning person here. If that were the case, the first thing they would do upon arrival would be to investigate the situation of the Mo Family.","Xue Fan considered himself clever; he even set a trap using Chen Wu and Wang Lin.","Little did he know, these petty tricks couldn't withstand close scrutiny at all.","Xue Fan was afraid that Mo Jiuye would sprinkle that dreadful powder on his wound again, so he hurriedly assured, \"I didn't gain anything here. There's no way I would send any messages to the capital. You must believe me.\"","As he spoke, he kept his eyes on Mo Jiuye's hands, afraid that if something went wrong, he would open that small paper package...","Seeing this, Mo Jiuye deliberately waved the small paper package in front of him.","\"Besides sending you to the northwest, does the Xue Family have any other plans?\"","\"No, there aren't any. I came to the northwest only to find out about the whereabouts of Prince Heng from you, and nothing else,\" Xue Fan spoke rapidly, afraid that if he spoke slowly, Mo Jiuye would make another move.","All the necessary inquiries had been made, and as for Xue Fan sending people to capture Wang Lin's family as a threat, Meng Huaining, the official in charge, had taken care of it, and Mo Jiuye couldn't be bothered to say more.","Mo Jiuye looked at Mo Chuhan and said, \"Elder Brother Mo, this man can be handed over directly to the yamen.\"","Mo Chuhan nodded. \"I understand.\"","Though he didn't have the scheming mind of his other brothers, he understood one thing very well: even if Xue Fan were handed over to the authorities, he wouldn't be leaving alive. With the amount he knew, if it weren't for Ninth Brother's need for the case, Xue Fan would likely have met his end right here.","Dealing with someone like Xue Fan wasn't difficult for Mo Chuhan. Once Meng Huaining finalized the case, it would be Xue Fan's death sentence.","Wang Lin's mother had gone to report to the authorities in Yun City, and it would take some time for the officials to arrive from the prefectural capital.","Until the officials from the yamen arrived, the Mo brothers couldn't leave. Mo Jiuye took advantage of this time to thoroughly search both branches of the Jingxian Building.","And thus, he found a temporary peace of mind.","While searching Xue Fan's living quarters, he discovered several letters exchanged between him and contacts in the capital. All correspondence was with his father, Xue Jinchuan, and all related to capturing Mo Jiuye.","Xue Jinchuan's intention was for Xue Fan to first investigate the specifics of the Mo family's situation in the northwest before devising a plan to capture Mo Jiuye.","Furthermore, Xue Jinchuan urged Xue Fan to report back on what he learned in the northwest. The tone of Xue Jinchuan's letters suggested he wasn't very trusting of his son, reminding him constantly to listen to his orders and not act presumptuously.","From this, it could be deduced that Xue Fan hadn't followed Xue Jinchuan's instructions, instead acting according to his own ideas.","Presumably, he was eager to make a name for himself, thinking he had come up with a brilliant plan by using Tang Mingrui to disrupt the Mo family's income. Little did he know, this method seemed utterly ludicrous to Mo Jiuye.","The Xue family truly was something, sending someone so lacking in intelligence to handle affairs. Not only did they fail, but their intentions were exposed so quickly...","Whether it was because Wang Lin's mother was slow to act or because Meng Huaining had other matters to attend to, when the officials from Yun City yamen arrived to apprehend Xue Fan, it was nearing dusk.","Jingxian Building suddenly fell silent, becoming the talk of the town for the afternoon.","The townsfolk discussed how both branches of Jingxian Building had ceased business almost simultaneously, a coincidence that caught the attention of a passing yamen official.","The official reported the matter to the magistrate.","This magistrate had heard rumors that Jingxian Building had a powerful backer.","With such a powerful backing, how could a business just shut down at will?","Though Xue Fan's opening of Jingxian Building in the northwest hadn't involved the magistrate, he was concerned that something unfavorable might happen to Jingxian Building on his turf. Therefore, upon hearing of this, he personally brought along a few men to investigate.","This investigation coincidentally brought him face to face with Meng Huaining, who was leading the officials to arrest someone.","Meng Huaining's immediate superior was the magistrate, so he naturally had to explain the purpose of this trip in detail. After all, he was responsible for handling this case under the magistrate's orders. If he didn't address it now, he would have to explain everything in detail when the case was concluded.","The magistrate simply wanted to avoid unnecessary trouble, especially considering Tang Mingrui was from Yun City. That's why he handed the case over to Meng Huaining for handling.","Little did he know, this matter was also connected to the Jingxian Building.","At this moment, the magistrate couldn't help but feel relieved that he had delegated the case to Meng Huaining. If the evidence turned out to be solid, the people from the Jingxian Building would be prosecuted, indirectly offending the powerful figures behind them."]},{"number":443,"title":"Chapter 443: This is the Best Way","paragraphs":["In order to dissociate himself from this matter, the magistrate gave Meng Huaining a few instructions and quickly left with his men, afraid that people would find out he had been involved in this case.","Meng Huaining did not know the specifics of the Jingxian Building. Even if he did, given his character, he would not be afraid of the power behind it.","After inquiring about some of the circumstances from Mo Jiuye and others, he ordered his subordinates to tie up all the people from the Jingxian Building and bring them back to Yuncheng.","Among those captured at the Jingxian Building, apart from that assassin and Xue Fan who knew martial arts, the rest were just relying on strong physique and some boxing skills to make a scene there.","At the moment, the tendons in the assassin and Xue Fan's hands and feet had been severed by the Mo brothers, so there was no need to worry that they would escape under Meng Huaining's hands. The Mo brothers decided to leave first.","After all, they had been out for quite some time, and their families would worry if they did not return for a long time.","Considering that Meng Huaining would definitely interrogate the people overnight after taking them back, Mo Chuhua accompanied him back to the yamen.","Moreover, he still had an arduous task ahead, which was to get rid of Xue Fan after Meng Huaining had interrogated the case clearly.","The other Mo brothers and Liang Hao hurried back to Xi Ling Village.","The distance between the prefectural government and Xi Ling Village was not very close. Even though the brothers hurried, it was already night when they returned.","Except for He Zhiran, the others did not know what had happened today. They only thought the brothers had gone into town to do business. At this time, they had already had dinner and rested in their own yards.","After such an incident happened, Mo Jiuye was going to gather everyone together to talk about it, but considering the late hour, he did not disturb anyone and returned to his own small courtyard with He Zhiran.","He Zhiran had already sent Madam He away to rest earlier, and waited alone in the room for Mo Jiuye to come back.","Hearing the door sound, she immediately stood up.","\"Husband, how is the situation at the prefectural government?\" she asked as she handed over a clean towel for Mo Jiuye to wipe the sweat from his forehead.","Mo Jiuye took the towel and sat on the edge of the bed with He Zhiran.","\"Ranran, fortunately you were thoughtful today and asked sixth brother and the others to rush over to help, and also brought me those medicinal powders...\"","Mo Jiuye wiped his face while carefully telling He Zhiran what had happened at the prefectural government today.","He Zhiran frowned while listening.","\"In other words, this time as soon as Xue Fan made a move after coming to the northwest, he was discovered without causing any threat to the Mo family yet. But this incident is enough to show that those people in the capital still have not let go of the Mo family.\"","Mo Jiuye nodded deeply: \"Yes, that's right. Many people see the Mo family as a thorn in their side, an existence that poses a potential threat to their status. This time it is the Xue family. There is nothing to worry about. What I fear most is that Emperor Shunwu finds out about the Mo family's situation. If he takes action, it won't be as easy to deal with as today.\"","This was also He Zhiran's biggest concern. After all, Emperor Shunwu was the ruler of a country. If he wanted someone dead, it would only take an imperial decree.","At present, the fifth brother had made a batch of bombs. They could only hope that the seventh brother would bring his former subordinates from the south sooner.","Then, let the Mo brothers train a powerful army as soon as possible. That way, even if Emperor Shunwu sent troops, they would have the strength to resist.","These words were just thoughts in He Zhiran's mind. By now, the tacit understanding between her and Mo Jiuye had reached a point where they could understand each other without speaking.","Even if they were anxious, all they could do was wait and hope that no other bad things would happen during this period.","After talking about what happened today, Mo Jiuye asked again: \"Did Brother Tang come today?\"","\"Yes. He is a man with business ideas in his mind. How could he not come when he saw such a good deal?\" He Zhiran couldn't help but laugh when it came to Tang Mingrui.","He really was a business fanatic to still think of making money despite his legal troubles.","He Zhiran continued after a pause: \"Brother Tang will come with people early tomorrow morning to transport the watermelons. Husband needs to get up early tomorrow to arrange manpower.\"","\"After what happened today, I intend to suspend the jewelry business for a while.\"","Mo Jiuye was a little puzzled by this. Although there were people eyeing the Mo family, it would not affect doing business and making money.","\"Why?\"","\"If nothing unexpected happens, it will take less than a month for the seventh brother to come back from the south. Then there will be so many people who need housing.","The village is out of the question. Too many people are too conspicuous, not to mention inconvenient for training.","We decided earlier to let them operate secretly in the mountains, so I was thinking of building some houses on the mountain so they would have a place to stay after coming over.\"","Speaking of this, He Zhiran was also quite embarrassed.","After all, these were people who were not meant to see the light of day. It was impossible for them to live in the village openly like Tao Ran and the others.","Building housing for 1,800 people in the mountains was no small project. Just the materials alone would be substantial, not to mention the huge manpower required for construction.","If it was normal circumstances, Hu Cong would be quite capable in this area, and would spare no effort to help if informed.","But they did not want anyone other than Mo family members and their confidantes to know about this matter, so He Zhiran was at a bit of a loss.","Although Mo Jiuye was not stupid, his mind was still not as meticulous as He Zhiran's. He only knew that there were several caves in the mountains where the subordinates from the south could temporarily live when they arrived.","But he did not consider that it was a number of 1,800 people. Even if the mountain caves could accommodate so many people, living in such dark confinement for a long time would make anyone weary.","Moreover, these were all stalwart men ready to protect their homeland. They should not live like that.","With this reminder from He Zhiran, Mo Jiuye also realized the problem.","At the same time, he was also thinking about how to make it more comfortable for the brothers after they arrived.","Suddenly he had a flash of inspiration, as if he had thought of something.","\"Ranran, when I was browsing Taobao Mall, I inadvertently saw something called... yes, called movable integrated housing.\"","Reminded by Mo Jiuye, He Zhiran also remembered it.","Many scenic spots in their previous lives would install such movable houses.","The built-in structure of movable houses could be customized according to the needs of guests, and installation was very simple.","\"Husband, do you mean to place these movable houses on the mountain for the soldiers to live in?\"","\"Currently, this seems to be the best solution.\" Mo Jiuye was very curious when he first saw such houses and had deliberately clicked into the link to take a closer look.","In his opinion, there was currently nothing more suitable for housing those soldiers than these movable houses.","\"You don't need to worry about the source of the houses. Leave it to me when the time comes.\""]},{"number":444,"title":"Chapter 444: I'll arrange it right away.","paragraphs":["Mo Jiuye also felt there was no need to dwell too much since He Zhiran had already said that.","\"Alright, tomorrow you take me up the mountain to buy movable housing,\" he said.","Not only that, He Zhiran intended to take this opportunity to purchase all the daily necessities they might need all at once, such as quilts, pots and pans for cooking, etc.","When it came to taking He Zhiran up the mountain, Mo Jiuye really felt bad.","Especially when he saw her huge belly, the guilt in Mo Jiuye's heart grew stronger and stronger.","He had thought that after settling down in the northwest, his wife would be able to live a good life, but instead, she had to worry about the family with a big belly.","Particularly since he had to take her up the mountain tomorrow. It should be known that the place where those soldiers lived was not halfway up the mountain or anywhere close.","Even without using his lightness skill, it would take him more than an hour to walk there.","But he couldn't go without his wife either.","After all, he needed the space in her bracelet to shop on Taobao.","Seeing his distress, He Zhiran stood up in front of him and walked around a few times.","\"Don't worry, husband. Although my belly has grown a bit bigger, it won't hinder my movement at all. As long as you take good care of me along the way, there will definitely be no problem,\" she said.","He Zhiran really didn't feel like being pregnant was a big problem. She had seen many women in her previous life who worked up until it was almost time to give birth.","Why shouldn't she be able to do what others could?","Moreover, she was a doctor herself. No one understood her physical condition better than her.","The two little ones in her belly had always been safe and sound, and her body was fine as well.","It was just a mountain; as long as they were careful, nothing would happen.","Mo Jiuye also figured there was no avoiding taking his wife up the mountain this time. As long as he was there, he would definitely not let any harm come to her or the children.","After chatting for a while as husband and wife, seeing that it was getting late, they entered the space to rest.","The next day, Mo Jiuye left before dawn, calling some men to go busy themselves in the melon fields.","Only after Tang Mingrui was satisfied hauling away several cartloads of large watermelons did he return to the quadrangle courtyard.","He had just walked to the second elder's door when Sixth Bro called out to him.","\"Ninth Bro, Eighth Bro just got back and went to report what happened yesterday to Father and Mother. Everyone is waiting for you to come discuss countermeasures.\"","Discuss countermeasures?","What good countermeasures were there?","There was only what he and his wife had talked about last night - hoping Eldest Bro could bring people back soon from the south, and once an army was built up, even if Emperor Shunwu sent thousands of horses and troops, there would be no need to worry.","Mo Jiuye entered the second elder's room to find all his brothers neatly seated on both sides except Eldest Bro who had gone south.","They looked as serious as back in the border when the commander-in-chief gathered everyone to discuss countermeasures against the enemy.","When Mo Jiuye stated his opinion, not a single person, including Mo Qing, disagreed. After all, no one could come up with a better countermeasure.","Finally Mo Qing spoke up.","\"From today onwards, we Moes will patrol in shifts. If anything or anyone suspicious is discovered, it must be taken seriously,\" he said.","Mo Yunfeng immediately stood up.","\"Father, leave this matter to me. I will arrange it right away.\"","At present, the Moes were not lacking in manpower either.","With Liang Hao and the other four, plus the 30 plus medicine men saved by Tao Ran taking turns patrolling, there would be no issues.","On Fifth Bro's side, he continued leading people to manufacture explosives. By now they were completely familiar with the process and the speed of production had also increased significantly.","It was believed that by the time Mo Yuance returned from the south with people, they would at least be able to distribute two bombs per person.","Of course, they would continue production until the amount was completely sufficient before stopping.","At the same time, Mo Chuhan also reported the news from the government office.","Meng Huaining had conducted overnight interrogations and the truth had already come to light.","It was just as Mo Jiuye had guessed - Xue Fan would not foolishly confess his true purpose for coming to the northwest. The testimony he gave Meng Huaining was that he intended to sabotage the cold rabbit business of Tang Ji Restaurant.","By doing so this way, he was not helping the Moes cover anything up, but hoping his crime would be lighter. As long as he was not executed on the spot after questioning, people from the capital would come to his rescue as soon as they got the news.","But his wishful thinking was wrong. After being thrown into jail at midnight, he was delivered to the King of Hell by Mo Chuhan without knowing what hit him.","As for this, Meng Huaining also turned a blind eye, and only announced externally that Xue Fan had suddenly died in his cell.","Fortunately, Mo Chuhan mastered his murder technique so none could find out Xue Fan had been killed.","Mo Chuhan's method of murder was very special. He inserted a silver needle into a certain death acupoint on the top of Xue Fan's head. To not leave any traces behind, after Xue Fan had breathed his last, Mo Chuhan took out the needle again.","Not even the most skilled coroner would be able to detect anything with such a murder technique.","It was the same for the dead assassin, but his life and death would not get anyone's attention in the first place, let alone any investigation.","As for those arrogant bullies, they did not truly participate in this matter after all, so they were sentenced to three years imprisonment then released.","Although Chen Wu had also been used, he was still an accomplice, thus sentenced to one year imprisonment.","As for Wang Lin, even though he only did it under coercion due to his impoverished situation, he had killed with his own hands in the end.","Considering he was forced, Meng Huaining did not sentence him to death, but rather exile to do hard labour in the Western regions for life, unable to leave.","After hearing these people's sentences, Mo Jiuye did not actually object. But those thugs were still Xue's men in the end.","Once the Xues discovered something amiss, they would surely send people to investigate.","Therefore, the safest method was still for them to shut up as well.","The Mo brothers were not random killers; to slay the Xue's men and those assassins were reasonable.","Although those thugs were not righteous people either, the Mo brothers would not simply take their lives.","In the end, it was still Mo Jiuye who obtained the wits-robbing drug from He Zhiran and passed it to Eighth Bro.","Eighth Bro was originally let off to rest by Meng Huaining since he had worked overnight at the government office.","But considering the potential threat those people posed to the Moes, Eighth Bro did not intend to rest for even a moment. Clutching the medicine packet, he headed back to the government office.","With the family matter discussed, only then did Mo Jiuye take He Zhiran along to go up the mountain. They only told Madam He they were going out for a walk.","Madam He was happy her daughter and son-in-law were affectionate and supported the couple going out together.","All the way there, Mo Jiuye kept a tight hold on He Zhiran's hand, and his walking pace accommodated her as well."]},{"number":445,"title":"Chapter 445: Don't Be So Nervous","paragraphs":["Not until the two walked to a place where no one could see them did Mo Jiuye lightly pick He Zhiran up. He utilized his lightness skill to dash straight towards the place prepared to settle those old subordinates.","It was fine for him to work harder, as long as his wife was not suffering. Otherwise, he really did not know to what extent he would feel guilty.","The journey went smoothly. Mo Jiuye was also very careful, afraid that his wife would feel uncomfortable.","In fact, He Zhiran was not as delicate as he had imagined. When they arrived at the destination, she did not have any issues at all.","She was not aware of the nervous mood in Mo Jiuye's heart. She was just about to enter her space to take a look at the Taobao Mall when Mo Jiuye grabbed her hand.","\"Ranran, you should rest first. If you feel uncomfortable, tell me immediately.\"","Hearing him say that, He Zhiran only then realized his nervousness.","\"I'm fine. Don't be so nervous.\"","After saying that, she pulled Mo Jiuye along to enter the space together.","Last night, the two had already selected several types of movable integrated houses in the space. They were just waiting to check the slope of the land after going up the mountain before deciding which one to purchase.","It had to be said that this location was really suitable for placing these movable houses.","Because this was a mountain depression, the flat land area was very large. Not only that, not far away up the mountain was a waterfall that formed a stream passing through here.","Although He Zhiran had only taken a glance before entering the space, she sincerely liked this place from the bottom of her heart.","Not only was this place concealed well, the most important thing was that the surrounding environment gave people a feeling of refreshment.","If there was no clutter on the outside, she really wanted to live in such a place for a lifetime.","Bringing her thoughts back, the couple finally decided to purchase a simple and stylish movable house.","After all, the location of a mountain depression was limited. It was impossible for everyone to live in single rooms.","The house they chose had four small compartments. In their previous lives, such movable houses were basically purchased by factories to be used as employee dormitories.","Although the rooms were not very big, they came with an iron frame bed and a wooden wardrobe inside.","With such specifications, it was perfectly sufficient for two people to live in each room, and it was much more comfortable than the large bunk beds they lived in at the border.","On average, each movable house could house eight people. Preparing one hundred or slightly more would be enough.","In addition to these, He Zhiran also selected a movable house that could be used as a kitchen.","After selecting the styles, the couple left the space together.","He Zhiran was like a fairy. Every few steps, a simple and stylish integrated movable house would magically appear.","After about two hours of busy work and checking that there was nothing missing, the husband and wife sat down to rest on a rock nearby.","He Zhiran simply looked around. Suddenly, her gaze was fixed on the hillside not far away.","Mo Jiuye followed her line of sight. It was a patch of flowers that were not very white.","\"Ranran, do you like those flowers? I'll go pick some for you.\"","He Zhiran also got up. Her eyes kept staring at that small patch of flowers.","\"Husband, those flowers look a bit like tea flowers. Let's go take a look.\"","Hearing that she wanted to go see it together, Mo Jiuye specifically looked at the height of the hillside.","From the foot of the mountain, it would probably take one incense stick worth of time. Also, the hillside did not look steep.","At the same time, he also knew clearly that his wife was a strong-minded person. Even if he said he would pick some back for her to see, she would not agree.","\"Alright, I will hold your hand. Let's walk slowly to take a look.\"","Upon arriving at the destination, He Zhiran bent over to carefully examine the shape of the flowers.","The flowers were white to pale orange in color, with elongated petals. The flower diameter was about 2-3 centimeters, looking exactly the same as the flowering Iron Goddess tea she had seen in her previous life.","In her previous life, she had accompanied her supervisor back to his hometown once. Her supervisor’s family were tea farmers. It just so happened to be the season when the Iron Goddess tea flowers were in full bloom. Her supervisor’s mother had picked some to bring home for viewing.","Because the flowers were inserted in a vase, He Zhiran did not see what the leaves looked like.","However, she still had a fresh memory of the scent of those flowers.","In order to confirm whether these were really tea flowers, He Zhiran leaned forward and gently sniffed them.","A faint fragrance was mixed with a subtle tea aroma.","\"This is it.\"","Mo Jiuye had been standing by her side watching her actions.","\"Ranran, what is this?\"","He Zhiran plucked a few tea tree leaves and placed them in front of Mo Jiuye.","\"Do you still remember a kind of tea I once gave you to drink? That tea was a small round ball before being soaked in water.\"","\"Ranran, are you saying this is Iron Goddess Tea?\" Speaking of Iron Goddess Tea, when Ranran let him taste it at that time, he had also praised the special stir-frying skills involved.","In addition, the taste of Iron Goddess Tea was very pleasant, leaving Mo Jiuye with a deep impression of it.","At this moment, He Zhiran's eyes lit up, not because she had found Iron Goddess here, but because it made her think of a new way to make money.","That was tea cultivation.","In the future when those subordinates from the borders arrived, they might be living here every day in addition to military affairs.","It was impossible for them to keep training all the time. How would they pass the time during their leisure?","It would be different if a tea plantation was opened up here. During the times they were not training, they could grow tea plants. This way, they would have something to do and also be able to generate some profit.","Of course, it was not that He Zhiran could not support them, but this would allow them to have more income.","After all, they were all young people. In the future when they married and had children, the extra income would enable He Zhiran to believe that they would all become wealthy.","\"I do have this idea in mind. You also know that I can cultivate better quality tea saplings and seeds in my space.\"","\"Ranran, this idea of yours is not bad. Growing tea here would also resolve any issues with manpower.\" Although his wife had started paving the way, Mo Jiuye could still think of the follow up without her saying anything more.","\"Mm, tonight I will cultivate tea tree saplings in the space. It probably would not take many days for them to mature. By then, you can bring Tao Ran and them here to plant some first.\"","Anyway, it would not take long before Tao Ran and them would come here with him, so letting them know earlier would not hurt."]},{"number":446,"title":"Chapter 446: Taste it and you'll know.","paragraphs":["He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye looked at the sky. There was still plenty of time before dark, so He Zhiran told Mo Jiuye to pick some tea leaves to take back.","She could try researching tea frying to pass the time. He Zhiran took out a back basket from her space. Mo Jiuye filled the basket full of tea leaves before they went back down the mountain.","Madam He originally thought her son-in-law had taken her daughter out for a walk. She didn't expect they hadn't returned even by lunch time, and worried something might have happened to He Zhiran. She stood at the door, looking out for them.","Seeing the couple's figures in the distance, Madam He went up to meet them.","\"Zhiran, Jiuye, did you go into town? Why were you gone for so long?\"","As she spoke, Madam He carefully looked over He Zhiran to see if she was hurt, worried something might have happened to her.","He Zhiran knew her mother truly cared for her. She had been gone for quite some time, so she quickly pulled her mother's arm.","\"Mother, Jiuye and I just went for a walk. We got carried away playing around, which is why we took so long to get back.\"","At this time, Madam He noticed the back basket behind Mo Jiuye's back.","\"You went up the mountain?\"","After living in Xi Ling Village for some days, Madam He understood that the villagers often carried similar back baskets when going up the mountains.","Mo Jiuye put the basket on the ground.","\"Mother, Zhiran and I just wandered around. We accidentally discovered some tea leaves and picked some to bring back, which is why we took longer.\"","As an aristocrat from the capital, Madam He naturally knew a lot about tea.","In her opinion, the best tea in the capital came from the south. She had also only seen processed and roasted final tea products.","Seeing Mo Jiuye carrying a basket of unknown leaves, she couldn't help asking doubtfully: \"Zhiran, Jiuye, don't tell me those are tea leaves?\"","Madam He's question didn't surprise He Zhiran at all.","Tea was already scarce in Da Shun. Coupled with its rarity, tea prices were very high.","Not only that, tea farmers would roast the tea leaves before selling them elsewhere. The only form consumers saw was the dried, roasted tea.","Moreover, ancient tea frying techniques were backward. No matter the tea variety, the roasted tea leaves looked blackish-brown. Even when brewed, one couldn't discern the original shape of the leaves.","Most importantly, when He Zhiran first let Mo Jiuye try Tieguanyin tea, she had specially asked if Da Shun had such tasting tea.","Therefore, Madam He mistaking random plant leaves for tea was understandable.","\"Mother, don't worry. This is absolutely tea leaves. I once read about this kind of tea in a book. It's extremely rare and has exquisite flavor. I'll research tea frying tomorrow. You'll know after tasting it.\"","Seeing her daughter's enthusiasm, Madam He didn't want to dampen it. She could only nod perfunctorily.","As long as her daughter was happy, it didn't matter whether these were actually tea leaves.","The next day, Mo Jiuye took Liang Hao, Tao Ran and others up the mountain to prepare. He Zhiran went to her own courtyard's small kitchen.","After picking those tea leaves, she had bought a book on tea frying techniques from Taobao. She now grasped the frying method and had nothing to do at the moment. It was just right to practice with those mountain tea leaves.","Not only that, to prepare for yesterday's plan, He Zhiran planted large quantities of tea saplings in her space.","The seeds came from her space. Like other crops, they weren't picky about climate or soil. Let alone growing well on the Tieguanyin mountainside, they wouldn't even be affected by saline-alkali soil.","After a busy day, He Zhiran successfully shocked Madam He speechless.","\"Zhiran, this is real tea?\" Madam He held a small ball that looked slightly inferior to the Tieguanyin He Zhiran had bought online. Her eyes shone brightly.","Although He Zhiran wasn't very satisfied with the tea's appearance, its taste proved her roasted tea had nearly succeeded. As long as she practiced more, she firmly believed she could roast Tieguanyin like her previous life.","She happily responded, \"Mother, it should have succeeded.\"","She then instructed Yu Er, who was helping by the side, to brew several cups for everyone to taste.","Lan Er and Yu Er were maidservants who had grown up beside the Fourth Princess. They were naturally quite familiar with Da Shun's fine tea.","As soon as Lan Er lifted the lid of her cup, she deeply inhaled the aroma.","\"Ninth Madam, in Lan Er’s opinion, this tea can absolutely be called the finest of the finest. Even the palace tributes pale in comparison.\"","He Zhiran knew Lan Er was knowledgeable. Her high appraisal meant the future tea business would earn them barrels of money.","Madam He nodded continuously as well. \"I didn't expect that such delicious tea could be produced in this barren land of the northwest.\"","She never imagined the tea had nothing to do with where it grew. Its deliciousness completely came from her daughter's frying technique.","Madam He's assumption saved He Zhiran the trouble of explaining.","When Mo Jiuye returned from the mountain with the others at dusk, everything had been properly arranged there.","He Zhiran didn't bother asking what excuses he had used. In any case, Liang Hao and the others didn't notice anything wrong after coming back.","Not only that, Mo Jiuye had brought everyone to pick more tea leaves.","Last night, he had watched his wife learn tea frying methods in her space.","He originally thought it would take her many attempts to grasp such a complicated process. Hence, he decided to pick more tea leaves for her practice.","Unexpectedly, his capable wife succeeded after only a day. The taste was just as good as the Tieguanyin bought online.","This made Mo Jiuye realize one thing — aside from jewelry making in the future, the tea business would also become a major source of income for the Mo family.","In fact, Mo Jiuye still underestimated his wife.","Although He Zhiran wasn't very interested in business and lacked Tang Mingrui's business savvy, she truly possessed insight from a millennium in the future. With that alone, even without business smarts, she could still earn barrels of money in ancient times.","Dinner was still in Old Lady Mo's courtyard, except for the Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran household.","Considering that Madam He had travelled far to the northwest to accompany her daughter's childbirth, and the He family had so many sons, Old Lady Mo knew Madam He still wasn't completely accustomed to rural customs despite the Mo family shedding many aristocratic rules.","She worried the mother-in-law would feel uncomfortable dining like this. So she sent Yu Er to He Zhiran's courtyard to handle her meals daily.","By now, Madam He had completely fallen in love with the meals from her daughter's home."]},{"number":447,"title":"Chapter 447: Fried Pork Belly with Chili","paragraphs":["Lan Er's cooking skills were good in one aspect.","More importantly, the chili peppers the Mo Family had planted in the fields had matured over the past few days.","At present, the chili peppers were still green instead of having turned red, but using them to stir fry dishes did not affect the taste. On the contrary, there was a different texture.","Over the past few days, dishes made with green chili peppers appeared on the Mo Family's dining table almost every meal.","Although the chili peppers were spicy, they went extremely well with rice. The family members sweated profusely from the spiciness every day, yet they could not resist the craving for this taste.","The Mo Family had been running a cold rabbit meat business for over half a year. The sisters-in-law all knew that one of the most important seasonings for cold rabbit meat was chili peppers.","Seeing that the chili peppers had matured, everyone was curious why the ninth younger sister had not let them be harvested.","After asking, they found out that the chili peppers would gradually turn red after growing for a period of time. By then, picking and sun drying them meant they could be stored until next year when the chili peppers matured again.","Understanding the reason, the sisters-in-law then gave up the idea of immediately going to pick chili peppers.","Anyway, the vegetables grown on their own land could be eaten casually by the family, and there was such a large quantity that not only could they be used to feed the family, even selling some was fine. There was absolutely no need to worry that there would be no chili pepper seasoning to make cold rabbit meat next year.","On this day, in Old Lord Mo's courtyard, a stir fried dish of green chili peppers and pork belly had also been prepared. Everyone was about to start eating when Yu Er's voice sounded from outside the door.","\"Old Madam, Master Meng is here.\"","When she heard Meng Huaining had come, Mo Hanyue shyly lowered her head and sat behind her eldest sister-in-law.","There were seven days left before their big wedding day.","Since settling the wedding date with her, Meng Huaining had not come to visit. If he had not been caught up with all kinds of matters, he would have come to see his future little wife earlier.","Following Lan Er's words, Meng Huaining had already walked into the main hall.","He was about to pay his respects to Old Lady Mo when he noticed an elderly man with innate dignity sitting beside her. Not only that, on either side of the elderly couple sat two middle-aged men with unfamiliar faces.","Meng Huaining was stunned. His first reaction was to look towards Mo Chuhan.","\"This is our father,\" Mo Chuhan introduced.","Father?","Meng Huaining reacted quickly. Without overthinking, he hurriedly knelt before Mo Qing and Old Lady Mo.","\"Junior pays respect to Old Duke.\"","Mo Qing liked the demeanour of this young man before him. But when he thought that his precious daughter would become this person's wife in a few days, he felt somewhat unhappy.","As for the matter of this fellow not having come to see him after he returned to the Mo Family for so long, he could not blame the other party for that.","It was him who had insisted on not letting Mo Chuhan say anything.","Although he felt unhappy inwardly, as an elder he could not make things too difficult for his future son-in-law.","\"Mm, rise.\" His voice was cold, making even the Mo family members feel somewhat unaccustomed.","Meng Huaining did not feel anything wrong with that.","After all, his future father-in-law was once the Commander-in-Chief who led thousands of troops and the first Duke of Da Shun.","Meng Huaining respectfully stood up, keeping his head lowered to maintain a humble attitude.","However, from the corner of his eye he did not give up observing everyone.","Although his future father-in-law's body seemed somewhat emaciated, his hair white, appearing ten to twenty years older compared to Old Lady Mo, his extraordinary bearing and prestige were still difficult to ignore.","As for the two middle-aged men sitting beside the elderly couple, similarly, the innate dominance they exuded simply could not be concealed.","At the same time, a shocking guess appeared in his mind.","Could it be that these two were the Eldest and Second Eldest Brothers of the Mo Family?","Meng Huaining did not dare to stare directly at the father and sons as he was their junior. Moreover, he would become the Mo Family's son-in-law in a few days. So Meng Huaining was extremely careful not to overstep any boundaries.","Therefore, he maintained his slightly lowered head posture and waited for his elder to speak.","This gave Meng Huaining the opportunity to observe everyone.","He could see that the appearances of the two middle-aged men bore some similarities with the other Mo brothers.","Now that Old Duke Mo had come back alive, it was no longer too shocking if the Eldest and Second Eldest Brothers of the Mo Family were also alive.","The only thing Meng Huaining felt strange about was why the whole world knew that people who had died in battle were appearing alive one by one.","Could there be some earth-shattering conspiracy behind this?","Countless question marks had appeared in Meng Huaining's mind at this moment. Just as he was pondering, Mo Qing finally spoke.","\"I heard your grandfather was the former Senior Minister?\"","Meng Huaining quickly pulled back his thoughts and respectfully answered: \"This junior's grandfather was indeed former Minister Meng.\"","Mo Qing was not unfamiliar with former Minister Meng at all. After all, the two had been colleagues in court for many years.","Although one had been a civil official and the other a military commander, they were both loyal and righteous people and had good impressions of each other.","As the grandson of Minister Meng, his character must also be quite good.","Especially after he returned to the northwest, everyone in the family, including his wife, had praised what an outstanding young man Meng Huaining was.","Now seeing the man standing before him, his etiquette done extremely properly, Mo Qing found it somewhat difficult to pick faults with him.","Then looking at his own precious daughter hiding behind her eldest sister-in-law while sneaking glances at Meng Huaining from time to time - if there were not so many people present, this girl would certainly find him to plead not to bully this young man.","Before meeting Meng Huaining, Mo Qing had thought of countless ways to make things difficult for him.","Now seeing his daughter's pleading gaze, in the end, he softened.","To put it bluntly, it was because he could not find faults with the other party, so he had no way to attack...","Although he had given up the idea of trying to make things difficult for his future son-in-law, Mo Qing still did not look very happy.","He pointed at an empty seat at the table and said, \"Since you've come at the right time, have a meal with us!\"","Facing his future father-in-law, Meng Huaining was still somewhat cautious. However, he deliberately concealed the nervousness he felt.","After greeting the elderly couple again, he obediently sat down in the seat Mo Qing had designated.","Old Lady Mo knew that her husband was being difficult with their son-in-law, so she introduced Meng Huaining to the eldest son and second son in order to ease the atmosphere and deflect everyone's attention.","That stubborn old man had been told countless times that their future son-in-law was an outstanding young man that the whole family looked favorably upon, yet he still would not approve of him.","Well, if he was unwilling to be polite to the young man, Meng Huaining could simply ignore him...","Seeing that his mother-in-law was bailing him out, Meng Huaining gave her a grateful smile.","At the same time, he also confirmed his previous guesses.","The sons of the Mo Family who had died were now all alive.","This was the first time meeting two uncles, so Meng Huaining naturally could not escape having to greet them properly.","Unlike their father, the eldest and second eldest brothers smiled and nodded at him.","Meng Hui Ning's mind which had previously been full of thoughts was soon distracted by the enthusiastic offering of stir fried pork belly with green chili peppers from the Mo brothers."]},{"number":448,"title":"Chapter 448: Blessed are the people of Yuncheng.","paragraphs":["Meng Huaining was no stranger to spicy food.","He had eaten Mo Family's cold spicy rabbit many times before, and even at home, there would always be a hint of that irresistible spiciness in the meals.","However, this green, spicy ingredient was something he had never seen before.","Mo Chuhan, who usually interacted with him the most, naturally had to explain more.","He took the initiative to clarify for Meng Huaining.","\"This is the chili pepper we grow ourselves. Jiudimei said that chili peppers are green when they are just ripe, and in a few days, they will slowly turn red. When dried, they become the chili pepper seasoning in the cold spicy rabbit.\"","In Meng Huaining's understanding, the chili peppers used by the Mo Family were obtained from foreigners.","He never expected that they would also grow such vegetables in the northwest.","Thinking about the livelihood of the people in the northwest, Meng Huaining couldn't help but speak up.","\"Since chili peppers can grow here, the people of Yun City are fortunate.\"","As soon as he finished speaking, he heard He Zhiran's voice at the door.","\"Brother Meng means to promote the cultivation of chili peppers?\"","He Zhiran was about to eat when Yuer said that Meng Huaining had come to the main house.","She put down her chopsticks and followed Mo Jiuye to see what was happening.","As soon as she reached the door, she heard someone coveting her chili peppers.","Meng Huaining was a shrewd person, and it was not difficult to judge from He Zhiran's tone that she was not willing to promote the cultivation of chili peppers.","Moreover, he was well aware of the situation in the Mo Family, where Jiuge and Jiusao were always in charge.","Even if he had this idea, he would need their consent. He had indeed spoken out of excitement.","He quickly stood up.","\"If Jiusao is unwilling, brother, I will never force it.\"","It's not that He Zhiran was stingy, although she had wealth that she couldn't spend, in order to use this money openly, she needed a few profitable deals in hand.","Making food with chili peppers was one of them, so she naturally wouldn't want to promote chili peppers too early.","She also knew that Meng Huaining was a good official dedicated to the people, and she was also aware of the hardships of the people in the northwest.","\"While these chili peppers are delicious, they can be said to be optional, unlike some other high-yielding grains that can feed the people.\"","Meng Huaining did want to make the people under his rule prosperous, at least enough to not go hungry.","He also understood the value of these chili peppers. If such a flavorful ingredient was used to make dishes like those of the Mo Family and sold in restaurants, it would definitely bring in a great profit.","The reason he couldn't control himself and spoke out was because he thought of the value of the chili peppers. If the people of Yun City could all grow chili peppers, sell them at a high price when ripe, they would undoubtedly earn a high income.","With money in the hands of the people, wouldn't it be easier to eat a full meal?","But now, the Mo Family relied on these means to make a living. If they spread the cultivation of chili peppers, wouldn't they be cutting off their source of income?","The more Meng Huaining thought about his thoughtless words, the more guilty he felt.","\"Brother Nine and Sister-in-law Nine, you don't have to take my words to heart. I just couldn't resist praising the deliciousness of these peppers for a moment.\" He Zhiran chuckled at his tone.","She was seated at the table with the sisters-in-law, supported by Mo Jiuye.","\"I know Brother Meng is a good official dedicated to serving the people. Don't worry, it won't be long before the sweet potatoes and potatoes in the fields ripen.","I've said before, planting sweet potatoes and potatoes is simple, yields are high, and they provide a strong sense of satiety. If you want the people to have enough to eat and wear, planting these is much more cost-effective than peppers.","Not only that, during the autumn harvest season, there's also corn. Dried corn can be ground into corn flour and cornmeal, which is great for making porridge and cakes.\" He Zhiran wasn't exaggerating at all.","Compared to the rough cornbread and cakes eaten by the poor families of this era, food made from corn is much tastier.","In fact, when the Mo family initially planted those peculiar crops, they were often talked about behind their backs by the villagers, and Meng Huaining had heard some of it.","But knowing the Mo Jiuye couple well, they were not reckless people.","Therefore, after He Zhiran carefully explained the benefits of these crops, Meng Huaining began to look forward to it.","\"If Brother Nine and Sister-in-law Nine are really willing to promote such good grains, you will be the benefactors of the people.\"","You see, the northwest region is barren, and it snows in winter. If the harvest is bad, many people starve to death every year.","The reason why the Mo family has not heard of people starving to death in Yun City is also because of Meng Huaining's arrival.","Last winter, many families had run out of food, and the whole family went out begging.","At that time, Meng Huaining made an important decision to use the limited food stored in the granary to help those who were on the brink of starvation.","At the same time, he also went to the prefecture several times to ask the prefect for help. The prefect was worn down by him and had no choice but to allocate some food from the granary to him.","But this food was far from enough. Meng Huaining also instructed people to work for those wealthy people, hoping they would lend a hand.","After much effort, Yun City welcomed its first winter without anyone starving to death.","But this was by no means a long-term solution. The winter in Yun City, where food and clothing are scarce, will come again. The grain in the granary was all used up last year, which was the most troublesome thing for Meng Huaining.","He was aware that this was something he, as the county magistrate, should worry about, without disturbing the harmony of the Mo family.","Anyway, when Sister-in-law Nine mentioned providing high-yield grains, he finally saw hope.","\"Brother Nine, Sister-in-law Nine, on behalf of the people of Yun City, I thank you for your benevolence. As long as we get through this harsh winter smoothly this year, with such crops next year, the people will no longer have to worry about going hungry.\"","The matter of the Mo family's crops was just a small episode of Meng Huaining's arrival, and once it was settled, the topic shifted.","Of course, this topic naturally shifted to the marriage between Meng Huaining and Mo Hanyue.","Such matters naturally needed to be mentioned by the elders, and Meng Huaining went to discuss the details.","Although the Mo Family provided Mo Hanyue with a courtyard as part of her dowry, Meng Huaining still purchased a residence in Yun City.","The residence was not very large and was located not far from the county yamen.","Meng Huaining had already arranged the bridal chamber there. On the day of the wedding, he would come to Xi Ling Village with a bridal sedan chair to pick up Mo Hanyue and take her to Yun City for the ceremony.","The newlyweds would stay there for two days, and when Mo Hanyue returned home after three days, they would move to Xi Ling Village.","It must be said that Meng Huaining's considerations were quite thoughtful.","He did not want Mo Hanyue to suffer any grievances and did not want others to think that the person she married was unwilling to prepare even a new house, or that the house was given by her family."]},{"number":449,"title":"Chapter 449: Crying Makes your makeup look Bad.","paragraphs":["Going to the city to worship at the ancestral temple was very different, which was enough to show Meng Huaining's respect for his wife. After the wedding, he accompanied her back to live in Xiling Village because of Mo Hanyue's preference.","In short, Meng Huaining's treatment of Mo Hanyue was comprehensive in every way.","Mo Qing listened to Meng Huaining's arrangements and had to say that he liked his son-in-law more and more as he looked at him.","The bit of discomfort in his heart had gradually disappeared like smoke.","...","In the blink of an eye, it was June 12th. The Mo Family was filled with joy and excitement, and it could be said that all courtyards were decorated with lanterns.","With the villagers watching like this, how could this be considered sending off a daughter to be married?","It was almost more grandiose than when a wealthy family in the city took a daughter-in-law.","These were all arranged by Mo Jiuye. His wife had everything available on Taobao e-commerce platform, and the prices were much cheaper than the goods sold in the stores of this era.","Except for Mo Yuance, all the Mo brothers gathered together. Even Mo Qing sat in an electric wheelchair that He Zhiran had asked Hu Cong to make and was pushed forward by his son to appear in front of everyone.","Nan Rui, Consort De, the Fang Chuanzhou family, the Xie Tianhai family, Hu Cong, the Mo Family's old subordinates and their families had arrived at the foot of the mountain early.","There was also Tang Mingrui. Because of the incident last time where he was wrongly framed for hiring someone to commit murder, he had become increasingly familiar with Meng Huaining.","Although both sides were people he considered to be good friends, he still planned to prioritize the Mo Family.","Therefore, he also became a guest of the Mo Family to escort the bride today.","The villagers also came with gifts. As the hostess of the Mo Family, Old Lady Mo was very capable in receiving all the different guests effortlessly.","He Zhiran's belly was too big. Madam He did not allow him to come forward. He stayed in a more distant place from the crowd with Li Auntie to watch.","Mo Hanyue wore beautiful red bridal clothes embroidered with exquisite peony flowers and sat in the bridal chamber.","The sisters-in-law were busy helping her tidy up her makeup.","\"Look at our Hanyue. Dressed up like this, she's just like a fairy who walked out of a painting.\"","Second Sister-in-law couldn't help but praise.","The other sisters-in-law also chimed in agreement.","\"Yes, Hanyue was born beautiful. These bridal clothes make her look even more beautiful.\"","\"It's still Ninth Brother and Ninth Sister-in-law who have great taste to buy such beautiful jewelry to make our sister look more beautiful.\"","\"...\"","Hearing the compliments from the sisters-in-law, Mo Hanyue shyly lowered her head.","At this moment, the makeup was complete. Old Lady Mo brought in a white-haired old woman.","\"Hanyue, this is Granny Zhao from the village. She is the oldest person in Xiling Village and the one with the most blessings of having a house full of children and grandchildren. I specifically asked her to come comb your hair.\"","When it came to combing the bride's hair, it was very particular in Dashun Kingdom.","It was necessary to invite an older, blessed woman with a house full of children and grandchildren to do it. This was also a blessing for the bride, wishing that the bride would be as healthy and blessed with children and grandchildren as the blessed granny in the future.","Despite Granny Zhao's age, her hair combing skills were very skilled, showing that she had done this kind of thing countless times before.","Soon, Mo Hanyue's thick black hair was perfectly coiled up. Although the style could not compare with the special female attendants who styled the mistresses’ hair in the noble families of the capital, Mo Hanyue was born beautiful. Even with a simpler hairstyle, she still looked charming and gorgeous.","Amidst waves of compliments from the sisters-in-law, Old Lady Mo reluctantly helped her daughter put on the red bridal veil.","\"Hanyue, from today onwards, you will be a married woman. In the future, you must restrain your little temper...\"","As she spoke, Old Lady Mo became choked up and couldn't continue.","Eldest Sister-in-law quickly stepped forward to comfort her, \"Mother, Hanyue is not going far for her marriage. You can see her every day when she returns in three days, so don't be upset.\"","Old Lady Mo also knew this was reasonable. Compared to the nine daughters-in-law in the family, except for Second Sister-in-law whose parents lived in the same village, the rest were all from the capital thousands of miles away. From the current situation of the Mo Family, unless their families were willing to come to the northwest to visit their daughters like Madam He, they would probably never see each other again in this lifetime.","Thinking of this, Old Lady Mo felt much more relieved.","She gently wiped away the tears from the corners of her eyes and continued to admonish Mo Hanyue about what she should and should not do after getting married.","Seeing her mother in tears, Mo Hanyue couldn't hold back her tears either.","Fifth Sister-in-law stepped forward with a handkerchief and dried her tears before they could stream out.","\"Hanyue don't cry, if you cry and ruin your makeup you won't look pretty.\"","Mo Hanyue couldn't hold back as soon as Fifth Sister-in-law tried to persuade her.","She threw herself into her mother's arms, sobbing.","\"Mother, please rest assured. I will take good care of our family like you and my sisters-in-law...\"","Seeing the mother and daughter like this, all the women in the room also had tears brimming their eyes.","At this moment, Mo Chuhan's voice came from outside.","\"Get ready fast, the new young master has arrived at the door.\"","Of the women closest to the door, Eighth Sister-in-Law pushed the door open and vaguely heard the sound of drums and music resounding outside. From the volume of the sound, they judged that Meng Huaining's welcoming team had just entered the village.","\"Dear husband, the welcoming team is clearly still very far. Why are you in such a hurry?\"","Eighth Sister-in-Law couldn't help but ask her husband. Hanyue’s makeup had just been ruined from crying and had not been touched up yet. If the new young master arrived now, it would really make them flustered.","Her husband had run with a flushed face and did not immediately answer his wife’s words. He strode over the threshold and quickly closed the door.","\"I won't let him take my sister so easily.\"","As soon as this was said, the women who were wiping away tears just now couldn’t help but burst into laughter.","Seeing her son’s earnestness to protect Mo Hanyue, Old Lady Mo reproached, “How difficult could you make it given that your sister has to marry out sooner or later?”","“Mother... Hanyue is getting married but I can’t let the lad think he can so easily get a wife.”","“Husband, what are you going to do?\"","What was he going to do?","Mo Chuhan had just hurriedly rushed back to block the door and hadn’t thought about how exactly he was going to make things difficult for Meng Huaining.","After a pause, he looked at the women in the house.","“Although Meng Huaining is talented and literary, he also knows some martial arts, but he is definitely not as skilled as us brothers. On such an auspicious day, we can’t spar with him right?”","“Does Eighth Brother mean he wants to compete in literary talent with him?” Second Sister-in-Law asked.","“Why not? Several sisters-in-law also come from scholarly families and are very literary. Why not have a literary competition with him?”","Ever since childhood Mo Chuhan liked fencing and martial arts. In terms of literary talent he was just like a blank sheet of paper. If it wasn’t for Old Lady Mo forcing him to study for several years, he probably wouldn’t even recognize many words.","So he could only place his hopes on the women.","“Eighth Brother, even though we have studied, how could we compare literary talent with the brother-in-law? Wouldn’t you just be making us embarrass ourselves?”","“Yes Eighth Brother, I just know some words.”","Second Sister-in-Law shook her hands again and again. “I’m not much better than Eighth Brother, don’t get me involved in this.”","Amidst their refusals, the sound of drums and music outside was getting closer and closer."]},{"number":450,"title":"Chapter 450: You Guys are so Confused.","paragraphs":["\"Tomorrow I will let my father and brothers know about this matter. No matter what, everyone needs to be mentally prepared,\" Mo Jiuye frowned as he spoke, clearly worried.","He Zhiran came up and gently comforted: \"We will meet the enemy's attack by every possible means, there are always more solutions than problems. Things have not become too serious yet. As long as we take precautions early, there will definitely be no issues.\"","At present, she could not do anything and could only comfort Mo Jiuye not to worry too much.","The next day, Mo Jiuye went to the second elder's yard. It just so happened that because of Mo Hanyue's marriage, the brothers were all there. He told them about the matter in public.","Mo Chuhan was impulsive and stood up first.","\"Our Mo family has been loyal to the court. If it weren't for brother Jiu, we would all have become Yuan Meng's sacrifices by now.","Although we all disdain to rebel, we can’t let people shit on our heads either.\"","Although the words were a bit vulgar, they spoke to everyone present.","The second elder also stood up indignantly.","\"Why don't we brothers secretly sneak into the capital and get rid of that dog emperor, so that he stops thinking about how to deal with our Mo family every day.\"","As soon as these words came out, people immediately echoed them, all thinking about assassinating Emperor Shunwu in the capital.","Just as Mo Jiuye was trying to stop them, the silent Mo Qing spoke up.","\"You are really confused.\"","The second elder was not convinced.","\"Dad, rather than waiting for people to bully us when they come, it's better to get rid of him early to eliminate future troubles.\"","\"Reckless!\" Mo Qing severely reprimanded his second son.","\"Dad, according to what brother Jiu said, even if we don't make a move, Emperor Shunwu will still frame us with the crime of deceiving the emperor, and in the end we still have to rebel.\" At this time, Mo Chuhan could best understand the mood of the second elder.","Mo Qing was not unable to understand the feelings of his two sons, he just did not agree with their approach.","\"Jiuye just said that the empress adopted the Fourth Prince. The Xue clan nurtured countless influences in the court to help Nan Heng ascend to the throne back then.","After Emperor Shunwu’s death, Nan Qi may not be the opponent of the Xue clan. Once the Fourth Prince succeeds to the throne, this world will completely become the Xue family’s world.","At that time, our situation will be dozens of times more difficult than when Emperor Shunwu was in power.\"","The reason why Mo Jiuye did not advocate assassinating Emperor Shunwu in the capital was for this reason.","\"Second elder, eighth elder, what I mean is, let's first try to undermine the Xue family's power, and then try to assassinate Emperor Shunwu, only then can we achieve lasting results.","Of course, we can’t relax our vigilance in the northwest either. If anyone secretly makes trouble, we must not let them off easily.”","Although the second elder and the eighth elder were a little impatient, they were not completely brainless either.","After being reminded by their father and Mo Jiuye, both of them lost their previous momentum.","\"Dad, brother Jiu, do we really have to just wait helplessly for death now?\"","\"We are not waiting helplessly for death, but making full preparations.\"","As Mo Jiuye spoke, he looked at the fifth elder.","\"Fifth elder, how many bombs have we made now?\"","\"One thousand bombs have been made, all stored by me on the mountain.\" The fifth elder said.","Mo Jiuye scanned everyone.","\"Seventh elder went south. It will take at least half a month for him to come back. Now our brothers plus Tao Ran, Liang Hao and the others add up to dozens of people.","We’ll gather everyone together in a moment and distribute the bombs to them while teaching them how to use them.","In addition, Rang Rang and I also have some repeating crossbows that can fire continuously up to twenty times.","We will equip everyone with weapons. Starting today, everyone will have to work a little harder to take turns guarding, to prevent intruders.","While protecting our own family, we must also take care of the villagers of Xi Ling Village and not let them get involved.\"","The eldest brother stood up.","\"I’ll go arrange this matter.\"","While the eldest brother went to gather people, Mo Jiuye also asked He Zhiran to purchase a large number of repeating crossbows and enough arrows on Taobao and store them in an empty room.","After preparations here, the eldest brother also gathered all the manpower at the foot of the mountain.","Mo Jiuye called a few people to take enough repeating crossbows and went up the mountain with his brothers to train everyone.","Considering the physical condition of the daughters-in-law, he only used one day to teach everyone about the bombs and repeating crossbows before returning home.","Next was the time for Mo Hanyue to return home. The newlywed little couple has since lived in the quadrangle courtyard in Xi Ling Village.","Meng Huaining was also happy about this.","The facilities and furnishings of the quadrangle courtyard were the same as those of the Mo brothers. The furnishings in the room were also very popular with young people.","Meng Huaining simply felt reluctant to leave this place.","In order to accompany his young and delicate wife, he handed over the yamen affairs to his subordinates to handle before the wedding, preparing to rest for a few days.","If Meng Huaining came to the Mo family occasionally, they would not notice anything. But after staying here for a few days, he discovered that the Mo brothers ran up the mountain every day.","At first, he thought that the Mo brothers went up the mountain to hunt. Later, he found that they did not have any game when they came back.","If it was those ordinary commoners it would be fine, but the Mo brothers, as martial arts masters, could not have come back empty-handed after going up the mountain.","He was sensible enough to know that the Mo family had secrets. Although he was now half a Mo family member, if the family did not want to tell him things they did not want him to know, it would be inappropriate for him to take the initiative to inquire.","Mo Jiuye was more attentive and had long noticed his brother-in-law's curiosity.","After discussing with He Zhiran, he decided to tell him some of the things.","After all, Meng Huaining would be living with them in the future. If some clues were discovered after a long time, it would be better to tell him in advance.","It was better than making him feel that the Mo family did not trust him enough, and then discovering some things slowly by himself.","Of course, the bombs secretly produced by the Mo family and the seventh elder's trip to the south to gather his former subordinates were automatically concealed by Mo Jiuye.","In fact, when Meng Huaining presided over Tang Mingrui's case of hiring a murderer to kill, he had already discovered something wrong with the Xue family.","Especially during the interrogation process, Xue Fan directly admitted that he was of the same clan as the empress. This made Meng Huaining feel that things were not simple.","Later, Xue Fan and that assassin also mysteriously died in prison, and those thugs inexplicably became idiots. If someone told him this had nothing to do with the Mo family, even beating him to death could not make him believe it.","At the same time, he also guessed that the Xue family choosing to open Jingxian Building in the northwest was most likely related to the Mo family.","Now after listening to Mo Jiuye's account, it completely confirmed his previous speculation.","He thought of the favor he had received from Fei Nanyu when he came to the northwest to take office. The purpose was to observe the movements of the Mo family.","Because of his relationship with the Mo family, he eventually chose to lean towards their side.","As a result, he never passed on any information related to the Mo family to Fei Nanyu."]},{"number":451,"title":"Chapter 451: Little White Is Back","paragraphs":["Mo Hanyue's makeup was redone by her sisters-in-law, and her red bridal veil was put back on.","At this moment, the little maid was nervous, listening to the increasingly loud drum music, as well as Eighth Young Master's intention to make things difficult for Meng Huaining, which made her both afraid and anxious.","In her perception, apart from Second Sister-in-Law, the literary skills of the other sisters-in-law were quite good. What if Meng Huaining was humiliated?","While she was worrying, Meng Huaining's wedding procession had already arrived at the door.","There were other elder brothers guarding the main entrance, and although they did make things a little difficult, they still let him into the courtyard.","Meng Huaining was escorted to the door. He bowed very courteously, then stepped forward and knocked on the door.","According to Old Lady Mo's intention, she did not want to make things difficult for Meng Huaining, but that willful Eighth Son insisted, so she was helpless.","At the same time, the old lady also wanted to see what literary skills this son-in-law from a scholarly family had.","The sisters-in-law were still young after all, and loved liveliness. Seeing that mother-in-law didn't object, they rushed to the door one after another.","Third Sister-in-Law's specialty was couplets, while Fourth Sister-in-Law was more enthusiastic about writing poems. There was also Sixth Sister-in-Law, who also showed her skills.","As a result, these questions that they considered quite advanced were simply unable to stump the eager-to-marry Meng Huaining.","In the end, Mo Chuyi looked at the defeated sisters-in-law resentfully, and unwillingly opened the door.","Meng Huaining rushed in first and saw Old Lady Mo. He solemnly knelt down and knocked his head on the ground.","\"Son-in-law pays respect to mother-in-law.\" After speaking, he knocked his head heavily on the ground three times.","What Old Lady Mo valued most was Meng Huaining’s scholarly family background. Thanks to Eighth Young Master today, she also got to see his literary talent.","At this moment, the more Old Lady Mo looked at her son-in-law, the more she liked him.","The way she addressed him also changed from the original \"Master Meng\" to \"Huaining\".","\"Huaining, please get up quickly.\" As she spoke, she stuffed a red envelope into Meng Huaining's hand, as money to mark the change in how she addressed him.","When Mo Family’s Eldest Brother saw that there was no clamor coming from his sister's room, he strode in.","Under his mother's direction, Eldest Brother gently carried Mo Hanyue on his back.","\"Hanyue, Eldest Brother will carry you onto the bridal sedan.\"","Mo Hanyue nodded lightly and lay on her eldest brother's broad back.","Everyone rushed out together, with Mo Qing being pushed in his wheelchair to send them off at the main entrance.","After Mo Hanyue got into the bridal sedan, Meng Huaining knelt down in front of the elderly couple again.","\"Father-in-Law, Mother-in-Law, please rest assured that Huaining will definitely take good care of Hanyue for life.\"","Seeing Mo Hanyue get into the bridal sedan, not only Old Lady Mo, but even Mo Qing in the wheelchair was somewhat tearful.","Old Lady Mo didn’t want their emotional loss of control to affect her daughter’s auspicious wedding hour just because the elderly couple was there. She quickly went up to help Meng Huaining stand up.","\"Good child, get up quickly. Hanyue will rely on you from now on.\"","Meng Huaining stood up with her help, bowed deeply to the elderly couple again, then turned around to urge the wedding procession to set off.","The guests from Mo Family’s side naturally had to be treated.","The banquet was prepared at noon, and there was still some time before it started.","The big watermelons from Mo Family's fields became the best refreshment to entertain the guests. In addition, there were peanuts, melon seeds, and fruit candy that He Zhiran had purchased from Taobao.com, with the packaging removed and placed on plates.","Apart from the peanuts and melon seeds, poorer people would not bear to eat them on ordinary days, but would not find them to be rare delicacies either.","But those sweet and juicy big watermelons and fruit candies immediately drew praise from everyone.","For many of Mo Family’s guests, big watermelons were nothing special.","Neither Mo Jiuye nor He Zhiran were petty. Selling the ripe watermelons to Tang Mingrui was one thing, they also gave some to acquaintances to let them taste.","However, the number of watermelons given away was still limited after all, and they would run out quickly when divided among the whole family.","Today at Mo Family, there were enough big watermelons for all the guests to have their fill.","As for those crystalline, translucent candy pieces, they were many times sweeter than the maltose candy they usually ate, and there were many different flavors. They simply made the guests sweet to their hearts.","As for the banquet, there was no need to elaborate. Some of the vegetables grown on Mo Family’s land had begun to mature, many of which were varieties that didn’t exist in this era. Naturally, the dishes made from them were extremely delicious.","It was not until the afternoon period of Shen that the banquet ended.","The enthusiastic villagers took the initiative to stay and help Mo Family clean up properly before leaving satisfied.","He Zhiran was kept under tight watch by Old Lady He. Afraid that something might happen to her as she was nearing childbirth, Old Lady He took her back home after the meal.","She had indeed been a little uncomfortable recently, mainly because her belly was too big and she often felt tired.","When she returned home, she was just about to take a nap when she heard Mo Jiuye's voice at the door.","\"Xiao Bai, you're back.\"","Following the voice as it drew near, Mo Jiuye had already brought Xiao Bai into the room.","He Zhiran also sat up.","\"Husband, did Xiao Bai bring any letters?\"","Mo Jiuye put Xiao Bai on the table.","\"Yes, I'll take them off now.\"","Although He Zhiran was eager to read the letter, she also knew of Xiao Bai’s hardship.","After Mo Jiuye removed the note from its leg, He Zhiran directly sent Xiao Bai into the space, and prepared its favorite food with her thoughts.","When Xiao Bai entered the space, it naturally went to \"catch up\" with Rice Ball. He Zhiran didn't bother with them, and read Fei Nanyu’s note together with Mo Jiuye.","It was less of a note and more like a letter. Because this time, Fei Nanyu wrote a lot of content and used larger sheets of paper.","The letter said—","Fortunately, Mo Jiuye had sent him the three Gu worms. Otherwise the Gu Master would not have succeeded in detoxifying several important ministers.","It was just that those people had been afflicted by Gu for quite some time, and their bodies were still very weak, but there was no longer any danger to their lives.","In addition, Fei Nanyu also reminded Mo Jiuye to be careful, because he discovered that the Empress’ clan had not been behaving recently.","He had already sent people to secretly keep watch on the Empress. If Xue Prime Minister had not been afflicted by Gu, he would have taken action long ago.","As for what actions, he has not yet discovered any definite leads.","At the same time, Fei Nanyu also urged Mo Jiuye to remember that it was the Empress’ clan who hated Mo Family the most back then. Because of Mo Jiuye’s relationship with Nan Qi, everyone would think that Mo Family belonged to the Prince of Qi’s party.","Although Mo Family had already been exiled to the northwest, as long as Mo Family still had its men, the Empress’ side would not let down their guard.","Just a few days ago, the Empress suddenly adopted a son.","The child was only seven years old now. It was said that Emperor Shunwu had been promiscuous while drunk, and favored a palace maid.","As a result, that palace maid became pregnant and gave birth to a boy.","At that time, afraid that there would be another prince to threaten Nan Heng’s status, the Empress planned to secretly execute the palace maid after discovering she was pregnant.","Fortunately, Empress Dowager discovered it early and stopped her in time.","Empress Dowager stated that if the Empress dared to plot to harm the imperial prince, she would no longer be fit to be Empress."]},{"number":452,"title":"Chapter 452: Make him completely disappear from this world.","paragraphs":["Due to the Empress Dowager's prestige, the Empress could only spare the palace maid's life, allowing her to give birth to the Fourth Prince safely.","Although the Fourth Prince was born safely, the Empress did not want his identity to be made public, let alone allow him to appear in public.","In front of Emperor Shunwu, she claimed that if the Emperor acknowledged this Fourth Prince, it would mean he was unprincipled as a ruler, having secretly associated with a lowly palace maid.","Not only that, the Empress also asked her own father, Xue Prime Minister, to secretly submit a memorial reminding Emperor Shunwu not to do anything that would damage his imperial image.","To save face, Emperor Shunwu listened to the words of the Empress and her father, abandoning the Fourth Prince and his mother to fend for themselves.","In the end, it was the benevolent Empress Dowager who could not bear to see the imperial offspring killed for no reason, and she kept reminding the Empress not to go too far.","As for other matters, the Empress Dowager did not interfere too much.","As a result, the days of the mother and son in the palace were like walking on thin ice. Eventually, under the direction of the Empress, the palace maid was tortured to death.","Although the Fourth Prince was in the palace, the Empress sent him to work with the eunuchs.","Now that Nan Heng was missing, in order to maintain her own position and that of the Xue family, the Empress had to find someone who could rival Nan Qi.","Therefore, she set her sights on the Fourth Prince.","The Empress went to Emperor Shunwu and said that ever since Nan Heng's disappearance, she had felt empty, and now the Fourth Prince had no mother, so she was willing to adopt him under her name so that she could have someone to rely on in her old age.","Emperor Shunwu also considered that his two sons were missing, and having only one prince would surely be criticized by his ministers. Moreover, the Fourth Prince was still young, and he never doubted that the Empress would have any ambitions. Thus, he readily agreed to the Empress's request.","Although Emperor Shunwu had never publicly recognized the Fourth Prince, paper could not contain fire. Nan Qi's people had already investigated his existence a year ago.","Back then, with Nan Heng and Nan Rui still around, he did not pay attention to an inconspicuous prince who was not recognized by the Emperor.","But now, he did not expect that this inconspicuous Fourth Prince would become the Empress's final chess piece.","Of course, Fei Nanyu could not write so much content on a piece of paper. His account was simpler, but Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran could read between the lines.","The main purpose of Fei Nanyu telling so much about the Fourth Prince was to remind Mo Jiuye to be more careful. The Empress did not know that the relationship between Nan Qi and Mo Jiuye had soured. Once Nan Qi succeeded, she would definitely try to pardon the Mo family's crimes. At that time, with Mo Jiuye's protection, it would be very easy for her Xue family to lose their foothold at court.","Even without Fei Nanyu's reminder, this was something Mo Jiuye would pay close attention to, especially since the Xue family had just opened the Jingxian Building in the northwest. This showed that the Empress's side was already making moves, it was just that Fei Nanyu had not noticed it yet.","Initially, they also knew that one of the three officials who were enchanted in the capital was the Empress’s father, Xue Prime Minister, but they did not know which of the three mother centipedes controlled General Jin.","Left with no other choice, the two of them could only choose to hand over all three mother centipedes to Fei Nanyu.","If it weren't for saving General Jin's life, after Xue Prime Minister was stung, even with imperial physicians helping to prolong his life, it would only delay his death.","Now, in order to save General Jin, it allowed that old fellow Xue Prime Minister to take advantage...","There was no alternative, neither He Zhiran nor Mo Jiuye wanted to dwell too much on these matters.","After putting down the letter, the couple's expressions were very solemn.","They believed it would not be long before news that the Mo men and Old Duke Mo were still alive would reach the capital.","Emperor Shunwu had two ways to deal with the situation if he did not want the Mo family men alive.","The first was to directly issue an edict, slapping the Mo family with another charge of feigning death to evade serving the country.","The other method was simpler: in order to eliminate a thorn in his side, he could send assassins here.","No matter how Emperor Shunwu dealt with the Mo family, they would inevitably be charged with rebellion.","\"Ranran, once something irreversible happens, take the women and children of our family and hide.\"","Mo Jiuye gently placed his hands on He Zhiran's shoulders, his tone extremely solemn.","He Zhiran also realized the gravity of the situation.","She had thought that with Nan Heng dead, the Empress would have no more chips to vie for power.","But she was still ambitious, adopting a Fourth Prince to contest the throne.","Although on the surface the Jingxian Building in the northwest established by the Xue family had been razed to the ground, even so, the Mo family could only buy temporary peace.","With no news from the people of the Jingxian Building in the northwest, the Xue family would surely be alarmed, and later they would send someone more capable to investigate. The news that the Mo men were all alive would certainly not remain a secret.","\"Husband, although things are developing in an unfavorable direction, there are still ways out.\"","\"What do you mean?\" Rebel?","He Zhiran nodded, \"What's wrong with that? When an incompetent ruler is in power, right and wrong are confused. Is it worth keeping such a person on the throne?\"","Mo Jiuye clenched his fist and slammed it heavily on the table.","After a long time he spoke, \"If Seventh Brother's trip to the south goes smoothly, he should be able to bring his men back in about half a month.","By then we will have produced enough bombs, and we brothers will hurry to train the old troops up the mountain.\"","\"Training one's own army is understandable, but have you ever thought that no matter whether the Mo family succeeds or fails, once Emperor Shunwu wants to deal with the Mo family, we will be slapped with the crime of rebellion.","Rather than fretting over this, let's not hesitate anymore. If he Emperor Shunwu does not make a move, fine. But once he does, we will become irreconcilable enemies.\"","She paused, then He Zhiran continued.","\"Of course, if no one harbors malicious intentions against the Mo family, I think the same as you, and am willing to live this simple and comfortable pastoral life in the northwest for the rest of my life.","But this needs to be built on the premise that no one provokes us. On the day we have to fight back, we must make them so afraid that they will not dare to have such thoughts again.\"","It was obvious from He Zhiran's words that she did not want to be a rebel either.","Moreover, she still had some understanding of the history of this dynasty. Although many things had changed now because of her arrival, that did not alter the big picture.","He Zhiran did not want to do things that would change history. Besides, according to history, Emperor Shunwu would pass away in another two years, and the empire would fall into Nan Qi's hands.","After Nan Qi ascended the throne, he basically ignored state affairs, leaving everything in court to be handled by Fei Nanyu.","Fei Nanyu was not the kind of unscrupulous person. At that time, the Mo family would surely obtain true peace.","It's just that according to recorded history, there were still two years before Emperor Shunwu's passing. For these two years, the best thing the Mo family could do was to keep their family safe without rebelling.","Mo Jiuye sat in the chair at the table, tapping the tabletop lost in thought.","How could he not be thinking the same as He Zhiran?","\"We still have to make adequate preparations for what needs to be done. I just hope Emperor Shunwu does not make too big of a move. As for others trying to secretly deal with the Mo family, I will take people into the capital and make them completely disappear from this world.\"","\"Well, currently we can't see what their next move is.\" He Zhiran said, looking down at her huge belly.","\"If I wasn't pregnant in my sixth month, we could go to the capital now and secretly eliminate the Empress's entire clan. There's no defense against a hidden arrow. We really can't let our guard down.\"","After the husband and wife talked so much, they still couldn't take any action for the time being."]},{"number":453,"title":"Chapter 453: Step by Step","paragraphs":["The chapter was posted incorrectly. Chapter 452 - if you can't find it, jump back two chapters to find it. The author was careless. Please understand, my friends.","At that time, he still thought he would be blamed by Fei Nanyu, but he did not know that Fei Nanyu was not very interested in the Mo Family's situation.","He only appreciated Mo Jiuye's abilities and hoped to make use of him one day. That's why he wanted to keep up with the Mo Family's developments from time to time.","Therefore, even if Meng Huaining told Fei Nanyu about the Mo Family's situation, Fei Nanyu would not make things difficult for the Mo Family. On the contrary, he might even lend a helping hand.","For example, with the letter that Little White brought back, if Fei Nanyu did not value Mo Jiuye highly, he would not have passed on that message.","Even for the sake of his beloved young wife, Meng Huaining decided to support the Mo Family.","But he also knew clearly that supporting the Mo Family one day could mean rebelling, of course this was also Meng Huaining preparing for the worst.","If the Mo Family could come up with other ways to resolve these crises, everything would naturally be resolved.","Meng Huaining looked very solemn: \"Ninth brother, no matter what happens to the Mo Family, please believe me, I will definitely stand by your side.","Also, when I get promoted in Yun City in the future, I will pay more attention. As soon as there is any sign of trouble, I will have eighth brother send the news back immediately.\"","As for other things, since the Mo Family did not let him participate, there was not much else he could do at the moment.","Mo Jiuye patted him on the shoulder, \"The Mo Family does not intend to offend the Emperor. Even when our whole family was exiled to the northwest back then, we never had any other intentions.","Our whole family went through great hardships to finally reunite. From now on, we just want to live a safe and peaceful life.","But some people just don't want the Mo Family to live well. For the sake of my family, some things may be unavoidable.\"","\"Ninth brother, I understand everything you said. Nothing stays the same forever. For now, we can take it one step at a time.\"","\"Mm, that's what we think too. No matter how those in power struggle in the royal court, as long as the Mo Family is not implicated, I will choose to turn a blind eye.\"","As the two were talking, Nan Rui hurried over from the direction of the village.","\"Young Master Mo, I have been looking everywhere for you. Turns out you were here.\"","Seeing that it was Nan Rui, Meng Huaining greeted him and then left to give them space.","\"What brings you looking for me, Rui?\" Mo Jiuye's eyebrows relaxed naturally, and he had a carefree look about him, as if nothing had happened these past few days.","Nan Rui walked up to him and took out a note from his robe to hand to him.","\"This is the latest news from the capital city sent by my people.\"","Mo Jiuye unfolded the note. Although the contents were not as detailed as what Fei Nanyu had written, they were roughly the same - all talking about the Empress adopting the Fourth Prince.","Mo Jiuye handed the note back to Nan Rui, deliberately pretending not to understand.","\"The Empress adopted the Fourth Prince. These are matters of your imperial family. Why tell me about this news?\"","He didn't know if Nan Rui could see through his ruse, but Nan Rui said:","\"Even before Nan Heng went missing, I noticed the Empress's clan was always targeting the Mo Family. Later, when Nan Heng disappeared, the Empress no longer had capital to compete and quieted down a lot.","I thought she would withdraw from the fight, but I didn't expect her to adopt a Fourth Prince now.","This shows that she and her maternal clan have not given up on that position. Everyone in court knows you have a good relationship with Nan Qi. Now that it is Nan Qi's time to appoint people, she will definitely spare no effort to eliminate anyone who can help Nan Qi.\"","I'm telling you this news so that you can be prepared after understanding.","No matter Nan Rui's motives for informing him, Mo Jiuye was grateful.","This was no trivial matter. If Fei Nanyu had not sent Little White with a letter, he might not have gotten the news from Nan Rui at all.","\"Thank you for letting me know, Rui. I will be more careful.\"","Seeing that Mo Jiuye still seemed indifferent, Nan Rui thought he did not take the matter to heart.","But he would still do what he should.","\"I came to notify you of this news, and also - I plan to return to the capital city tomorrow.\"","\"Return to the capital city?\" Mo Jiuye was somewhat surprised.","Ever since Nan Rui brought the Consort De to the northwest, no matter how Mo Jiuye tried to probe, the other party never showed any intention of returning to the capital city. His behavior today was quite puzzling.","Nan Rui revealed a sincere smile.","\"My mother also found out about things in the capital city.","She said it was the Mo Family who saved her life. Now that the Mo Family is in crisis, she asked me to do my best to help resolve it.\"","He paused, then continued:","\"As you know, there is no longer a Consort De in the palace now. I brought my mother away back then precisely because I did not intend to set foot in that pit of intrigue again.","So this time when I return to the capital, I cannot bring my mother along. I can only trouble you and your family to take good care of her, so that I can handle things in the capital city without worries.\"","Upon hearing this, Mo Jiuye could fully ascertain that Nan Rui truly harbored no ill intentions toward the Mo Family.","Not only that, he really wanted to help the Mo Family.","One must understand - Aunt Mei was the most important person in Nan Rui's life. If not so, he would not have committed the crime of deceiving the Emperor by faking her death, and then abandoned glory and wealth to bring her to this barren place to live incognito.","On the surface, Nan Rui said he asked the Mo Family to help take care of things as a favor. But in reality, Nan Rui had entrusted his greatest weakness to the Mo Family.","This was also Nan Rui's way of indicating his stand - I'm going to the capital city to repay your life-saving grace to my mother. I will never do anything to wrong the Mo Family.","Seeing Nan Rui like this, Mo Jiuye could not help but feel grateful.","However, Nan Rui and his mother had finally attained the life they wanted after much difficulty. He could not selfishly ask Nan Rui to continue wading in the muddy waters of court politics.","\"I understand your kind intentions, Rui. Aunt Mei is advanced in years and in poor health. You two finally managed to leave that place after great difficulty. You should not court danger for our sake again.\"","But Nan Rui insisted.","\"My mother and I have always been at a loss as to how to repay your life-saving grace. Now there is finally a chance. I cannot just sit by idly.\"","Seeing Nan Rui's solemn expression, he had clearly made up his mind. Mo Jiuye did not try to dissuade him further.","Moreover, having such a person to help in the capital city would be a huge boon for the Mo Family.","\"The political climate in the capital is about to change. If you get involved, it will only hasten the struggle between the Empress's faction and Nan Qi.","If something goes wrong, you may get embroiled as well. Have you considered how to handle it?\"","Mo Jiuye's words were rather euphemistic, but Nan Rui understood.","Everyone would think he had reappeared in the capital city for the sake of that position."]},{"number":454,"title":"Chapter 454: Vegetable Harvest","paragraphs":["\"I have always said that I have no interest in that position.","I just want to live a peaceful life with my mother forever.","The main reason I went to the capital this time is to deal with the Queen's faction because they pose the greatest threat to your Mo Family.","As long as the Queen's faction is completely overthrown, I won't compete with Nan Qi. Besides, Nan Qi has been friendly with you since childhood. If he successfully ascends to that position, I believe your Mo Family will also have a chance to rise.","By then, I will surely achieve my goals and retire.\"","The reason Nan Rui said this is that he was completely unaware that the relationship between Mo Jiuye and Nan Qi had already soured.","Nan Qi didn't make a move against the Mo Family, probably still cherishing their past brotherly bond.","Mo Jiuye never thought that Nan Qi, once he took that position, would pardon the Mo Family's crimes.","He just hoped that during his short time in power, he wouldn't target the Mo Family like Emperor Shunwu did.","However, the reason he fell out with Nan Qi concealed a huge secret. If it weren't for Nan Rui's earnestness in leaving Consort De in the northwest, Mo Jiuye wouldn't have revealed it.","Considering that Nan Rui took the risk of going to the capital for the sake of the Mo Family, Mo Jiuye had to give him a reminder.","\"When you arrive in the capital, you can secretly contact one of Nan Qi's staff members named Fei Nanyu. Perhaps he can help you.\"","As for Fei Nanyu's identity, Mo Jiuye planned to keep it a secret.","After Nan Rui left the northwest, he would have Little White deliver a message to Fei Nanyu, explaining Nan Rui's situation in going to the capital.","As long as these two can stand on the same front, they will both have an additional card to play in their struggles.","Whether Fei Nanyu chooses to reveal his true identity to Nan Rui is his personal issue.","Since Nan Rui has no intention of seizing the throne, once they establish contact, they will undoubtedly become a great help to each other.","Nan Rui nodded. \"When I arrive in the capital, I will contact him when necessary,\" he said, looking up at the sky.","\"It's getting late. I'll go back and get ready. We'll leave early tomorrow.\"","Mo Jiuye also returned to his parents' courtyard and told them about Nan Rui's journey to the capital.","Mo Qing couldn't help but sigh. \"I never expected that Nan Rui would be the most trustworthy one.\"","He wasn't a fool. Nan Rui left Consort De in the northwest precisely because he was afraid that the Mo Family wouldn't trust him.","Now that he has done this, if they continue to doubt him, there will be no trustworthy person in the world.","Although everyone understands why Nan Rui left Consort De, Old Lady Mo still plans to take care of her.","Not to mention anything else, the two of them get along very well now, just like good sisters.","\"Starting tomorrow, I will visit Consort De every day. She must be the most worried one about Nan Rui going to the capital. No matter what happens, I will spend more time with her.\"","\"Yes, it's up to you, Mother.\"","...","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran, this couple, talk about everything, so naturally, he had to tell his wife about Nan Rui's journey to the capital.","He Zhiran's view was the same as his. They both believed that Nan Rui was the person the Mo Family could trust nowadays.","She even thought about letting Nan Rui take the throne so that the Mo Family wouldn't have to worry about anyone coveting it anymore.","However, such matters couldn't be forced. Neither she nor Mo Jiuye had any intention of participating in the court's power struggles, nor did they want to alter history because of them.","In this regard, they could only go with the flow.","As long as no one harbored any ulterior motives towards the Mo Family, they could remain indifferent to all the glory and wealth.","When it was just getting dark, Mo Jiuye wrote a letter to Fei Nanyu and had Little White deliver it to the capital city.","He Zhiran's sleep had not been good lately. The two little ones in her belly were becoming more and more active, often waking her up just as she had fallen asleep.","In addition, her belly had grown so big that lying flat or on her side would make her feel tired, causing her to get up multiple times every night.","Mo Jiuye had always been a light sleeper. Whenever she made even the slightest movement, he would wake up and inquire about her well-being.","This kind of life continued for more than ten days, and the time entered early July.","Many vegetables in the Mo Family's fields had already ripened.","Although He Zhiran didn't find these vegetables particularly fresh, she had personally brought them here and witnessed the process of planting, watering, and fertilizing. For her, it was a different kind of experience.","It could be said that she was looking forward to a bountiful harvest of vegetables and grains in the first year of cultivation in the northwest.","And indeed, it was a bountiful harvest.","Madam He accompanied her daughter to the fields to see everyone picking vegetables, giving her a sense of wonder.","Looking at the baskets filled with vegetables in the field, many of which she had never seen before.","Madam He carefully approached the vegetables with He Zhiran and kept asking about their names.","In order to satisfy her mother's curiosity, He Zhiran patiently explained the names of the vegetables to her and even had Yu Er cook a table full of dishes using these greens.","Many villagers from Xi Ling Village were helping to pick the vegetables.","Someone saw a bell pepper fall to the ground and rot halfway, feeling a bit regretful, so they picked it up and asked He Zhiran.","\"This is from the Ninth Young Master's family. It's rotten halfway. Can I taste it?\"","He Zhiran wasn't the kind of stingy person.","\"Auntie, if you want to taste it, pick a fresh one. Just throw away the rotten one!\"","Auntie kept waving her hands.","\"No, no, such precious vegetables shouldn't be wasted. I'm just curious about the taste. Just let me try this one.\"","As she spoke, Auntie had already peeled off the half that had rotted and took a bite.","The bell pepper was thick and didn't have the spiciness of other peppers.","Especially since these seeds came from He Zhiran's space, the vegetables that grew from them were even more flavorful.","After taking a bite, Auntie couldn't stop praising.","\"These vegetables are really delicious, and they have a sweet taste.\"","Seeing that she liked it, He Zhiran took a few from the bamboo basket beside her and handed them to her.","\"Auntie, if you like them, take a few home. Bell peppers are delicious when stir-fried with meat or eggs.\"","Auntie was indeed won over by the taste of the bell pepper but didn't want to profit from someone else and take their things.","He Zhiran received a few sweet peppers from Liang Hao and quickly turned to work in the field, saying, \"Thank you for the vegetables from your family, Laojiu. You can sell them for money.\"","Seeing Auntie walking away, He Zhiran helplessly put the sweet peppers back in the bamboo basket.","At that moment, Liang Hao returned with Tang Mingrui.","Tang Mingrui's watermelon business made another big profit, and now he was waiting for the Mo Family to have other things to sell so that he could approach them!","He had seen those strange vegetables planted by the Mo Family in the fields as he passed by.","Today, he heard from Liang Hao that those vegetables had ripened a lot, so he left everything else to his subordinates and personally came to Xi Ling Village."]},{"number":455,"title":"Chapter 455: Don't be afraid when I'm here.","paragraphs":["Seeing so many bamboo baskets placed on the ground, Tang Mingrui was like a curious baby, pulling Liang Hao along the way and asking questions.","Liang Hao had been involved in planting on the land, so he was more or less familiar. After explaining all the way, Tang Mingrui's cognition was also completely refreshed.","Tang Mingrui was naturally well-informed, but more than half of these vegetables were still ones he had never seen before.","For example, the red tomatoes, the bell peppers that looked like lanterns...","He was not unfamiliar with potatoes. When he came to the Mo family before, he had seen them on the dining table. In order to satisfy his curiosity, He Zhiran had also shown him what potatoes originally looked like.","There were also some green leafy vegetables that he had never seen before.","In short, he was convinced of one thing in his heart - the products of the Mo family must be the best quality.","Even if his own restaurant could not use up all these vegetables, if they were taken to the market for sale, they could definitely sell for a sky-high price.","After gaining a thorough understanding, Liang Hao took him to He Zhiran.","With He Zhiran there, business talk did not need Mo Jiuye.","She made an agreement with Tang Mingrui that no matter how many such vegetables were produced on the Mo family's land, the latter would exclusively purchase them, with profits still divided 50/50.","Considering that vegetables were not easy to store and it was the hot July weather, He Zhiran was liable to suffer losses. So she intended to give Tang Mingrui 10% more profit, but he refused.","In Tang Mingrui’s own words, “Sister-in-law, you underestimate my business abilities. Not to mention these vegetables, even if there were twice as many, I could still sell them all out at top speed.”","In order to obtain profits earlier, Tang Mingrui went back to the city after seeing the vegetables to hire people to transport them.","By dusk, all the vegetables harvested from the house that day had been taken away by him already.","The ripening of the vegetables was staggered. As long as people came to pick every day, looking at the current quantity, material could be supplied to Tang Mingrui continuously for at least a month.","He Zhiran directed the workers to stop for the day and continue tomorrow.","In addition to having Lan'er distribute their wages, she also gave each person some fresh vegetables to take home, not only that, but He Zhiran also instructed Lan'er to teach everyone how to cook them.","Everyone smiled from ear to ear as they took the generous wages and the vegetables given to them by He Zhiran.","Especially since Tang Mingrui had been discussing vegetable prices with He Zhiran earlier, and many people had heard bits and pieces.","They could confirm that these vegetables were priced higher than meat, yet others had generously given them these.","They couldn’t bear to eat such expensive vegetables...","He Zhiran had already anticipated that the villagers might come up with the idea of taking the vegetables into the city to sell them, which would definitely affect her cooperation with Tang Mingrui. Therefore, before everyone left, she made it very clear:","These vegetables were for them to sample. If she ever discovered someone selling them in the city, they would no longer be allowed to come work at the Mo house.","With He Zhiran's reminder, the villagers did not dare sell the vegetables in the city, no matter how reluctant they were.","Seeing the villagers had all left, Madam He urged He Zhiran, “Ranran, you have been out here all day. Your health must be suffering. Go back and rest early.”","Coming to the Northwest had truly broadened her horizons - not only could she eat countless delicacies, she could also see so many vegetables she had never seen before.","If she hadn’t been considering her daughter’s health, Madam He would not have wanted to leave the fields.","This kind of life was much better than Beijing, not boring at all.","Madam He even had the thought that she did not want to leave this place.","He Zhiran was indeed more tired today than usual. Although she didn't really do anything, Lan'er had brought over a small stool for her to sit on when she was tired, but somehow she still felt a dragging sensation in her stomach.","In her previous life she was a doctor, but not an obstetrician. As an unmarried woman, she really did not have much understanding about omens before giving birth.","“Mother, my stomach feels heavy today.”","Hearing this, Madam He immediately changed her expression.","“Ranran, you should be about to give birth!”","She herself had given birth twice, and would indeed have this feeling of heaviness before birth.","However, it was not always consistent - when she gave birth to her eldest, this bodily sensation occurred two days prior, but when birthing He Zhiran, it appeared in the morning and she gave birth before nightfall.","“Ranran, this is your first child, it should not come too fast. Don’t panic for now. Mother will walk you back slowly while supporting you. If you feel uncomfortable anywhere, you must tell Mother.”","As she spoke, Madam He ordered Lan'er to quickly find Mo Jiuye.","Zhang San had not yet returned from Beijing with the esteemed gynecologist, and now that He Zhiran was showing signs of labor, Madam He could only place her last hopes on Mo Jiuye.","It was just as the saying goes, speak of the devil - she had thought He Zhiran was quite stable these last few days without signs of premature birth, but as things stood, her wishful thinking had been too optimistic.","In fact, He Zhiran was not panicked at all. She was also aware that with a twin pregnancy, she was bound to give birth a bit early.","She had calculated a mid-July due date herself, and it was only July 5th now, just 10 days sooner than expected.","Supported by Madam He, He Zhiran could clearly feel that her palms were already soaked with sweat.","“Mother, don't worry, I can safely give birth.”","Although extremely anxious inside, Madam He did not want to reveal these negative emotions.","“Mother is not worried. Jiuye has been studying delivery methods for so long, you will definitely be alright. Mother is just overexcited at the thought of being able to meet my two little grandsons soon.”","The mother and daughter comforted each other as they walked back home. Mo Jiuye, still busy working in the fields, rushed over in an instant upon hearing from Lan'er that his wife was uncomfortable - it could be said that he completely ignored everything else to fully utilize his qinggong. In the blink of an eye he appeared before He Zhiran.","\"Ranran, Lan'er said you weren't feeling well. Where exactly are you uncomfortable?\"","Seeing how flustered he looked, it was fair to say he was even more distressed than Madam He.","\"Husband, don't panic. Just now I only felt some heaviness in my stomach!\"","He Zhiran wanted Mo Jiuye to calm down - if this feeling really was a sign of impending labor, it would be best for him to make preparations in advance.","As soon as she finished speaking, Madam He could no longer remain unfazed.","\"Jiuye, Ranran must be going into labor. Childbirth for a woman is like walking through death's door. You must not let your guard down!\"","Mo Jiuye had just steadied his emotions a little, but hearing his mother-in-law's words made them roil again.","His hand holding He Zhiran's kept shaking uncontrollably.","\"Ranran, don't be afraid with me here. I won't let you walk through any door of death.\""]},{"number":456,"title":"Chapter 456: You gotta see if she's having a baby.","paragraphs":["Mo Jiuye was really more and more afraid the more he talked about himself, even though he hadn't been this nervous even the first time on the battlefield.","All along the way, he pulled He Zhiran with him, speaking incoherently.","This was the first time He Zhiran had seen him like this, and didn't know what to say to make his emotions more stable.","Of the three people, it looked like only she, the one about to give birth, was the calmest.","Returning to her family's courtyard house, Madam He immediately ordered Li Auntie to go call Old Lady Mo over.","Facing her own daughter giving birth, Madam He felt like an ant on a hot pan, without a clue what to do.","Not much later, Li Auntie called Old Lady Mo over, along with her sisters-in-law.","Old Lady Mo also clearly knew the danger of a woman giving birth to twins, but someone who had seen countless storms would still be much calmer than others.","Because there was a woman about to give birth in the house, Old Lady Mo had already asked around clearly that there was a midwife in the village who reportedly had over twenty years of birthing experience.","In this era, women gave birth by asking a midwife, and rich families would also ask a doctor to stand by, so that if the birthing mother encountered any danger, the doctor could provide timely treatment.","On the way over, she had already sent someone to the village to ask the midwife to come over, and told Liang Hao to rush into the city to ask a doctor.","At this time, He Zhiran was being supported sitting on the bed by Mo Jiuye.","In fact, she didn't feel any discomfort at this time. It was probably because she had been out all day that she just felt some fatigue.","Old Lady Mo sat at the bedside, holding He Zhiran's hand.","\"Ranran, don't be afraid. Your mother and I will be here with you the whole time.\"","He Zhiran could see that although her mother-in-law looked calm on the surface, she was also extremely nervous inside.","\"Mother, I'm not afraid. It's just giving birth. I can do it.\"","Seeing her say this, the Third Sister-in-Law came over with red-rimmed eyes.","\"Little Sister-in-Law, we all know you are working hard. We will all be with you. After the baby is born, you won't need to worry about anything.","There are so many sisters-in-law in the house. We'll take turns looking after the baby, and make sure you can properly rest after birth without any hardship.\"","\"That's right Little Sister-in-Law. We sisters-in-law can help you take care of the babies. But with only two, that's a bit few. We don't know how long we'll have to wait for our turn to look after them for a day.\" The Eldest Sister-in-Law spoke with a slightly joking tone in order to relieve everyone's tension.","This was indeed quite effective. The women all said they wanted to be first to help the Little Sister-in-Law look after the babies on the first day.","Following that was the scene of sisters-in-law scrambling to be the first to help the Little Sister-in-Law take care of the children, with no one wanting to fall behind.","With this scene occurring, it temporarily made everyone forget about He Zhiran's danger.","While everyone was discussing seven ways to eight who would take care of the babies first, the midwife Zhao had already been brought over.","Seeing the person arrive, Old Lady Mo hurriedly got up to ask:","\"Midwife Zhao, please help check on my daughter-in-law quickly. She was in the fields for a rather long time today, and after coming back discovered a feeling of heaviness in her stomach.","There are still about ten days until her due date. Please take a look and see if she's going to give birth now.\"","In her lifetime, Zhao Midwife had helped with the births of countless babies. She had encountered a twin pregnancy once before as well.","That time, with her own eyes she saw the birthing mother and three lives lost because of a difficult labor.","Therefore, she was extremely reluctant at heart to help a pregnant woman with twins give birth.","If it wasn't for Old Lady Mo finding her many times and offering ample payment, she truly would not have wanted to make this trip.","When Zhao Midwife now looked at He Zhiran, it was as if she was looking at someone on the brink of death, with eyes full of pity.","However, as a midwife, it was not good for her to show too much in front of the pregnant woman. She could only nod heavily towards Old Lady Mo with a solemn expression.","\"Don't hurry first. Let me examine her.\"","In He Zhiran's mind, she wanted to do a full examination after everyone left and she entered her medical space.","But seeing everyone's anxious and concerned manner, she didn't have the heart to tell them to leave, and could only let Zhao Midwife examine her.","Although called an examination, Zhao Midwife also just relied on her experience to feel He Zhiran's stomach and ask about the circumstances.","After examining, Zhao Midwife's expression relaxed somewhat.","To tell the truth, Zhao Midwife was still very skilled at examining single births. As for twin births, she had only encountered that one time, and didn't have much experience.","The examination was also just feeling the babies' heartbeats. She couldn't give a full account of the specific circumstances even if asked.","She told everyone: \"The feeling of heaviness in the stomach is indeed a sign that birth is approaching. She has only just started feeling discomfort. I don't think there will be much movement today.\"","\"Let this old woman give you all some advice. Those with no business here should go back early to rest. With everyone crowded around watching her, the Ninth household will also feel nervous. This is extremely bad for her giving birth.\"","This just happened to align with what He Zhiran was thinking.","After all, she was a doctor who had seen life and death. Her views on women giving birth were still stuck in her own understanding.","It was indeed very difficult and inevitably painful for women to give birth, even in completely normal situations.","If nothing else, she had already taught Mo Jiuye the c-section surgery, and also had that against-the-heavens medical space. No matter what, there was no possibility of her being in danger.","But facing the upcoming birth, He Zhiran was still inevitably nervous.","However, no matter how strong she was mentally, facing the anxious manner of her family members, she would naturally feel an increased mental burden.","After giving birth ten times, Old Lady Mo saw that Zhao Midwife spoke this way, and her mood relaxed somewhat. She pulled Zhao Midwife to ask:","\"What is the position of the babies in my daughter-in-law's womb?\"","When she was in the capital, she always asked a rather famous midwife from the capital city to help her give birth.","At that time, the midwife would always first check her fetal position.","Seeing Zhao Midwife examining He Zhiran's stomach in the same way, she wanted to understand more so she would know what to expect.","It was important to know that an abnormal fetal position was the main cause of difficult labor for women. Especially since He Zhiran was pregnant with twins, if it really was an abnormal fetal position, it would be fatal.","Asked about the fetal position, Zhao Midwife was clearly somewhat embarrassed, but she still chose to tell the truth.","\"I'm sorry, Lady Mo. Your ninth daughter-in-law is carrying twins. The two babies are squeezed tightly together. I have no way to judge this point.\"","Although Madam He had not given birth as many times as her mother-in-law, she was also very concerned about the question just now.","Hearing the midwife's answer, she completely lost her composure.","Madam He looked at Zhao Midwife tearfully.","\"Do you mean that currently there is no way to determine whether or not my daughter can give birth smoothly?\"","Old Lady Mo saw that her mother-in-law was overthinking things out of concern. Fearing that Zhao Midwife would say something unfortunate here that would affect He Zhiran, she hurriedly pulled the person away.","\"Mother, my daughter-in-law is carrying twins. Zhao Midwife can't see the fetal position but that is definitely not what you're thinking...\"","While speaking, Old Lady Mo was also blinking vigorously at Madam He behind her back, signaling her not to ask any more questions."]},{"number":457,"title":"Chapter 457: Husband, don't be nervous","paragraphs":["Madam He had just asked those words and regretted them too.","She was too nervous and actually forgot to think about He Zhiran.","Now that Old Lady Mo reminded her, she hurriedly closed her mouth.","\"What Granny Zhao said makes sense. It's normal that you can't tell the position of twins.\"","The sisters-in-law also saw that something was wrong, and they crowded around the two old madams and Granny Zhao and left He Zhiran's room.","The Eldest Sister-in-law took the lead.","\"Since even Granny Zhao said so, Ninth Younger Sister will not give birth today. Let's go back early and let Ninth Younger Brother and Ninth Younger Sister rest early and build up their strength to safely deliver our little nephew or niece.\"","\"Yes, you should all go back and rest.\" Old Lady Mo echoed, and exhorted Lan Er.","\"You stay here. Come get me immediately if there is any movement.\"","\"Old Madam can rest assured that Lan Er will stay here the whole time.\"","While giving her promise, Lan Er followed the crowd out of the room and thoughtfully closed the door.","Seeing everyone had left, He Zhiran smiled helplessly at Mo Jiuye, who was still standing there in a daze.","\"Husband, don't be nervous. I'll go check inside the space now.\"","Hearing her reminder, Mo Jiuye also came back to his senses.","He knew Lan Er was still guarding outside the door. He was just about to go instruct her that they were going to rest and not to let anyone come disturb them unless it was very urgent.","Before he could take any action, he heard the voices of Old Lady Mo and Madam He again.","\"The doctor is here. Let him take a look at Ranran first, so we can sleep peacefully tonight.\"","He Zhiran smiled helplessly at Mo Jiuye again and jerked her chin towards the door.","\"Since the doctor is already here, it would be impolite not to let him examine me. Otherwise, I'm afraid the family won't be able to sleep well tonight.\"","\"Mm,\" Mo Jiuye responded and opened the door from the inside.","Old Lady Mo and Madam He were together, and behind them was a man who looked fifty-something years old with a beard.","Mo Jiuye let the people into the room.","\"Doctor, please help examine my daughter-in-law.\"","Ever since she found out she was pregnant, He Zhiran had always gotten her checkups done inside the space. She had never consulted a doctor here before.","She also wanted to see what this era's doctors were capable of, and very cooperatively extended a wrist.","The doctor put down his medicine box and sat in a chair to take He Zhiran's pulse. Not much later, his brows were tightly locked.","\"You're pregnant with twins?\"","\"My wife is indeed pregnant with twins. Doctor, do you have any good solutions?\"","Mo Jiuye anxiously asked.","He had originally thought he had learned how to perform a C-section, but when he considered that the person he would have to operate on was his own wife, that he would have to personally take a knife and cut open his wife’s stomach, whenever he imagined that scene, he would inexplicably feel suffocated.","If the doctor could come up with a way for his wife to give birth smoothly, it would avoid having to use the knife, which would not only spare him from enduring tremendous psychological pressure, but also prevent any scars from being left on his wife’s perfect skin.","The doctor got up with a helpless shake of his head.","He was much more sensible than Granny Zhao and did not open his mouth in the room, but was the first to walk out the door.","Everyone except He Zhiran followed him out.","The doctor stood in the yard and, not bothering to look around the distinctive quadrangle courtyard, said in a deep voice:","\"From her pulse, the mother and children are very healthy and strong.\"","\"Doctor, do you mean to say that my wife will absolutely have no problem giving birth?\"","Upon hearing this, Mo Jiuye was thrilled. As long as his wife and two children were healthy and strong, what did he have left to worry about?","However, the doctor's next words soon dragged his beautiful mood down into the abyss.","\"In my many years of medical practice, I have seen pregnant women with twins before. They and the fetuses were very healthy before birth, but those who could actually give birth to twins smoothly with the safety of mother and children were few and far between.\"","Having said that, the doctor had already walked towards the outside of the yard, still saying:","\"This lady has no physical issues. Whether she can give birth smoothly depends on her fortune. Even if I stay here, I would be powerless to help. So I shall take my leave now.\"","Seeing the doctor about to leave, Old Lady Mo hurried forward to stop him.","\"Doctor, please stay. In case my daughter-in-law runs into any danger during childbirth, you can also treat her in time. Rest assured, for this consultation fee, we are willing to pay ten times the price, how about it?\"","She was also anxious. Asking the doctor to come over in the first place was to give He Zhiran extra protection during childbirth.","If the doctor left, and if something bad happened to her daughter-in-law, wouldn't they be left without even a thread of hope?","At this point, even Madam He was in tears. She silently cursed Zhang San and her Old Master for being incompetent.","It had already been over a month since Zhang San left this place, yet there was no news from him at all.","If he could bring the gynecology saint here at this time, her daughter and grandchildren could be saved.","Just as Madam He was about to step forward to join her mother-in-law in pleading with the doctor to stay, faint hoofbeats were heard from afar.","The sky was already dark at this hour, and not only the Mo family, even villagers rarely went out and moved around.","And in the whole village, only the Mo family had a carriage. The carriage that Liang Hao took to fetch the doctor from the city was parked in front of the door where everyone could see.","Old Lady Mo didn't bother to continue blocking the doctor. Of course, after hearing about the ten times consultation fee, the doctor was already disinclined to leave anyway, and just stood there. As long as they said another word to retain him, he could reluctantly stay...","At the same time, Mo Jiuye had already strode out. \"I'll go take a look.\"","Not having walked far out, he saw a carriage speeding towards him.","Before Mo Jiuye could walk up to check, Second Brother who lived in the east side had already come out of his house to stop the carriage.","At the same time, a group of dogs also chased up and surrounded the carriage, barking nonstop.","Second Brother first ordered the dogs to leave before walking up to the carriage.","The carriage was forced to stop, and Zhang San said to the carriage interior, \"Eldest Young Master, this is the Mo family's territory.\"","He Ziming opened the curtain and got out of the carriage, facing Mo family’s Second Brother directly.","Second Brother did not recognize the visitor, but he could hear the carriage driver spoke in a Beijing accent.","\"Who are you looking for?\"","He Ziming was also unfamiliar with Mo family’s Second Brother. But anyone who could appear on Mo family territory must be someone from the Mo family.","He cupped his fists towards Second Brother.","\"I am He Ziming, He Zhiran's elder brother.\"","\"You are the He family's Eldest Young Master?\" Upon hearing He Ziming report his family status, Second Brother immediately dropped the stern look on his face, and his tone became much gentler.","At this time, Mo Jiuye had also walked over. Naturally, the brief dialogue between the two did not escape his ears.","Moreover, with the moonlight he could also see that the one driving the carriage was Zhang San who had sent his mother-in-law to this place last time.","He Ziming was not a stranger to Mo Jiuye either. Although they had only met on the day he married He Zhiran, Mo Jiuye had an extremely deep impression of the moist and beautiful appearance of his big brother-in-law."]},{"number":458,"title":"Chapter 458: The Holy Hand of Women","paragraphs":["He Ziming warmly stepped forward and cupped his fists towards Mo Jiuye: \"Brother has travelled a long way, please come back home with me first and we can talk slowly.\"","He Ziming was not unfamiliar with Mo Jiuye either, who was a great general who had made outstanding contributions to Da Shun. Not only had he seen him a few times when Mo Jiuye returned triumphantly and paraded through the streets, but also on the day his younger sister got married.","\"Brother-in-law, how is Ran Ran's condition now?\"","What He Ziming cared most about at the moment was his younger sister's physical condition. He was afraid that something might happen to his sister if he came late.","Hearing his uncle ask about his wife's condition, Mo Jiuye subconsciously looked towards the carriage.","Although he had learned how to perform a Caesarean section, he still hoped to avoid operating on his wife if possible. He just hoped that the gynecological expert his uncle brought this time could come to the Northwest smoothly. This way, his wife would have a chance to give birth without surgery, which would provide an extra layer of safety.","However, he found that the carriage was completely empty.","In order not to shatter the glimmer of hope in his heart, Mo Jiuye looked behind the carriage again, hoping that he had missed it and there were two carriages, with the gynecological expert sitting in the one behind.","But this only led to his disappointment.","\"Didn't you bring the gynecological expert with you this time, brother?\"","Seeing him ask this, He Ziming laughed lightly with his fist against his lips.","\"What if I say that I am the famous gynecological expert everyone talks about, would you believe it, brother-in-law?\"","Mo Jiuye was stunned.","When he was in the capital city, although he didn't have much contact with this uncle-in-law, he had heard that He Ziming had read widely since childhood and rarely socialized externally.","Especially when he heard recently that He Ziming had passed the imperial examination with flying colors, it just verified that he was well read.","If He Ziming claimed his own learning, Mo Jiuye would have no doubts. But what did he just say?","He said he was the famous gynecological expert in the capital city?","How is this possible?","Seeing Mo Jiuye froze there, Zhang San stepped forward to help explain:","\"I didn't hide this from Sir, our young master is actually the famous gynecological expert.","When I sent the letter back to my master, Madam told him to find this gynecological expert to come to the Northwest no matter what.","Everyone in the capital city knows that the whereabouts of the gynecological expert are unpredictable. If you want to find him, you have to go to the locust tree outside the south gate of the capital city and leave a note on it.","The gynecological expert will send someone to collect the notes every now and then, and then choose a few families with serious conditions to see.","The most important thing is that the gynecological expert comes and goes without a trace. Whenever he shows up, he is always dressed in white with a hood on, and no one knows his true identity.","When my master heard that young lady was pregnant with twins, he wanted to ask the gynecological expert for help. We could only try our luck by leaving a note on the locust tree.","In order to make sure the gynecological expert noticed our request, my master and I went to hang lots of notes on the locust tree every day.","My master was very worried that the gynecological expert might not see our request. He was also afraid that if the expert didn't check the notes for some time, even if we found him later, it would be too late for my young lady to give birth.","When the young master saw my master and I running to the city gate every day, he asked about it and then realized that we were trying to find the gynecological expert to save my young lady in the Northwest...\"","Minister He was shocked when he heard that his own son was the famous gynecological expert in the capital city. After all, he had taught this son himself since childhood. Other than reading, all this son did was read. When did he become a gynecological expert?","Though others didn't know, He Ziming actually started learning medical skills inspired by He Zhiran.","When he was eight years old, he noticed that his mother would have abdominal pain about once a month.","At that time, He Zhiran was five years old and spent all day sticking with her mother.","When the little girl wanted her mother to hug her one day, her mother said she didn't feel well today and would hug her tomorrow.","The little girl didn't get what she wanted and said distressedly, \"Mother is sick, Ran Ran wants to learn medicine to treat mother.\"","These words happened to be overheard by He Ziming, who had just finished school. He thought, how could a little girl practice medicine to treat her mother's illness?","As her brother, he naturally had to lead the way for his sister.","However, his father was usually very strict with him, so it was impossible for him to let He Ziming learn any medical skills.","Therefore, he could only secretly buy books to teach himself.","After learning for a period of time, He Ziming was able to confirm that his mother had a gynecological disease that was very difficult to treat.","Otherwise, why did the doctor come almost every month but his mother's condition never seemed to improve?","He Ziming secretly made up his mind to specialize in gynecological medicine in the future and definitely improve his mother's health.","Without compromising his studies, he worked hard to secretly learn gynecological medicine.","Once when he was out travelling on horseback, he was suddenly blocked by a crowd of people standing around up ahead.","When he got off his horse to check, he learned that a pregnant woman had gone into premature labor while traveling outside. She couldn't continue traveling in the carriage and was sitting on the ground writhing in pain. Her maid kept pleading to passersby to be kind enough to please find a doctor nearby.","Having studied gynecology for many years, He Ziming naturally knew that the pregnant woman should give birth immediately to avoid danger.","But as a man, it was inappropriate for him to assist a woman in childbirth. He could only ask the maid to find something to cover her mistress with.","The maid went to get a cloak from the carriage and covered her mistress with it.","He Ziming checked the woman's pulse through the cover and then pressed on her abdomen, before instructing the maid what to do next.","Under He Ziming's guidance, the woman successfully gave birth to a child on the official road.","This act of He Ziming was witnessed by an elderly man who also happened to pass by.","Right after the woman had given birth smoothly and He Ziming was getting ready to leave on horseback, he was stopped by the old man.","The elder only told He Ziming that he had the natural gift for practicing medicine, especially the way he had directed the maid to assist her mistress to give birth, which demonstrated his extraordinary understanding of gynecology.","The elder took out an old yellow book from his bag and pressed it into He Ziming's hands.","He then told him that he didn't have long to live, and that the book contained the lifelong medical learnings and essence of his practice. He hoped that He Ziming would carry on and promote what he had learned in his lifetime.","After saying this, the elder left without waiting for He Ziming's response.","At first, He Ziming didn't take the elder's book seriously. However, when he opened it for casual reading in his leisure time one night, he was shocked.","It turned out that the elder was the highly acclaimed Gynecology Divine Doctor that everyone in Da Shun talked about. It was said that no one had ever seen his true face.","Also, this divine doctor had a strange temper. Whether someone was rich and powerful wouldn't matter, he only helped those based on his own mood.","The reason why He Ziming knew about this Gynecology Divine Doctor was because of his own mother's illness.","He had known since young that his mother had a gynecological condition that caused her excruciating abdominal pain every month when she had her period.","His father had sent people out on numerous occasions in a desperate attempt to locate this divine doctor to treat his mother, to no avail."]},{"number":459,"title":"Chapter 459: Do I have to get my mother stabbed before I come out","paragraphs":["Unexpectedly, he happened to meet this divine doctor by a fluke.","Not only that, according to the contents of the book, He Ziming could be sure that he had obtained the true teachings of this divine doctor.","At that time, although he had been studying gynecology for several years, he still hadn't found a way to cure his mother's illness.","It made He Ziming feel that his mother's illness might be incurable.","But after reading the book given by the divine doctor, he suddenly understood.","It turned out that his mother's illness was not completely incurable...","He Ziming read the divine doctor's book obsessively for almost three days. Other than eating and sleeping, he spent all his time at the inn learning.","Within five days, not only could he recite the contents of the book fluently, he had even thoroughly comprehended many of the methods.","Therefore, in his heart, he already regarded the gynecology divine doctor as his own teacher.","The teacher said that he didn't have long to live. As his student, he had to do his best to carry forward and develop everything the teacher had learned in his life.","Moreover, from his understanding of the gynecology divine doctor, the old man never revealed his true appearance when healing people. Everyone only knew that he always appeared in a gray robe and wore a hat.","Perhaps because the divine doctor didn't take action to save people that day, when communicating with He Ziming, he didn't wear a hat. But the gray robe was real.","When he heard the divine doctor say that he didn't have long to live, he deliberately observed the doctor's complexion. Indeed, there were signs of serious illness.","He estimated that if the doctor wasn't really in dire straits, he wouldn't have given the compiled medical book to a young man he barely knew so generously.","Coincidentally, on the day He Ziming helped the premature delivery woman on the official road, he also wore a hat so no one saw his true appearance.","In order to thoroughly inherit the divine doctor's mantle, He Ziming simply learned his style and helped people without revealing his true identity, just like the teacher did.","Additionally, he did this partly out of self-interest.","His father at home was strict and didn't know about his secret medical practice. So He Ziming did this to avoid exposing his identity and incurring his father's wrath.","He first appeared in this guise and cured his mother's dysmenorrhea, then cured many women's illnesses in the capital.","Gradually, such a rumor spread among the people of the capital: Da Shun had produced another saintly hand of gynecology whose medical skills were comparable to those of the former divine doctor of gynecology...","He Ziming was the saintly hand of gynecology. No matter how temperamental he was in his medical practice, since it was his sister who was in danger, he naturally wouldn't stand idly by.","Of course, Minister Heo was going to interrogate his son carefully, now that his son suddenly had the additional identity of the saintly hand of gynecology.","In order to ensure his sister's safety, He Ziming could only explain his identity clearly to his father.","After listening, Minister Heo felt both angry and gratified at the same time.","He was angry that his son had secretly studied such an incredible medical technique and hid it from him so tightly.","He was gratified that the saintly hand of gynecology turned out to be his own son, which meant his daughter's life could be saved.","Without further ado, as soon as Minister Heo found out his son was the saintly hand of gynecology, he immediately asked Zhang San to take him to the northwest as quickly as possible.","Thinking of his suffering daughter pregnant with twins in the northwest, not knowing if father and daughter would ever meet again in this life, Minister Heo wished he could disregard everything and rush to the northwest with his son.","But his reason kept reminding him that once the Emperor found out he had left for the northwest, he would surely vent his rage on their whole clan.","So Minister Heo had to abandon the idea and stay firmly in the capital.","While he couldn't leave the capital, He Ziming had no such worries.","Some time ago, the attempted rebellion of Ninth Prince had occurred. The suspicious Emperor Shunwu had issued an edict requiring all those related to Ninth Prince's estate to be suspended from their posts pending investigation.","Although He Ziming was forced to become engaged to Princess Yu, he was still on the list of people associated with Ninth Prince's staff.","Until all of Ninth Prince's accomplices had been captured, he had no qualification to resume his post.","Fortunately, the investigators of Ninth Prince's rebellion case knew clearly that he was forced into the engagement with Princess Yu. So although he was on the list, he had absolutely no connection with the case itself.","Therefore, He Ziming was only nominally suspended and his movements were not restricted at all.","With no official post, leaving the capital to travel could be easily explained as sightseeing. No one would have any reason to stop him...","...","After listening to Zhang San's explanation, Mo Jiuye was thoroughly convinced that his uncle-in-law was indeed the saintly hand of gynecology.","He felt oddly relieved. His wife was the saintly hand's own younger sister. Judging by the He family's attitude, they all cared deeply about He Zhiran.","Especially the speed Big Uncle-in-law had traveled to the northwest, which must have been much faster than he imagined. It showed Uncle-in-law must have hardly rested on the road.","Seeing He Ziming's dust-covered appearance, Mo Jiuye quickly invited him back home.","At that time, other Mo brothers also came out one after another to see the guest. After hearing he was the saintly hand of gynecology invited by Madam He's people, they were all astonished for a moment.","But the Mo family were not gossipy people. Moreover, they clearly understood that since the saintly hand of gynecology never showed his true appearance when treating patients, they even less wanted to spread the news.","After everyone chatted briefly with He Ziming, they saw him off as he left for home with Mo Jiuye.","Madam He was waiting at the gate, looking into the distance. Seeing a group of people walking over, she asked loudly:","\"Jiuye, are those guests coming?\"","\"Mother, it's me, Ziming.\" Before Mo Jiuye could respond, He Ziming had already answered his mother.","No matter how unclear it was in the dark, a mother would never mistake her own son's voice.","Madam He was stunned for a moment and walked towards them, saying:","\"Ziming, why are you here? Has the saintly hand of gynecology arrived?\"","Although she also missed her son, seeing the saintly hand was still more important at the moment.","\"Mother, let me see my sister first. We can talk more afterward.\"","On the way to the courtyard, Mo Jiuye had already given him a general overview of He Zhiran's condition.","He Ziming just wanted to examine his sister's condition as soon as possible, so he could have a better grasp of it in his mind.","Just as Mo Jiuye went out to see the guest, He Zhiran suddenly felt the dragging sensation in her belly getting worse.","Luckily no one else was in the room then. She quickly entered her space dimension to check.","The result made her scratch her head in puzzlement.","Obviously when she had last checked the fetal position ten days ago, everything was fine. Why did it look so different today?","The two babies were still very healthy, but they had now shifted into a head-up position.","With such a situation, a cesarean section was safer no matter if it was one or two babies.","He Zhiran smiled helplessly, gently caressing her round belly, and said tenderly:","\"You two little rascals really know how to torture your mother. You have to make your mother go under the knife before consenting to come out, don't you?\"","Just as her voice fell, Mo Jiuye had brought He Ziming into the yard.","Anxious to check on his sister, He Ziming asked Mo Jiuye, \"Which room is Rana in?\""]},{"number":460,"title":"Chapter 460: Big Brother Check you First.","paragraphs":["Mo Jiuye walked in front, pointing to the brightest room and said: \"She is inside.\"","Following the direction of Mo Jiuye's finger, He Ziming rushed past him, showing how anxious he was at the moment.","Seeing the person at the door, He Zhiran was stunned for a moment.","\"Big brother, why are you here?\"","The siblings had a good relationship since childhood. Seeing He Ziming, He Zhiran also inexplicably felt a sense of intimacy.","In the original host's memory, the first thing Big Brother would do when he saw her was to raise a gentle smile, then call out her nickname.","Today's He Ziming was completely different from the one in her memory. He had a tense look on his face. As soon as he got to the bed, he grabbed her wrist.","\"Big brother will check you first.\"","\"Big brother...\" He Zhiran wanted to say, big brother, what are you doing, but before she could finish speaking, she heard Mo Jiuye say:","\"Ranran, don't worry first. Let your big brother finish checking you. Then I will slowly explain it to you.\"","Although He Zhiran was still confused, seeing Big Brother checking her pulse so carefully, she obediently kept quiet.","A while later, He Ziming removed his fingers from He Zhiran's wrist.","\"Ranran, lie down. Big brother will take a look at your baby's position.\"","He Zhiran was full of puzzlement, but still did as he was told.","She saw He Ziming frowning more and more, to the point that he lost his composure when using force.","It wasn't until He Zhiran let out a \"hiss...\" that he came back to his senses.","\"Big brother, is the baby not in the right position?\"","He Ziming had wanted to hide it from her, but was caught off guard by her question and did not react for a moment.","\"How did you know?\"","He Zhiran revealed a mischievous smile.","\"Did big brother forget? Since I was little, I read medical books. And the baby is in my belly. I caress them every day, so of course I would know.\"","On this point, He Ziming had no argument, because he did not know to what extent his sister had learned medical skills by reading medical books.","Just like himself, before meeting the sage doctor teacher, he had been able to assist women in premature labor to give smooth birth through self-study.","He also acknowledged his own talent for learning medicine. He had the talent to learn well, and others could have the same talent.","His sister's condition was the most urgent matter right now. He Ziming had no time to think about irrelevant things.","After helping his sister finish the examination, in order not to put pressure on her before giving birth, he deliberately spoke very lightly.","\"It's not as serious as you think. You don't know yet that your big brother has an innate ability to make these little ones afraid and obediently change their position as soon as they sense my presence.\"","As soon as he said this, he successfully made He Zhiran laugh.","\"Big brother, how come I never noticed before that you have the ability to joke around?\"","Madam He had been confused all along. Her son came here to help examine her daughter's condition, and she just heard Ranran ask if the baby was not in the right position.","This news was like a bolt from the blue for her.","The doctor who examined her daughter just now said that she and the babies were very healthy. Madam He had still clung to a ray of hope then, thinking that as long as the mother and children were fine, her daughter would not be in danger during childbirth.","But after hearing the conversation between her children just now, she felt more and more that something was wrong.","After all, she was the one who had raised her children with her own hands, so no one knew better what kind of temperaments they had than her as their mother.","Especially He Ziming, he had been brought up by his father since he was young and taught how to act and speak in front of others. He had never been so reckless before.","The more Madam He thought about it, the more she felt something was wrong. She slowly walked up to He Ziming.","\"Ziming, have you and your father still not found the sage doctor?\"","Seeing sweat on his mother-in-law's forehead, Mo Jiuye quickly stepped forward to explain:","\"Mother-in-law, the sage gynecologist is Big Brother himself.\"","It was as if Madam He did not hear Mo Jiuye's words. She kept staring at He Ziming.","After a long while, she turned her head to look at Mo Jiuye.","\"What did you say?","You said he is the sage gynecologist?","How is that possible? I raised this child myself. He has never studied any medical skills before, how could he possibly be the sage gynecologist?","Don't make up such excuses to comfort me and Ranran. If we really can't find anyone, we can still think of other ways now.\"","The reason why Madam He did not respond to Mo Jiuye's words just now was because she did not believe him at all.","At the same time, she was also trying her best to remind herself to stay rational and keep her emotions under control. That was why she said so much.","He Ziming knew that his mother simply did not believe that he was the sage gynecologist.","\"Mother, I really am the sage gynecologist that everyone talks about. If you don't believe me, go ask Zhang San.\"","At this moment, He Ziming's attitude was sincere. He had become the rigid person that Madam He knew in her mind again.","But no matter how she thought about it, she just could not understand how her son had become the sage gynecologist?","Zhang San had been waiting outside the door all along and could hear the conversation inside the room.","In order not to let the madam get so anxious that something bad happened, he said loudly: \"Madam, the young master is indeed the sage gynecologist.\"","Hearing Zhang San say this, Madam He stepped outside.","\"Zhang San, please explain clearly. What exactly is going on here?\"","When He Ziming admitted to his father that he was the sage gynecologist, he carefully explained the whole process of how he learned medicine and the chance encounter where he obtained the inheritance from the sage doctor.","At that time, he was no longer intending to continue hiding his identity as the sage gynecologist from his family. Moreover, he also knew that since he was rushing to the northwest to help his sister give birth, Zhang San would definitely lead the way, so his identity could not be kept secret anyway.","Therefore, when he was explaining his identity to his father, he did not hide it from Zhang San either, so Zhang San was very clear about the whole matter.","\"Madam, the young master is indeed the sage gynecologist. When I returned to the capital and went out with the master to find someone...\"","Zhang San started explaining on behalf of the young master. Knowing that the young miss must also be curious about this matter, he deliberately raised his voice a little.","Like telling a story, Zhang San spent half a stick of incense thoroughly explaining the young master's situation from start to finish.","After listening, although Madam He and He Zhiran both felt somewhat incredulous, neither mother nor daughter had any doubts.","Madam He could no longer slowly digest this sudden information. She pulled He Ziming along to head outside.","After mother and son left the courtyard, Madam He looked at where they were standing, which was already some distance away from He Zhiran's room. Only then did she stop.","\"Ziming, how is your sister's condition really?\"","He Ziming knew that his mother cared most about his sister. He could only try to make things sound less serious.","\"Mother, don't worry. I'm here to guarantee that Ranran and your two little grandsons will be safe and sound.\"","This was the sentence Madam He was waiting for.","\"Now that you said this, mother will stop worrying.\"","At this moment, Madam He suddenly felt a sense of pride rise up in her heart. Her son turned out to be the famous sage gynecologist..."]},{"number":461,"title":"Chapter 461: I will Hold on","paragraphs":["In short, the tense feeling that Madam He originally had in her heart had now completely disappeared without a trace.","She was just blindly trusting in the gynecology saint. As long as the gynecology saint was there, Ran Ran would definitely be able to give birth smoothly.","The mother and daughter returned to He Zhiran's room. He Ziming spoke of her condition again.","\"After I just examined Ran Ran, if nothing unexpected happens, she should go into labor early tomorrow morning.\"","Hearing that she was going to go into labor, He Zhiran felt somewhat nervous in her heart.","Although her big brother looked calm and relaxed on the surface, as a doctor herself, she naturally knew what great difficulties she would face in giving birth with a breech presentation.","Could her big brother be a god?","Could he even help her give birth smoothly to twins in breech presentation?","Just as He Zhiran was puzzled, He Ziming spoke again.","\"According to reason, Ran Ran still has at least three more days before she goes into labor, but her breech presentation needs to be corrected immediately.","The process of correction will be somewhat painful, and it will also stimulate her to go into labor prematurely.\"","As for the deeper meaning, He Ziming did not intend to explain too much.","Through the examination just now, he had already determined that the fetus in his sister's belly was in an abnormal position. Fortunately, he was able to arrive in the northwest today.","If it was a little later, even if the Divine Medicine Teacher came, it would be too late.","The reason why He Ziming was so confident was because of the very magical needling techniques left in the book given to him by the Divine Medicine Teacher.","He could use needling combined with manipulations to turn the position of the fetus in the abdomen.","With the fetus in the proper position in the abdomen, basically there would be no possibility of dystocia for a pregnant woman without any physical problems.","Even though He Zhiran was carrying twins, she could still give birth smoothly.","Most importantly, he had also learned from the book a set of needling techniques to assist childbirth, which could shorten the painful time for the pregnant woman and allow the child to be born sooner.","Although He Zhiran did not know the specific method her big brother used to turn the fetus, in her understanding, it was nothing more than a medical procedure.","She had also heard of this method in her previous life. It involved turning the position of the child in the pregnant woman's belly through her abdominal skin.","This method was indeed very painful for the pregnant woman. Using the phrase excruciating pain to describe it was not an exaggeration.","For these things, He Zhiran did not care.","She was not the delicate young miss like the original owner. Facing the pain that might come in a moment, she did not have any fear psychologically.","When Uncle He said turning the breech would be somewhat painful for Ran Ran, Mo Jiuye became a little uneasy.","\"Big brother, isn't there another way?\"","His Ran Ran had suffered so much following him. It was a pity that he could not take over this kind of thing, otherwise he would have agreed without hesitation to take it all on himself.","He Ziming just shook his head heavily at him, then looked at He Zhiran.","\"Ran Ran, your big brother hopes that for the sake of the children in your belly and yourself, you must grit your teeth and persevere. As long as you can persevere, your big brother guarantees everything will be fine.\"","He understood his own sister. She had been pampered by their parents since she was a child and had never suffered a bit.","The kind of pain from turning a breech was unbearable for ordinary people.","If it wasn't for his sister and his two little nephews or nieces to survive safely, he as the big brother would not be able bear to do it.","Faced with her big brother's reminder, He Zhiran seemed very calm.","\"Big brother, don't worry, I will definitely endure it.\"","He Ziming did not believe this at all. But even if she could not endure it, she would still have to go through it. Compared to suffering, life was more important.","\"Alright, there's no time to delay. Let's start now.\"","After finishing speaking, he looked around the room.","\"Brother-in-law stay, everyone else go outside and wait.\"","The news of He Ziming's arrival had already been passed on to the two elders by the older brothers.","Old Lady Mo greeted the eldest daughter-in-law who lived closest to her to accompany her over.","When she arrived, she saw Mo Jiuye and He Ziming closing the door to the room on the left and right sides, and the worried expression in Madam He's eyes.","Her sons had only told her that the He family eldest young master had arrived just now. They did not say anything else, so Old Lady Mo still did not know that He Ziming was the gynecology saint.","Seeing that everyone had abnormal expressions on their faces, she pulled Madam He and asked.","\"Mother-in-law, is Ran Ran going to give birth?\"","But this did not seem to be the case either. With two grown men closing the door to the room and no midwife going in, it was impossible for He Zhiran to be giving birth. But apart from this, she could not think of what had happened for the time being.","There was no movement from the room at this moment. When Mother-in-law asked, Madam He told her about her son's identity as the gynecology saint, as well as He Zhiran having a breech presentation and He Ziming getting ready to turn the fetus for her.","Even a normally composed person like Old Lady Mo was given quite a lot to thoroughly digest with so much news all at once.","Especially when mother-in-law said He Zhiran had a breech presentation, it made her heart jump to her throat.","Not carefully inquiring about He Ziming's identity, she trembled as she held Madam He's hand.","\"Mother-in-law, you said Ran Ran has a breech presentation, how could the midwife not find out?\"","It wasn't that she did not believe He Ziming. A breech presentation was not something to joke about. Especially since He Zhiran was carrying twins, this could be a life-threatening situation at any time.","She only hoped that He Ziming had diagnosed it incorrectly. Her daughter-in-law did not actually have a breech presentation problem.","But Madam He's words were like pouring cold water over her head.","\"I'm sure mother-in-law has heard of the title 'gynecology saint'. In the Capital city everyone knows him. As long as it is an illness for us women, or a difficult childbirth for a pregnant woman, as long as he takes action, there is nothing that cannot be cured.\"","Speaking to here, Madam He took out a handkerchief and wiped the tears about to spill from the corners of her eyes, looking worriedly toward He Zhiran's room.","Old Lady Mo had only left the Capital city for a year, so she naturally knew of the existence of the gynecology saint.","Just now she was also muddled by concern, and unwilling to believe that He Ziming really was the gynecology saint.","But a naturally sensible person could not let concern cloud their mind for too long.","\"Mother-in-law, since Eldest Young Master He is the gynecology saint, Ran Ran's safety is assured.\"","Madam He nodded: \"Yes, Ziming rushed here at top speed in order to save his sister's life.\"","Her tears kept swirling around her eyes. It was mainly because her daughter was going to suffer that pained her as the mother, yet she had no way to take her place and endure the suffering.","The two old madams consoled each other in the yard, while in the room He Ziming had already taken out silver needles and pierced several acupoints around He Zhiran's belly.","Mo Jiuye stood at the bedside, holding He Zhiran's hand tightly, with sweat beading his anxious forehead.","After about the time it takes to burn one incense stick, He Ziming removed the silver needles and instructed Mo Jiuye.","\"Brother-in-law, bring me a thinner bedsheet.\"","Mo Jiuye did not know what he was going to do, but still swiftly did as told."]},{"number":462,"title":"Chapter 462: Shout If it Hurts.","paragraphs":["He Ziming saw him bring over the sheets and continued to instruct, \"Cover Ran Ran's lower abdomen with the sheets.\" Mo Jiuye still did it obediently even though he was confused.","He didn't understand the intention behind it, but He Zhiran did. It was nothing more than taking great precautions between men and women during this era. He Ziming had to use his hands to turn the fetus, so he must think of some effective measures to avoid physical contact, after all he was a master gynecologist and his patients were all women.","Seeing Mo Jiuye cover his sister's belly with the sheet according to his words, He Ziming couldn't help but warn again before taking action.","\"Ran Ran, if it hurts, just shout out.\"","Right now he needed to save his own sister, and He Ziming had never felt such nervousness before.","If it was someone else, he wouldn't care so much at all, but if his sister suffered, he as her elder brother would surely feel heartache.","However, if his sister didn't suffer now, her life couldn't be saved at all. He Ziming tried his best to calm the strange emotions in his heart and maintain a good mentality as much as possible.","\"Big brother is going to start.\"","After he said that, He Ziming began operating.","Mo Jiuye held He Zhiran's hand tightly, constantly comforting her, \"Ran Ran, don't be afraid, big brother will definitely be gentle.\"","Looking at He Ziming's actions, Mo Jiuye didn't even feel confident about his own comfort.","As for He Zhiran, at first when He Ziming was turning the fetus, she could still grit her teeth and endure.","But as time went on, she couldn't stand it anymore. The piercing pain was indescribable.","Finally, He Zhiran couldn't help but break down.","\"Ah...It hurts so much...\"","Although her voice was not loud, it still made He Ziming's hands pause.","No one understood better than him as the gynecology genius doctor how much pain He Zhiran was in right now.","At first, He Ziming was very curious. Could it be because he was exceptionally careful with his strength that his sister didn't feel as much pain?","But after seeing He Zhiran's tightly pursed lips and flushed red face, he realized it wasn't that his technique was gentler, but that his sister was too strong.","\"Ran Ran, if it hurts then shout it out, don't hold it in and hurt yourself.\"","While reminding her, He Ziming didn't stop his actions.","He Zhiran gripped Mo Jiuye's big hand tightly, as if only this way could she be stronger.","Mo Jiuye watched his delicate wife's face become distorted from pain, and his heart ached so much that tears were about to fall.","But his heartache was very powerless at this moment. All he could do was accompany her.","This was also He Ziming's true intention for having him stay.","Ran Ran was bearing great pain to pass on the Mo family line for him. This scene must be engraved in Mo Jiuye's heart.","If one day he had other ideas, thinking back to Ran Ran's suffering today would also give him a reason for sudden awakening.","He Zhiran had overestimated her own endurance. At this moment she had completely lost control and couldn't help crying out in pain.","Mo Jiuye hugged her distressedly, his tone choked with sobs.","\"Ran Ran, if you're in pain then hit me. Let's never have a child again in the future.\"","How could He Zhiran even listen to Mo Jiuye's words right now? She gripped his hand tightly, her nails digging into his flesh unconsciously.","Seeing the wounds on his hand left by his wife, Mo Jiuye felt it was too light.","Compared to his wife's suffering, this was still far from enough. Thus, he also rolled up his sleeves to let He Zhiran scratch his arms.","Old Lady He and Madam He were listening to the movement in the room, and the two old ladies' tears flowed like rain.","Madam He didn't know her daughter's situation and could no longer stand waiting there. She quickly walked to He Zhiran's door and tried hard to push it open to see what was going on inside.","But the door was locked from inside by Mo Jiuye, so she couldn't open it at all.","Left with no other choice, Madam He could only scream with all her might,","\"Ziming, Jiuye, open the door and let Mother come in to see Ran Ran.\"","Right now was the critical moment of turning He Zhiran's fetus. He Ziming didn't dare be distracted or negligent at all.","He looked at the helpless Mo Jiuye.","\"Guard the door, don't let anyone in.\"","Mo Jiuye numbly nodded then reluctantly pulled his arm out of He Zhiran's hand and went to the door.","\"Mother-in-law, big brother said the treatment is very critical now, you can't come in yet.\"","Hearing that she couldn't come in, Madam He became even more agitated.","\"Jiuye, open the door. Mother just wants to accompany Ran Ran. I promise I won't disturb Ziming treating her.\"","Although He Zhiran was in unbearable pain, she hadn't lost her mind. She knew her mother must have heard her cries of pain and become worried.","She tried her best to endure the abdominal pain and said to the door, \"Mother, I'll be fine, don't worry.\"","When Mo Jiuye heard his mother-in-law say that just now, he was already somewhat swayed and was hesitating whether to open the door for her.","But after hearing his wife's words, his determination was completely strengthened.","\"Mother-in-law, don't worry, Ran Ran has me accompanying her.\"","Madam He was already sobbing at this time. She leaned against the door and her whole body seemed to collapse as she slid down.","\"Mother's Ran Ran, if something happens to you, Mother won't be able to live either...\"","Old Lady Mo saw that her mother-in-law's emotions were completely out of control. She called Eldest Daughter-in-law and Lan Er to come over and forcibly helped her up.","\"Mother-in-law, let's take you back to your room to rest first. I'll stay here and stand guard.\"","How could Madam He let people take her away in her collapsed mental state?","Just as she was about to struggle forcibly, the door of He Zhiran's room opened from the inside.","The sweaty He Ziming walked out from inside.","\"Mother, Aunt Mo, don't worry. Ran Ran's fetus has been successfully turned. The two babies will definitely be born smoothly.\"","Facing the two old ladies, He Ziming didn't explain too much.","He Zhiran was pregnant with twins. Even if the fetus position was normal, there could still be difficulties in childbirth.","Before helping He Zhiran turn the fetus, he had considered this problem already. In his master's book there was a record.","It was a record of his master personally helping to treat a woman with malpositioned twins.","Not only did he turn the fetus position correctly, he also used a special technique combined with acupuncture to unblock the birth canal, allowing her to give birth smoothly without any obstruction.","At the same time, the genius doctor master also detailedly recorded this treatment method in the book.","Although the method was good, it had extremely high requirements for both the doctor and the pregnant woman.","First, the doctor had to be proficient in acupuncture and techniques to ensure no mistakes during treatment.","Secondly, the pregnant woman herself needed extremely strong endurance, otherwise she would faint from the pain before the treatment was completed.","This was the first time He Ziming had used this treatment method today. Although in the past he had also encountered pregnant women with the same condition as his sister,","he didn't use this method because that pregnant woman was too delicate. Just turning the fetus had already made her suffer terribly, so he omitted the next steps."]},{"number":463,"title":"Chapter 463: I'm a mother willing to take ten years off my life.","paragraphs":["This time when helping Zhiran turn the fetus, Ziming had planned in advance that if his sister couldn't stand the pain, he could only succeed in turning the fetus.","What Ziming didn't expect was that Zhiran turned out to be so strong that during the whole process of helping her turn the fetus, Zhiran didn't even moan once.","It was because of this that Ziming was completely determined to help clear her birth canal.","Zhiran cried out in pain, only after Ziming started to help clear her birth canal. That kind of pain was really not something ordinary people could withstand.","What comforted Ziming was that although his sister was suffering a bit more, successfully clearing the birth canal meant not only that she wouldn't face difficulties during labor on one hand, but more importantly, the speed at which the child would be born would also be very fast.","At this moment, although there were still big beads of sweat on Ziming's forehead and his speech was slightly panting, none of this could stop the corners of his mouth that had begun curving up.","When Madam He heard that her daughter was fine, she didn't know where she got the strength. She went forward and pushed Ziming aside to barge in.","Yes, she barged in. It looked to others as if she was afraid someone would continue to stop her.","After the treatment, in order for Zhiran to rest well, Ziming used silver needles to pierce her sleep acupoints, so Zhiran was already asleep now.","Jiuye didn't leave. Instead, he used a handkerchief to wipe the sweat from her forehead, and from time to time he would reach out to tidy her slightly messy hair.","When Madam He came to the bed and saw her sleeping daughter, she finally couldn't hold back her tears and cried out loud.","\"Ranran, you have suffered... woo woo... \"","As she spoke, she turned to the door, put her palms together and prayed,","\"Merciful Heaven, I beg you to open your eyes and stop tormenting my daughter. As long as she can give birth smoothly, I, her mother, am willing to give up ten years of my life...\"","Old Lady Mo also felt distressed for her daughter-in-law. Although she didn't see Zhiran's screams at the scene just now.","As someone who lived with her every day, she knew Zhiran very well. This girl had a tough temperament, not like other daughters-in-law who would cry at everything.","If it hadn't been too painful just now, she would never have shouted like that.","Thinking of this, Old Lady Mo's eyes became wet. She quickly took out a handkerchief and casually dabbed them before coming to the bed.","\"Jiuye, mother will stay with Zhiran. You take Ziming to rest.\"","Ziming was Jiuye’s uncle, and they were of the same generation, so it was most appropriate for him to host Ziming.","Jiuye was reluctant to leave Zhiran, and was about to turn around.","But Ziming didn't mean to leave.","He solemnly said to Jiuye, \"Ranran is likely to go into labor in the morning, so we should get the midwife here as soon as possible.\"","Although Ziming was a gynecological genius, there was no precedent for a man to deliver babies in this era.","The best he could do was to stand outside the delivery room and direct things when there were special circumstances.","Or if the parturient really couldn't make it, her family would have to cover her properly first before Ziming went in to treat her.","No one knew Zhiran's condition better than him. She could give birth smoothly as long as the midwife was here waiting at all times.","Especially after he had cleared Zhiran’s birth canal for her, her labor would progress very quickly. It would be dangerous if there was no midwife around who knew how to deliver babies.","As long as his sister-in-law didn't have to have a caesarean section, Jiuye could do whatever he wanted.","When Jiuye heard Ziming say to get the midwife, he didn't hesitate and ran towards the village.","Midwife Zhao was dragged all the way here by Jiuye. At this time, the old lady had already gone to bed. Jiuye didn't care much. He jumped over the wall and broke in, the loud sound of him banging on the door woke Midwife Zhao from her sleep.","Seeing Jiuye so anxious, Midwife Zhao thought Zhiran was giving birth. She hurriedly got dressed and went out.","As soon as she got to the door, she was pulled outside by Jiuye.","That’s not all. Thinking she was too slow, Jiuye dragged the old lady back home.","Midwife Zhao was already quite old. How could she withstand such dragging? By the time she reached the courtyard, she collapsed limply to the ground, one hand still tapping her chest.","\"Why are you in such a hurry, young man? When I left your house just now, your wife hadn't even gone into labor yet. Even if she gave birth, it wouldn't be too fast. You dragged this old lady until she almost fell apart. How can I still deliver the baby?”","Jiuye was just too anxious before, and always felt it would be safer if the midwife waited at home. He had forgotten to be gentle.","At this point, he also realized his mistake and quickly apologized.","\"Auntie, I'm so sorry, it's all my fault for being too impatient.\"","Facing such a scene, Jiuye really didn’t know what to do. It was all because he was too worried about his wife that he had forgotten he shouldn’t treat an old lady like this.","Seeing this, Old Lady Mo glared fiercely at Jiuye before putting on a smiley face and walking over to carefully help Midwife Zhao up from the ground.","\"I’m really sorry. Our family’s brat is going to be a dad for the first time and was too nervous. Please don't take it to heart with him.","Let me know if you feel uncomfortable anywhere, I'll have someone go into town to ask the doctor to check you out.\"","Midwife Zhao was not an unreasonable old lady either. Although her body was a little uncomfortable, she knew clearly that she was not seriously injured. She would be fine after moving around a little.","She sighed, \"Alas... Old lady me has tough luck. I won't die. Hurry up and take me to see the Ninth Missus, is she going to give birth?\"","As she spoke, Midwife Zhao staggered towards Zhiran’s room.","Old Lady Mo quickly explained, \"My ninth daughter-in-law is still sleeping. I asked you to come just in case. Let me take you to another room to rest first.\"","Old Lady Mo supported Midwife Zhao and walked towards the side room, and said unhappily to Jiuye,","\"Stinky boy, you hurt Auntie Zhao. Go get some nice food to calm her down.\"","On the surface, this was to instruct Jiuye in front of Midwife Zhao, but actually it was for Lan Er to go do it.","Lan Er always understood subtle cues. After hearing Old Lady Mo's words, she immediately went to prepare things.","This girl had also seen what happened to Midwife Zhao earlier. Seeing her condition didn’t seem pretended, and the old lady didn't ask for any compensation afterwards. Lan Er felt that she didn’t dislike her.","Therefore, she prepared the food for Midwife Zhao with extra care.","The food was all homemade. Watermelon was cut into uniform small pieces, there were also cakes Zhiran taught her to make, a cup of boiled milk, dried fruits and nuts platter...","This was nothing new to the Mo family. Zhiran often had Lan Er and Yuer make them and distribute them to each room. Not only here, but the elders and sisters-in-laws also never lacked them.","Midwife Zhao came this afternoon to check on Zhiran because she happened to be free, and didn't take a close look at their house.","Now that she was sitting here resting, she finally saw the furnishings in the room clearly.","Her mood could be described by the phrase \"huge waves crashing on the shore\".","How could a rural family have such a nice house..."]},{"number":464,"title":"Chapter 464: It Just Hurt","paragraphs":["When Zhao Midwife was young, she had gone to wealthy families in the city to help deliver babies. At that time, she felt that their lives were simply heaven.","Now when she saw the Mo Family's situation, Zhao Midwife felt that those wealthy families in the city were nothing compared to them.","Just as she was looking around everywhere, Lan Er had already walked in carrying a tray full of food.","She neatly arranged the food on the table and patiently introduced each dish before leaving.","Old Lady Mo had no plans to chat with the midwife here. She now only wanted to keep an eye on her daughter-in-law, so there would be more people around in case anything happened.","\"Sister-in-law Zhao, please rest here for now. I will come get you as soon as something happens with my daughter-in-law.\"","Zhao Midwife now understood clearly. The reason why Mo Jiuye had gone to such great lengths to bring her here was to have a midwife by his wife's side when she went into labor.","For her, this was not surprising at all. For women who lived far away and went into labor, their families would ask her to be there early.","She had thought that since they all lived in the same village and were so close, the Mo family could just come get her when the time came.","Who knew they had dragged her over urgently even before anything had happened.","Now that she was here, Zhao Midwife had no plans to leave either. She might as well stay and rest here.","After being dragged all the way here by Mo Jiuye, even if she had felt tired earlier, that was all gone now. Zhao Midwife started eating the food on the table.","As soon as she took a bite, she just couldn't stop.","No matter which dish it was, she had never eaten anything like it before. And in her opinion, this must be the most delicious food in the world.","In that instant, all of Zhao Midwife's slight annoyance at Mo Jiuye disappeared without a trace.","The Mo family really had good intentions, treating her to such wonderful food.","The shock she had received earlier was now completely made up for by this food...","He Zhiran slept very soundly, and in her dreams, she saw her two children.","They looked so cute and chubby, grinning at her.","Just as she was about to hug the children, she suddenly felt the urge to pee.","He Zhiran instantly woke up.","As soon as she opened her eyes, Mo Jiuye's handsome yet somewhat haggard face zoomed in.","\"Ranran, you're awake. Do you feel uncomfortable anywhere?\"","He Zhiran reached out her hand to him, and Mo Jiuye cooperated by gently helping her sit up.","\"Husband, let's go...go to the restroom.\"","She wanted to say go to the space, but upon glancing around, she saw her mother, mother-in-law, sister-in-law and brother all in the room. So she changed her words at the last minute.","At this moment, her sister-in-law also came over.","\"Little sister-in-law, I'll go with you.\"","With Mo Jiuye supporting her on one side and her sister-in-law on the other, the two helped He Zhiran walk towards the independent restroom in the room.","Due to being pierced by He Ziming's silver needles at her acupoints to make her sleep earlier, He Zhiran still felt a little dizzy now. Fortunately there were people helping her, so she didn't try to act tough. Relying on the two's strength, she slowly walked forward.","After coming back from the restroom, He Zhiran still felt sleepy. It was just that the constant urge to go to the restroom prevented her from sleeping for an extended period of time.","That entire night, she went to the restroom countless times.","Mo Jiuye became somewhat impatient, thinking something was wrong with his wife's body.","Seeing his furrowed brows full of worry, Old Lady Mo explained, \"Jiuye, don't worry. This is normal for women before giving birth.\"","\"But if Ranran can't rest properly like this, how will she have the energy to give birth tomorrow?\" Mo Jiuye asked worriedly.","Although this was the first time he saw a woman about to give birth, the books he read during his leisure time were not read in vain.","The books said that in order to give birth more smoothly, pregnant women must conserve their strength and energy before delivery.","Old Lady Mo felt helpless about this too. Such things could only be endured relying on one's own perseverance, which she had personally experienced countless times.","By daybreak, He Zhiran was still going to the restroom every short while. Her lower abdomen had also begun to feel slight pain.","Seeing her abnormal complexion, He Ziming asked, \"Ranran, does your stomach hurt?\"","With one hand supporting her huge belly, He Zhiran frowned, \"It just hurt for a moment, it went away quickly.\"","Just as her words fell, her frown grew even tighter as that pain hit her again.","He Ziming rushed up to her in a few quick strides, reaching out to check her pulse at her wrist.","\"It's started, please ask the midwife to come keep watch!\"","He Ziming looked very nervous. Because the woman in labor was his own younger sister, he couldn't remain as calm as when facing other people.","At this time, Mo Jiuye didn't even want to leave He Zhiran's side for one step. He shouted towards the door,","\"Lan Er, go ask Zhao Midwife to come over!\"","Zhao Midwife had eaten well last night and slept soundly. Out of everyone there, she looked the most spirited.","At this moment, she felt that if she didn't try extra hard, she wouldn't live up to all the delicious food she was treated to last night.","\"Don't panic, it just started so she won't give birth immediately. You all go wait outside, let me examine her first.\"","The examination was different after labor had started. Idle people couldn't remain at the scene.","He Zhiran naturally knew what kind of examination Zhao Midwife wanted to give her. It was nothing more than checking how dilated she was.","This examination was no big deal, yet it left Zhao Midwife dumbstruck.","She stared at He Zhiran full of disbelief.","\"Young lady from the Mo family, didn't your stomach hurt at all last night?\"","He Zhiran shook her head. \"It only started hurting just now.\"","\"How strange. It's already dilated eight centimeters, how could you have only started feeling pain now?\" Zhao Midwife muttered to herself, eyes full of incredulity.","He Zhiran didn't really understand this either. To get herself examined, she could only enter her space and use those modern medical devices. But ever since last night, someone had never left her side, so there was never a chance for that.","Although this was her first delivery, she had never heard of a woman dilating eight centimeters with just a few light stomach pains. That was a bit too outrageous.","So either Zhao Midwife's examination was inaccurate, or her physique was special...","Just as she was filled with doubts, Zhao Midwife had already turned around and opened the room door.","Seeing the room door open, the people waiting outside swarmed over.","\"Granny, how's my wife's condition?\" Mo Jiuye asked.","Zhao Midwife repeated the results of the examination she had just done on He Zhiran, then instructed, \"The baby's coming fast. Hurry and boil some hot water. Also take advantage of the time before she gives birth to have her eat as much as possible.\"","Hearing that water needed boiling, Madam He rushed to the kitchen without needing to be told.","Both Old Lady Mo and Madam He looked at Zhao Midwife full of disbelief.","The two of them had gone through childbirth before. How could He Zhiran have dilated eight centimeters when her stomach had only just started hurting?","What did dilating eight centimeters represent?","It represented she was about to give birth very soon.","They should know that during their own labors, even if it wasn't their first child, they still had to endure pain for several hours before reaching eight centimeters dilation.","At this moment, Old Lady Mo didn't even care if questioning Zhao Midwife would displease her. She asked,","\"Are you sure my daughter-in-law has already dilated eight centimeters?\""]},{"number":465,"title":"Chapter 465: Never Again","paragraphs":["If it were usual times, Zhao Midwife would definitely be unhappy if someone questioned her like this. But He Zhiran's situation today was really too special that not to mention Old Lady Mo asking like this, even she had to check carefully before believing He Zhiran had really dilated eight centimeters now.","Just as Zhao Midwife was thinking about how to explain, He Ziming spoke up.","\"Auntie Mo, it is not strange that Ranan has dilated eight centimeters now.\"","Old Lady Mo was even more puzzled.","\"Not strange?\"","\"When I was helping Ranan align the fetus, I deliberately used silver needles and techniques to help smooth her birth canal, with the goal of making it so Ranan suffers less pain when giving birth.\" He Ziming explained in a way that others could understand as much as possible.","Other than Zhao Midwife, everyone present was clear about He Ziming's identity. Although He Zhiran's current situation was a bit inconceivable, it was not anything strange for someone called the saintly hand of gynecology to be able to do this.","As experienced people, Madam He and Old Lady Mo showed looks of gratification on their faces when they heard this.","He Zhiran's safety during childbirth was the first thing they cared about, and second was hoping she could suffer less pain.","It seemed now that both of these things had been resolved with He Ziming's arrival.","Old Lady Mo specifically ordered that today, the Mo family's meals would be made by her daughters-in-law, and she called Yu'er over to help prepare some appetizing food for He Zhiran.","With He Ziming having smoothed He Zhiran's birth canal, her labor pains came very suddenly.","When Lan Er brought in a bowl of yangchun noodles that she usually liked to eat, her pain had already brought sweat to her forehead.","Mo Jiuye had been by her side the entire time. Although his wife had not groaned once, he could completely see how painful she was right now.","Mo Jiuye took the bowl of yangchun noodles from Lan Er's hands and brought it in front of He Zhiran.","\"Ranan, I'll feed you. Eat a bit more.\"","Although He Zhiran was currently in severe pain, she knew that she would need strength to give birth soon. Even if just as medicine, she had to eat more.","\"Okay, I'll eat.\"","After eating half a bowl of noodles, He Zhiran was defeated by a sudden abdominal pain, completely losing her appetite.","This abdominal pain came intensely and fiercely. She rolled around on the bed.","Seeing this, Mo Jiuye turned pale with fright and went forward to prop He Zhiran up.","Just at this moment, Zhao Midwife walked over.","\"Old Nine, don't move her. Let me take a look first. The child should be about to be born.\"","Hearing Zhao Midwife's words, Mo Jiuye's outstretched hand paused in midair.","\"Auntie, I'll leave it to you.\"","Zhao Midwife came to the bedside and saw Mo Jiuye still standing frozen there without moving. She couldn't help but remind, \"Old Nine, this is the birthing room. You can go wait outside now.\"","In all her years as a midwife, this was still the first time she had seen a grown man insist on staying in the birthing room the entire time.","She knew everyone cared about their daughter-in-law, but who didn't know the birthing room was an unclean place and men staying inside would bring bad luck.","Hearing the midwife chase Mo Jiuye out, Old Lady Mo and Madam He at the door did not react at all.","If not for He Zhiran, forget being reunited, it was likely those people would not even be alive now.","He Zhiran had risked her life to give birth to children for the Mo family. It was only natural for Mo Jiuye as her husband to accompany her. Superstitions of bad luck or not did not matter.","The Mo family had already suffered enough misfortune, wrongly convicted and exiled to the northwest. They had endured such injustice, so what other misfortune could there be that the Mo family would care about - it would just be a drizzle to them.","Madam He did not think too much about it. By convention, it was indeed inappropriate for Mo Jiuye to remain in the birthing room.","Seeing her mother-in-law take no action, she was about to go into the room to pull Mo Jiuye out.","Old Lady Mo saw her intention and stopped her, \"Mother-in-law, don't mind him. Ranan suffered so much and risked her life to give birth to children for him. It's only right for him to accompany her.\"","\"This...\" Madam He hesitated.","From her perspective as a mother, having the son-in-law accompany the daughter giving birth would also give the daughter some sense of security. This was absolutely not a bad thing.","Since even the girl's own mother did not care, she as the mother-in-law would naturally not meddle too much.","\"Since that's the case, I will go accompany Ranan too.\"","Seeing the mother-in-law go in, Old Lady Mo also followed into the room.","At this time, several sisters-in-law who had just finished up their tasks also rushed over. Hearing the ninth younger sister was about to give birth, not only was ninth brother staying in the birthing room, but both old madams had gone in as well. The few women looked at each other, also intending to go accompany He Zhiran.","Seeing herself unable to dissuade Mo Jiuye, Zhao Midwife could only let him be.","But when she turned around, she discovered this many people had appeared in the room.","In all her years as a midwife, this was still her first time encountering such a spectacle.","Forget the man refusing to leave, this...this...almost the whole family had come in to accompany her!","Zhao Midwife steadied her mind, \"I know you all care about Ninth Young Master's family, but leaving just one person to help will do.\"","With so many people, she even felt suffocated, let alone the birthing woman.","Old Lady Mo also understood this point. If not for the mother-in-law going in earlier, she would not have followed.","Looking at the group of daughters-in-law behind her, she waved her hand, \"Let's all listen to the midwife and go wait outside.\"","Madam He had wanted to stay, but seeing even Old Lady Mo leading the women out, if she insisted on staying and got chased out by the midwife, that would not look good.","She looked at her daughter writhing in pain on the bed, reluctantly following the Mo women out.","He Zhiran also agreed with Zhao Midwife's actions. With so many people watching her, especially surrounding her tightly without any gaps, she would inexplicably feel suffocated.","Her pain now was completely unlike just at the start. The agony would come in waves with brief respites in between.","Ever since everyone left, her pains had not stopped once.","To conserve her strength, even when the anguish made her want to vent, she still endured strongly.","Having lived together for a long time, Mo Jiuye naturally understood her every move. He distressingly used a handkerchief to wipe away her sweat.","\"Ranan, if it hurts then yell, or you can hit me too.\" Mo Jiuye moved closer to make it convenient for He Zhiran to vent her pain.","Although He Zhiran was in agonizing pain, she had not lost her reason.","Seeing Mo Jiuye move nearer, she shifted back a bit.","Seeing her act this way, Mo Jiuye's mood could only be described as distraught.","His eyes were red as he grasped He Zhiran's hand.","\"Ranan, let's just have this one child. We won't have any more in the future. Seeing you suffer, I feel like death would be better than life.\"","He truly felt distressed. His wife was a strong woman, yet even she couldn't endure such torment. One could imagine without thinking how much pain it was.","\"I really won't have any more in the future...\" He Zhiran squeezed out these words almost through gritted teeth.","She didn't even know how to describe this kind of agony."]},{"number":466,"title":"Chapter 466: You are the Great Hero of my Mohist School","paragraphs":["Mo Jiuye gently patted her: \"Okay, we won't have any more children from now on.\"","When Zhao the midwife heard the young couple's conversation, she really shouldn't have interfered, but she couldn't help herself.","\"In our Da Shun Dynasty, we emphasize having many children. You two are still young and good-looking. Any babies born to you will surely be chubby and fair. How can you not have more?\"","\"No more!\"","\"We'll never have another one even if you beat us to death!\"","The couple spoke almost in unison.","He Zhiran had been tortured by this agony. As for Mo Jiuye, when he thought of letting his wife suffer so much again, his heart bled.","Seeing the attitudes of the young couple, Zhao the midwife immediately closed her mouth.","But in her heart, she was thinking to herself that she had seen many women who talked like this, yet in the end, they all gave birth again anyway.","In her opinion, giving birth was like \"once the scar heals, the pain is forgotten.\" How could they possibly not have more children?","Although she was grumbling to herself, Zhao the midwife didn't dare let down her guard. She kept a close eye on He Zhiran's condition at all times.","Just as He Zhiran was at a loss as to how to endure the excruciating pain, Zhao the midwife finally opened her mouth.","\"Hurry, get ready. It's coming out soon.\"","Hearing the midwife's words, Mo Jiuye hurriedly asked, \"Madam, what should I do now?\"","Zhao the midwife glanced at the hand He Zhiran was still clutching.","\"Go stand by her head so she can grab onto you easily to push. That will make it easier for her.\"","The circumstances were special for this birth at the Mo house since the husband was accompanying his laboring wife. Zhao the midwife had been spared the trouble of finding a place for He Zhiran to brace herself.","Mo Jiuye obediently took up his position.","\"Zhi Ran, grab onto me however you want, as long as it makes you feel a little better.\"","He Zhiran cooperated fully, gripping Mo Jiuye's arm for dear life, hoping with all her heart that the baby would come out sooner so that she could suffer a little less.","Zhao the midwife was extremely skilled at delivering babies. She quickly readied the tools she would need.","She went over to examine He Zhiran and nodded with satisfaction. \"Listen to my instructions. Push when I tell you to push.\"","With great difficulty, He Zhiran managed a slight nod...","Soon hearty cries of a newborn baby rang out in the room.","Zhao the midwife deftly wrapped the baby in a prepared small blanket and thrust it into Mo Jiuye's arms.","\"Congratulations, it's a boy!\"","Mo Jiuye was still somewhat in a daze with a little meatball suddenly stuffed into his arms out of nowhere.","Seeing his reaction, Zhao the midwife couldn't help joking, \"You must be overjoyed that it's a son. You look silly with happiness!\"","Before Mo Jiuye could react, the door was shoved open from outside.","Madam He and Old Lady Mo burst into the room together.","Although the baby's cries weren't very loud, they could be clearly heard from outside.","How could these two grandmothers not be anxious?","But instead of going to check on the baby first, they headed straight for He Zhiran.","Tears rolled down Madam He's face as she looked at He Zhiran's haggard and disheveled appearance.","She grabbed He Zhiran's hand in distress.","\"Zhi Ran, you've had such a hard time. The midwife said you gave birth to a son. Hang in there a little longer until the next one comes out and you won't hurt anymore.\"","Tears also involuntarily welled up in Old Lady Mo's eyes.","\"Zhi Ran, you really suffered for us Mos. You're the hero of our family!\"","She didn't say this because she valued boys over girls or because He Zhiran had given birth to a son for the Mo family.","These heartfelt words of Old Lady Mo's contained no deliberate intent.","The Mo family had nine sons. Each had taken a wife, and Old Lady Mo had been waiting for a grandchild for over ten years since Mo Junrui had married.","Now that she finally had a cute little grandson, how could she not be emotional?","Although the abdominal pain didn't disappear after birthing one child, He Zhiran's body felt much lighter, making her feel considerably more comfortable.","She didn't want to talk at all at the moment. She had exerted tremendous energy giving birth to her first baby earlier and hoped to recover quickly through self-regulation.","Seeing the two elderly ladies chatting away with the new mother without anyone going to look at the chubby little grandson, Zhao the midwife couldn't help reminding them, \"The baby is so fair and plump. Aren't any of you going to take a look?\"","It was really odd. For other families whose births she attended, everyone would scramble to see the fat little boy when told it was a big chubby son.","But the Mos were different. So many of them were here, yet no one talked about seeing the baby.","At this point, Mo Jiuye also reacted, still holding his son in his arms.","It was just...his son was so tiny. His body remained rigid, not daring to move for fear that his strength would accidentally hurt the fragile baby.","\"Mother, Mother-in-law, can one of you take the baby?\"","He wanted to look at his son but didn't dare make the slightest movement.","The scene reminded Old Lady Mo of when she had given birth to Mo Junrui years ago.","Her husband, Mo Qing had reacted the same way back then. Because it was their first child, he had no experience holding a baby. When the midwife handed him the child, he had stood there woodenly like a statue, not daring to move an inch just like Mo Jiuye now.","Beating Madam He to it, Old Lady Mo stepped forward to take the baby from Mo Jiuye's arms.","Madam He gently flipped open a corner of the blanket.","Soon involuntary smiles spread across both their faces.","\"Sister-in-law, my little grandson is so fair!\"","Old Lady Mo happily chimed in. \"Yes, other newborns are usually red all over, but this child is fair and delicate.\"","\"Look at his features. He resembles Jiu Ye at least eighty percent,\" remarked Madam He.","\"Sister-in-law, you didn't see Jiu Ye as a child. This father and son pair simply looks like the same person carved from the same mold,\" Old Lady Mo countered.","Overhearing their conversation, He Zhiran momentarily ignored her physical pain.","\"Mother, bring the baby here and let me see him.\"","She wanted to see her son she had carried with such difficulty for ten months and endured tremendous suffering to give birth to. She was curious what he looked like.","At her request, Old Lady Mo carried the baby over to the bedside to show He Zhiran the little one's face.","\"Zhi Ran, doesn't he look exactly like Jiu Ye?\"","The tiny baby had only cried out a few times after being born. After Zhao the midwife neatly wrapped him in the blanket, he soon fell into a deep sleep.","His little face was rosy and full of baby fat. His tiny mouth pursed together as if blowing little bubbles.","So adorable! To He Zhiran, this was the cutest baby she had ever seen.","A surge of innate maternal love welled up in her heart. If not for her current condition, she really wanted to hold the treasure in her arms and smother him with kisses.","While tenderly gazing at her son, she suddenly felt a sharp pang in her lower abdomen again, catching her off guard.","He Zhiran involuntarily frowned for a second before letting out a soft moan.","Mo Jiuye had also wanted to take a look at his son. But hearing He Zhiran's voice, he immediately rushed over to grab her hand instead, not even glancing at the baby.","\"Zhi Ran, does it hurt again?\""]},{"number":467,"title":"Chapter 467: Two Sons and Daughters","paragraphs":["Zhao Midwife from the other side also went to check quickly, and then anxiously said, \"You two, first take the children out, the second baby is coming soon.\"","Madam He and Old Lady Mo looked at He Zhiran and gave her an encouraging look before taking the children out.","The birth of the second baby was even smoother than the first one. He Zhiran had experience, and she was not as exhausted.","As soon as Zhao Midwife said to push, she cooperated with all her might.","This time, after pushing hard, the second baby fell to the ground crying.","Zhao Midwife excitedly said, \"Congratulations, congratulations! The second child is a girl. Congratulations to you young couple on having both a son and a daughter!\"","In the Great Shun Dynasty, the words dragon and phoenix were only allowed for the royal family. Ordinary people did not dare mention these two words, otherwise it would bring disaster.","He Zhiran lay quietly there to rest and heard the midwife say she had given birth to another girl. She was happy in her heart.","She had the mindset of modern people and did not have any special ideas about having a son or daughter.","In her heart, as long as the children were healthy, it did not matter whether they were male or female.","That was why when she had prenatal checkups at the clinic, she never intentionally looked at the gender of the child.","Even so, hearing that she had given birth to a pair of dragon and phoenix twins, she still felt pleasantly surprised.","Giving birth to two babies at once was already a blessing from heaven, and to have both a son and daughter was something that would make anyone happy.","However, after giving birth to the second child, she had used up all her energy. At this moment, she did not even have the strength to open her eyes to look at her daughter.","In her groggy state, she could feel Zhao Midwife helping her clean up, and Mo Jiuye was also at her side, using a handkerchief to wipe her face. She even seemed to feel a drop of warm tears landing on her cheek.","Mo Jiuye finally could not hold back his tears.","He witnessed the whole birthing process of his wife and understood the hardship and pain better than anyone.","He felt heartache for his wife having to endure so much pain alone to bear children for him.","Mo Jiuye had silently made a vow that in order not to let his wife get pregnant again, he would rather become a monk for life...","In fact, Mo Jiuye really was ignorant in this area.","He had not considered that the sisters-in-law at home were secretly given medicine by the Empress so they could not conceive, and the doctors at the clinic could also prescribe herbal soups for contraception. If they did not want to have children, it was not difficult.","In short, as long as his wife did not suffer again, he did not care about anything else.","Just now, Zhao Midwife also saw that Mo Jiuye, the father, did not know how to hold the baby at all. After wrapping up the second baby, she placed her beside He Zhiran.","Because Zhao Midwife had deep-rooted ideas and was naturally biased against girls herself, when she saw that He Zhiran had given birth to a girl, she thought the Mo family would not care much either. So she was not as excited as when the first baby was born.","In ancient times, this was indeed the case. When she helped other families deliver babies, the labor fees she received for delivering a boy and a girl were different.","For families that had a boy, even if they were not wealthy, they would try their best to give more.","Those who had a girl were different. Even if they had money, some were still unwilling to give more and wanted to give less instead.","Who knew, when the people waiting outside heard that He Zhiran had given birth to a girl, they suddenly swarmed in together.","Old Lady Mo was unusually unrestrained compared to her usual dignified manner.","\"Where is my cute granddaughter? The cute granddaughter Rongrong gave me, where is she?\" she cried.","As she spoke, she no longer cared for the sleeping chubby grandson in her arms and directly handed him to Madam He.","Although the other Mo women did not speak, their eager expressions showed how much they wanted to see their little niece.","The actions of the Mo women stunned Zhao Midwife.","What were they trying to do?","It looked as if they were trying to snatch the baby!","She instinctively glanced at the sleeping baby beside He Zhiran. After a brief pause, she woodenly picked up the child.","She brought the baby to Old Lady Mo and said, \"Here is your granddaughter, fair and delicate, as beautiful as her mother. Congratulations on the addition of two grandchildren.\"","Old Lady Mo took the child from Zhao Midwife's arms and sat down at He Zhiran's bedside. She said softly,","\"Rongrong is our Mo family's lucky star. Not only has she brought our family good fortune, she has good fortune herself. After suffering once, she immediately had both a son and daughter. This is something others don't even dare dream about.\"","The second sister-in-law also came up and chimed in, \"Mother is right. I realized early on that Ninth Sister has extraordinary good fortune.\"","As she spoke, she wanted to lean over to take a look at her little niece. But before she could get close, she was pulled back by the other sisters-in-law behind her.","\"Second Sister-in-law, the little niece belongs to all of us. We should look at her together. Don't block Ninth Sister from our view. We want to see Ninth Sister too!\"","\"That's right, you've blocked our view of Ninth Sister!\"","\"...\"","Although the women did not speak loudly, Old Lady Mo was still afraid they would disturb He Zhiran's rest.","She quickly picked up the second baby and stood up, \"All of you, go outside. Don't make noise here and disturb Ninth Sister's rest. If you want to see the second baby, go outside.\"","She realized that her daughters-in-law, like her, also doted on girls. If she did not let them see the baby immediately, they would keep causing a fuss.","Madam He held the older baby in her arms and watched as the group surrounded the second baby and left. Then she looked down at the older baby in her arms. How could he not be as precious anymore?","No, the older baby was also precious. It was just that her mother-in-law had given birth to so many sons and only one daughter, Mo Hanyue. Their family's girls were certainly treasured.","Thinking that the cute newborn grandson in her arms now faced possible neglect, Madam He inevitably felt worried for the child.","She held the older baby tighter and whispered, \"Our older baby is the best. Grandma loves you.\"","The older baby still did not know that on the very first day after being born, his dear grandma had already imagined him as an neglected child...","Mo Jiuye also felt happy about having both a son and daughter.","However, seeing his wife's haggard appearance now, he had no mind to look at the twin babies.","He just silently accompanied her, unable to share her pain but at least able to feel more at ease.","After Zhao Midwife swiftly cleaned up He Zhiran, she left the room with a grin after giving Mo Jiuye some reminders.","This was the first time in her life she had successfully delivered twins and both were safe.","Just this point alone was enough for her to boast about for miles, making those midwives who competed with her jobs jealous to death.","Although it was warm outside, they were after all newborns.","Old Lady Mo had already taken the second baby into another room. The women were surrounding her to look at the baby.","\"Mother, my little niece is so beautiful. Her eyebrows and eyes look exactly the same as Ninth Sister.\"","\"My little niece will definitely grow up to be a beauty.\"","\"Mother, can I hold my little niece too?\"","\"Mother, do you think my little niece is laughing?\"","\"...\""]},{"number":468,"title":"Chapter 468: We Just wanted to See It","paragraphs":["Old Lady Mo looked at the cute little face of the baby girl sleeping in her arms, feeling like her heart was melting.","After so many years, Mo Family finally had a new life born, and even welcomed two at once.","She was afraid the daughters-in-law would disturb the granddaughter's rest by quarreling, so she scolded fiercely: \"You nine sisters-in-law and Older Baby also need to be taken care of, don't all crowd around here...\" and compete with me for the baby granddaughter.","Furthermore, the Ninth Daughter-in-law and Older Baby are just as important. She was doing this mainly to take the granddaughter back to show Mo Qing.","When he sees that there is such a cute little granddaughter added to the family, he would even laugh himself awake from sleep.","Thinking back to when Mo Hanyue was born, Mo Qing barely slept a wink for almost a whole day and night, always taking care of his precious daughter. If it wasn't for affairs at court, I guess he could have accompanied his daughter the whole time.","The Eldest Sister-in-law has always played a leading role among the sisters-in-law, so even if she wanted to hold her little niece again, she had to consider the big picture at this time.","Especially since the Ninth Sister-in-Law had just given birth, preparations need to be made for some nourishing food to recover her health, and she had to personally lead people to prepare it.","Reluctantly taking one last look at the sleeping baby, Eldest Sister-in-law called the sisters-in-law to leave.","Seeing that no one was competing with her for the granddaughter, Old Lady Mo also got up to take the child back to her own courtyard.","Just as she came out of the room, she bumped into Zhao Midwife.","As a midwife, auspicious words came easily in order to earn more money.","Moreover, the twins born in Mo Family were really auspicious and joyful, she didn't even need to embellish much.","\"Oh my... Congratulations to you! The daughter-in-law gave birth at once to a grandson and a granddaughter. You are clearly a fortunate person. From now on your days will be surrounded by children and grandchildren, no one can compare to you...\"","If it were before, Old Lady Mo did not like to hear these compliments. But today was different, the more she listened to Zhao Midwife's words, the better she felt.","At the same time, she also remembered that the midwife had been busy for so long and had not yet been paid.","Old Lady Mo had prepared the money reward in advance and had been keeping it in her pocket. If she had not been so enthralled by the granddaughter just now, she would have already given it earlier.","Now after hearing Zhao Midwife say so many auspicious words all at once, not only did she give the reward she had originally prepared, but also took out extra silver from her own pocket to give to her.","\"You've worked hard too, take this silver.\"","When Zhao Midwife took the silver and looked at it, she was startled to see there were actually several taels all together.","It was the first time she had received such a large reward. Although there were times when other families would give more rewards after giving birth to a big fat son, compared to what Mo Family gave, it was not even enough to look at.","The wrinkles on Zhao Midwife's face folded into smiles.","\"Thank you Lady Mo, thank you... hehe...\" Originally she still called Old Lady Mo Big Sister, but now she directly changed to calling her Lady.","With so much silver, it would last her a long time. She had originally thought that with the Ninth House pregnant with twins, there would be no chance of a smooth delivery. Frankly speaking, it would not be strange at all to lose one child to gain another three lives.","She did not expect the family to not only deliver safely, but also give birth to such handsome little siblings, both safe and sound.","When Zhao Midwife thought of these things, she felt a sense of glory. If this matter was brought up by outsiders, it would also be a great opportunity for her to spread her name.","Seeing Zhao Midwife off, Old Lady Mo hugged her granddaughter and walked briskly towards her own courtyard.","Just as she went out the door, she saw her sons rushing over.","\"Mother, we heard that Ninth Sister-in-Law has given us a nephew and a niece. Let us see them quickly!\"","Seeing her sons' eagerness, Old Lady Mo hurriedly took a few steps back.","\"Lower your voices, don't frighten your niece.\"","Mo Jiacheng felt embarrassed and scratched his hand.","\"Mother, we just want to take a look and promise not to make any noise.\"","As he spoke, the brothers slowed down their actions a lot, but still kept leaning forward.","Seeing this, Old Lady Mo could only reluctantly lift the corner of the baby's quilt and admonish, \"Be gentle, if you ruin my precious granddaughter with your coarse hands, be careful I make you kneel to repent.\"","Kneeling to repent was a punishment they often suffered when they were young. Whenever they did something wrong, their mother would order them to go to the ancestral hall to kneel and repent. And during the punishment period they were not allowed to eat either. Ever since they grew up, their mother never punished them like that again. After not having heard those words for many years, hearing them from their mother’s mouth again showed how fearful she was that her little granddaughter would be frightened.","Even with the threat of kneeling to repent, they still must see the baby.","When Old Lady Mo lifted the corner of the quilt, Mo brothers instantly felt their hearts melting.","The pink tender face, the little mouth still squirming from time to time, made them as uncles eager to immediately snatch her from their mother's arms and fawn over her.","\"Mother, is this our niece or nephew?\" Mo Chongyuan asked softly.","Old Lady Mo was also looking at her granddaughter, the more she looked, the more she liked her, unable to take her eyes off at all.","\"So beautiful, of course she's your niece.\"","\"No wonder she's so beautiful, even cuter than Hanyue when she was little.\" As Mo Jiacheng spoke, he couldn't help reaching out a finger, trying to touch his niece's tender pink cheek, only to be slapped away by Old Lady Mo.","\"Get away! Don't ruin my granddaughter with your coarse hands!\"","Rebuked by his mother, Mo Jiacheng was so frightened that he quickly withdrew his hand.","He was still reluctant. After being married for so many years, not having a single son or daughter of his own, he had been hoping that one of his brothers in the family could give birth to the next generation sooner, so that he could also bask in their glory and dote on them.","The Ninth Brother and his wife were respectable, giving birth to two babies at once for Mo Family. But Mother still wouldn't let him touch.","Mother only said he couldn't touch, she didn't say he couldn't hold.","Taking advantage of when Mother was tidying the baby's quilt, Mo Jiacheng suddenly grabbed the child from her arms.","\"Mother, you are too old and have no strength. It's better if I hold her.\"","The other brothers actually had the same idea, but were afraid it would upset Mother, so they endured without doing the same.","Now that Niece was taken by Mo Jiacheng, the brothers instantly became excited.","\"Second brother, hold her for a while then give her back to me.\"","\"Yes, let's take turns holding niece.\"","\"Me too...\"","Seeing her sons like this, Old Lady Mo didn't know whether to laugh or cry.","It was good that there were more people to dote on her granddaughter together, but she herself hadn't had enough time to fawn over the baby yet!","\"Jiacheng, quickly give the baby back to me. You are so clumsy, what if you hurt her accidentally?\"","Before her words had even fallen, she had already pushed past the sons in front of her and grabbed the child back from Mo Jiacheng's arms.","Successfully snatching her granddaughter back, Old Lady Mo did not dare to pause for a moment and hurried towards her own courtyard."]},{"number":469,"title":"Chapter 469: Three Joys at the Door","paragraphs":["The brothers saw Mother take away their little niece and hurriedly followed her. After all, as long as they stayed with Mother, they would still have a chance to see such a cute baby...","At this time, Dabao was sleeping soundly in Grandma's arms.","He still didn't know that as soon as he was born, his sister had taken away the affection from him.","He Zhiran was always thinking about seeing her twins. She thought that as long as she closed her eyes to rest for a while, she would be able to soon.","Because she was so exhausted, as soon as she closed her eyes, she fell asleep.","He Ziming had been waiting outside the room. When Mother had carried Dabao out just now, he had already seen him.","As an expert gynecologist, he had of course seen many newborn babies before, but He Ziming felt that even if he excluded his blood relationship with the child, just looking at it from an outsider's perspective, his little nephew was the best looking among the newborns, without a doubt.","At the moment, he still wanted to go and see his eldest nephew, but Mother had been inside his younger sister's delivery room all this time. He was an extremely proper man who even treated his own younger sister as an outsider to the family.","Therefore, He Ziming could only gaze longingly in the direction of He Zhiran's door, hoping that Mother would carry out little nephew soon.","After waiting for a long time, the door finally opened.","Madam He came out lovingly carrying Dabao.","He Ziming quickly stepped forward.","\"Mother, let me hold the little one.\"","Unlike Old Lady Mo, although reluctant, Madam He carefully handed Dabao into He Ziming's arms, while not forgetting to remind him, \"Be careful, you must be very careful.\"","Without his mother's reminder, He Ziming would still be careful. This was the treasure that his sister had suffered so much to give birth to, who would one day call him big uncle.","Holding Dabao, He Ziming's heart softened.","This was his little nephew!","The little nephew that warmed one's heart at first sight!","\"Mother, in our excitement, we haven't weighed little nephew yet.\"","Madam He slapped her forehead.","\"Look at me, I'm so muddled that I forgot something so important.\"","The scale had been prepared in advance and was placed in the side room. Mother and son carefully placed the little bundle on it.","Madam He was pleasantly surprised.","\"He actually weighs six pounds. No wonder he looks so chubby.\"","Speaking of this, Madam He's eyes reddened again.","\"Zhiran really suffered...\"","He Ziming held little nephew with one hand and patted Madam He on the shoulder with the other.","\"It's all over now. I'll help Zhiran recuperate later. She'll recover quickly.\"","Madam He wiped the tears from the corners of her eyes and nodded, \"Yes, fortunately you are here.\"","Mo Jiuye had the same thought, fortunately He Ziming was here.","When He Zhiran had first gone into labor, he had already panicked. In that situation, he really didn't know if he could have successfully completed the C-section.","Now he didn't want to do anything, not even look at the children. He just held He Zhiran's hand, looked at her tenderly, and hoped her body would recover quickly.","Old Lady Mo was escorted back to her courtyard by a group of sons.","Mo Qing had already heard the good news. Unfortunately, he was immobilized and couldn't go outside Mo Jiuye's courtyard to wait like his sons.","But he was truly eager to see his little grandson and granddaughter.","Therefore, after making up his mind, he tried using the crutches that his daughter-in-law had commissioned for the first time to walk.","Perhaps it was because he had a yearning in his heart, he actually managed to stand up with the crutches.","While overjoyed, he tried to take a step forward...","Originally, Mo Qing had never had much hope for his legs. Just being able to straighten them was very satisfying.","Although his legs had regained some sensation, they couldn't exert any strength at all and were soft as noodles.","He didn't want to trouble his old wife again by practicing the impossible of walking, so the crutches had been left in the room for a month and he had never thought of trying them.","But today, in order to see his precious grandchildren, Mo Qing really went all out.","Although it took great effort, he still managed to get out of the room successfully.","As soon as he opened the door, he saw his old wife holding a bundle in her arms, surrounded by a group of sons walking towards him.","Old Lady Mo and several sons were all dumbfounded at the sight.","Mo Junrui and Mo Yunfeng ran over at almost the same time.","The joy in their eyes was unmistakable.","\"Father, you can stand up and walk now?\"","As they spoke, the two brothers had already come to his sides to support him.","At this moment, Mo Qing didn't have the heart to respond to his sons. He didn't pretend to be strong either, and let the two sons support him as his eyes remained fixed on the bundle in his old wife's arms.","\"Is this my grandson?\"","Seeing that Mo Qing could stand up, Old Lady Mo was equally delighted.","She didn't immediately answer Mo Qing's question, but asked back, \"Lord, you can stand up now, how wonderful.\"","\"Father, Mother, our Mo family really has double joy. Ninth brother and sister have given birth to two babies for Mo family at one go, and Father can stand up again.\" Second brother said excitedly.","\"Second brother is wrong. Ninth brother and sister gave birth to two babies, which is already double joy. And Father being able to stand up should make it triple joy.\" Fifth brother smiled and corrected.","\"Elder Fifth is right, it should indeed be triple joy.\" Second brother quickly corrected his slip of the tongue after realizing his mistake.","Seeing them bantering and ignoring him, Mo Qing was anxious.","\"Stop talking, show me my grandson first.\"","Only then did Old Lady Mo realize that she had brought back the precious granddaughter to show Mo Qing.","She instructed her sons,","\"Help your father back into the room first.\"","Mo Qing also knew newborns were susceptible to chills. Even if he was eager to see them, he could only endure.","Helped back into bed by his sons, Old Lady Mo also placed the second child beside him, then gently flipped up a corner of the small quilt.","\"This is our granddaughter, she's the younger one of the two babies.\"","Mo Qing craned his neck to look. The impatient expression eager to see his grandson just now instantly disappeared, replaced by eyes full of tenderness.","\"What a beautiful child, even prettier than our HanYing.\"","\"Of course, with such good-looking parents, how could the child not be good-looking?\"","Mo Qing was annoyed at what his old wife said.","\"Are you saying I'm ugly?\" When I was young, wasn't I also very handsome and dashing?","Old Lady Mo refused to back down.","\"You're not ugly, but neither are you as good-looking as Jiuye, and I'm not as pretty as Zhiran. Isn't that right?\"","Mo Qing...","He couldn't refute this because what his old wife said was the truth.","He shut up and continued looking at his precious granddaughter."]},{"number":470,"title":"Chapter 470: Milk Name","paragraphs":["At this time, the several brothers could also see the appearance of Er Bao more clearly. Her chubby little face looked fleshy.","\"Mother, how much does our little niece weigh?\" Being asked by her son, Old Lady Mo only just remembered that she was so preoccupied with holding her darling granddaughter that she actually forgot to weigh her.","Seeing his mother's appearance, Mo Jia Cheng knew that she must have forgotten to weigh their little niece.","\"Mother, there's a scale in my yard. I'll go get it now.\"","After weighing, everyone laughed.","\"I knew it, my precious granddaughter gets heavier after holding her for a long time. It turns out she's so chubby, actually five catties and nine taels. \" Five catties and nine taels was considered skinny in modern times. But this was ancient times, with scarce resources.","The rich families were still alright. Pregnant women would be given silver to nourish their bodies during pregnancy.","In poor peasant families, there was no such treatment. Pregnant women could only eat what everyone else was eating, as long as their stomachs were not empty, it was already heaven's grace.","There was another reason - the low medical standards here. Too large a fetus would make it difficult for the mother to give birth. Therefore, many people would appropriately control weight gain even during pregnancy, not daring to let the child grow wildly in the womb.","As a result, few people here could give birth to children over five or six catties.","Moreover, twins are much smaller than singletons to begin with, and even the combined weight of twins may only equal that of one singleton.","And now their family's twins turned out to be so heavy, which made Old Lady Mo happy while also feeling distressed over He Zhiran.","One could only say that her ninth daughter-in-law was lucky to have such chubby twins born safe and sound.","Her two grandsons were already born with blessings - their disabled grandfather could now walk with a cane on this very day.","The more Old Lady Mo looked at little granddaughter, the more she liked her.","\"Master, our Mo family has always had more males than females. This little granddaughter will be the pearl in the palm of our Mo family. We must give her a nice sounding name.\"","In Dashun, it was the elder with the highest seniority in the family who would name a newborn child. By saying this, Old Lady Mo was also reminding Mo Qing that he should be thinking of names for the two babies.","Mo Qing had now completely let go. The way he currently was, if not for his family taking care of him, even if he was saved, he would not have been able to survive.","On the first day he returned to Xiling Village, he had already made his stance clear that the Mo family affairs would now be handled by Mo Jiuye couple going forward.","Moreover, after a period of observation, he found that his ninth daughter-in-law was exceptionally wise. For something like naming his grandchildren, he did not want to assert his seniority.","He believed that whatever names his ninth daughter-in-law picked would definitely be better than his own choices.","Although he thought this way, he still had to put on a show on the surface.","\"Let's leave the children's official names for their parents to decide. I'll suggest some milk names that we can call them.\"","Everyone agreed with this.","\"Ranran has made such great sacrifices to continue the Mo family line. Naming should be left to her as their mother.\"","He paused, then Old Lady Mo asked: \"What milk names does Master plan to give the two grandchildren?\"","Looking at his sleeping granddaughter next to him, Mo Qing said gently, \"I just said, she is the pearl in the palm of our Mo family. Her milk name will be Mingzhu (Bright Pearl).\"","\"Mingzhu, what a nice name. Precious, tough, resilient - that's how the Mo family's daughters should be.\" Mo Chongyuan agreed.","With everyone's approval, Er Bao successfully got the milk name Mingzhu.","Although Mo Qing had not seen his precious grandson with his own eyes yet, his wife had just roughly described his looks to him.","After thinking for a bit, he said, \"Our grandson's milk name will be Zhu (Pillar).\"","\"Zhu?\" Old Lady Mo very much disapproved.","She may not have carried the grandson back to her own yard, but that did not mean she only doted on the granddaughter. She liked the grandson just as much.","Why did the granddaughter get such a nice-sounding milk name, while the grandson only deserved to be called a Zhu?","Mo Qing knew his wife had misunderstood him and quickly explained,","\"I love my grandson just as much. He is the eldest grandson of our Mo family. I gave him this milk name because I hope he becomes the pillar of the next Mo generation.\"","Pillar was a good thing, but the name Zhu was just too casual, same as those West Ridge village children.","This was what everyone present thought - that even if it was just a milk name, it should still sound grander since he was the Mo family's eldest grandson.","Although Old Lady Mo also felt the milk name did not do her grandson justice, she did not want to contradict her husband's intention either. After all, this was the first time she had seen him so happy since he returned, and she could also see that he had put careful thought into naming his grandson.","\"It's just a family milk name that we find easy to call. Outsiders won't refer to the children this way anyway, besides, Zhu will still get an official name. When he goes to school in the future, he would also have a courtesy name.\"","Seeing that mother approved of father's choice, the few Mo brothers had also firmly made up their minds about something.","Just like them, ever since Huan Ying was born, their parents obviously favored their younger sister. It seemed that the two elders of the Mo family were really exceptionally fond of girls over boys...","The two Mo elders were oblivious that their sons had labeled them representatives of gender bias favoring females over males. Happily, they gazed at the cute little Mingzhu.","The more the brothers thought about it, the more they felt a sense of kinship with their little nephew - a shared experience of being the victims of parental favoritism towards daughters. Exchanging looks, they decided to go take a look at the boy so that their nephew would not feel even the slightest bit neglected growing up feeling like the lesser preferred gender in the Mo family, with them as uncles failing in their duties.","The few brothers noisily ran towards Mo Jiuye's yard again. Unsure of which room the little nephew was in and also afraid to disturb the recently delivering younger sister, the brothers blinked at each other at a loss standing in the yard.","Although Mo Jiuye had devoted all his attention to his wife, as a man accustomed to staying vigilant, he could still hear the footsteps in his yard.","He gently placed He Zhiran's hand back down, covered her with the blanket, before lightly treading out of the room.","Hearing the door open, the brothers' gazes unanimously shifted over.","\"Ninth brother, where's our little nephew?\" There was pity in the second brother's eyes as he spoke.","Having had a sleepless night facing his own brothers, Mo Jiuye did not bother noticing their odd behaviors.","\"Mother-in-law just took him to the side room.\"","\"Let's go see little nephew.\" Knowing his location, big brother took the lead, as long as it wasn't their sister's room, it was convenient for them to visit.","Following closely behind big brother, the few brothers appeared together in the side room.","At this time, He Ziming was hugging Dabao, eyes softened to mush. Seeing the big group of people suddenly swarm in, he was dumbfounded for a moment before hurriedly hugging Dabao tighter."]},{"number":471,"title":"Chapter 471: Our little Nephew looks Good.","paragraphs":["He knew very well that as soon as the Mo brothers came over, the little nephew would no longer be his alone. Although he was unwilling, he would still show the courtesy that should be given.","\"Greetings to several brothers.\"","Since the Mo brothers were all older than him, he simply addressed them as brother like his sister and brother-in-law.","\"We are all family, Eldest Young Master He does not need to stand on ceremony.\" The eldest brother said, and then rushed to the pillar impatiently.","Although Zhu Ziming was reluctant to let others hold his little nephew, he also understood clearly that the people who had come were all uncles of the little nephew, and it would be unreasonable not to let them hold the baby for a while.","He reluctantly handed the little nephew over to Eldest Brother Mo.","\"Eldest Brother, be gentle.\" Zhu Ziming couldn't help reminding them. The young men of the Mo family were all martial artists with great strength. If they accidentally hurt the little nephew, it would not be worth it.","There was no need for Zhu Ziming to remind them.","The eldest brother knew that his strength was too big and he was afraid of hurting his little nephew. When holding the child, he was even more careful than Zhu Ziming.","Seeing that the eldest brother was holding the little nephew, the brothers gathered around.","However, from their actions, it could be determined that they were all being gentle.","\"Eldest brother, our little nephew is so cute,\" Mo Chongyuan said softly, with obvious fondness in his tone.","\"Well, this child is indeed handsome, much better looking than Jiuye when he was born,\" the eldest brother said as he looked at the sleeping nephew in his arms. Then he said to Mo Jiuye, \"Jiuye, father has already given the two children milk names.\"","Mo Jiuye was not very surprised by this. It was an ancient custom for the elders in the family to give a child his formal name. Giving them a milk name was not strange.","\"Eldest brother, what milk names has father given them?\"","Second brother sighed.","\"Oh... I really don't know what father was thinking. Our little niece's milk name is Bright Pearl, which sounds very nice and has good meaning. She is the treasure in the palm of the Mo family.\" As he spoke, he looked at the little nephew in his big brother's arms sympathetically and couldn't help reaching out to touch his little hand that was exposed.","\"Such a good child, he had to be called Zhu. It's a down-to-earth milk name, the same as those children in Xi Ling Village.\"","After all, they had grown up in the capital since childhood and had been in contact with children of wealthy families. They had never seen anyone from a prominent family give a child such a milk name.","Afraid that Jiuye would be unhappy because of this, the eldest brother quickly explained, \"Jiuye, father feels that your eldest son is the eldest grandson of our Mo family and will be the pillar of the Mo family in the future, so he gave him this milk name. A milk name is just for family members to call him. When the time comes, you and your wife can give your child a nice formal name.\"","Mo Jiuye had never thought about what to call his children.","In his heart, what they were called didn't matter, as long as they grew up safe and sound.","\"If father thinks it's fine, then it's fine. A milk name just needs to roll off the tongue easily.\"","Seeing Mo Jiuye say this, the brothers glanced at each other.","Jiuye really had no sense that father valued daughters over sons.","Never mind, his nephews still had their uncles who would dote on him.","Seeing that he had no more business here, Mo Jiuye went back to keep He Zhiran company.","He Zhiran had always been a light sleeper. If she hadn't been so exhausted from giving birth earlier, she wouldn't have been able to sleep so deeply.","As soon as Mo Jiuye came to her bedside, she opened her eyes.","\"Ranran, you're awake?\" Mo Jiuye hurried over.","He Zhiran pushed herself up into a sitting position with both hands. Mo Jiuye quickly went forward to support her.","\"Ranran, do you feel uncomfortable anywhere? Are you hungry? I'll have Yu'er make you something to eat.\"","He Zhiran shook her head and leaned against Mo Jiuye's arms. Her eyes looked around the room.","\"Where are the children?\"","\"Mingzhu was taken by mother to show father. Zhu is with mother-in-law in the other room.\"","Mo Jiuye smiled. \"Mingzhu and Zhu are our children's milk names.\"","He Zhiran also smiled. She had only been asleep for a short while and the children already had milk names.","\"Did you pick them?\"","She knew the rules of Da Shun Dynasty very clearly. The given names of children had to be chosen by the elders in the family. These milk names must have been thought up by Mo Jiuye himself.","However, they rolled off the tongue well enough. She didn't see anything wrong with her son's name Zhu either.","A milk name just had to be easy to say.","\"Father named them. He said Zhu is our eldest grandson and will be the pillar of the family in the future, so he gave him that milk name.\"","Mo Jiuye was worried that his wife would be unhappy about their son's milk name and quickly explained.","He Zhiran didn't think there was anything wrong with her son's milk name. When she was little, she often heard the elders chatting that giving a child an unattractive name was good for raising them well.","Besides, Zhu wasn't a terribly unattractive name for her son either. It sounded nice enough.","Therefore, she didn't realize that Mo Jiuye was explaining something to her.","At the moment, all she wanted was to see her twins. Also, it had been several hours since she gave birth and the babies still hadn't eaten.","Speaking of the babies eating, He Zhiran felt her chest. It didn't have that swollen feeling that would come later on.","Fortunately, she had prepared newborn formula in advance from shopping on Taobao.","\"Dear, the children must be hungry by now.\"","Mo Jiuye looked outside. Indeed, it had been over two hours since the babies were born and they still hadn't eaten.","\"Alright, I'll go bring the children back now.\"","Thinking that his son and daughter must still be hungry, he felt a little anxious as their father.","But just as he had opened the door, he heard faint cries of a baby from the yard.","It was Old Lady Mo carrying Bright Pearl back in a hurry.","\"Jiuye, is Ranran awake? Bright Pearl must be hungry and crying from it.\"","At the same time, Madam He also came out from the other room carrying Zhu.","\"I think Zhu must be hungry too. He's not crying but his little mouth keeps moving.\"","Mo Jiuye had intended to carry one baby in each hand back to the room and then enter the space with his wife to feed them formula.","But as soon as he took Zhu from his mother-in-law's arms, he became a little nervous.","The child was so small and soft. He was afraid he might accidentally hurt him if he wasn't careful enough.","If he tried to hold Bright Pearl too, he probably wouldn't even be able to walk properly.","Left with no other choice, Mo Jiuye could only let his mother keep carrying Bright Pearl as they went back to the room together.","Just in time, Madam He also wanted to check on her daughter, so she followed behind them.","By now, Bright Pearl was still crying relentlessly. As soon as Old Lady Mo saw He Zhiran sitting up, she immediately brought the child to her arms.","\"Ranran, Bright Pearl must be hungry. Quickly feed her.\"","Actually, a month before He Zhiran's due date, Old Lady Mo had suggested getting a wet nurse.","But the offer was refused by He Zhiran.","Her reason was simple. She hoped to be able to breastfeed the twins herself. If that didn't work out, she could always buy formula from Taobao Mall."]},{"number":472,"title":"Chapter 472: I don't want them to Starve.","paragraphs":["He Zhiran did not reject the custom of hiring wet nurses in this era. After all, she was a soul from the modern era and felt that the parent-child bonding time should start from raising the babies themselves.","Once a wet nurse was hired, the child would rely on her even more than their birth mother. Although this was a short-term phenomenon and the dependence would slowly recover after the child was weaned, He Zhiran still did not like it.","Besides, as long as you bought the right brand of formula, the nutritional content would be even higher than breast milk.","He Zhiran unconsciously glanced at her own chest and smiled bitterly.","\"Mother, I probably don't have any breast milk.\"","Now Old Lady Mo was at a loss in front of He Zhiran, circling around her.","\"I should have listened to you and hired a wet nurse to come back.\"","When He Zhiran refused to hire a wet nurse, she did not insist.","After all, her ninth daughter-in-law had always been in good health, and she did not vomit severely or unable to eat like others during pregnancy.","Therefore, she never thought that her ninth daughter-in-law would have the problem of not having milk.","As she spoke, Old Lady Mo had already turned and walked outside.","\"I'll go to the village to find out which family has a woman who has just given birth, to come and help.\"","She couldn't let her precious grandson and granddaughter go hungry.","Watching Old Lady Mo's back, He Zhiran quickly called her back.","\"Mother, don't worry for now, my husband and I have prepared.\"","Old Lady Mo stopped and turned her head.","\"You two have prepared?\"","Mo Jiuye explained, \"Mother, have you forgotten that we have raised so many dairy cows on our ranch?\"","Old Lady Mo knew that the family had dairy cows, but she had never heard that those cows had started producing milk.","In fact, the cows were not yet producing milk. But for He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye, producing a lactating dairy cow was not difficult at all with the aid of the space.","\"Mother, I found early this morning that a dairy cow was producing milk, and the milk quality was very good. Zhiran learned a method to make the cow's milk softer, which is very suitable for newborn babies to drink,\" Mo Jiuye lied effortlessly without any sense of dissonance.","He explained this way because his wife had told him about the benefits of formula milk and the differences from fresh cow's milk.","He was just relaying this to his mother.","His main purpose was to get both mothers to leave so that he and his wife could take the babies into the space for their first meal in this world.","Afraid that Mo Jiuye's words were not convincing enough, He Zhiran chimed in, \"Mother, please rest assured. I went through so much hardship to give birth to them, I certainly can't bear to let them go hungry.\"","\"Since that's the case, Mother will stay and help you feed the babies,\" Madam He did not want to leave.","Her daughter had just given birth and her body was still so weak. Her son-in-law looked somewhat clumsy. She would not feel assured without staying to help.","At this moment, it seemed that Old Lady Mo realized something.","She went forward and pulled Madam He along.","\"Sister-in-law, they are the parents. Since they don't want to hire a wet nurse and want to feed the babies with cow's milk, let them handle this themselves.\"","Without further ado, Old Lady Mo had already pulled Madam He to the door and closed it behind her.","Madam He was puzzled, but the children’s grandmother had already pulled her out, so it would be inappropriate for her to go back in.","After the two elderly women left, He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye did not immediately enter the space.","After all, they could not be sure if the two would come back again.","At this time, Mo Jiuye was holding Zhu and He Zhiran was holding Mingzhu.","Perhaps because they were beside their parents, the little brother and sister were not making any fuss at all.","There were still traces of tears in the corners of Mingzhu's eyes. She had fallen asleep in He Zhiran's arms.","Since the children were not crying, He Zhiran was in no hurry to enter the space.","She and Mo Jiuye sat side by side, looking at their son and daughter together for the first time.","The more they looked, the more they loved them. They loved both equally.","Mo Jiuye sincerely said, \"Zhiran, thank you.\"","For this word of thanks, He Zhiran did not respond like she usually would by saying something like \"We're family, no need to be so polite\".","Because no one knew better than her what kind of torment she had suffered to successfully give birth to the twins.","Especially when her brother-in-law helped turn the fetus, that feeling could be described as a fate worse than death.","But looking at the silly and cute baby son and daughter sleeping soundly, she felt that it was all worthwhile.","Mo Jiuye listened to the movement outside and knew that both mothers had walked away before the family of four flashed into the space.","It happened to be the hot summer season, and He Zhiran had just given birth and was confined to bed rest. The room door and windows were closed airtight without ventilation, in sharp contrast to the suitable temperature in the space.","Perhaps feeling the temperature difference, the two sleeping babies woke up one after another.","Maybe they preferred the temperature in the space. The siblings did not cry or make a fuss.","With a thought from He Zhiran, the baby cribs she had purchased for the babies from Taobao Treasure Mall appeared before her eyes.","The two gently placed their treasures in the cribs while Mo Jiuye went to the medical room to prepare milk powder for his children.","At this time, Rice Ball, who was playing in the bamboo forest, also heard the sounds from this side.","Because she gave birth, this was the longest time He Zhiran had not accessed the space.","Perhaps because it had not seen its master for so long, Rice Ball ran towards her at a much faster speed than usual.","Its four little short legs moved swiftly back and forth, and its round big head kept swaying.","When it got close to its master, Rice Ball immediately sensed an unfamiliar aura.","As a result, it did not rush into its master's arms like it usually did. Instead, it slammed the brakes at a distance more than one meter away from He Zhiran.","Then the little guy began looking around for the source of the unfamiliar aura, eventually fixing its eyes on the two baby milk dolls.","He Zhiran was amused watching Rice Ball's series of actions. She knew that it must have felt unfamiliar.","She beckoned Rice Ball over, then pointed at her twins and patiently explained,","\"Rice Ball, they are all my children.\" As she spoke, He Zhiran picked up Zhu, who was closer to her, and carefully brought him in front of Rice Ball for it to see.","\"Look, isn't he very cute.\"","In order for Rice Ball to understand, she also pointed at her now flattened abdomen,","\"They were originally here and have now been born...\"","Rice Ball seemed to understand. It bleated a string of sheep calls.","He Zhiran could now roughly discern the meaning conveyed in Rice Ball's bleats. She knew that the sheep calls represented happiness, which meant that it had probably understood her words.","However, she still had to give it a reminder.","\"Rice Ball, you have to be softer. They're sleeping. If you wake them up, they'll cry.\"","Rice Ball was just about to let out another bleat to respond to its master to prove that it understood."]},{"number":473,"title":"Chapter 473: Mother found out my secret","paragraphs":["However, it soon seemed to realize something. Its two furry big black hands covered its mouth, forcibly swallowing back the sound that was about to come out.","He Zhiran was relieved to see Rice Ball being obedient, and reached out to touch its head.","Receiving its owner's leniency, Rice Ball regained its lively appearance. It scooted forward, wrapped its arms around He Zhiran's calves, and stretched its head high to look at the little baby in her arms.","As it watched, it lowered its little head over and stuck out its tongue at the same time.","He Zhiran knew that Rice Ball's actions showed that it liked Zhu. However, the way Rice Ball showed its fondness was not yet suitable for Zhu.","\"Rice Ball cannot do that. He is still too young.\"","Rice Ball stopped its actions in frustration, clearly feeling its owner was very disappointed.","But soon it changed its target, climbed onto the baby bed where Mingzhu was lying, and stuck out its round, plump head to watch from there.","He Zhiran did not mind Rice Ball liking her pair of children, as long as it did not have any excessive actions, she would not stop it.","From Rice Ball's eyes one could ascertain that it really liked the two little ones.","Mo Jiuye came back with milk powder. Although the composition was different from the Puppy Milk that it usually drank, the milky aroma was exactly the same.","However, it could feel that these two bottles were for the little babies.","If it were in the past, as soon as it smelled this scent, it would have rushed over to hug Mo Jiuye’s legs.","Today Rice Ball forcibly endured it, only looking at them yearningly with its little eyes, which still moved He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye.","Mo Jiuye stroked its head.","\"Rice Ball's puppy milk has to wait a little bit.\"","As the father of the two babies, he wanted to personally go feed them himself, not to mention his wife’s body was still very weak now, unsuitable for doing these things.","Rice Ball understood everything, uh-huh'ed twice, and then obediently sat to one side watching.","He Zhiran was about to take a milk bottle from Mo Jiuye's hand, but was refused by Mo Jiuye.","He held a milk bottle in each hand, and separately brought the nipples to the two babies' mouths.","The two babies were indeed hungry, immediately sucking on the nipples to start eating.","Seeing this, Rice Ball arduously climbed onto Zhu's little bed, standing on the edge and reaching out to take the milk bottle in Mo Jiuye's hand.","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran looked at each other, both guessing Rice Ball’s intention.","He tentatively let go of his hand, giving the milk bottle to Rice Ball.","Rice Ball’s furry claws grabbed the milk bottle tightly without the position changing at all.","This scene made He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye laugh.","He Zhiran fondly rubbed Rice Ball's head.","\"Rice Ball can't speak, but understands everything.\"","\"Uh-huh...\" Rice Ball responded very cooperatively, and continued to attentively feed Zhu milk wholeheartedly.","Only after the two little ones were full did Mo Jiuye make more puppy milk for Rice Ball.","Rice Ball rushed happily to one side to drink milk. Looking at the two sleeping children, He Zhiran said:","\"It's not a long-term plan for us to always run into the space to feed the children.\"","Mo Jiuye also had this in mind.","\"Why don't we change the packaging of the milk powder and take it outside the space.\"","\"Can you explain where the milk powder comes from?\" At the moment, He Zhiran really did not have the energy to consider these things, after just giving birth she was exhausted.","Mo Jiuye was already used to being a scapegoat.","\"Didn't you notice when we asked the two mothers to go out before feeding the children? Mother should have noticed something. Even when mother-in-law was still hesitating, she took people out. You may not have seen that when Mother left, she also gave me a reassuring look.\"","\"Do you mean Mother found out my secret?\" He Zhiran felt a little unbelievable.","\"Not necessarily. They must be aware that we often have some inexplicable behaviors, but Mother won't say anything or ask anything.\" Mo Jiuye explained.","\"According to what you said, as long as Mother can help explain it, the matter of us taking out milk powder can be considered passed?\" He Zhiran asked.","\"Well, we don't really need to explain much. I just thought, milk powder is made from cow's milk after all. Our family raises so many dairy cows, and once they start producing milk, the quantity must be considerable.","Moreover, from my understanding, it's not easy to store cow's milk, especially in this hot summer weather, it would probably go bad in a day.","Although the Mo Family does business extensively, dairy products like milk are not easy to transport over long distances for sale either.","I've looked at the space console before, it can process milk into milk powder. Why don't we use the cow's milk to start a milk powder business? Not only does milk powder taste good, it's easy to preserve. I believe that working with the Mo Family, we will certainly earn a lot of income.\"","After listening to Mo Jiuye's words, He Zhiran felt like her mind was enlightened. She had not expected that a military general who went to battle could now have business acumen.","\"Husband, your method is really good, how could I not have thought of it?\" He Zhiran couldn't hide the delight in her tone at all.","She continued: \"Using the console to produce milk powder is not a long-term solution. We can buy a book on milk powder production methods from Taobao later and learn it. When the dairy cows start producing a lot of milk, we’ll open a milk powder workshop.\"","This was a business that could easily make big money with eyes closed.","It must be known that in Da Shun, due to the scarcity of milk, the selling price had always been very high.","Moreover, people could not drink milk whenever they wanted.","The reason was simple: Da Shun did not yet have the dairy cow breed. Even if people occasionally got to drink cow's milk, it was the small amount of supply produced after those yellow cows gave birth to calves.","As long as they successfully produced milk powder, it would be difficult not to make money.","\"Well, I’ll handle it when the time comes. You just focus on recuperating.\"","Considering there might be people coming to see the babies outside, the couple dared not stay in the space for too long.","After He Zhiran changed the packaging of the milk powder to bamboo tubes, she took some and left the space.","The family of four had just appeared in the room when they heard someone knocking on the door.","\"Madam, the kitchen has just prepared millet porridge and eggs for you. Lan Er has brought them in.\"","He Zhiran patted her chest and whispered to Mo Jiuye, \"Fortunately we came out from the space.\"","It seemed that with these two babies, it would be almost impossible for them to freely go in and out of the space in the future. Because there would always be someone coming to see the babies at any time. If someone found them not in the room, it would really be hard to explain.","Along with Lan Er was Madam He.","She first walked over to He Zhiran and asked caringly: \"Ran Ran, are the children full?\"","He Zhiran raised the two unwashed glass milk bottles to her mother's face.","\"Mother, look, they've finished all the milk that was prepared.\"","The reason why He Zhiran dared to take out the milk bottles openly was because glass was no longer a scarce item in the Mo Family home.","The windows of all their courtyards were made of glass, and there were also foreigners acting as scapegoats."]},{"number":474,"title":"Chapter 474: Six Brothers and Sisters, What's wrong with you","paragraphs":["Sure enough, after a brief moment of bewilderment upon seeing the milk bottle, Lady He soon realized this.","But she thought the milk bottle was made of translucent porcelain, quite valuable.","Although she thought this, she only felt the milk bottle was valuable. She didn't have any other suspicions.","In any case, the two little treasures had full stomachs, and as their grandmother she felt assured.","That night, the Mo Family were in joy because of the birth of the twins.","Not only that, but the news that He Zhiran had smoothly given birth to a pair of twin siblings also spread through the village.","Early the next morning, villagers came one after another to the Mo Family to offer eggs, local specialties, and the like as gifts of celebration.","Fang Chuanzhou, Xie Tianhai, Hu Cong, and Consort De also came over.","The gifts they brought were naturally much higher quality than those the villagers brought.","The villagers didn't know, but these people were clear.","The Mo Family seemed to have been cursed - although their sons were all married, not one had been able to have children.","Now that He Zhiran had successfully given birth to twins, it could be said that this unspeakable anguish of the Mo Family was thoroughly broken.","These several people were truly happy for the Mo Family.","Old Lady Mo kept praising that her ninth daughter-in-law was one with great fortune, giving birth all at once to two children who together formed the character for \"good\".","With descendants, the Mo Family people had even more hope for their future life.","They went about their daily work even more diligently than before, all hoping that through their own efforts, they could create an even better and more comfortable living environment for the two little ones.","On the day the two little ones had their head shaving ceremony, the Mo Family was exceptionally lively, with many guests coming without even needing to be invited.","The guests were naturally still the people close with the Mo Family and the villagers.","After the liveliness, the two little ones were held and brought back to He Zhiran's side.","The guests had just left when the seventh son, who had gone south to search for the old troops, returned.","He came back alone. Seeing the guests who had just left the house one after another with happy expressions, he guessed something auspicious must have happened in the family.","Therefore, Mo Yuance quickened his pace.","The eldest and second brothers were seeing the guests off. With one glance, they saw the travel-stained Mo Yuance.","\"Big Brother, Second Brother.\" Mo Yuance came to stand in front of the two elder brothers and pulled them towards the courtyard. \"Father and our brothers are home right?\"","\"I'll go call everyone right now.\" Knowing he had something to say, Second Brother immediately ran off to gather people.","Soon, with the exception of Mo Chuhan who was away taking up office, the Mo men gathered together in the main house.","Mo Yuance first paid his respects to his parents, then excitedly said, \"Thanks to good fortune, my trip south went very smoothly. I've brought back nine hundred brothers.\"","\"I took into consideration that bringing such a large group of people into the city in broad daylight would be no good. So I had them disguise themselves as ordinary commoners and enter the city bit by bit, taking a roundabout way to enter the village from the west side.\"","Mo Qing nodded in satisfaction. \"Mm, Yuance has gone to great effort.\"","Then he turned his head to look at Mo Jiacheng. \"Jiacheng, take a few people to the west side and when those subordinates arrive, arrange for people to escort them up the mountain.\"","Mo Jiuye had already installed mobile housing up the mountain. Although Mo Qing hadn't directly participated, he was aware of the matter.","Now that these people had arrived, they could immediately settle up the mountain without needing many people to worry over and arrange things.","Seeing his father mention this, Mo Jiacheng was reminded. \"Father, don't you plan to meet them first?\"","How could Mo Qing possibly not want to first meet those good brothers who had followed the Mo sons through life and death?","It was just that his legs and feet were really inconvenient right now.","His inconvenient mobility was just an excuse in his heart. The true reason was that Mo Qing always felt he had already become a cripple, too ashamed to show his face before those people.","\"I won't go today. Everyone has gone to great pains hurrying on the road. Send them to go rest first.\"","His sons of course understood their father's thoughts. They saw through it but didn't speak of it.","\"Alright, I'll go to the west side to receive them now.\" After speaking, the second son went out to gather people.","After the second son left, Mo Yuance asked, \"Father, Mother, I saw a lot of guests being seen off from the house earlier. Did something festive happen in the family?\"","His younger sister's wedding had been on June 12th. He hadn't made it back from the south for it. Could it be that his ninth younger brother's wife had given birth?","Speaking of the family's festive event, Old Lady Mo's expression lit up with a smile.","\"While you were gone, you really did miss two happy events in the family. You weren't here for Han Yue marrying into the family. Then a few days ago, your ninth younger brother's wife gave your father and me a grandson and a granddaughter.\"","\"Mother, did you say ninth younger brother's wife gave birth to a pair of twins, a brother and a sister?\"","Old Lady Mo nodded with a smile. \"Yes, precisely as you said. The pillar is the elder brother, Mingzhu is the little sister.\"","Mo Yuance already came to stand in front of Mo Jiuye, heavily thudding him on the shoulder.","\"Still, it's impressive for you little rascal, continuing the incense for our Mo family.\"","Although the punch looked a bit heavy, for Mo Jiuye it was nothing much.","\"Seventh brother, Zhiran gave the sisters-in-law health preserving medicine. I trust it won't be long before more and more children will be born in our family.\"","Whether others believed it or not, he wouldn't doubt his wife's medical skills one bit.","It was only a matter of time before his sisters-in-law became pregnant and gave birth.","Because Mo Yuance returned and was saying serious matters in the main house, the sisters-in-law, even if curious, wouldn't come forward and intrude to listen together.","Some of the rules they had in the capital still hadn't completely changed yet. That was, women wouldn't crowd forward when men were discussing major affairs.","Although they couldn't come forward and listen openly, that didn't stop them from waiting outside the house.","Mo Jiuye hadn't lowered his voice too much just now when speaking, plus he didn't intentionally try to avoid anyone hearing. Therefore, his words had been heard very clearly by the sisters-in-law.","Now, the second sister-in-law was completely unable to remain calm.","She quickly strode to the door and loudly asked those inside the house, \"Ninth younger brother, you weren't just trying to comfort your seventh elder brother earlier, were you?\"","Otherwise, why was there still no sign whatsoever from their group of sisters after having already taken the medicine for so long?","\"Impossible. Ruan Ruan's medical skills are clear for all to see. Since she said the poison in the sisters-in-laws can be eliminated, then it definitely can be eliminated.\"","Just as the second sister-in-law was about to retort something, there was a sudden din from the crowd of women behind her.","\"Sixth younger sister-in-law, what's the matter, hurry and wake up.\"","\"Sixth sister-in-law... sixth sister-in-law...\"","Hearing this voice, everyone rushed to the courtyard. There they only saw the sixth sister-in-law with a somewhat pale complexion, eyes tightly shut, half slumped and supported in the arms of the eldest sister-in-law.","When something happened with their daughters-in-law, the sixth elder brother rushed to the very front.","But he didn't lose his head to anxiously. He stepped forward to wrap his arm around his wife's waist and pick her up. Looking towards Mo Jiuye, he said, \"Ninth younger brother, terribly sorry to trouble asking your wife to take a look at sixth sister-in-law.\"","Xi Ling Village didn't have any doctors. When villagers got sick, they either had to go to the neighboring village to ask doctors to make a special trip over or go the Yun City medical center.","Even so, the medical skills of those doctors still weren't as superb as the ninth younger sister-in-law.","It was just that the ninth younger sister-in-law was currently in her postpartum confinement period. If it wasn't because the sixth elder brother was too worried about his wife's condition, he also wouldn't suggest going to disturb her."]},{"number":475,"title":"Chapter 475: It's True","paragraphs":["Mo Jiuye did not have time to react before Sixth elder brother had already darted away with his wife in his arms using lightness kungfu.","Seeing this, Mo Jiuye quickly followed, while the women anxiously ran after them.","Sixth elder brother was worried about his wife's health, so he was the first to arrive at the courtyard of Mo Jiuye's home.","However, he still had good judgement and told Lan Er to first go in and inform Ninth younger sister and brother.","Soon, Lan Er came out, followed by He Zhiran.","Although He Zhiran was still recovering from childbirth, her family had taken good care of her and she felt her body had almost fully recovered. If not for Madam He watching over her every day, she would have gone out to get some fresh air long ago.","When she reached the door and saw Sixth elder brother holding his unconscious wife, she quickly moved aside.","\"Sixth elder brother, quickly take Sixth Sister-in-law to the bed.\"","Seeing that she was unconscious, Sixth elder brother did not care that this was his younger sister's postpartum room, and quickly carried his wife to He Zhiran's bed.","At this time, the two little ones were sleeping soundly on the side of the bed, and were not woken by the commotion.","Everyone's attention was on Sixth Sister-in-law, so those who wanted to see the two babies could only restrain themselves for now.","He Zhiran took Sixth Sister-in-law's pulse. Not long after, she smiled and stood up.","\"Sixth Sister-in-law is fine.\"","\"Fine?\"","She's unconscious, how could she be fine?","Sixth elder brother was completely bewildered.","The others were also equally confused, staring at He Zhiran.","He Zhiran sat calmly by the bedside.","\"Sixth Sister-in-law is pregnant, around one month along. Her fainting is due to different reactions in early pregnancy for each woman, as well as Sixth Sister-in-law's somewhat weak constitution. It's a manifestation of qi and blood deficiency.\"","After hearing He Zhiran's words, Sixth elder brother stood motionless for a long time before reacting.","\"Younger... younger sister, are you saying my wife is pregnant?\"","He Zhiran nodded. \"Absolutely, Sixth Sister-in-law will wake up after sleeping for a while. I'll have Yu Er make some nourishing meals later to help regulate her body over the next few days.\"","No one in the Mo family would doubt her words.","Especially not Second Sister-in-law, who had urgently asked Mo Jiuye earlier because she was so eager to have a child of her own.","Now seeing that Sixth younger sister had successfully conceived, she believed that she too would have such a day sooner or later.","At this moment, the sisters-in-law could not help turning red-eyed in unison.","In the decade plus they had married into the Mo family, especially the older sisters-in-law, they had been longing for the day they could have a child of their own.","Now, seeing the joyful news from Sixth younger sister, in addition to feeling hopeful, they also felt more urgency.","Second Sister-in-law had always been easygoing. Seeing that Ninth younger sister was still spirited, she stretched out her wrist in front of her.","\"Ninth younger sister, take a look at Second Sister-in-law for me. Our sisters-in-law took the antidote together, so the timing should be about the same.\"","He Zhiran did not know how to respond to such unreliable words. She simply reached out silently to take Second Sister-in-law's pulse.","Before long, He Zhiran retracted her hand.","\"Second Sister-in-law, don't be impatient. You will have a child sooner or later.\"","Although a little disappointed, Second Sister-in-law still smiled.","\"Ninth younger sister is right. With my healthy body, I'm sure to have my own child.\"","She would definitely make her husband put in more effort tonight so they could have their own child sooner...","Since she had taken Second Sister-in-law's pulse, He Zhiran could not show favoritism. With the sisters-in-law present, she took each of their pulses in turn.","Surprisingly, her actions brought another piece of good news to the Mo family.","It turned out Third Sister-in-law was also pregnant, about a month earlier than Sixth Sister-in-law, meaning Third Sister-in-law was already two months along.","This news greatly shocked Third Sister-in-law. Her monthly cycle had always been irregular, with delays of one or two months being common. Plus she could eat and sleep well every day without any discomfort, so she had not considered this possibility at all.","Third Sister-in-law excitedly grabbed He Zhiran's hand.","\"Ninth younger sister, are you saying I'm really pregnant?\"","He Zhiran smiled and gently patted her hand. \"Third Sister-in-law, you're going to be a mother.\"","Pointing to He Ziming standing outside, she added, \"If Third Sister-in-law doesn't believe me, the gynecological saint is right there. Why not let him take another look?\"","He Ziming had intended to do so as well. He could hear everything his younger sister diagnosed in the room loud and clear.","Although he knew she had started reading medical books at a young age, he did not know the extent of her learning.","Just now she had determined pregnancy and its duration simply from pulse reading. He could not help but feel surprised.","Therefore, when He Zhiran said to let him take a look, he was already at the door.","\"Third Sister-in-law, I can examine you again if you don't mind.\"","With Ninth younger sister's renowned medical skills being undisputed in the Mo family, and the gynecological saint also living up to his reputation, Third Sister-in-law naturally would not decline his initiative to help.","Unsurprisingly, He Ziming's diagnosis for Third Sister-in-law was exactly the same as He Zhiran's. She was two months pregnant.","Having the pregnancy confirmed again, Third Sister-in-law's eyes welled up with tears that fell like pearls with severed strings, but the corners of her lips remained upturned.","Heaven knows how bitterly she had longed for this day.","After wiping the tears from the corners of her eyes, under the envious gazes of her sisters-in-law, Third Sister-in-law walked out of the room.","She knew her husband was in the courtyard. She wanted to immediately inform him of this joyful news.","Little did she expect that the Mo brothers were all martial artists with keen hearing. They had heard He Zhiran's diagnosis clearly.","Before his wife had even come out, Third elder brother was already waiting at the door.","\"Husband, Ninth younger sister... Ninth younger sister said, she said... we're going to have a child... wuwuwu...\"","Third Sister-in-law broke down in sobs again.","Third elder brother was also very emotional. If not for his brothers being present, he would have eagerly picked up his wife and spun her around.","The others looked at the couple with envy.","Since He Ziming had already lent a hand, he simply followed his younger sister's example and took the pulses of all the Mo sisters-in-law together. The conclusion was the same - they were all perfectly healthy, and having children was only a matter of time.","On the bed, Sixth Sister-in-law was also showing signs of waking up. Regarding women's illnesses, He Zhiran admitted she was not as skilled as He Ziming.","\"Eldest brother, why don't you take another look at Sixth Sister-in-law and prescribe some regimens.\"","Unlike the aloof image of the gynecological saint described by the common people, He Ziming did not hesitate at all in his treatment of the Mo family.","\"Alright. As long as I'm here, sisters-in-law can come to me anytime with concerns.\"","With He Ziming's words, the sisters-in-law were all thinking of asking him for health regimens during their free time, to conceive sooner."]},{"number":476,"title":"Chapter 476: Don't You Remember","paragraphs":["The news made the Mo family women look forward to their future life even more, at the same time, the Fifth Elder Brother also ran to inform the Two Elders.","Hearing that there were two more pregnant daughters-in-law in the family, the Two Elders simply couldn't help grinning from ear to ear.","However, they were not complacent because of joy. In order for the whole family to live a comfortable life, it was not yet time for them to relax.","Meng Huaining married Mo Hanyue and had been living in Xi Ling Village ever since the wedding three days ago. No matter how busy he was with official business, he would rush back every night.","Today, maybe there were more things to deal with in the yamen, he and Mo Chuhan were on their way back, and they just happened to meet the last batch of Old Department of Southern Territory coming into the village from the west.","Although there were not many people, it was late at night, and they looked sneaky, which would inevitably arouse suspicion.","Seeing this, Meng Huaining immediately leapt up and rushed towards the group, Mo Chuhan was no slower than him, and the two almost blocked the old department’s way at the same time.","“Who are you? Why did you come here so late at night?”","At this moonless and windy night, the old department simply couldn’t see the looks of the coming people.","However, they soon recognized Mo Chuhan's voice.","\"Is it Eighth Master?\"","Mo Chuhan couldn't match the voice to a name, but it did sound familiar.","\"Who exactly are you?\"","\"Eighth Master, it's me, Zhao Liu. Back at the days in Border Pass, I had always been your vanguard!\"","\"Eighth Master, and I'm Li Liang. I was with Zhao Liu. Don't you remember?\"","\"Eighth Master...\"","These old subordinates were obviously very excited. Before coming here, they had heard from Seventh Master that all the Mo family men, including the retired Duke, were alive. Now seeing Eighth Master alive with their own eyes, they didn’t know how to vent the excitement in their hearts.","Mo Chuhan didn't expect that after years of separation, he could still stand with these good brothers who had gone through life and death together.","\"Are you few the only ones who came to the northwest this time?\"","Li Liang took a few steps forward. Instead of answering Mo Chuhan right away, he took a look at Meng Huaining beside him.","Seventh Master had already told them to go to the northwest secretly, and they might not see the light for some time in the future.","Just now when they greeted Eighth Master, the one beside did not speak.","If it was another master of the Mo family who saw them, he would certainly be as enthusiastic as Eighth Master, after all, they often followed the Mo family men and understood their temper very well.","Therefore, Li Liang did not dare to answer Mo Chuhan rashly, but wanted to see Eighth Master's reaction first.","Mo Chuhan saw Li Liang's concerns. With his understanding of Meng Huaining, this guy was very shrewd. He could figure out the general idea from the few words just now. If he wanted to keep it from him now, that would be futile.","\"This is Han Yue’s husband, Yun City Magistrate Meng.\"","Mo Chuhan's intention was very obvious, telling them that Meng Huaining was not an outsider.","Although Meng Huaining was rarely involved in the affairs of the Mo family, through correspondence with Fei Nanyu, he more or less knew something about the situation of the Mo family.","He even had the idea of reminding the Mo family to train private soldiers to protect themselves.","Later, seeing Ninth Brother and the others go up the mountain frequently, and always acting mysteriously, he guessed that they might have realized this too, and had already started taking actions.","Since it was so, it would be better for him to continue pretending to be muddled, to allow the Mo family to feel at ease doing what they wanted.","After listening to the dialogues between them earlier, Meng Huaining probably couldn’t pretend to be ignorant anymore.","\"Rest assured, I know what should and should not be said.\"","This was addressed to the old subordinates, as for Eighth Brother here, the two had been together for a long time and already had a tacit understanding.","What’s more, if Eighth Brother wanted to hide it from him earlier, he wouldn’t have talked to those people face to face either.","Seeing that Eighth Master remained silent, which could be regarded as approving Meng Huaining’s words, Li Liang finally said, \"Eighth Master, we are the last batch. The others have already gone up the mountain.\"","As he was talking, Second Brother, who had just sent people down the mountain, rushed over with Liang Hao and others.","After greeting each other, Second Brother continued to escort people up the mountain, while Eighth Master and Meng Huaining went straight to the Two Elders' yard.","Mo Chuhan and Meng Huaining came so late, there must be some important things to say. Old Lady Mo immediately sent people to gather all her sons.","Except for Second Brother who was arranging the old department on the mountain, the rest of the brothers all arrived in less than a quarter of an hour.","Mo Chuhan saw his brothers looking at him and explained, \"It wasn't me. My brother-in-law has something to say.\"","Meng Huaining did not beat around the bush either. He took out a note from his arms, unfolded it and handed it to Mo Qing.","\"Father-in-law, this is a homing pigeon message Father Fei gave me today, asking me to remind the family members to be extra vigilant.\"","Although Meng Huaining did not say the content of the note out loud, it was not difficult to see from his expression that there was no good news on it.","Mo Qing took over the note with a solemn expression on his face. Old Lady Mo brought the oil lamp next to her closer to provide better lighting.","Glancing over the contents on the note under the bright light, Mo Qing then heavily patted the table next to him.","\"Father, what exactly happened?\" Big Brother asked in a deep voice.","\"Mr. Fei said that he had just investigated that the Xue family had sent people to the northwest not long ago. He suspected the Xue family came to the northwest with the purpose of dealing with the Mo family.\"","\"Humph! Unfortunately for him, the people he sent to the northwest have all been wiped out by us brothers. This matter should not cause further trouble.\" Mo Chuhan had been involved in the whole process of dealing with the group of people from Jingxian Building. In his opinion, the people the Xue family sent to the northwest had all been wiped out by them brothers, and no longer posed any threat.","\"No matter how many people the Xue family dared to send again, we’ll kill every one that comes. We’ll never show mercy.\"","Looking at Eighth Brother's indignant appearance, Mo Jiuye was not as relaxed as him.","\"While we have already dealt with Xue Fan and his accomplices, no one can guarantee that no fish will slip through the net and escape. We must not be negligent about this matter.\"","Mo Qing nodded in approval at his ninth son’s words and continued, \"What Jiuye said is right. I haven't finished what’s written on the note yet.\"","After a short pause, Mo Qing went on, \"Mr. Fei also said that the Empress had not received any news from the northwest for a long time, so she was preparing to send out a second batch of men. According to his investigation, this time the Empress would send highly trained assassins, not small in number.\"","Hearing this, Mo Jiuye interrupted him, \"Father, what date was marked at the end of the note?\"","\"July ninth.\" Mo Qing replied.","Mo Jiuye frowned. \"Today is July sixteenth. That means Mr. Fei got the news at least seven days ago. If the Empress did send people, they must already be on the way. From the Capital City to the northwest, even hurrying day and night, it would take little more than ten days or so.\"","Big brother clenched his fists tightly and said coldly, \"In that case, we’ll let none of those people the Empress sent return alive.\""]},{"number":477,"title":"Chapter 477: This is not what the Mohists wanted.","paragraphs":["The other Mo Family men also had similar thoughts. When they saw the eldest brother voice out what was on their minds, they came forward to echo his words.","\"Eldest brother is right. As long as we brothers work together, we will definitely make them unable to come and go freely.\"","However, Mo Jiuye did not think it would be as easy as his elder brothers had assumed.","\"Since Mr. Fei could write to warn us about this matter, the actions taken by the Empress this time are clearly not small.\"","\"On the way to exile in the northwest, the exile convoy encountered ambushes a few times. The assassins sent by Nan Heng number at least over a hundred.\"","\"From what I know, the death warriors and assassins used by the Empress and Nan Heng were secretly trained by the Xue Family. This time, the assassins sent by the Empress also came from the Xue Family camp.\"","\"Judging from the previous incident, the number of death warriors trained by the Xue Family is clearly not small. Especially since they sincerely want to destroy my Mo Family, if they take action again, the numbers will definitely not be fewer.\"","\"Ninth brother, even if your analysis is right, aren't we brothers all survivors who have escaped death on the battlefield? When have we ever feared anyone in our lives?\" Mo Chuhan still felt somewhat unconvinced. He felt that his ninth brother had become timid.","Mo Jiuye had indeed become more timid.","\"Eighth brother, do you know what it was like when news of each of your deaths were relayed back one by one?\"","\"Mother and the sisters-in-law were basically living deaths, faces washed with tears every day. Now that the Mo Family has finally reunited after overcoming thousands of hardships, I don't want the scenes from back then to happen again.\"","\"What's more, I am already married with children now, and there are also the elders who need me to attend to them filially. This life of mine already does not belong solely to myself.\"","\"Before taking any risky actions, I have to prioritize safety first.\"","\"Jiuye is right. Our Mo Family has already suffered a major catastrophe once. Now that we have finally reunited with difficulty, we can no longer withstand any more blows. We must carefully plan for the long term regarding this matter and not act rashly.\"","As Mo Qing spoke, his gaze swept back and forth among his few sons.","This kind of gaze was all too familiar to the Mo Family men. In the past on the battlefield, their father would also have such piercing eyes when gathering subordinates for discussion in the camp tent.","In an instant, all the Mo men tightened up, instantly entering their roles, just like when they were on high alert on the battlefield in the past.","At this moment, Mo Qing naturally slipped into his role as well.","\"Jiuye, what good countermeasures do you have now?\"","\"Father, no matter how we respond, the premise is that we must ensure the safety of our own people.\"","\"Mm, tell me your specific methods.\"","When everyone was arguing just now, Mo Jiuye had already swiftly devised countermeasures in his mind.","\"Mr. Fei obtained the news seven days ago. If the Empress's people started taking action from that time, it would take them at least seven more days to reach the northwest.","\"There is not much difficulty for the veterans to use explosives. With just a little guidance they will know how.","\"I plan to use these few days to drill them in using explosives.","\"Of course, explosives make too loud a commotion when set off. It would be best not to use them if possible. It can also be said that explosives are the final trump card of my Mo Family.","\"I also still have twenty continuously-firing repeating crossbows remaining which I will distribute to everyone.","\"Counting from today, I will arrange for subordinates to conceal themselves with the repeating crossbows and explosives on the necessary roads to Yun City at the latest seven days from now. This will definitely make it so the assassins can come but cannot leave.\"","\"Mm. What Jiuye said makes sense. We must not give them any chance to enter Yun City,\" Mo Qing highly approved of Mo Jiuye's suggestion.","That was without even mentioning that the many women of the Mo Family and the two newly born grandchildren simply had no ability to evade danger. The villagers of Xi Ling Village were the same as well.","If those death warriors came here and the Mo Family resisted resulting in a big fight, innocent people would inevitably get hurt.","This was not a result the Mo Family wanted to see.","\"It's decided as such. You brothers go and handle the arrangements,\" Mo Qing finalized. In principle, he wanted Mo Jiuye to take full command of this matter. But considering that he still needed to care for He Zhiran and the two babies, he let the brothers handle it together instead.","Of course, he believed his other sons could fully listen to Mo Jiuye's command.","Seeing the Mo Family was prepared, Meng Huaining felt slightly more relieved.","He was just about to bid farewell and leave when he was called to stop by Mo Qing.","Ever since marrying Mo Hanyue, this was the first time his father-in-law took the initiative to call him.","Mo Qing waved his hand to dismiss his sons first before letting Meng Huaining sit beside him.","\"The situation in the Mo Family now is also clear to you. Things are not as peaceful as they seem on the surface. Heaven is unfair, unwilling to even grant us a period of stability.","\"Since this is so, we of the Mo Family are not pushovers who can just be arbitrarily manipulated. Judging from the current circumstances, at the minimum we have to fend off the people the Empress sends over in secret. In truth, danger lies all around.\"","\"Hanyue is my only daughter. I don't want her to get embroiled in anything. She is now a daughter-in-law of your Meng Family. I hope you can bring her away from the Mo Family.\"","Mo Qing did not say the words that followed, but he knew Meng Huaining would understand the meaning behind them.","Meng Huaining stood up solmenly and bowed to Mo Qing.","\"Father-in-law, Huaining is not a coward who fears death. Living together now with the Mo Family, I already regard myself as one of you. When the Mo Family encounters adversity, how can I shrink back just to save my own skin?","\"If I did that, even if grandfather was alive he would not forgive me.","\"The sages' books say a person may not have ability, but cannot be without affection and righteousness. Moreover, I also understand the Mo Family's circumstances. When grandfather was still alive, wasn't he suspected as well...\"","The two of them were clear who that suspector was - the muddle-headed Emperor Shunwu.","\"Father-in-law, since we have talked to this point, I will speak frankly with you as well.","\"I originally did not intend to enter officialdom. It was because grandfather died wronged that I only wanted to rely on my own efforts to restore his innocence.","\"But after working in court these past few years, I have seen through everything clearly. With an emperor as muddled as the one on Great Shun's throne, he is simply a nightmare for the common people.","\"What's more, I have trained in martial arts since I was young. Although I am not as capable as eldest brother and the rest, protecting Hanyue is still not an issue.","\"So please believe me, father-in-law. As long as there is still breath left in me, I will protect Hanyue well. I also want to share in the same fortunes and adversities as the Mo Family.\"","Mo Qing did not expect Meng Huaining to take such an attitude. The Mo Family was currently like a pond of muddy water now. Whoever waded in would easily attract lethal disaster upon themselves.","At the same time, he also greatly admired this son-in-law's integrity and courage.","He was not the naggy sort to begin with. Furthermore, he was also able to discern Meng Huaining's extremely resolute attitude. Since this was the case, further persuasion would be futile.","\"Although you are unwilling to take Hanyue away to protect only yourselves, I still hope you two will take care of your own safety.\"","\"Father-in-law, please rest assured. Huaining understands,\" Meng Huaining spoke.","Both had the same thoughts, so many words were unnecessary. An unspoken understanding had formed between them.","Mo Qing shifted his body slightly and said, \"It is already quite late. Go back to rest!\"","\"Father-in-law should also rest early. Huaining shall take his leave.\"","Meng Huaining had just pushed the door open when barks sounded from outside."]},{"number":478,"title":"Chapter 478: Finally Made It Here Alive","paragraphs":["He stopped in his tracks and looked towards the source of the sound in the moonlight.","A black shadow was being chased by a group of dogs, stumbling towards the direction of the Mo Family. But in the blink of an eye, it collapsed.","The Mo brothers had not gone far and ran back together, walking towards the fallen black shadow.","The dogs were humane and would only bark to drive away strangers to the Mo Family if they did not attack. They would not bite.","The eldest brother rushed forward first to lift up the fallen person.","As a martial artist, he had good night vision. He examined the stranger in the moonlight but did not recognize him.","At this time, Mo Jiuye also came over. After seeing clearly who it was, he was somewhat shocked.","Seeing his expression, his brothers could ascertain that this person was an acquaintance of their ninth younger brother.","\"Ninth younger brother, who is he?\" asked the eldest brother.","\"He is Zhou Laoba, the government official sent to escort us to the northwest. He's quite decent. Let's carry him back first to see what exactly is going on,\" said Mo Jiuye.","As the closest place was their second uncle's yard, the brothers carried Zhou Laoba to the side room.","In the bright oil lamp light, they scrutinized Zhou Laoba carefully.","He was much thinner than when they parted from the Mo Family. His originally ordinary face was covered in healed whip marks, his lips were chapped, and his whole body looked as if he was dead.","Having followed He Zhiran to study some medical knowledge, Mo Jiuye first felt Zhou Laoba's pulse. Although it was slightly weak, he could still feel it.","As for why Zhou Laoba lost consciousness, he could not conclude.","Logically, He Zhiran should be able to ascertain Zhou Laoba’s condition clearly with one look. But He Zhiran was currently sitting the month after giving birth and was in no state to check Zhou Laoba’s body.","Mo Jiuye had a brain wave and thought of his uncle.","Although He Ziming was hailed as a specialist in gynecology, he was still a doctor and could not have only specialized in women’s illnesses.","Mo Jiuye said in a low voice, \"Who will go get my uncle?\"","\"I'll go,\" Meng Huaining voluntarily stepped forward.","He had already stated his stance today in front of his father-in-law, so he would naturally go all out for the Mo Family’s affairs.","Soon, Meng Huaining brought He Ziming over.","After He Ziming took Zhou Laoba's pulse, he said, \"His body should have gone without food for days, and he also has internal injuries.\"","When it came to internal injuries, no one understood better than the Mo brothers.","They were all martial artists and were often internally injured on the battlefield.","Mo Jiuye reached out and ripped Zhou Laoba’s shirt open. Besides being emaciated, there was nothing wrong with the front of his body.","He carefully turned the person over, and countless whip marks entered his eyes.","The whip marks had scabbed over. But from the depth of the scabs, one could see that the person wielding the whip was exceptionally strong.","This was the rhythm of whipping someone to death.","Without a doubt, the internal injuries He Ziming mentioned came from these whip marks.","Mo Jiuye looked at He Ziming, \"Eldest brother, I'll have to trouble you to treat him.\"","\"Let me apply acupuncture first to rouse him and get him to eat something. That should make him feel better. Internal injuries are no trivial matter and need to be nursed back to health slowly,\" said He Ziming.","He Ziming worked quickly. As soon as he finished speaking, the silver needles in his hand accurately pierced Zhou Laoba's acupoints.","After about the time it takes to burn one incense stick, Zhou Laoba finally woke up groggily.","He scanned the room and eventually fixed his gaze on Mo Jiuye.","\"I...I'm not dreaming right? I finally got here alive.\"","Mo Jiuye did not answer him immediately, but brought over a bowl of water to Zhou Laoba instead.","\"Drink some water first, then slowly tell me what happened.\"","Zhou Laoba wanted to reach out to take the cup of water Mo Jiuye handed over. But he felt that he had no strength in his body at all.","Mo Jiuye still had a decent impression of Zhou Laoba and Peng Wang, who were responsible for escorting them. Even though Zhou Laoba and his sister-in-law had that misunderstanding back then, it was after all a misunderstanding, and he was not petty enough to hold a grudge over that little thing.","He personally held the water up to Zhou Laoba.","\"I'll support you. Drink some water first.\"","After a few sips of water, Zhou Laoba finally felt his throat was not so dry.","He spoke urgently,","\"Mo Jiuye, hurry and hide with your family!\"","Mo Jiuye frowned and asked, \"What happened?\"","Zhou Laoba was still very weak at this time, but he felt the matter was urgent. If he did not say it out early, his suffering would have been for nothing.","\"Twenty days ago, the chief and our group of officials responsible for escorting all of you were successively arrested and thrown into a dungeon.","There, those people tortured us and interrogated the entire process of escorting your family’s exile.","We are just trying to fill our stomachs with jobs at the government office. Where would we have seen such ferocious people before? We told them everything about escorting all of you to the northwest when pieced together. \"","\"Do you know who caught you?\" Mo Jiuye did not ask about the contents of their confession. He could guess without thinking that in order to survive, those officials would say anything whether true or false.","He was not worried about the rest. He was only concerned about the matter of them rescuing his eighth brother midway. Those officials were fully aware of that.","\"On the night we were caught, I vaguely heard the two guards mention Prime Minister Xue while chatting.","Those two people talked without any intention of hiding things from others. The chief guessed that they might want to kill us to keep things quiet.","Sure enough, what we feared came true. Soon after, a large group of people came and whipped us without explanation.","At that time, I was the furthest inside. When someone blocked me, I could turn my back to face the whips lashing my back.","I watched my brothers collapse one by one, and I pretended to faint like them.","Fortunately, I had that foresight. After whipping us for a while, someone said to check if we were still alive and continue beating us if we did not die.","At that time, I could no longer hear the groans of my brothers. I could only pretend I was dead to grasp any chance of living.","Fortunately, those people did not check very carefully and did not notice anything wrong with me when I held my breath. \"","At this point, Zhou Laoba started sobbing loudly.","\"When I climbed up from the mass grave after those people left, I found that my brothers had all passed away...sob...sob...\"","Hearing that Zhou Laoba's brothers had all passed away, Mo Jiuye also felt extremely anguished.","\"What about Chief Peng? Did those people beat him to death too?\"","Zhou Laoba nodded as he wept, \"The chief was beaten the most severely because he refused to talk about the Mo Family's situation.","Those people were determined to obtain more information from him since he was the head in charge of the escort.","When those people came to silence us, the chief only had one breath left. After we were dumped at the mass grave, I went to check on the chief and found that his body had already stiffened...sob...sob...\"","At this point, Mo Jiuye fiercely hammered the table next to him and gnashed in anger, \"These vicious, inhumane bastards!\""]},{"number":479,"title":"Chapter 479: I must go to Beijing","paragraphs":["Mo Chuhan was also following the exile team for some time. At that time, he did not have much contact with those officials like Mo Jiuye because he was injured.","Despite this, he also knew that those officials took good care of their family.","It was also because of their care that their family did not suffer too much along the way.","Now that he heard all those officials had died, he inevitably felt sad.","\"Ninth brother, I'll take some capable men to the Capital City to get rid of those people who keep thinking of ways to deal with our Mo Family,\" said Mo Chuhan.","Mo Jiuye had just had the same idea, so he did not refute his eighth brother's words.","It would be more practical to get rid of them once and for all than to counter their moves one by one.","\"Eighth brother, we still need to plan this carefully, especially now when we can't leave the northwest,\" Mo Jiuye said.","Mo Chuhan asked impatiently, \"Why?\"","\"I just received news from the Capital City. Lord Zhou also came to report that the people sent by the Empress should be on their way.","If I guess correctly, the assassins sent by the Empress will arrive in about seven days.\"","The eldest brother also patted Mo Chuhan on the shoulder.","\"Eighth brother, ninth brother is right. We have to resolve the immediate crisis first.","Also, the Empress and the Xue Family can train so many assassins because their security is very tight. Even if we go to the Capital City, we must have a detailed plan to ensure success.\"","Mo Chuhan knew his eldest and ninth brother made sense, but he just couldn't restrain the anger in his heart.","\"I just want to take their dog lives immediately.\"","Although He Ziming was not from the Mo Family, this was his sister's in-laws. He also understood the situation in the imperial court and sympathized with what had happened to the Mo Family.","But it was still inappropriate to discuss such things in front of an outsider like him.","He coughed lightly and said, \"The brother from the Capital City is still very weak. I'll go order some suitable food for him.\"","Only then did Mo Chuhan realize he had lost his composure in front of an outsider.","He looked awkwardly at He Ziming's leaving figure and sighed deeply.","\"Anyway, after resolving the immediate crisis, I will definitely go to the Capital City.\"","Just as he finished speaking, Mo Jiuye strode out.","Because he heard Xiao Bai's cry.","Xiao Bai had been away in the Capital City for quite a long time, over half a month.","Just yesterday, he and He Zhiran were talking about how Xiao Bai had not returned with any news yet. And today the little guy came back.","With so many things happening, Mo Jiuye did not tease Xiao Bai like usual before checking the note. He directly took the note off Xiao Bai's leg.","The note was still handwritten by Fei Nanyu.","The content was like an extension of the news brought by Meng Huaining.","Three days ago, he discovered the Xue Family had sent out hundreds of masters from the Capital City. He secretly sent people to follow them and found out they were heading northwest.","After confirming the news was accurate, he let Xiao Bai bring the message back to notify Mo Jiuye to make preparations in advance.","At the same time, Fei Nanyu also analyzed when the assassins would arrive in the northwest.","The three days ago he mentioned was before he wrote the letter. His people had followed them for three more days before doubling back. It would take Xiao Bai two days to fly back to the northwest.","That meant the assassins would arrive at the border in about seven days.","This was consistent with Mo Jiuye and his family's calculations.","Fei Nanyu also mentioned Nan Rui. It had to be said, he really knew how to handle big matters.","In the letter, Mo Jiuye told Nan Rui he went to the Capital City to help resolve the Mo Family's crisis. He also explained that Nan Rui had left his most important relative, Consort De, here.","This alone showed Nan Rui could be trusted.","If it was an ordinary person, or an overly suspicious ruler like Emperor Shunwu, they would still find many reasons to doubt Nan Rui's intentions even if they were pure.","But Fei Nanyu did not, because he understood how important Consort De was to Nan Rui.","To repay the Mo Family, and to avoid arousing their suspicion, he actually left his own mother in the northwest.","From this it could be seen that Nan Rui had no ulterior motives.","If such a person still could not be trusted, then who could he trust?","Using people without doubt and doubting people without use, Fei Nanyu applied this very well.","This was also why the historical records showed that many capable ministers were cultivated during Fei Nanyu's reign, creating a rare prosperous empire in history.","Of course, that was for later. In the letter, Fei Nanyu only said that Nan Rui had established covert contact with him.","Although he did not explain in detail, Mo Jiuye could ascertain they had reached a consensus. As for the specifics, he did not intend to care too much. After all, it was the royal family's business.","At present, he only wanted his small family to safely get through the current crisis.","After reading the letter, Mo Jiuye did not immediately discuss the contents with his brothers.","He let Liang Hao stay here for now to take care of Lord Zhou, and called his brothers back to the main house.","Although Fei Nanyu's news was slightly more accurate than what Meng Huaining brought, the original defense plans did not need much change.","Mo Jiuye gathered everyone only because he wanted to announce the contents of the letter, to let them be more clear about the situation.","It was not until late at night that Mo Jiuye returned with Xiao Bai.","When Mo Jiuye was away, Madam He was worried that taking care of two babies would be too tiring for her daughter. So she and Granny Li stayed in her room until her son-in-law returned.","He Zhiran rested in her room every day. Her sisters-in-law took turns coming to help care for the two babies.","With nothing to do during the day, she would take a nap.","So at this time, she was not sleepy either.","She knew Seventh Uncle had successfully brought his former men back today. Mo Jiuye returning late must be because of this.","But unexpectedly, Mo Jiuye brought news that shocked her.","\"Husband, you're saying Brother Peng and the others were all harmed?\"","This was completely unexpected for He Zhiran. Recalling the officials during the exile, although they were fierce in the beginning, they took very good care of the Mo Family later on.","Especially Peng Wang. Although they were a little discordant in the beginning, they got along very well later.","And after getting to know each other for a few months, they also knew Peng Wang was a decent person.","Thinking of his death, He Zhiran felt sad.","There were over a dozen officials escorting them to the northwest. For them to die in vain like this, the Empress's people were truly ruthless in order to achieve their goals.","Mo Jiuye's mood was also very heavy. He understood his daughter-in-law's feelings.","But it had already happened, so all they could do was find an opportunity to avenge them."]},{"number":480,"title":"Chapter 480: This weapon is called the Crossbow.","paragraphs":["That night, the husband and wife did not rest well, with Peng Wang and those officials constantly appearing in their minds. Mo Jiuye got up early the next morning to organize his brothers and subordinates to go up the mountain.","He had originally intended to let those old subordinates who had returned from the South rest for a few days, but plans could not keep up with the changing circumstances. In the current situation, it seemed that rest was out of the question.","Those old subordinates had arrived in the Northwest only one night ago, yet they already liked it here.","The living environment the Mo Family had prepared for them was a hundred times better than what they had in the South.","Among these people were chefs who had specifically cooked in the barracks. After arriving in the Northwest, they continued their original work.","The ingredients had also been delivered by Mo Jiuye after Mo Yuance returned.","The various fresh vegetables grown on the Mo Family's farmland, as well as the meat and grain He Zhiran had secretly taken out of the space—although it was the hot summer, the temperature on the mountain was naturally lower than at the foot of the mountain. The caves were even cooler, practically natural storage rooms.","The ingredients left in the caves could easily be kept fresh for days.","When Mo Jiuye arrived with his men, those old subordinates had just finished breakfast and were sitting together discussing how the Mo Family had not mistreated them, and had actually prepared so much delicious food for them.","Seeing the Mo brothers arrive, the old subordinates crowded around.","Although they had arrived in the Northwest yesterday and heard that the Mo brothers and the old Duke were still alive, they had only seen a few people.","Meng Huaining knew the Mo Family had important things to deal with today, so he had given Mo Chuhan a long vacation.","Therefore, the nine Mo brothers appeared before the old subordinates this morning.","Seeing the nine Mo masters, the old subordinates' eyes were brimming with tears, and some had already started sobbing loudly.","Wang Kai clutched Mo Junrui's hand tightly.","\"Master, if you hadn't saved me back then and brought me to the barracks to train, I'm afraid I would have died on the road fleeing from the famine.","The reason I stayed in the South was that I hoped to see the enemies who harmed you die one day, so I could go to your graves and tell you the news.","When I heard that you were still alive, I didn't even dare to rest, for fear that I would wake up and find it was all a dream.\"","Although these people were all insignificant soldiers, the Mo brothers had never treated them as subordinates when leading troops, but as their own good brothers.","Hearing Wang Kai's words now, everyone present had reddened eyes, and several could not help crying loudly.","Mo Junrui beckoned for several brothers to come forward and comfort everyone. After the emotions had stabilized, Mo Jiuye solemnly said:","\"You must have heard from Seventh Brother on the way back to the Northwest that the Mo Family is currently beset by enemies on all sides.","When I went to the South on business not long ago and passed through the South, I saw some brothers go to my father and brothers' graves to pay respects.","I knew then that you were not doing well in the barracks, so I thought that one day I would take you away from there.","Who would have thought that at this time, my Mo Family would be in peril again. I had intended to let everyone rest for a few days, but the enemies won't give us time to rest. Regrettably, I can only ask everyone to start training today.\"","As he finished speaking, Mo Jiuye took a semi-automatic crossbow from Tao Ran and showed it to everyone.","Before Mo Jiuye could explain the details of the semi-automatic crossbow, someone asked, \"Master Nine, are these crossbow bolts?","I've seen the Emperor's imperial guards holding similar weapons.","It's said that the range of these crossbows is much longer than bows and arrows, and they're also more accurate.\"","\"This is indeed a crossbow, but it's very different from the ones you've seen.\" Mo Jiuye said.","\"Master Nine, this crossbow does look much more intricate than the ones used by the imperial guards. What are the differences?\" an old subordinate asked.","Many of them had seen crossbows in public, and knew these were extremely rare, with reportedly only a hundred or so in the entire Da Shun Dynasty.","Yet each person behind the Mo brothers was holding a dozen or so, far exceeding the number of crossbows owned by the Da Shun Dynasty.","Mo Jiuye did not explain immediately. Instead, he raised the crossbow in his hand, aimed at a flying bird in the sky, and fired several bolts in the blink of an eye.","At the same time, before anyone could react, three birds of varying sizes fell in front of them.","The birds all had feathered bolts stuck in them.","The old subordinates kept rubbing their eyes, completely disbelief at what had just happened.","After a long while, someone asked, \"Master Nine, if I'm not mistaken, you just fired three bolts in succession?\"","Mo Jiuye walked closer so they could examine the semi-automatic crossbow more clearly.","Just then someone exclaimed, \"Master Nine, there are still a dozen or so bolts in this crossbow?\"","\"That's right. This weapon is called a semi-automatic crossbow. It can continuously fire twenty crossbow bolts,\" Mo Jiuye said while removing the bolt clip so everyone could see more clearly.","\"Not only that, installing the bolts is extremely easy. Just gently push the clip in and it's done. You'll never have a situation of not having time to install bolts when facing the enemy.\"","Mo Jiuye slowly pushed the clip containing the bolts back in, under everyone's gaze.","He inserted and removed the clip several times, then handed out the semi-automatic crossbows brought for everyone to practice first.","After all, with nearly a thousand people on the mountain, they could not have brought enough for everyone. Later they would send some people down the mountain to retrieve more.","His goal now was to let them get acquainted with the semi-automatic crossbow while quickly learning how to use it.","The bolts inside could be reused. They could spend the next two days practicing their aim.","What soldier isn't interested in weapons?","Even though several people had to share one crossbow, everyone was still extremely excited.","The semi-automatic crossbow wasn't difficult to operate. Especially the ones He Zhiran had bought from Taobao Treasure Mall, which came with a sight, so aim wasn't too big of a concern either.","As long as their arm strength was sufficient, and they didn't shake when firing, there basically wouldn't be any deviation.","In less than an hour, the soldiers had grasped the use and techniques of the semi-automatic crossbow. All that remained was more practice.","To get everyone proficient with the semi-automatic crossbow as soon as possible, Mo Jiuye brought more people down the mountain to retrieve enough crossbows and bolts.","Two days later when he came to inspect again, the soldiers could hit flying birds in the sky just like him.","Mo Jiuye was very satisfied with everyone's progress. Next was to teach them to use explosives."]},{"number":481,"title":"Chapter 481: Little White Hurt","paragraphs":["The bombs were originally stored up the mountain, so they were convenient to retrieve.","Recently, the Mo Family brothers had been working hard, and even though they had produced thousands of bombs, these things were too precious in their eyes for the soldiers to use them as casually as they would use repeating crossbows when practicing.","Nevertheless, Mo Jiuye decided to take out fifty bombs for everyone to learn with.","Bombs were even simpler to use. One only needed to take aim at the target, then light the fuse and throw it.","The soldiers could understand this with one look.","Their time training up the mountain was brief, and six days flashed by in the blink of an eye.","Mo Jiuye also explained the specific circumstances clearly to the soldiers, needing them to lie in ambush at the locations outside Yun City he had chosen in advance.","That night, Mo Jiuye made the arrangements himself, leaving one hundred soldiers led by Third Older Brother behind to conceal themselves all around the Mo Family residence in case of unexpected trouble.","Mo Jiuye and his other brothers took everyone else and rushed to lie in ambush outside the suburbs of Yun City.","The ambush locations were chosen together by the Mo Family brothers. This was the only passageway from the Capital City to Yun City.","On both sides of the passage were continuous, undulating mountains, extremely well-suited for concealing troops. Not only so, but the view overlooking the passage was also very good.","The Mo Family brothers split up to several locations, leading troops to hide themselves in the dark places, estimating that it would take at most three days before the Empress's people arrived here.","When Mo Jiuye came out, he deliberately brought a mini telescope from his wife's space.","Aside from that, he also brought Little White along by his side.","He discovered that Little White really could understand his words. At this time, Little White would definitely be able to render outstanding service.","After lying in ambush, Mo Jiuye called Little White over.","\"Little White, fly towards the Capital City, just wandering within a hundred li. If you run into any suspicious people, hurry back here fast to notify me.\"","\"Coo coo...\" Little White flapped its wings a few times to demonstrate it understood his command, then it flapped high up into the sky, flying towards the direction of the Capital City.","They lay in ambush for three days without discovering any suspicious people, nor did Little White bring back any news.","Second Brother grew somewhat restless. He called his brothers over and spoke heavily, \"Now the time based on our conjectures has already passed by a full day. Waiting like this will get us nowhere.\"","\"What do you think we should do?\" Eldest Brother asked.","\"I'm planning to scout towards the Capital City a bit,\" Second Brother replied, looking towards Mo Jiuye as he spoke.","\"Ninth little brother, I don't mean to call you out, but are you placing too much trust in a single bird? It might be spiritual, enough to deliver letters, but entrusting it with such a big task of scouting information, do you really feel at ease?","What if Little White doesn't understand all this and just flew out to play for a few days? With us lying in ambush here, unable to obtain advance notice of the enemy's arrival, if those people suddenly pop up and catch us unprepared, wouldn't that be a tremendous loss?\"","Although Second Brother was usually more hotheaded, at this moment all the brothers felt his words made sense.","Entrusting the scouting of information to a single bird was not looking too reliable however one thought about it.","At this moment, Mo Jiuye also lacked confidence in his heart. Little White was quite spirited in his understanding, but after it had left for three days without the slightest bit of news, could it have run into some danger along the way, to the point it was simply unable to send any messages back?","He had never doubted Little White before, only worried that something might happen to it.","\"In that case, I'll personally go scout it out.\"","\"You mustn't. We still need Ninth Younger Brother here to oversee the bigger picture. Of us brothers, my qinggong is the best, so scouting information should be left to me,\" Mo Chuhan puffed out his chest and stood out.","Mo Jiuye also didn't have any intention to force him. Of the nine brothers, Eighth Brother indeed had the best qinggong, and was most suited for scouting information.","\"Since this is the case, let me trouble Eighth Brother to run a trip. Similarly, you only have to check out the circumstances within a hundred li to be sufficient. Whether or not you obtain any intelligence, you must rush back here by nightfall.\"","\"Alright, I'll set off immediately.\"","Mo Chuhan had just turned around when Mo Jiuye became aware of a familiar sound.","Raising his head to look into the sky, it was precisely Little White.","Only now, Little White's flying speed was much slower than before, as if it had lost all strength.","As Mo Jiuye was wondering with puzzlement, Little White lost its balance in midair, and its tiny body began plummeting downwards from the sky.","Mo Jiuye instantly circulated his qi and leapt upwards, and right before Little White hit the ground, he steadily caught it.","\"Ninth Younger Brother, Little White is injured?\" At this moment, Mo Chuhan didn't leave either, as the brothers all crowded over to examine the situation.","Mo Jiuye cupped Little White in both hands. He could feel wet stickiness against his palm.","Right now, Little White appeared extremely feeble, but it still made the effort to let out weak chirps, vigorously facing towards the direction of the Capital City with its head.","As Little White's master, Mo Jiuye could of course understand what it was struggling to express.","Little White was telling him it had already discovered something amiss over there.","In other words, suspicious people had appeared.","\"Little White has already discovered our target. And it's extremely obedient. I told it to search within a hundred li, so it certainly wouldn't have flown beyond that range.","Therefore I can confirm, those people must be within less than a hundred li from us.\"","While explaining to his brothers the intelligence Little White brought back, Mo Jiuye also flipped its body over to check its condition.","Sure enough, Little White had a wound on its belly where it touched his palm. Fresh blood had already dyed its snowy white feathers red.","To prevent any casualties, Ke Zhiran had prepared ample medicine for them.","Mo Jiuye lightly squeezed Little White's body. Little White didn't demonstrate any reactions of pain.","He could already confirm Little White only had that one injury on its abdomen.","Moreover, judging from the look of the wound, it seemed to be a scratch. He deduced Little White must have swerved off course in panic to dodge danger, and its body slid against some hard object somewhere.","Due to excessive blood loss from the injury, this led to its current feeble state.","Although the bond between him and Little White was already profoundly deep, he still lacked the means to communicate with Little White like one could with a human. He simply had no way to inquire about the exact details of how it sustained its injury.","He took out a cotton ball soaked in iodine and disinfected Little White's wound, then sprinkled on some anti-inflammatory powder before wrapping up the injury with bandages.","Right now, Little White had not lost consciousness. Mo Jiuye also fed it some water and food before solemnly speaking to Mo Chuhan,","\"Eighth Brother, since Little White has already brought back accurate news, we should also get a clearer grasp of the specific circumstances. So you still have to take a trip out.\"","As he spoke, Mo Jiuye glanced at the skies.","\"It's nearly the end of the noon hour right now. If I'm guessing correctly, the road will have many travelers around this time, so a group as conspicuous as them would surely conceal themselves somewhere to wait until nightfall before taking action.","So when you go scout this time, passing yourself off as an ordinary traveler would do. That way it'll be less prone to rousing suspicion.\"","Having said this much, Mo Jiuye turned around to rifle through the pack he took medicine for Little White from earlier, and took out a fake beard that he stuck on Mo Chuhan's face.","Then mimicking how Ke Zhiran disguised him last time, he thickened Eighth Brother's eyebrows.","Dressed up like this, even his own family might fail to recognize him without looking closely."]},{"number":482,"title":"Chapter 482: The Mohists are not to be messed with","paragraphs":["Mo Chuhan left, and Mo's brothers also began to be on high alert here, waiting for him to bring back the news.","In the anxious wait of everyone, Mo Chuhan finally rushed back when the sky had just darkened.","Judging from his outfit, he still maintained his original appearance, so it was evident that he had not fought with anyone.","Mo Chuhan quickly approached the brothers.","\"Those people are indeed not far from us, hiding only eighty li away from here. I waited until they moved before rushing back to deliver the letter.","It is estimated that it won't take more than two time periods before they get here.","Also, their outfits are not the black clothes and masks that we imagined, but are disguised as ordinary commoners, and they are hiding in multiple places. If it weren't for me seeing that their physiques were strong and mighty, and not as weak as ordinary commoners, I would really have been fooled by them.”","Mo Jiuye turned his head towards his subordinates and commanded: \"Everyone get into position and prepare to resist the enemy.\"","As his words fell, Mo's brothers took their respective teams of people to ambush according to their previous plans.","Mo Jiuye stood at the highest point, using night vision binoculars to check the situation in the distance.","Two hours later, a group of people did indeed appear on the official road, with at least two hundred people estimated.","The assassins sent by the Empress were all top masters, so their hearing was naturally not going to be bad.","Mo's brothers brought their soldiers to hide separately. Mo Jiuye could not shout loudly to remind them that someone was coming. He took out the signal flares that had been prepared in advance, and when those people were about two li away from them, he launched it.","After the signal flare was launched, its shape was very special. There was no sound at all, only a thin ray of light, just like a meteor streaking across the night sky.","If you don't know, you would indeed think it was a meteor.","Although this was in ancient times, this was a very common natural phenomenon and would not arouse any suspicion from those people.","Sure enough, the leader of the assassins just glanced at the quickly disappearing ray of light, and then gestured for the people to keep moving forward.","\"Everyone walk faster, we have to arrive at Xi Ling Village before midnight.\"","As the voice fell, he had already taken the lead in using qinggong, and the speed was raised to the extreme. The assassins closely followed him at this speed.","Soon, the assassins came to the encirclement set up by Mo's brothers.","Mo's brothers and their subordinates were all people who had rolled around on the battlefield, and they were very experienced in ambushing enemies.","The only difference today was that the enemy all had internal energy martial arts, not like those soldiers on the battlefield who only knew some fist and foot skills and were easy to deal with.","So what if they have internal martial arts?","They would still be left with no way to return.","Mo's brothers each commanded their squad of soldiers to take action.","Countless arrows flew across the night sky and shot towards those assassins.","The leader of the assassins reacted extremely quickly. Feeling that something was wrong, he shouted loudly to warn, \"It's an ambush, be careful!\"","However, his voice was simply not as fast as the continuous crossbows. As soon as his voice fell, he could hear the sound of people falling down one after another.","It was too late to warn again, because the second batch of arrows had already shot towards various parts of his body.","The assassins quickly drew out the soft swords hidden at their waists to resist the dense arrows.","The leader of the assassins suddenly felt that things were not good, knowing that resisting like this was not a long-term plan. Who knows when someone might get careless and get hit by an arrow.","Like those subordinates behind him - at this time, many of them had already fallen.","Under these circumstances, the best way was to find the hiding place of the archers and counterattack.","However, how could Mo's brothers possibly give him such an opportunity?","The arrows were like rain points, shooting at those assassins without stopping, showing no sign of stopping at all.","The assassins could only desperately resist, and they had no chance to find the location of the hidden people.","In the blink of an eye, half of the assassins had fallen, and screams were endless.","Fortunately, this place was remote with continuous mountain ranges around it and no villages or pedestrians.","No matter how loudly they screamed, it would not attract anyone's attention.","Mo's brothers had come prepared for the ambush, and they had also considered that the number of people from the capital would not be small. Before leaving, they had brought enough arrows.","Those soldiers had not experienced the thrill of killing enemies for a long time either. Especially when they saw the increasing numbers of fallen assassins, they also became more and more brave in battle.","According to the pre-planned strategy to prevent assassins from quietly escaping, Mo Jiuye led a team of people to secretly flank the assassins from behind.","Now the assassins could be said to be attacked from both front and back, and it was impossible for those timid ones who wanted to take the opportunity to escape.","In ten minutes, all the assassins had completely fallen to the ground, even if some of them were still alive, they had also been shot full of holes by the crossbow arrows.","Regarding the origins of these people, Mo’s brothers already knew it well, so there was no need to ask for any confession.","Mo Jiuye shouted loudly, \"Stop!\"","With this order, the soldiers all stopped their actions, and orderly surrounded the assassins from all directions.","At the same time, the eldest brother had ordered someone to light the torches.","The torches were lit and the surroundings instantly brightened.","Looking again at those fallen assassins, they were indeed dressed in ordinary people’s clothes as Mo Chuhan had said, and they were all strong men.","Without Mo’s brothers ordering them, the soldiers took the initiative to go up and check if they still had any breath - any that were still alive, they would finish off with another knife, ensuring that none survived.","In the past, after Mo’s brothers and their men had dealt with these assassins, they would have secretly disposed of the corpses and cleaned up the battlefield, making it look like nothing had happened here.","However, considering that the Empress had gone too far in deceiving people, Mo Jiuye was the first one who did not want to do so anymore.","He deliberately left the corpses of these assassins here.","The corpses could be left here, but Mo Jiuye was not careless enough to leave the crossbow arrows shot here as well.","And most importantly, the money and tokens and other things on those assassins were all taken away.","The soldiers also understood this reason. They did not need Mo’s brothers to order them. After killing all those assassins, the arrows they shot out were collected without exception.","Although this place was not far from Yun City, it was under the jurisdiction of the local government.","It was believed that the next morning, the Prefect would receive the news that there were more than two hundred corpses here.","There was no live mouth among the assassins to investigate further even if he wanted to, he could only report the matter to the imperial court.","By then, the people behind the scenes would surely know what was going on with these assassins.","So many assassins were wiped out overnight without knowing it, if they wanted to make another move against the Mo family, they would have to carefully weigh their own capabilities.","Of course, those behind the scenes could only speculate that this was done by the Mo family, but they could not do anything openly without any evidence to prove that the Mo family had killed them.","In short, Mo Jiuye did this to warn Empress and her party."]},{"number":483,"title":"Chapter 483: Surely it will be reported to the court.","paragraphs":["With the cunning and craftiness of the Empress's father, the Prime Minister Xue, he would certainly realize the severity of the situation and clearly see that the Mo Family is not without the power to fight him now. Without assurance of victory, he would not dare to recklessly take action against the Mo Family again.","After all, he had spent huge efforts cultivating those death warriors, so if they were all lost here, he would likely face a crisis of having no capable men in the future.","As such, the Mo Family could enjoy a temporary respite for some time.","It was not the Mo Family's style to passively take hits. They would choose the right time to go to the capital and turn the tables!","After confirming that none of the death warriors had survived, Mo Jiuye finally gave the order for the troops to gradually return to Xi Ling Village.","On the way back, the soldiers seemed exceptionally excited.","This was their first time achieving such an easy victory, especially since their enemies were all martial arts masters, yet under their barrage of crossbow bolts, the enemies did not even have a chance to fight back.","Regrettably, Ninth Master had instructed earlier for the soldiers not to use explosives unless absolutely necessary. Otherwise, those death warriors would not even have left complete corpses behind...","Although Meng Huaining did not participate throughout the Mo Family's ambush operation this time, the Mo brothers did not hide their plans from him when they were discussing tactics.","As such, he was very clear about the details of the Mo Family's ambush setup.","Since he was a scholar, he tended to overthink things more. Mo Jiuye and his men had been away for longer than expected. This not only caused worry among the Mo Family members staying behind in Xi Ling Village, even he felt somewhat anxious.","Although it was late into the night, Meng Huaining simply could not rest easy.","After coaxing his delicate little wife to sleep, he tidied himself up and headed towards the entrance of the mountain foot.","Meng Huaining would not rashly go over to check on the situation at Mo Jiuye and the others’ ambush point. He only wanted to wait here to get the news of their return at the first instance.","Standing under the moonlight and listening to the chorus of frogs in the surroundings, Meng Huaining silently stood there for more than two hours.","Finally, just as he was preparing to head back, he heard faint footsteps coming from the direction of the village.","Those soldiers would continue resting up in the mountains, so they still took the same path down that they first came by. The ones appearing before Meng Huaining’s eyes now were only the Mo brothers and Liang Hao and the others.","Not daring to inquire loudly, Meng Huaining walked over to meet Mo Jiuye’s group instead.","“Ninth brother, did everything go smoothly?”","Mo Jiuye nodded. “Yes. Other than their arrival being slightly later than expected, everything else went very smoothly.","Also, I deliberately did not move those death warriors’ corpses, leaving them for the prefectural authorities to handle first thing tomorrow morning.”","Meng Huaining was clever. Naturally, he understood Mo Jiuye’s intentions for leaving the death warriors’ corpses behind.","“Tomorrow at first light when the Prefectural Magistrate discovers so many corpses in his jurisdiction, he will surely order the surrounding county magistrates to come help investigate. I’ll head to the scene then too. I’ll send any updates back at the first instant if there are any developments over there.”","“Mm. With a case of such magnitude occurring, I believe that Prefect wouldn’t dare conceal it and will surely report it to the imperial court.” Having said that, Mo Jiuye walked towards home.","He was cradling Little White in his arms right now. Its body was burning hot, and was becoming increasingly feeble.","He feared Little White would suffer any mishaps and wanted to hurry back for his wife to treat it.","Meng Huaining knew the elder Mo brothers must be exhausted after lying in ambush for several continuous days. He did not intend to disturb them much, satisfied just seeing them return safely.","Although He Zhiran did not doubt the Mo brothers’ ability to defeat enemies, Mo Jiuye had been gone for a good number of days this time. Even with her faith in him, it was inevitable that she would still be concerned.","To prevent being unaware when Mo Jiuye returned, He Zhiran did not rest in the space with the kids these past couple of days. Also, she tended to be a light sleeper, able to hear even the slightest sound outside.","Just after feeding the two little ones, she heard footsteps at the door. Very quickly, the room door was pushed open.","Knowing his wife’s habit of being a light sleeper, especially when he was not home, Mo Jiuye softly said the moment he pushed the door open, “Ranran, I’m back.”","He Zhiran promptly sat up. “Husband, how did things go?”","Mo Jiuye strode over to her side.","“Ranran, things went very smoothly. I’ll tell you the details later. Take a look at Little White first, it’s injured.”","“Little White is injured? Let me see quickly.”","At the end of He Zhiran’s words, their family of four along with Little White appeared in the space.","The two little ones continued sleeping soundly in their cribs. Rice Ball liked them a lot and would take the initiative to watch over them without its masters needing to instruct it. This spared He Zhiran a lot of trouble.","Whenever she walked too far away, even if the little ones woke up, Rice Ball would immediately run over to notify her.","She brought Mo Jiuye and Little White to the medical room. After examination, He Zhiran felt somewhat more at ease.","She first fed Little White some glucose for it to swiftly recover its strength.","Then she redressed its wounds while explaining to Mo Jiuye at the same time.","“Little White has an infected wound which led to its fever. Its current weakness is probably due to excessive blood loss from the wound. I’ll apply medication on it later and nurse it for several days. It should be fine.”","For the Mo Jiuye couple, Little White was a great contributor that had helped them tremendously recently.","Moreover, they thought very highly of this little fellow’s loyalty. Neither wanted any mishaps befalling it.","Fortunately, after He Zhiran applied medication for Little White, its temperature soon recovered to normal. It was just somewhat feeble for the time being.","Animals inherently possessed regenerative capabilities. It was believed that Little White would quickly recuperate.","...","The Mo Family resolved this crisis inexplicably. The family enjoyed temporary peace.","The Prefectural Magistrate, however, was scared witless.","People of ancient times did not have much nightlife and generally cultivated the habit of sleeping early and waking early.","Many commoners would get out of bed before daylight. Especially during this season, many vegetables grown in their family gardens were already ripe. To earn a bit of money, farmers would carry their vegetables early into the city to sell.","The official road where the Mo Family massacred the Empress’ death warriors last night was also a necessary route for many commoners entering the city.","And so, the Prefectural Magistrate was roused from his sleep before daybreak by people creating a din, with crowds of commoners continually coming to report a case, saying that over a hundred corpses were discovered on the official road leading towards Yun City.","The Prefectural Magistrate was still dazed with sleep then. He felt this was an enormously ridiculous joke.","But with more and more people coming to report the case, he could no longer disbelieve it even if he wanted to.","The Prefectural Magistrate rushed to the scene with his men, paling with fright upon arrival.","This was way more than just over a hundred dead. At least over two hundred...","He was just a minor Prefectural Magistrate. How could he have seen such a major case before?","The Prefectural Magistrate promptly sent men to notify the county magistrates of the surrounding counties to come assist in investigations.","Having gotten early notice of the matter, Meng Huaining was well prepared.","After splitting off from several uncles, he rushed to the Yamen to wait for the Prefectural Magistrate's men coming to notify him. As a result, he was the first county magistrate to arrive at the scene. His only purpose was to not miss any slightest details and updates."]},{"number":484,"title":"Chapter 484: Sweet Potato","paragraphs":["When Meng Huaining arrived at the scene of the crime, he could tell that the Prefectural Magistrate was in a state of panic.","Upon seeing Meng Huaining, the Prefectural Magistrate forgot to maintain his dignity in front of his subordinates and with a tearful voice said,","\"Mister Meng, take a look, take a look. What are we going to do?\"","Meng Huaining also pretended to be startled.","\"Your Excellency, why have so many people been killed?\"","\"I don't know either. I was called here while I was still asleep...\"","At this moment, the Prefectural Magistrate felt overwhelmed. If someone could help him handle this matter, he would gladly obey.","Meng Huaining also understood his intention and reminded him after a while, \"Your Excellency, considering the magnitude of this incident, should we report it to the court?\"","These words were like a sudden realization for the Prefectural Magistrate.","\"You're right, we should report it to the court.\"","The Prefectural Magistrate wiped the cold sweat off his forehead and continued, \"But with so many people dead, even if we report it to the court, we need to have an explanation, don't we?\"","\"Does Your Excellency mean that we should investigate and find the culprit before reporting?\" Meng Huaining spoke in a calm tone, but inside, he was mocking the Prefectural Magistrate's incompetence.","To hold the position of Prefectural Magistrate, one must have some level of intelligence. However, it wasn't surprising that the Prefectural Magistrate would be at a loss when faced with such a major incident.","After conversing with Meng Huaining for a while, the Prefectural Magistrate had calmed down somewhat.","He instructed his subordinates, \"Go and investigate the cause of death for these people.\"","Seeing this, Meng Huaining couldn't help but curl his lips.","Was it necessary to investigate the cause of death for these people?","They were covered in wounds, bloodstains everywhere. It was obvious that they had been beaten to death.","In this situation, the investigation would only reveal the type of weapon used to kill them and whether there were any traces of the culprit nearby.","Although he inwardly criticized, Meng Huaining didn't show it. He wished for the Prefectural Magistrate to remain clueless!","It would be best if nothing could be found, and when reporting to the court, he could only say that over two hundred people were killed on the official road.","After all, the Mo Family's purpose in not cleaning up the battlefield was to give a show of force to the Queen's faction. As long as the effect could be achieved, the process was not important at all.","After searching and investigating, the Prefectural Magistrate's men could only determine that these people were killed by random arrows and some had knife wounds. As for any clues, it could be said that there were none.","Although there were countless footprints on the ground, on the official road, there were already numerous passersby. These footprints couldn't be considered as clues to finding the culprit.","The Prefectural Magistrate had no idea about this matter to begin with. He could only reluctantly write a report to the court, stating that a major murder case had occurred under his jurisdiction, with a death toll of over two hundred and a very cunning culprit who left no traces.","He tentatively concluded that it might have been bandits from the surrounding area who attacked and injured the people.","As for whether there were bandits in the vicinity, the Prefectural Magistrate had no knowledge. But when submitting the report to the capital, he couldn't possibly say that these people died under mysterious circumstances without even suspecting anyone. The Emperor would surely consider him incompetent.","Meng Huaining personally accompanied the Prefectural Magistrate back to the yamen and helped him write the report. He watched as the messengers took the letter and left. It was no longer his concern as to how those bodies would be handled.","As long as everything proceeded according to the Mo Family's plan, it would be fine.","Instead of going to the yamen, he went straight back to Xi Ling Village and informed Mo Jiuye of the news.","Mo Jiuye had the same idea. They were not yet prepared to go to the capital, and he planned to listen to the news from Nan Rui or Fei Nanyu in the capital before making any decisions.","The events of today were unfolding as he had anticipated, so it was best to wait and see for now.","After this incident, life for the Mo family returned to its usual calmness. However, the soldiers on the mountain continued their training without any slack. Besides Mo Jiuye, his older brothers also joined them on the mountain for training every day.","Mo Jiuye himself was also busy. He had to take care of all the big and small matters at home while He Zhiran was in confinement.","For example, the sweet potatoes they planted in the fields this year had ripened. With all the old members of the family training on the mountain, he had to go to the village to hire people to help with the digging.","Because the seeds were from a space, the crops were not affected by climate or soil conditions. The sweet potatoes they dug out were unusually large. Mo Jiuye specifically checked the yield per mu and was astonished to find that it reached over 5,000 catties, almost the same as the yield in his wife's space.","To verify the quality, Mo Jiuye set up a bonfire in the field and roasted the sweet potatoes in front of everyone.","The aroma of the ripe sweet potatoes attracted a crowd of onlookers.","He intended to share these roasted sweet potatoes with everyone, so he didn't hold back. Besides, they had planted thirty mu of sweet potatoes at home, yielding over one hundred thousand catties. There was more than enough for everyone to eat.","Mo Jiuye distributed the roasted sweet potatoes to the villagers who had helped with the work.","If it were spring, the villagers wouldn't have understood the strange things the Mo family was planting and might have thought they were wasting arable land due to their wealth and whims.","However, after the Mo family successively harvested some vegetables and fruits, they no longer had such thoughts.","The villagers had participated in many of the Mo family's harvests and had tasted a bit of everything. Every kind of food was delicious, far beyond their imagination.","Therefore, when Mo Jiuye shared the roasted sweet potatoes with them, apart from the enticing aroma, based on their experience with the previously matured foods from the Mo family, they knew that these sweet potatoes would be extraordinary.","It was not an exaggeration to say that the sweet potatoes from the space were even sweeter than the candies of this era and had a strong satiating effect.","Anyone who tasted the sweet potatoes would give a thumbs up in praise.","\"Jiuye, these sweet potatoes are so delicious. They must be worth a lot, right?\" a member of the Zhao family asked.","When the Mo family was planting in the spring, their clan leader had kindly advised Mo Jiuye not to mess around and avoid wasting arable land.","The northwest region's barrenness was not just a casual remark. It was mainly because the soil quality of the region's arable land was poor, and the grain yield was far lower than in other areas.","However, today they completely overturned this perception. It wasn't that their arable land was bad; it was that they didn't have such good seeds.","Take the sweet potato, for example. Its yield reaches an astonishing five thousand kilograms per mu, surpassing the wheat and sorghum they cultivate by dozens of times.","Moreover, the taste of sweet potatoes is indescribably delightful.","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran had already promised Meng Huaining that they were willing to sell corn and sweet potato seeds to the government for large-scale cultivation by the people of Yun City in the coming year.","Therefore, there was no need for them to keep it a secret.","\"Sweet potatoes have a high yield, so naturally, the price will be very affordable.","I have already promised Mr. Meng that we will keep some of these sweet potatoes for ourselves, and sell the rest to the government, hoping that next year, all the families in Yun City can plant them together.\"","\"Old Nine, are you telling the truth? Are you willing to share such good sweet potato seeds?\"","The villagers of Zhao Family were thrilled and almost rushed forward to hug him, but fortunately, Mo Jiuye dodged in time."]},{"number":485,"title":"Chapter 485: Living Up to God's Gift.","paragraphs":["Mo Jiuye stepped back and smiled at the villagers, \"Of course it's true.\"","Just as the villagers wanted to inquire further, Meng Huaining came over with several officials.","He had known since he took office today that the Mo family was going to dig up sweet potatoes today.","As Mo Jiuye's son-in-law, sweet potatoes were not unfamiliar to him, and He Zhiran had also said that sweet potatoes were not only delicious and filling, but also had extremely high yields.","He had specially arranged the yamen's affairs early today and brought people back to check.","As soon as he reached the edge of the field, he smelled the familiar sweet and sweet smell.","\"Ninth brother, are you roasting sweet potatoes?\"","Mo Jiuye threw the roasted sweet potato he was holding to him.","Meng Huaining deftly caught it. Although it was still a little hot, he couldn't wait to take a bite.","\"Ninth Brother, roasted sweet potatoes are delicious, and I can never eat enough.\"","Meng Huaining smiled and sat beside Mo Jiuye. This move made the officials who followed him somewhat dumbfounded.","Their adults had always been very serious, so they had always thought that he simply couldn't smile.","What did they see now?","Their master smiled so unrestrained, simply a far cry from his usual self.","Meng Huaining didn't care what his subordinates were thinking. Although he was eating happily, he didn't forget the purpose of his hurry back.","\"Ninth Brother, how's the yield of sweet potatoes?\"","When it came to the yield of sweet potatoes, a kind of proud expression automatically appeared on Mo Jiuye's face.","Pointing to the pile of sweet potatoes on the ground, he said, \"Did you see that? These are all produced by one mu of land. We just carefully weighed them, and the yield per mu can reach five thousand catties.\"","\"Ninth brother, did you say that sweet potatoes can reach five thousand catties per mu?\"","Meng Huaining was completely no longer calm at this point, and he stopped eating the sweet potato in his hand and stood up with a swoosh.","\"Ninth Brother, we have agreed that all these sweet potatoes will be provided to the government for seeds next year.\"","He was afraid that Mo Jiuye would go back on his word, and his tone was extremely serious when he spoke.","Of course, Mo Jiuye would never go back on a promise.","Moreover, the couple also discovered a problem that grain crops produced by the space, such as sweet potatoes, potatoes, corn and rice, etc., even if they were planted and harvested with seeds from the outside, they would not decrease production when replanted next year.","In contrast, those delicious fruits and some vegetables from the mountains were just the opposite. The seeds collected from cultivation outside would decrease production by a lot.","Originally, they had thought that after the sweet potatoes were harvested, they would quietly exchange some of them with the inventory in the space.","Now it seems that this humanized rule really helped the couple avoid a big trouble.","Otherwise, they would have to find a way to get seeds out of the space every year. Now it's good, the seeds of these high-yielding crops planted outside are fine.","\"Don't worry, 100,000 catties of these sweet potatoes will be provided to the government. We will keep the rest to earn some profits, but on the condition that after the government has collected these sweet potatoes, they cannot be sold on the market before planting next year. \"","Meng Huaining did not know the background of Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran. He only thought that the Mo family's source of income was just these things on the surface.","Especially since the Mo family now raises so many private troops, they must be very tight on money.","If it weren't for the livelihood of the common people, he certainly wouldn't bring it up.","He had originally thought that Ninth Brother would only give a small portion to the government as seeds for next year. He didn't expect that Ninth Brother would support him so much and offer 100,000 catties of sweet potato seeds in one mouth. This was more than half of the Mo family’s sweet potato production!","Thinking of this, Meng Huaining solemnly saluted Mo Jiuye with his fists.","\"Ninth Brother, on behalf of the people of Yuncheng, I thank you and Ninth Sister for your great righteousness.\"","At first, he still wanted to ask Ninth Brother and Ninth Sister for chili seeds to help the people of Yuncheng get high income.","Seeing the bumper harvest scene of sweet potatoes now, compared with chili, it was much more beneficial for the people’s livelihood.","Selling chili was silver, and if it couldn't be sold in a few days, it would become a pile of mud.","Sweet potatoes were not only delicious, but more importantly, they could fill the stomach. If the commoners could store some sweet potatoes to get through the winter, they would at least not starve to death.","Although Mo Jiuye was not an official in the court, he did not want to see the common people living in hunger and cold. He didn't feel anything about this.","Moreover, his wife also said that the space was a gift from heaven, and she also wanted to follow the will of heaven and try her best to help those in need, only in this way could she not fail the gift from heaven.","\"Alright, we are all family, and it is right for me to help you. Yuncheng has now greatly improved under your governance. In the future, the common people will be able to fill their stomachs, which is also what we are happy to see.\"","Meng Huaining was in a hurry, and when he heard Mo Jiuye say that the sweet potatoes could be transported now, he was so excited that he even forgot to discuss the price. He turned around and ordered his men,","\"You guys hurry back to the yamen immediately, bring all the officials here, and every ox cart in the city without exception.”","This was the first time Ma Junshan saw his master act so unorganized.","He couldn't help but remind, \"Sir, weren't you still pondering the price of sweet potatoes on the way here? Are you sure you want to ship them away now?\"","Reminded, Meng Huaining suddenly realized that he was indeed overly excited.","Feeling a little embarrassed, he looked at Mo Jiuye with a red face, \"Ninth Brother, I got too excited in my joy that I actually forgot to ask about the price.\"","When Mo Jiuye promised to provide sweet potato seeds to the government at first, the reason why he did not mention the price was because he was still unsure about the yield of sweet potatoes.","Before organizing people to dig up sweet potatoes, he and He Zhiran had already discussed that if the acreage yield of sweet potatoes exceeded 3,000 catties, they would sell it to the government at cost.","Of course, as seeds, the price must be higher than that of ordinary grains.","According to the price of modern sweet potatoes, high-yielding ordinary sweet potatoes are priced at around 3 yuan per catty in the market, which is equivalent to the purchasing power of 3 copper coins in this era.","That is to say, the price of sweet potatoes only needs to be 3 cents per catty.","However, sweet potatoes were the first to appear in the Da Shun Dynasty and even the surrounding countries, so the price could not be as low as 3 cents per catty.","Moreover, the price of seeds still had to be several times higher than that of grains themselves."]},{"number":486,"title":"Chapter 486: I will thank the nine brother and nine sister-in-law for the people of Yuncheng","paragraphs":["In addition, he also had to consider the sweet potato business that would be left behind. After weighing things from both sides, Mo Jiuye and his wife decided that as long as the yield reached 3,000 catties per mu, they would set the price at 20 wen per catty for the government.","Don't look down on the price of just 20 wen per catty. 100,000 catties of sweet potatoes was still a considerable income in the eyes of the farmers.","You have to know that the most expensive pork in this era only cost seventeen or eighteen wen per catty.","This was also only when selling to the government. Ordinary commoners still could not afford it.","\"Brother-in-law, my wife and I have already discussed the sweet potato seeds. Since this is the first year of production, we still need to take care of our family's sweet potato business, so the price can't be less than 20 wen per catty.\"","100,000 catties of sweet potatoes was 2,000 taels of silver.","This amount of silver was nothing to Mo Jiuye and his wife. They didn't expect to make much money from farming in the first place.","But it looked very different in the eyes of others.","Especially those villagers who had been toiling in the fields their whole lives. Although they were slow at calculating, after discussing together, they also understood the value of these sweet potatoes.","Before Meng Huaining could react, those villagers were no longer composed.","\"If I didn't miscalculate, the sweet potatoes collected by the government are worth 2,000 taels, right?\"","\"My calculations are the same as yours, also 2,000 taels.\"","\"Oh my god, the Mo family is going to strike it rich!\"","\"The crops from thirty mu of land can sell for so much silver. If this farmland was in our hands, forget about 2,000 taels, we'd have to thank the heavens if we had 20 taels of silver left!\"","\"We were too timid back then. We were hesitant about everything. With Old Nine's boldness, if we had asked to buy some seeds from him and planted even just three mu of land, wouldn't we also have an income of 200 taels?\"","For ordinary commoners, what did 200 taels represent?","It was something they could not attain in their entire lifetime...","Mo Jiuye did not pay any attention to the villagers' discussions. After all, he and He Zhiran had already contributed the sweet potatoes.","Whether they could plant them next spring was something the county magistrate Meng Huaining had to worry about.","After Mo Jiuye announced the price of the sweet potatoes, Meng Huaining was silent for a long time without responding. Mo Jiuye thought he was having difficulties with the silver payment.","\"Brother-in-law, does the yamen not have enough silver? Don't worry if you don't have enough for now. You can owe it to me first.\"","Yunchang County yamen was indeed poor. Fortunately, Meng Huaining was not a corrupt official. He would never embezzle a cent of the tax silver.","Because of this, Yunchang still had enough tax silver to buy these sweet potato seeds.","After all, he was the Mo family's son-in-law. Although he stayed out of many matters, it did not mean he was unaware of things.","For any crops produced on the Mo family's land, which would not be sold at an exorbitant price when they reached Tang Mingrui's hands?","Meng Huaining felt that although the Mo family's sweet potato yield was higher and they were selling to the government, the price would still be slightly cheaper. He had already prepared to be shameless. If the sweet potato price exceeded the amount of tax silver, he would thicken his skin to discuss with his ninth older brother, whether it was owing money or something else, in short he had to try his best to buy these sweet potato seeds.","As a result, the price per catty set by Mo Jiuye turned out to be only 20 wen. This was completely unexpected by Meng Huaining.","Before Mo Jiuye announced the price, Meng Huaining had also guessed it in his mind.","He felt the sweet potatoes would be priced at least 50 wen per catty by his ninth older brother.","\"Ninth older brother, is this price workable?\"","What he meant was, did Mo Jiuye purposely set the price so low in order to accommodate him?","Mo Jiuye knew what Meng Huaining was trying to express. He laughed and patted the latter on the shoulder.","\"Don't worry, this price was set by your sister-in-law.\"","Meng Huaining was not the sentimental type either. He knew this was his ninth older brother and sister-in-law's way of supporting him.","\"If that's the case, I will thank ninth older brother and sister-in-law on behalf of Yunchang's commoners.\"","Having said that, he turned around to face the yamen runners again.","\"Why are you still dawdling? Hurry back and prepare oxcarts!\"","Although the yamen runners did not know the exact value of the sweet potatoes, they could tell from their superior's expression that the government had gotten a good deal this time.","They looked longingly at the half-eaten baked sweet potatoes in people's hands, reluctantly turning around to quickly leave and take care of things.","Meng Huaining did not stay any longer either. With the sweet potatoes priced so low by his ninth older brother, he had to adhere to taking money in one hand and goods in the other. Only then could his heart be at ease.","Following the footsteps of those yamen runners, Meng Huaining also headed back to Yunchang.","The Mo family did not conceal from the villagers who had helped with the labor that they were selling sweet potatoes to the government. As a result, news that the Mo family had earned 2,000 taels from sweet potatoes quickly spread through the village.","Not only that, there were also exaggerated praises about the delicious taste of the sweet potatoes.","At the same time, Mo Jiuye also sent someone to the city to bring Tang Mingrui over.","He and He Zhiran still adhered to their previous profit-making principle, keeping a low profile and only acting as the suppliers in the background.","Tang Mingrui had never resisted anything produced by the Mo family. Even though it was already dark when he received the message, he still rushed over urgently.","Mo Jiuye understood Tang Mingrui the most. He was a business fanatic. As long as it was related to business, he was more enthusiastic than anyone.","Although it was a bit late when he sent someone to notify Tang Mingrui, he could be certain that the latter would still come to the Mo family no matter how late it was.","Indeed, when the Mo family was just starting dinner, Tang Mingrui arrived.","Because Mo Jiuye had anticipated Tang Mingrui's arrival, he had specifically instructed Yu'er to cook several dishes using sweet potatoes as ingredients tonight.","Tang Mingrui was familiar with the Mo family. He would certainly join in for dinner without any hesitation, moreover the Mo family's meals were the most delicious he had eaten in his life. Even the large restaurant he owned could not compare.","After greeting the Mo family elders and older brothers, Tang Mingrui sat next to Mo Jiuye.","Although he had tasted sweet potatoes at the Mo family before, this was still his first time seeing so many foods made from sweet potatoes.","The most eye-catching dish was shredded sweet potatoes.","Mo Jiuye personally demonstrated for him.","He was seen picking up a shred of shredded sweet potato, pulling out long fine strands, then dipping it in cold water before putting it in his mouth.","This was Tang Mingrui's first time seeing a dish that could be pulled into strands and had to be dipped in cold water before eating. He became even more curious about this dish.","On his rushed way here, the person who had invited him had already said that the Mo family's sweet potatoes were mature today and he was invited to come discuss sweet potato business. So he could ascertain that Mo Jiuye specially introduced this dish to emphasize it was made from sweet potatoes.","In any case, try it first before saying anything else.","Tang Mingrui imitated Mo Jiuye's actions and ate a shred of shredded sweet potato."]},{"number":487,"title":"Chapter 487: I will not be polite to Brother Nine","paragraphs":["For Tang Mingrui, peeling and eating sweet potatoes was definitely a new experience.","The cuisine of the Da Shun Dynasty was generally salty, so such a sweet and delicious dish was the first time he had tasted it.","He ran a restaurant business and knew customers' tastes best. Many women and children preferred sweetness.","The chef of the restaurant had also specially researched two sweet dishes, although those two dishes were indeed very popular with women and children, compared with this sweet potato shreds, the taste and texture were not that different, it can be said that there is a world of difference.","\"Ninth brother, can you sell me the cooking method for this dish?\"","\"The cooking method is given to you for free,\" Mo Jiuye answered without any hesitation.","Because this was what his wife had instructed last night.","In her previous life, He Zhiran had also read transmigration novels. Many female protagonists earned their first bucket of gold by selling recipes.","Although the recipes sold could reach more than a thousand taels at most, she did not intend to do so, especially when the person who needed the recipe was Tang Mingrui.","The two of them had always cooperated in doing business, and Tang Mingrui was very frank with the Mo family, and did not take small tricks in the profit sharing because the Mo family did not participate in the business.","Such a cooperative partner, He Zhiran felt, was rare and precious. Besides, they didn’t care about the tiny profit from selling recipes.","In order to sell sweet potatoes at a higher price, good cooking methods must be used to match them.","Having more contact with Mo Jiuye, Tang Mingrui also knew what kind of character he was. No matter how much he opposed, it would not have much effect on whatever the husband and wife said.","\"Since this is the case, I won't be polite with Ninth Brother anymore. I will try my best to create higher profits with sweet potatoes in the future and give Ninth Brother and Ninth Sister a share of the profits.\"","Mo Jiuye liked dealing with such refreshing people.","\"Well, the profits from sweet potatoes are for both our families, so Brother Tang doesn't have to consider the issue of recipes.\"","As the two men talked, Lan Er and Yu Er served another bowl of sweet potato porridge to each person.","After Tang Mingrui tasted it, he kept praising it.","Not only that, there were also sweet potato cakes and fried sweet potato dumplings on the table.","No matter what it was, it was absolutely top notch delicacy for Tang Mingrui.","After the meal, Mo Jiuye had a private conversation with Tang Mingrui in a room to discuss the sweet potato business in detail.","Since the cooperation with Tang Mingrui was in the form of profit sharing, neither party had to care about the cost of sweet potatoes. Mo Jiuye also did not conceal the price at which he sold sweet potatoes to the government as seeds.","Especially since here Tang Mingrui could only get a one-year exclusive deal for sweet potatoes.","Because from next year, the common people of Yun City would grow sweet potatoes on a large scale. When the sweet potatoes matured, they would no longer be a rare food item in Yun City.","By then, if Tang Mingrui still wanted to make big money by using sweet potatoes, there would almost be no such possibility.","Tang Mingrui also understood this truth clearly. He was not greedy. After all, there were still many good things from the Mo family. Just these 50,000 catties of sweet potatoes, he could completely make a fortune.","Moreover, Ninth Brother and Ninth Sister had mentioned that the fruit trees on Mo family’s mountain would have a large yield next year.","He had also tasted many kinds of Mo’s fruits. No matter which one, it was comparable to the delicacies of the world.","There was also the jewelry business that Ninth Brother and Ninth Sister had mentioned before. A product called milk powder could also be processed. It was said that the milk powder was very beneficial for preservation. Just add hot water to reconstitute it.","In short, there were countless businesses he could cooperate with the Mo family, and he would not be discouraged because the crazy profit of sweet potatoes would only last for one year.","Tang Mingrui was in a good mood. At the same time, he still maintained his usual business style without wasting a moment.","The next day, he brought the chef of the restaurant to Xiling Village, and was taught by Yu'er several cooking methods of sweet potato dishes.","The cooking methods of sweet potato dishes were not very difficult. The main advantage was that the dishes were novel.","While the chef was learning, Tang Mingrui also took people to carry away several carts of sweet potatoes.","After being busy for four or five days, all the sweet potatoes in Mojia fields were taken away by Meng Huaining and Tang Mingrui completely.","As for their own family's consumption, they didn't need to worry at all. He Zhiran’s space had as many as needed.","Time passed quickly. At the beginning of August, there was a lively scene in Mo family again.","It was the one month celebration banquet for Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran’s twins.","Considering what had happened recently, according to Mo family’s intention, they would simplify the one month celebration banquet for the two babies.","Simplifying didn’t mean not celebrating it, they just wanted to have fun with their own family members.","But they couldn’t decline the villagers' enthusiasm. They had already sent gifts and congratulations early.","Under such circumstances, it would be unreasonable not to hold a few tables to treat everyone.","Therefore, on the day when the two babies turned one month old, Mo’s family held a banquet again to entertain relatives and friends.","This day was not only the one month celebration for the twins, but also the ripening time for Mo family’s corn.","Otherwise, Mo Jiuye would have organized manpower to harvest corn a day or two ago.","However, Mojia’s banquet today was very different from usual.","The staple food was not the usual rice and steamed buns, but replaced with corn cakes, corn porridge, and boiled corn.","In addition to these staple foods, two dishes used corn as an ingredient.","One dish was pine nut corn, which was a very common modern dish.","The other one had corn as one of the ingredients for the hot pot.","The reason why Mo’s family chose to make so many kinds of food with corn was for one purpose only, which was to let the people attending the banquet today understand this kind of high-yielding and delicious food well.","Sure enough, the effect was amazing.","The villagers of Xiling Village regretted when they heard that this was something they had persuaded Mo family not to grow. One by one, they hated to slap themselves.","Especially when they heard from Mo Jiuye that the delicious corn could yield more than 1,000 catties per mu, they wished they could hit their mouths.","Especially Zhao Lijing, he suddenly felt a sense of guilt.","He was the one who objected most strongly when Mo family was going to grow these crops in early spring. So today he lost the most face.","Let alone anything else, just the corn cakes alone tasted much better than the coarse flour cakes they usually ate.","Boiled corn and corn porridge tasted more and more fragrant as you ate them. Such delicious food with such a high yield.","If he could have believed Mo Jiuye earlier and encouraged villagers to grow some together, let alone how much these corn would worth in silver, at least there wouldn’t be worry of starving in winter at home.","The more Zhao Lijing thought about it, the more annoyed he was, to the point that from the beginning to the end of the banquet he didn't say much.","In contrast to him were Fang Chuanzhou and Xie Tianhai.","Because they believed in Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran, they followed suit without hesitation to grow corn and sweet potatoes when spring began.","Needless to say about sweet potatoes. A few days ago when Mo family began organizing manpower to dig them up, their whole families also participated in harvesting."]},{"number":488,"title":"Chapter 488: Heaven's Gift to Mohism","paragraphs":["They had less farmland and naturally could not plant as much as the Mo family.","Moreover, their hearts were as clear as a bright mirror. They knew that the crops planted by the Mo family could be exchanged for a large amount of silver. Since the Mo family was kind enough to let them plant together, they certainly could not ruin the Mo family's business.","Therefore, without Mo Jiuye having to remind them, the Fang and Xie families automatically stored the harvested sweet potatoes in their own granaries for food during the winter.","Even so, the two families were already very satisfied.","They were not nobles now, just people exiled by the emperor. To be able to live such a comfortable life in the northwest was entirely thanks to the care of the Mo family.","If they did not know better and took the favor given by the Mo family to seize the family's business, wouldn't that be repaying kindness with enmity?","In short, Fang Chuanzhou and Xie Tianhai understood this matter very clearly, and would never do anything detrimental to the Mo family's interests.","Moreover, they were really satisfied now. The womenfolk at home made dolls with the Mo family. Not only was the income high, but it was also stable, allowing the family to have steady income.","Except for working in the fields during the busy farming seasons, the men could go out to teach, so although the days were not as glorious as when they were in the capital, they were comfortable.","Hu Cong did not even need to be mentioned. He also planted sweet potatoes and corn with the Mo family. He had mastered the technique of building siheyuan courtyard houses, and his orders were already more than he could handle.","Moreover, he had so many workers under him who needed a lot of food every day. The sweet potatoes and corn he planted were kept entirely to feed his workers, and he had no intention of selling them at all.","In short, the corn that appeared at the Mo family banquet today moved everyone present.","The villagers were even more regretful. The Mo family had not harvested much corn yet, so they did not know the yield.","Just based on the delicious taste, it had already moved them.","Although Meng Huaining was anxious to talk to Mo Jiuye about the government purchasing corn seeds, he was not an inappropriate person.","After all, Jiu Ge and Jiu Mei had already promised him that the Mo family's high-yielding grains could all be sold to the government as seeds for next year.","Even if he was anxious, it wouldn't make a difference in one day. The full month celebration for the nephew and niece was most important.","Tang Mingrui and Meng Huaining had almost the same thoughts, but they endured without saying anything because of the occasion.","The two little treasures were fast asleep, with Grandma Mo and Madam He holding one each in their arms.","The weather was neither cold nor hot this season, so there was no need to worry that the little ones would feel uncomfortable.","Smoothly giving birth to twins was rare enough in the Great Shun, let alone a boy and a girl like the Mo family. In the eyes of the common people, this matched up to make a good word. The Mo family's good fortune was limitless.","They even believed Zhu and Mingzhu were born with good fortune as lucky babies.","To get a little of the babies' good luck, everyone wanted to squeeze closer to the two little ones.","With so many people, there would inevitably be noise even with care.","Zhu was sleeping soundly in his grandmother's arms. Feeling something wrong, he frowned and opened his eyes.","Seeing her cute frowning grandson, Madam He laughed immediately.","She said to Grandma Mo next to her, \"Mother-in-law, look, my good grandson is awake, and even knows how to frown.\"","Grandma Mo leaned over holding Mingzhu to look. Indeed, as Madam He said, Zhu was frowning at her. He looked clearly unhappy. If it were another child, after frowning they would surely wail loudly.","However, Zhu did not. He was just unhappy, and would not cry easily like his sister.","This expression melted the hearts of both elderly women.","\"My good grandson, if you're unhappy, just cry it out. Don't force yourself.\"","Thinking of her nine sons, every one of them was strong like this since childhood. When they grew up and went to battlefields, no matter how heavily wounded, she had never seen them shed a tear.","At the time, she as a mother even felt proud that her sons were all emotionally tough, seldom shedding tears.","What did this toughness bring about?","It brought about the imperial order exiling the entire Mo family, the new daughters-in-law being secretly poisoned as soon as they married in, and the sons being secretly sabotaged one by one...","The current Grandma Mo now understood. In the future, the Mo family would no longer raise their sons to be so tough, and should be like children in ordinary families, with their own joys, angers, sorrows and delights.","But her precious grandson was naturally tough. Since his birth, the number of times he had cried could be counted on fingers.","Even when hearing a baby's cries, they were always from Mingzhu. Zhu was just unhappy, at most frowning like now.","Madam He did not experience the piercing pain that Grandma Mo did, and did not think of that layer.","\"Our Zhu is tough, like the Mo family men. He's so little but won't shed tears easily.\"","As the two elderly women talked about Zhu here, seeing the guests come over, Madam He revealed Zhu's little face for everyone to see.","Upon seeing Zhu, villagers immediately praised:","\"My god... this is the first time I've seen such a fat and white baby!\"","\"That's right, just look at this baby's brows and eyes, how could they not be extremely good-looking?\"","Their tone was somewhat exaggerated, but it was indeed so.","Not to mention Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran were both exceptional in looks, such premium genetic inheritance was something others did not have.","Just the food He Zhiran supplemented during pregnancy alone, things unavailable in this era. The villagers lived bitter lives, often unable to eat their fill when pregnant, let alone any supplements.","The villagers really were seeing such a good-looking baby for the first time, and all felt it was heaven's favor to the Mo family.","At this time, He Zhiran, who had just finished her confinement, came over surrounded by her sisters-in-law.","Not just the villagers thought this way, even the Mo family themselves did.","Eldest Sister-in-Law looked at Madam He holding Zhu fondly, and gently said, \"Our Zhu and Mingzhu are a month old already, and still don't have proper names. These treasures are heaven's blessings to my Mo family. Their names must not be too casual.\"","\"That's right, our Zhu and Mingzhu must have meaningful names,\" Second Sister-in-Law chimed in.","When it came to naming the babies, everyone looked towards He Zhiran as the mother.","Grandma Mo said, \"Ranran, when the children were born your father already said their names should be decided by you and Jiuye. I asked Jiuye the other day, and he said to listen to you. Why don't you give names to my precious grandson and granddaughter now?\"","\"That's right Sister-in-Law, you're the most knowledgeable among us sisters-in-law. The names you pick will definitely be good sounding,\" Eighth Sister-in-Law said, nudging He Zhiran.","Of course He Zhiran would not shirk naming her own children. She had thought of many names boringly while confined, but eventually denied them all herself.","She admitted she was useless at naming.","Now with so many people urging her, plus the babies were already one month old without proper names, which was rather unsightly."]},{"number":489,"title":"Chapter 489: A promise is a promise.","paragraphs":["He Zhiran suddenly thought of what her sister-in-law had just said, that the two babies were heaven's blessing to the Mo Family.","Since this was the case, why not use the word \"blessing\" to name the children?","After thinking for a moment, she spoke: \"Since everyone feels that Zhu and Mingzhu are heaven's blessings, why don't we call Zhu Tianci!","As for Mingzhu, let's call her Jing'en.\"","Tianci did not need much explanation, it was literal in meaning, he was the treasure that heaven had bestowed upon the Mo Family.","The dispute over Jing'en was a little bigger.","\"Sister-in-law, why is she called Jing'en?\" the second sister-in-law asked.","\"Jing refers to a woman's slender figure, graceful demeanor, and also means talent and brilliance. I hope Mingzhu will grow up to be a beautiful, graceful and talented woman.","The En character combined with Zhu's Ci character means that these two siblings fully embody the meaning of heaven's blessings.\" He Zhiran explained the reason for the names.","Hearing her explanation, everyone praised:","\"Ninth Sister-in-Law is really knowledgeable, the names she picked for the babies are meaningful and pleasant sounding.\"","\"That's right, Tianci, heaven's blessing, Jing'en, beautiful, graceful and brilliant.\"","The sisters-in-law kept praising the good names the two babies were given, and Old Lady Mo also highly approved.","\"Good names, Zhu will be called Tianci, and Mingzhu will be called Jing'en. Tomorrow when your eighth brother gets promoted, have him help register these little ones in the household register.\"","Although He Zhiran had come up with the names for the twins on the spur of the moment, she was very satisfied with them herself. Her children didn't need extravagant names, as long as the meaning was good and they were pleasing to say.","After the one month celebration banquet, of course the guests and hosts had a delightful time. As people gradually left, it was finally Tang Mingrui's time to lead.","During the meal, others were praising how delicious the corn was, while he alone thought differently, pondering over matters of cooperating with the Mo Family corn business.","Although Meng Huaining was not as exaggerated as Tang Mingrui, he too had been thinking about the corn for a long time.","Now that the two babies were full, they would not look for their mother, and had long been held by their aunties to dote on.","Mo Jiuyue and He Zhiran had long noticed that Meng Huaining and Tang Mingrui were absent-minded, so after sending off the last wave of guests, the couple summoned them to their own yard.","At this time, it was the season of crisp autumn air, and the outside temperature was very pleasant. Several people sat under the grapevine arbor in the yard.","The grapes had ripened, and He Zhiran had not gone out for a month, so she had not noticed.","The yard was planted with ordinary wild grapes, but because they were produced in the space, the fruit was a little bigger than wild mountain grapes.","Even so, they were still sour enough to pucker one's mouth. If not for this, Mo Jiuyue would have called people to come pick them long ago.","He personally felt that the grapes were too sour to eat, so rather than picking them and having them go to waste when no one ate them, it was better to leave them on the vines as ornamentation.","But He Zhiran did not think this way. She felt that these wild grapes were best for making wine.","In her previous life, she had only seen others use wild grapes to make wine, and had not tried it herself. So she did not plant many wild grape vines.","Now that the grapes were ripe, He Zhiran's mind became lively.","She wanted to use the wild grapes in everyone's yard to try making some wine. If it succeeded, next spring she would plant large amounts of wild grapes in the mountains.","It seemed this matter had to be put on the agenda as soon as possible too.","This kind of wild grape was not unfamiliar to Meng Huaining and Tang Mingrui. Generally, families with some means would plant some in their backyard, for the purpose of using them as shaded arbors in summer.","The two were also aware that wild grapes were very sour, and assumed the Mo family had not picked them simply because they were not palatable, so they did not pay much attention.","After sitting down, Meng Huaining and Tang Mingrui spoke at almost the same time.","\"Ninth brother, Ninth sister-in-law, you won't go back on your word about selling corn seeds to the government, right?\"","\"Ninth brother, Ninth sister-in-law, this corn can make big money, you won't not do this business, right?\"","The two's words made Mo Jiuyue and He Zhiran laugh.","Now that He Zhiran was out of postpartum confinement, business matters were naturally handled by her, since Mo Jiuyue did not have a wife's skills and brains.","After laughing for a while, He Zhiran spoke: \"Rest assured, we won't go back on a promise.\"","Seeing He Zhiran say this, the two almost simultaneously stood up and cupped their fists, \"Then thank you Ninth Brother and Ninth Sister-in-law.\"","\"We plan to personally take people to harvest the corn tomorrow. The price will be determined after the yield per mu is finalized, don't be impatient.","Besides, whether corn is used for seeds or ground into cornmeal, it needs to be dried before it can be processed. Fresh corn can only make a limited variety of foods.","For example, the puffed corn and one pot dish eaten today use fresh corn...\"","At this time, Meng Huaining and Tang Mingrui simply could not listen to He Zhiran's explanation. All they wanted to know was when they could buy the corn produced by the Mo family.","Especially Tang Mingrui, his eyes were full of the endless business opportunities corn would create. The sooner he got it, the sooner he could earn silver.","\"Ninth sister-in-law, how long does it take to dry the corn?\"","For this yield per mu, it was normally calculated based on the weight of the dried, shelled corn.","Especially since the Mo family corn had not been harvested yet, He Zhiran really could not estimate it.","However, based on the harvests in the space, the yield per mu of dried corn could reach 1,800 catties.","But that was after all the space, growing it outside, He Zhiran did not dare guarantee such a high yield.","In order to give Meng Huaining some peace of mind, after thinking for a moment, He Zhiran said: \"If I estimate correctly, the corn yield per mu should be between 1,300 and 1,500 catties.\"","\"What? Ninth sister-in-law, you said the corn yield per mu can reach 1,300 to 1,500 catties?\"","Meng Huaining was no longer calm, he excitedly stood up, his words shaking.","It must be known that the government's purpose in buying corn seeds was for the common people to be able to grow high-yielding grain crops.","Even if the common people planted a lot of corn, with their frugal nature, they would not casually use it to make things like puffed corn and one pot dish like the Mo family did. Most people would choose to grind it into cornmeal to serve as the staple for their family."]},{"number":490,"title":"Chapter 490: I Will Fund It","paragraphs":["Meng Huaining was so excited because he had heard an astronomical number for him.","The per mu yield of corn after drying could actually reach more than a thousand catties. It should be known that the millet that the common people usually grow, even counting the coarse flour made from the bran, the yield per mu is barely three hundred catties, and that is said to be in a good year.","Once the year turns out bad, reduced production is a small matter, and in severe cases it can be said that there is no harvest at all.","With low crop yields, the taxes collected by the government are also very limited. Even when granaries are opened for disaster relief in times of famine, it cannot solve too many problems, resulting in countless commoners starving to death.","If crop yields are high, it would be different. When the government collects 30 percent of the crops as taxes, it would be equivalent to more than all of the original crop yield.","If this is the case, there would no longer be worries about the commoners' livelihoods in times of natural disasters.","At the moment, Sister Jiu is also unable to give the specific price of the corn seeds. Even if the price is beyond his budget, he still has to find a way to get all the seeds.","\"Sister Jiu, I will go back to the yamen now to raise money for purchasing the corn seeds.\"","With that said, Meng Huaining was about to leave.","He only had three days to raise the silver, and it was urgent.","If Meng Huaining were to go somewhere to raise money, he could only reluctantly go to the prefect to try to figure something out.","The prefect was newly arrived, and they did not have much contact. However, judging from the way the prefect handled the matter of the two hundred dead officers last time, it was clear that he was not a particularly capable person.","Meng Huaining did not dare to have too high hopes for him, but without asking the prefect for help, he could not think of other ways for the time being, so he could only reluctantly give it a try.","When He Zhiran went home earlier, she mentioned that the government's tax revenue was almost used up. Meng Huaining was worried about raising money to purchase the corn seeds.","Seeing that he was in such a hurry to leave, Mo Jiuye stopped him.","\"Is brother-in-law worrying about money?\"","He had already discussed this matter with his wife. If the government could not come up with so much silver to purchase the corn seeds, they could temporarily lend it to him for the time being. They could not let Meng Huaining be in trouble over such a small matter.","As long as there was a good corn harvest next year, Meng Huaining would have no problem paying them back.","Being asked like this, Meng Huaining was apparently somewhat embarrassed.","\"I won't hide it from Brother Jiu, the government treasury is indeed not abundant, and I'm probably an official who governs thriftily for the people's benefit. The treasury definitely does not have much left. After purchasing sweet potatoes for 2,000 taels last time, I'm afraid the government coffer has been emptied.\"","Although Mo Jiuye does not walk around the officialdom, he has also heard from Mo Chuhan about what kind of person the prefect is.","There was a high probability that Meng Huaining would run into difficulties if he went to ask the prefect for ideas.","In fact, Meng Huaining was not unaware that this was the case. By going to the prefect to try to figure something out, he was just doing it as a formality.","Even if he could get a small amount of silver from the prefect, it would be of some help to him.","On the contrary, if he did not get anything out of this trip, it would allow him to clearly see the true face of the prefect.","Mo Jiuye went up to him and pulled him back to his original seat.","\"My wife and I know the government coffer is poor, and you are an official who governs with integrity and cares for the common people, so the treasury must indeed have little left. It spent 2,000 taels last time to purchase sweet potatoes, which probably emptied the government reserves.\"","As Meng Huaining listened to Brother Jiu's words, his face turned slightly red.","\"It's because I'm incompetent and unable to make Yun City prosperous.\"","\"Master Meng is not incompetent. What you have done is already good enough, this is evident to all the commoners of Yun City.\" Although Tang Mingrui had once regarded Meng Huaining as his rival in love, he also clearly knew one fact: that the two of them were a loving couple, and it was not something he could interfere with just because he wanted to.","Especially after the incident where he was falsely accused of hiring someone to commit murder, Meng Huaining helped clear his name so quickly.","To Tang Mingrui, he owed Meng Huaining a favor.","\"Tang is untalented, but ever since coming to the northwest, thanks to Brother Jiu and Sister Jiu, I have made quite a fortune doing business. I am willing to fund the master's purchase of corn seeds.\"","In fact, Tang Mingrui did not know that this was also the second idea Meng Huaining had thought of.","Although Yun City was not wealthy, it was not completely without rich people either.","If he went to the prefect and came back empty-handed, he would try to mobilize those wealthy people to lend a helping hand.","Since Tang Mingrui took the initiative to speak, he naturally had no reason to refuse.","\"Purchasing grains should have been something the government should undertake in the first place. It's just that I took over an impoverished government coffer and indeed do not have that much silver.","Since this is the case, I will thank Boss Tang on behalf of Yun City commoners for his generous assistance.\"","After he finished speaking, Meng Huaining bowed to Tang Mingrui without any hesitation.","Although Tang Mingrui was doing well in business and making strides, he had not yet reached the point described in historical records where he could call the wind and summon rain as the supreme merchant of the Great Shun Dynasty.","At present, apart from some money, he was just an ordinary commoner.","How could he dare to accept such a grand bow from the county magistrate?","Tang Mingrui quickly returned the bow.","\"Master Meng is too polite. Helping the commoners is something Tang would naturally undertake without hesitation. I cannot accept such courtesy from you.\"","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran had originally planned to say they would lend the corn seeds to the government first. As a result, Tang Mingrui had cut in and taken the lead.","Since this was the case, they no longer needed to compete over the limelight. Perhaps this was Tang Mingrui's first stepping stone on his way to becoming the supreme merchant in the future.","Tang Mingrui had originally thought Meng Huaining would politely decline at first before accepting. He did not expect the other party to agree so readily.","Anyway, these were not just perfunctory words he had said, so since the other party readily agreed, he would not stand on ceremony either.","\"Alright, Tang will send 10,000 taels of silver to the yamen tomorrow. If that's not enough, please let me know, Master Meng.\"","Although Meng Huaining still did not know exactly how much silver the corn seeds would require, 10,000 taels was not a small amount to him.","Even if he called on all the merchants in Yun City to donate money, the sum would probably be less than this.","The more he looked at Tang Mingrui, the more he liked his attitude.","\"I'll remember Boss Tang's generosity. If there's anything I can help with that does not violate principles, I will certainly do my best.\"","Although the silver for purchasing corn seeds was settled, Meng Huaining still planned to go to the prefecture to make a trip.","He had been the county magistrate of Yun City for a year and had never troubled the prefect over anything.","Since this matter concerned the livelihood of commoners, he decided to make a trip over.","Moreover, it was already afternoon now. By the time he arrived at the prefecture yamen, it might already be dark.","This was even better, letting the prefect know that he had come seeking help so late must be regarding some urgent major event.","\"It's getting late, so I'll go to the prefecture first. Brother Jiu, Sister Jiu, please chat with Boss Tang.\"","After Meng Huaining left, the several people chatted about corn again.","\"Brother Jiu, Sister Jiu, as you know, I'm now running a restaurant business, and today's dishes made with fresh corn were also very delicious. Can you also sell me some fresh corn?\"","\"Of course we can sell fresh corn to Brother Tang, but fresh corn doesn't keep for long, and the ripening period is very concentrated, so you would only be able to make dishes with fresh corn for a short period of time,\" He Zhiran explained."]},{"number":491,"title":"Chapter 491: Saltpeter to make Ice","paragraphs":["Tang Mingrui knew very well that the corn seeds from the Mo Family were meant to be sold to the government, and he only had one year to make high profits from it.","Although corn cakes were delicious, it was obvious that dishes made from fresh corn would be much more profitable.","He looked at He Zhiran: \"Sister-in-law, do you have any ideas on how to preserve the freshness of corn?\"","In Tang Mingrui's impression, not only was his sister-in-law very smart, she was also very knowledgeable, so perhaps she could come up with a good way to preserve corn.","When asked by Tang Mingrui, the first thing He Zhiran thought of was that fresh corn could be frozen for preservation.","The only way to freeze food during this season was to make ice.","It was no secret that people in the previous era used nitrates to make ice, something many children did in science experiments.","\"Fresh corn can be preserved by freezing,\" she said.","Tang Mingrui...","Sister-in-law, what you said is the same as not saying anything.","Even though the weather now is not as hot as summer, where can I get ice?","\"If I had known earlier, I would have gotten someone to store some ice cubes last winter. It's probably too late now,\" Tang Mingrui said, clearly somewhat discouraged.","In his knowledge, the ice cubes people used in summer were all preserved from winter.","Many mountain caves had extremely low temperatures. The ice cubes people stored in winter were kept in this kind of cave.","Not to mention these cold, gloomy caves were not easy to find, transporting the ice cubes was also a huge project, and many wealthy families hired a large number of workers to do it.","Even so, although the caves were cold, they were still not as cold as the winter air temperature, so the ice cubes stored inside could only slow down the melting.","By the time the ice cubes were used in summer, even the best ones would have lost half their volume to natural melting.","As a result, ice cubes were extremely precious in Da Shun in summer, and very few could afford them.","He Zhiran took in Tang Mingrui's disappointed expression.","She laughed and said, \"Brother Tang doesn't need to worry about ice cubes. You just need to find a bigger place, the bigger the room the better, large enough to store the fresh corn you want to eat.\"","Tang Mingrui was puzzled by her words, but found a bigger place was no problem. The courtyard he had bought for his family was very spacious, with many extra rooms.","He just could not understand what his sister-in-law was going to do. If he took her words literally, it meant his sister-in-law could get ice cubes.","\"Sister-in-law, what do you mean?\"","\"It's just as you thought, I can get ice cubes.\" He Zhiran was not too serious, but her tone inexplicably gave people an indisputable feeling.","Tang Mingrui was even more willing to believe her unconditionally. He stood up,","\"Okay, I'll go back and arrange a bigger room now.\"","He was about to leave when He Zhiran called him back.","\"Brother Tang, don't rush. It will take three days for my ice cubes to be ready. For the empty room you prepare, seal all four sides with mud, completely airtight except for the door. Only this way will the ice cubes not melt easily when stored inside.\"","In ancient times, unlike modern cold storage doors that could be tightly sealed, He Zhiran was thinking that they should try to make the room as enclosed as possible. With the weather getting cooler going forward, making the ice cubes a bit thicker should be no problem. At most, she could provide more ice cubes for replacement.","It would hold out at most another three months until the temperature in the northwest became subzero. By then, even without ice, the fresh corn could still be stored.","Tang Mingrui did not understand why He Zhiran asked him to seal the room with mud, but he believed her unconditionally.","\"Don't worry, sister-in-law, I'll go arrange it immediately.\"","After Tang Mingrui left, Mo Jiuye asked He Zhiran doubtfully,","\"Ranran, where are you getting the ice cubes?\"","He Zhiran did not answer right away, but pulled him back into the room and then flashed into the space.","Nitrates were readily available online in large quantities and at very cheap prices.","Since this was her first time trying it out, she had only bought a small amount for experiments.","After seeing He Zhiran produce ice with his own eyes, Mo Jiuye felt even more distressed for her. Even though she had recovered from childbirth, he still did not want her to exert herself one bit. He even brought warm foot bath water to He Zhiran on time every day.","He Zhiran had also gotten used to her husband's care. From childbirth until now, Mo Jiuye had pampered her into gaining a full circle.","She had gotten a little fatter, but it did not diminish her beauty at all, instead giving her a different kind of charm.","Making ice with nitrates could not be completed in a short time. Worried someone would come looking for them, the couple brought the nitrates and left the space together.","In their own room, they found several wooden basins of different sizes. Mo Jiuye followed He Zhiran's method to operate.","In fact, making ice with nitrates was not difficult at all. After following He Zhiran's instructions, Mo Jiuye excitedly discovered a thin layer of ice forming on the water in the small basin soon after.","\"Ranran, come and see, we did it!\" he said excitedly.","He Zhiran knew that success was guaranteed as long as the method was right.","But she was still very excited, because this was the first time in her two lifetimes that she had used this method to make ice.","\"My husband, by tonight, all the water in this basin will likely have frozen into ice cubes.\"","\"Ranran, you may not know, in this season, many people would be extremely envious of an ice cube this big.\"","Having grown up in the palace as a study companion to Prince Nanqi, he had witnessed with his own eyes the fight between two of Emperor Shunwu's concubines over a not very big ice cube.","Although there were special personnel in the palace responsible for storing ice cubes, it still took huge manpower and resources.","The ice cubes that could be stored until summer without melting were extremely scarce, so even in the palace, ice cubes were very rare in summer.","And they were only used by Emperor Shunwu, the Empress Dowager, the Empress, and several consorts of higher rank.","Something so precious, yet his Ranran could produce it so easily with such a simple method, it really opened his eyes.","Initially, he thought He Zhiran was just whimsically trying it out, and did not expect her to succeed so easily.","As I said before, He Zhiran did not have much talent for business. She could earn silver in ancient times entirely thanks to her modern knowledge.","If she had not thought of making ice to store Tang Mingrui's fresh corn today, she would not have come up with the nitrate ice-making method either.","\"It looks like the Mo Family has gained another source of income.\"","\"If Ranran had come up with this ice-making method earlier, catching the summer season, she would have definitely earned a lot of silver.\"","\"But it's not too late now either. As long as we keep our ice-making method secret, it will always be a source of income.\"","Now when it came to doing business and making money, Mo Jiuye could also talk eloquently about it.","It could be said that the changes in their living environment had, without them realizing it, gradually nurtured their business acumen.","Especially for He Zhiran, many ideas for making money with ice had already sprouted in her mind."]},{"number":492,"title":"Chapter 492: The Corn Harvest","paragraphs":["Mo Family was still not stable at the moment, and there would be many unpredictable crises to face in the future.","There were still some business plans that had not started, and the weather was getting colder and colder. It would not last long to make money with ice at this time.","Therefore, He Zhiran decided to use the ice made to help Tang Mingrui store fresh corn first, and talk about other things later.","\"My husband, although the method of making ice is simple, after all, we only made a small amount. Brother Tang needs to make an ice storage room there, and the amount of ice needed will not be small.\"","\"I know this clearly. As long as there is enough saltpeter, leave the ice making to me.\" Now there were so many soldiers raised at home, and they were all trustworthy people.","Mo Jiuye thought that when making ice in large quantities, he would call some soldiers to help.","Especially he had already figured out how to hide the key steps of making ice, and no one could possibly learn it to make ice.","\"Well, after arranging the corn harvest tomorrow, take people to Brother Tang's place.","More ice is needed there. It’s not very convenient to make it in Xi Ling Village and then transport it.\" He Zhiran reminded.","\"Okay, leave this matter to me.\"","As for the source of saltpeter, there was sale in city drugstores, although the price was expensive, it was not a rare thing.","Therefore, He Zhiran’s purchase of a large amount of it from the space would not arouse anyone's suspicion.","Moreover, Mo Jiuye wanted to hide the method of making ice. He also knew that Tang Mingrui was a sensible person who would not stare at other people's secrets.","In short, Mo Jiuye was asked to do this matter, and He Zhiran was at ease.","...","In the future, He Zhiran did not need to worry too much. Mo Jiuye arranged for people to reserve two acres of corn for normal harvesting, which was used to calculate the yield per acre. The rest of the corn in the field was classified.","The younger ones were piled in one place and used as fresh corn supply for Tang Mingrui. The older ones could be threshed after being dried in the wind and used as seeds provided to the government.","He Zhiran also drew a picture of a simple hand-cranked threshing machine and asked Hu Cong to help make it as soon as possible.","At Tang Mingrui's place, there were people arranged by Mo Jiuye to make ice cubes. It took two days to complete the frozen storage room. Although it looked simple on the outside, there was a cave paradise inside.","People would hug themselves and run out after just a moment inside, so there was no need to use any thermometer to measure the temperature to know that the corn would soon freeze when put inside.","Since the frozen storage room was built, Tang Mingrui was so excited that he almost shouted.","He actually had his own storage ice room in this season.","Of course, the raw materials and workers used to make ice cubes in the ice room were all provided by Mo Jiuye. Even if he didn't say it, Tang Mingrui would not let him contribute for nothing.","After negotiation between the two parties, they decided to split the income from fresh corn by 60% for Mo Family and 40% for Tang Mingrui.","Mo Jiuye didn't have any opinion on this at all. Although ice was rare in this season, he and He Zhiran could have as much as they wanted without worrying about the high cost.","He Zhiran only spent hundreds of yuan to buy saltpeter on Taobao, and an ice room was made. Even if more ice needed to be added later, very little saltpeter would be used. It was not a cost at all.","They gained an extra 10% profit from this, which was very suitable.","Since it was a cooperative approach, the fresh corn delivered to Tang Mingrui did not require him to pay for the goods either, just waiting for him to generate profits and give Mo Family their share.","Although there was no payment, Mo Jiuye was not unprincipled about this matter.","He estimated the size of Tang Mingrui's ice room, which could hold at least 50,000 catties of fresh corn.","Tang Mingrui used two days to transport fresh corn from Mo Family, and as expected, a total of 50,000 catties were taken away.","The remaining corn could be threshed after being dried.","Just in time, Hu Cong also helped make two hand-cranked threshing machines over there.","Mo Jiuye took people to thresh and weigh the corn that had been reserved to weigh, and once again the yield per acre stunned everyone present.","After shelling, the yield per acre of corn reached 1,200 catties, which was about the same as He Zhiran's estimate.","Meng Huaining was also present. He pulled Mo Jiuye excitedly and was a little incoherent.","\"Ninth brother, the world... No... Yun City folks are lucky...lucky...\"","Mo Jiuye patted him on the shoulder.","\"Well, the people of Yun City won't have to worry about starving next winter.\"","There was a lot of arable land in the northwest, but due to the soil conditions, no matter what was planted, the yield could never go up.","The corn from the space was different. It was not affected by the soil or climate. As long as it was not a year of flooding or drought, a bumper harvest was guaranteed.","When Mo Family planted crops in early spring, corn was mainly planted.","At first, they did not expect that the government would purchase corn for seeds to be used next year. He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye only thought that the corn yield was high and could be used as the raw material for staple food. Since they lived in the northwest, they couldn’t watch the surrounding people starve after their own family lived a good life.","So they chose to plant more corn to help those poor people.","Now that Parent Official Meng Huaining was here to arrange this matter, it was more suitable than them taking the lead.","A total of 60 acres of corn were planted. The fresh corn transported away by Tang Mingrui weighed several times more than those threshed corn kernels alone. Therefore, there was still a lot of corn left in Mo Family.","In addition to leaving some corn for their own consumption, Mo Family sold all the rest to the government as seeds for next year.","After weighing, Meng Huaining purchased a total of 50,000 catties of corn kernels from Mo Family, which was enough for the people of Yun City to plant next year.","Since Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran planted corn to help the surrounding people in the first place, they certainly would not charge Meng Huaining too much silver.","As a result, Meng Huaining insisted on handing over all the banknotes sponsored by Tang Mingrui to Mo Jiuye.","\"Ninth brother, I know corn is valuable. This is all I have, still sponsored by Boss Tang. If it's not enough, when the government has more tax revenue next year, I will pay you back slowly.\"","Meng Huaining spoke urgently, as if afraid that the deal would slip away.","Mo Jiuye didn’t intend to take so much silver from him. Just as he was about to carefully calculate in front of Meng Huaining, Meng Huaining had already slipped away in a flash, urging his men to transport the corn seeds to the granary as quickly as possible.","Seeing his eager look, it was as if he had taken a huge advantage that he was afraid the other party would ask for it back..."]},{"number":493,"title":"Chapter 493: Dad, there's gonna be a rush.","paragraphs":["Fang Chuanzhou, Xie Tianhai and Hu Cong although following the Mo Family only planted a small amount of corn, like sweet potatoes, they kept it for their own families to eat and would not take it out to affect the Mo Family's business.","The villagers envied the Mo Family, and blamed themselves for not having foresight initially, not believing the Mo Family could grow such good grains.","They were all honest and kind people. At first, Mo Jiuye had also told them to try planting, it was just that no one dared try.","Fortunately, the Mo Family people were generous, and the county magistrate was a good official who loved the people like his children, and bought the corn harvest for them to plant next year.","Although it was a year later, it was after all because they were timid and did not dare try new things that caused this, everyone could only feel vexed at their own lack of courage, and did not develop any jealousy towards the Mo Family.","Mo Jiuye was busy dealing with his own family matters, not only was the corn in the fields mature, other crops were also maturing one after another.","After being busy for half a month, the work in the fields was finally almost done, and he also started building greenhouses according to the method He Zhiran mentioned.","Actually building the greenhouses a bit later was also fine, it was just that He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye had not received any news from the capital these past days, and were feeling a bit anxious.","They planned to settle the household matters early, and head to the capital to take a look.","Mo Jiuye was busy with the fields, while He Zhiran was at home taking care of the children.","Speaking of taking care of the children, it was only at night that she as the birth mother could keep the two children peacefully by her side.","During the day, Madam He and Old Lady Mo were number one, one grandmother and one mother-in-law, wishing they could see the two little treasures every moment.","Zhu and Mingzhu both drank formula milk, and when feeding them neither He Zhiran needed to lift a finger, the two old ladies handled everything.","And there were the eight sister-in-laws and one little auntie, who tirelessly ran to He Zhiran’s place every day.","It could be said, every action of the two little ones had the whole family's hearts in their hands, and even more seriously, as long as Mingzhu's little nose wrinkled, everyone became extremely nervous...","Madam He and He Ziming discussed, the original plan was that after the two little ones turned one month old, the mother and child would set off back to the capital.","But they kept delaying the time because they could not bear to leave.","At this time, mother and son were sitting in the yard of He Zhiran’s home discussing this matter.","“Mother, I estimate if we don’t go back soon, father will definitely become anxious.” There was a testing tone in He Ziming’s words, but Madam He did not notice.","“When Ruan Ruan gave birth safely, didn’t you write a letter to him? What is there to be anxious about, also, being here we can not only see Ruan Ruan, but also have the little pair of cuties Zhu and Mingzhu. Going back to the capital we would not be able to see the mother and children three, I would certainly be heartsick over it.” Madam He's face was full of worries.","The things Madam He said, how could He Ziming not know?","When his younger sister was unwilling to marry into the Mo Family, although he did not help his parents drug her, he also did not promptly stop it.","Fortunately his younger sister’s days were not bad now, and her in-laws were also sincere people, but after all his sister married far away, once he left with his mother, seeing each other again would not be so easy.","Thinking of this, Madam He could not help but weep.","“Ziming, I know what you are saying, I have also thought it over, I do not plan to return to the capital.”","“You don’t plan to return to the capital? What do you plan to do?” Madam He was a little puzzled.","Although her son secretly had the identity of a skilled gynecologist, on the surface he was after all an imperial official. For someone of his status to leave the capital for a period of time was already not easy, how did he get the idea of not wanting to return?","“Mother, only after coming to the northwest, upon seeing the elder brothers of the Mo Family live such simple yet fulfilling days, did I realize the intrigues and deceits of officialdom do not suit me.","These days I have been pondering over a question, which is what do I want.","Now I know, I can say with certainty, I like this kind of self-sufficient and unrestrained life.”","As mother and son were speaking, Lan Er walked into the yard carrying a basket of grapes.","He Ziming’s face flushed for a moment when he saw Lan Er.","Lan Er's gaze towards He Ziming was also dodgy, it was just that the etiquette she learned in the palace since young made her used to maintaining grace.","She nodded towards Madam He and He Ziming.","“Madam He, Eldest Young Master He, these are grapes grown by Ninth Young Master and Ninth Young Lady in the mountains. Although it was the first year planted, the yield is not high, but there is enough for the family to eat. Today when I saw the grapes were ripe, I called Yu Er to go up the mountain together to pick some for everyone to taste.”","Although Madam He was not as perceptive as Old Lady Mo, she could still read people.","Especially today, Lan Er was very obviously somewhat restrained when speaking.","The Mo Family people had already found their place in the northwest, and followed local customs treating themselves as commoners.","Although Lan Er and Yu Er were attendants to the Fourth Princess, in the Mo Family's eyes they never treated them as servants.","Usually, Lan Er and Yu Er behaved gracefully and politely, but were never servile.","Today however was completely different, Lan Er was clearly very nervous when speaking, as if there was someone frightening in front of her.","Madam He felt she was very kind to people, and had never said anything excessive to these two maidservants before, so Lan Er behaving this way today was definitely abnormal.","Also, this maid kept lowering her head to look at her toes when speaking, looking closely, her face was also somewhat flushed.","Then looking at her own son, just a moment ago still telling her what was on his mind, the moment Lan Er appeared, he immediately became uneasy.","Madam He did not immediately respond to Lan Er's words, her eyes shifting between He Ziming and Lan Er.","As someone who had gone through this before, she seemed to understand something.","However, she also knew, for something like this she could only ask her own son.","“Alright, Lan Er has worked hard, grapes this big, later I will eat more.”","Madam He's expression changed swiftly, upon understanding she immediately reverted back to how she was originally, as if nothing had happened.","Hearing Madam He's response, the tension in Lan Er's heart finally eased a little. She acknowledged and immediately ducked into the kitchen to wash the grapes."]},{"number":494,"title":"Chapter 494: My Marriage is in no Hurry.","paragraphs":["Madam He looked in the direction of the kitchen and made sure Lan Er could not overhear her conversation with He Ziming from that distance before slowly speaking:","\"Ziming, tell your mother the truth, is there something you and Lan Er are hiding from me?\"","He Ziming had thought Lan Er was gone and his mother would still discuss with him why he did not want to return to the capital. He did not expect her to ask him this instead.","He instinctively glanced toward the kitchen. For a moment he did not know how to respond.","As the mother who raised her son, Madam He could naturally discern He Ziming's thoughts.","\"You're my son whom I raised with my own hands. How could I not see your intentions? If not for that incident with the Imperial Concubine, your father and I would have planned to find a suitable young lady for you this year.\"","\"Mother...\" He Ziming interrupted her words.","\"My marriage is not urgent. The incident implicated by the Prince's estate has not been resolved yet. It is inappropriate to discuss such matters at this time.\"","Lan Er had just been kept by Old Madam Mo after He Zhiran gave birth, tasked specifically with attending to He Zhiran's daily life.","Although there were many rooms in the courtyard residence, Lan Er went in and out every day, so she encountered He Ziming more frequently.","At first there was nothing between them. He Ziming would often give her medicinal formulas to make.","Lan Er did not have Yu'er's culinary talents. When she did not understand something, she would ask He Ziming.","Through more and more contact, the two became closer.","Gradually, He Ziming discovered that the innate gentility and grace Lan Er possessed was no less than those of the young ladies in the capital, and was even superior.","She was gentle and graceful yet without the pretentiousness and arrogance of those noble daughters.","This was the type of wife he had dreamed of having. Moreover, Lan Er was beautiful in appearance. No matter how he looked at it, she was the type of woman he wanted to marry.","Over time, He Ziming realized he must have fallen for this young lady.","Lan Er also felt that not only was the Eldest Young Master of the He Family handsome and learned, he was also the gynecology saint revered by the people of the capital city.","If she was not moved by such a talented and good-looking man, that would be a lie.","But Lan Er clearly understood her own status. Moreover, she had silently sworn before the Fourth Princess that she would live only to see the day vengeance was enacted for her hatred. As for affairs between men and women, she felt she did not have the qualification for them.","Although the two had feelings for each other, they were both well aware of the concept of appropriate social status. Neither had broached the subject.","Until today, Lan Er knew the Eldest Young Master's return to the capital was nearing. To prevent herself from falling deeper, she tried to avoid times they might encounter each other when going out.","He Ziming did the same. He did not know if his family elders would accept him marrying a maid with an unknown background, so he did not dare make any promises to Lan Er either.","These past few days, he had also lived in seclusion, reducing chances to meet her as much as possible.","If he had not come to ask his mother about returning today, he would not have been in the courtyard either.","He had intended to probe his mother's attitude originally. If she could understand his desire to resign his post and remain in the northwest, then he could move forward with his plan step-by-step and slowly communicate with his family.","But coincidentally, his mother had noticed clues so early.","As the mother who raised her son, Madam He could still discern whether he told the truth or not.","\"You are my son whom I raised with my own hands. How could I not see your intentions? From young, you were different from those sons of rich families. When they were indulging in fleeting romance, you did not even keep a single concubine in your residence. Mother knows you wanted to find a girl you like to spend your life with.\"","Seeing his mother had said it outright, He Ziming knew he could not hide his affairs from her anymore.","Since it was so, he might as well lay out all his thoughts honestly.","\"Mother, I feel Lan Er is gentle and intelligent, modest and courteous without the pretentiousness and arrogance of those young ladies... \"","How could Madam He not see Lan Er's composure and grace?","It was just that, in her deep-rooted ideology, her future daughter-in-law must be a girl matched to the He Family in status. She had never thought He Ziming would fall for a maid.","Although He Ziming did not directly say he liked Lan Er, as someone experienced in these matters, what could Madam He still not understand?","After spending some time in the northwest, she had adapted to the local customs here and even grown to like the equal interactions between people regardless of status.","For a time, Madam He fell into turmoil.","On one hand, she hoped her son could marry a young lady matched in status. On the other hand, she also hoped her son could be with the girl he liked.","He Ziming perceived his mother's conflict.","\"Mother, think about the Eldest Young Master of the Wang Family. Because his family did not approve of the young lady he loved from a humble background, he was forced to marry the daughter of the Minister of Personnel. In the end, what was the outcome?","Also, the Young Marquis of Jingyuan fell for a merchant's daughter. To obstruct their affection, the Marchioness immediately arranged for him to marry the granddaughter of Prime Minister Xue. Their married life was turbulent, even becoming the laughingstock of the capital.","There's also...\"","\"Alright, stop talking and let your mother think.\"","Madam He was aware of all these examples He Ziming spoke of.","The Eldest Young Master of the Wang Family drowned his sorrows in drink all day long while pining for his beloved lady, thus ruining his prospects and studies.","The Young Marquis of Jingyuan lived in melancholy every day, unable to endure the discord with Prime Minister Xue's granddaughter yet not daring to offend the Xue family's power. In the end, he died from depression before reaching thirty.","\"Ziming, are you saying you can only be happy with Lan Er?\"","He Ziming nodded solemnly.","\"I did not have a lady I fancied before, so I would naturally have no objections if you saw anyone suitable, Mother. But now there is someone in my heart already. If I were to marry another, I fear I would be unable to let go for the rest of my life.\"","To raise Lan Er's status, He Ziming went on, \"Although Lan Er is a maid, those serving princesses in the palace also have rankings. Her speech and conduct are modest, her etiquette and propriety no less than those young ladies.","Father taught me since I was young not to emulate those arrogant young masters, but to maintain an ordinary heart in viewing people and matters. I have never felt she is beneath me in status.\"","\"Mother, I agree with Eldest Brother's viewpoint.\" The conversation between mother and son was not overheard by Lan Er but had not escaped He Zhiran who had just emerged from the room.","She had focused her energy on Zhu'er and Mingzhu lately, and thus had not noticed anything unusual between He Ziming and Lan Er. Hearing their exchange now, He Zhiran realized something different was indeed going on between the two.","For instance, at meals, Eldest Brother preferred plainer tastes. Lan Er would always place the blander dishes in front of him.","Also, Eldest Brother was fastidious about cleanliness. When at home, maidservants specially helped him wash clothes and tidy his room every day.","Here, it was Lan Er who cleaned his room when he was not around, even bringing out the clothes he had changed out of."]},{"number":495,"title":"Chapter 495: I've been working for this responsibility.","paragraphs":["Seeing this, He Zhiran did not think much of it, because Lan Er had always been diligent and perceptive, and it was not unreasonable for her to take good care of her elder brother.","She did not notice the details.","Now, after hearing the conversation between her mother and brother, He Zhiran suddenly had a feeling of sudden clarity.","At first, she did not like people waiting on her, so Lan Er and Yu Er had the sense not to go to her room without being told. Perhaps it was because he was worried that Mo Jiuye would change his heart, so the two of them walked around when they saw Mo Jiuye.","First, not to mention how Lan Er was able to read between the lines, just her proper demeanor and knowledge was enough for her to have no problem being the mistress of the house in the eyes of He Zhiran, who believed in equality.","A marriage of mutual affection indicated that the two had compatible personalities, which was certainly better than an arranged marriage by the parents.","Her elder brother had finally gotten rid of Princess Yujun with great difficulty, and she truly hoped that he could live a happy life.","\"Ranran, do you also feel that your elder brother and Lan Er are a good match?\" Madam He was now wavering.","\"Mother, as long as elder brother likes her, I don't see anything unsuitable.","Lan Er is meticulous, and is more steady in her interactions than the young ladies in the capital. Don't let the fact that she is just the maid of the Fourth Princess fool you. Her knowledge and insightful mind make her fully capable of being a good wife and mother.\"","He Zhiran was not just saying this casually. Lan Er had been with the Mo Family for some time now, and no one knew her temperament better than He Zhiran.","Seeing his sister speak for him gave He Ziming courage.","He stood up and solemnly knelt before Madam He.","\"Mother, since childhood, father had brought me to his side and taught me to see through the deceit and hypocrisy of officialdom. I always thought that father hoped I would have academic achievements and obtain a position to bring honor to the He family.","I had been working hard for this responsibility.","But you and father did not know what kind of life I actually wanted.","Ever since coming to the Northwest, and seeing the Mo Family people living self-sufficient lives day after day, I really envied them.","There is no intrigue here, no deceit, only the simplicity and diligence of the people.","Mother, I ask for your consent to stay in the Northwest and open a medical clinic to treat illness and save lives, and live out my life in peace and simplicity.\"","When he finished speaking, He Ziming heavily kowtowed three times to Madam He, and then looked up waiting for her reaction.","He Ziming's words did shock Madam He. She never knew he had such thoughts.","If she had not come to the Northwest herself, she would probably be completely unable to understand He Ziming's ideas. But ever since coming here, even she did not bear to leave.","Madam He did not immediately ask He Ziming to get up, but solemnly examined him.","He Zhiran also did not expect her elder brother to have such thoughts. After all, the original owner only saw a hardworking and studious elder brother who was very obedient to his father.","He Ziming was already past the rebellious age of youth, and was exceptionally steady and moderate. He Zhiran absolutely believed he was speaking the truth.","Although she understood her elder brother's thoughts, she did not speak up to help him at this moment.","After all, Madam He came from a wealthy household, and many ideas were deeply ingrained in her mind.","Wanting to immediately change her thinking was impossible. This matter could only allow her to think through some principles herself.","As a daughter, she also did not want to push her mother too quickly, and wanted to give her some time to think.","Madam He was thinking, but she had not reached the point of being completely unable to accept these ideas.","She could not even figure out herself, if this was in the past, and He Ziming said such things, she would surely have thought he lacked ambition.","The current her did not seem to reject her son's words, and even felt an urge to stay here with him.","After about the time it takes to drink a cup of tea, He Ziming was still kneeling, Madam He stared at him deep in thought, and He Zhiran stood behind her.","Lan Er finished washing the grapes in the kitchen and came out, immediately seeing this scene.","He Zhiran knew Lan Er's thoughts. She was utterly loyal to the Fourth Princess, and only hoped to see the day she would avenge her grudge. And this girl was stubborn, if she insisted on not being with elder brother, wouldn't this situation with mother and elder brother become an embarrassing mistake?","\"Cough cough... Mother, elder brother is a grown man now, even if he makes mistakes you can't make him kneel like when he was a child!\"","Madam He reacted quickly as well, deliberately keeping a stern face. \"I'll let you off this time, get up!\"","He Ziming stood up and dusted off his clothes, continuing to keep his head lowered.","Lan Er did not know what had happened. She only thought that the He family's eldest young master had displeased Madam He, and hurriedly brought over the washed grapes.","\"Madam He, Eldest Young Master, Ninth Young Lady, these are the grapes Yu'er and I picked from the mountain. Please have a taste.\"","After speaking, she placed the tray on the stone table, and brought another tray of grapes to the main house for the women watching the babies.","Seeing Lan Er leave, He Zhiran pulled He Ziming to sit on either side of Madam He.","\"Mother, our lives are only a few decades short. If possible, everyone would want to live according to what they enjoy, not just elder brother, but me as well.","In the past in the capital, I spent my days in the inner residence reading, never considering what kind of life I wanted for myself. I thought I would be like you, mother, spending my days at home teaching my children after getting married.","Ever since following the Mo Family in exile, I've come in contact with more people and events, and we live by the fruits of our own labor every day. This kind of life is a bit more arduous, but it makes me feel more fulfilled.","Especially after coming to the Northwest, through our own hard work we claimed land, reclaimed barren mountains, and built homes...","As a result I discovered that this is the life I enjoy, compared to the mundane rules of the capital, I prefer the fulfilling days now.","\"Mother has also been struggling recently, and does not wish to return to the capital.","On one hand, I cannot bear to part with you, Zhu'er and Mingzhu. More importantly, mother enjoys life here.\"","In the capital, Minister He would rise early every day for court. She also had to get up at that time, although her husband often told her to sleep a bit longer, she did not agree, because this was the custom since ancient times.","If the wife was still lazing in bed when her husband got up, even if others did not gossip, the servants in the household would secretly ridicule her.","And in some wealthy households with lax discipline over the servants, these ugly matters would quickly spread in whispers.","Fortunately, Minister He did not have elders, so she did not need to pay daily morning and evening greetings, and also had no concubines causing trouble for the main wife.","Many distinguished ladies in the capital envied Madam He's days."]},{"number":496,"title":"Chapter 496: The Official is better off not doing it.","paragraphs":["Madam He had been quite satisfied with her life before, but since coming to the Northwest, she realized that she had just begun to experience what a happy life really was after living half her life.","Perhaps this kind of life could only continue if they stayed in the Northwest.","As her son, He Ziming could naturally see some of his mother's thoughts.","If his mother had disagreed with what he said today, she would have spoken up to refute it already. However, she did not immediately refute him today. Not only that, but she also seemed to have listened to what his sister said.","There is a saying that one should strike while the iron is hot. He Ziming felt that the timing was about right, so he said, \"Mother, what's so bad about me staying in the Northwest as you said? We can also build a courtyard like Ran Ran's family and raise some poultry and livestock. Not only that, but I would be close to Ran Ran, and we siblings can look out for each other.\"","Madam He had to admit that her son's words had struck right at her heart.","\"Actually, Mother also wants to stay in the Northwest, but your father...\"","She didn't need to explain too clearly. The siblings understood what their mother meant.","\"Mother, Father once said that after my official career stabilizes and I can support the He family, he plans to retire and return to his hometown to live an ordinary life with you and enjoy his later years.","The current political situation at court is unstable, and Father is a neutral party, so it is inevitable that he will offend some people in power. Rather than spending time dangerously in the capital, it would be better to persuade him to resign from his official post early.","There is a saying that goes, 'Without an official post, one's body is light.' Our whole family can stay away from that place full of slander and live a peaceful life instead.","Moreover, your son has medical skills. Don't just call me the 'gynecological saint hand' because I mainly researched gynecological medicine. Although that is the case, I have also studied other medical skills. I dare not say I have mastered them, but I am still better than most doctors in general.","In the future, I can guarantee that you two elders will have no worries about food and clothing.\"","\"Mother, I think elder brother is right. Emperor Shunwu is muddle-headed, and his sons are not very capable either. Plus Empress Dowager's party is messing up court principles. With such an unstable situation, it is better if Father resigns from his official post!\"","In her eyes, no power, wealth or honour was as important as her family's safety.","Moreover, she understood her father's temperament. He was too upright. If he saw something he disapproved of, it would be easy for him to offend others.","Rather than struggling to survive in that murky court, it would be better to live a carefree life in the countryside.","Even if elder brother could not guarantee their parents' livelihood in later years, she could definitely make sure the two elders had no worries about food and clothing.","She still had that magical space. She could buy some little trinkets to entertain them later and make sure they would not feel bored in their future life.","\"Ran Ran, you can't just casually say things like that,\" Madam He said. After all, she was timid. Although she also agreed with what her daughter said, such rebellious words could easily bring disaster if spoken out loud.","\"Mother, there is no outsider here. I'm just telling you my true thoughts,\" He Zhiran said.","\"If you have no objections here, I plan to tidy up the house in a few days before leaving for the capital with my husband. I will tell Father about this personally and let him decide for himself what to do.","You and elder brother don't need to rush back either. Wait until you hear back from Father before making any plans.\"","Madam He's mind turned very quickly. She had just been struggling with whether to persuade her husband to resign. But now her attention had completely shifted to He Zhiran's plan to go to the capital.","\"Ran Ran, you want to go to the capital?\" This was completely unexpected for her.","Everyone knew how sensitive the Mohist identity was in the capital, not to mention that they were still in exile now and were not allowed to leave Yancheng.","She knew that Mo Jiuye had gone to the capital recently, but that was because the county magistrate was his brother-in-law.","Now it was their couple's turn to go to the capital. If someone with ulterior motives discovered this and reported it to the court, it would bring deadly disaster.","He Zhiran had not originally planned to tell her mother about going to the capital. She had thought that since her mother had been away from the capital for so long, she would leave after her child turned one month old. Then she and Mo Jiuye could sneak off to the capital without anyone knowing.","But who knew, not only did her mother and brother have no plans to leave, they even seemed to have the idea of settling down permanently in the Northwest judging by what they just said.","She was truly willing from the bottom of her heart to have her maternal family live in the Northwest long term, especially since the political situation at court was unstable. She also did not want her father to get involved.","But in that case, she and Mo Jiuye would have to explain themselves when leaving this place to go to the capital.","\"Mother, I won't hide it from you. The current situation for the Mohists is not as good as it looks on the surface. Elder brother understands this best. The Empress adopted the Fourth Prince. Although my Mohist family no longer participates in court affairs, the Empress has always been suspicious. She won't let people who could obstruct the Fourth Prince's path to the throne live.","The reason my husband and I are going to the capital this time is to take preemptive action. There is a saying, 'Do not attack others if they do not attack you first.' When it comes to the Mohist family's safety and interests, we can't just sit here passively waiting to be attacked.\"","Although Madam He did not have the same wisdom and courage as Grand Madam Mo, she was not completely ignorant either.","\"Mother understands the rationale behind what you said, but I'm worried that it will be dangerous for you.\"","\"Mother, I think it is the right thing for Sister-in-law Ran Ran and Brother-in-law to go to the capital. The Mohists have always been loyal and righteous. If there are still people who don't want their family to live in peace after the Emperor wrongfully accused them and sent them to exile in the Northwest, then taking risks is very necessary.","As the saying goes, 'Nip problems in the bud.' Any potential dangers must be eliminated early on.\"","He Ziming strongly agreed with their idea of going to the capital, but he did not agree to his powerless little sister tagging along.","\"Ran Ran, it is right for the Mohists to go to the capital, but I don't agree with you going together with them.\" She had been physically weak since she was little. And now she wanted to pretend to be brave and follow them to the capital when she had two young children.","At this point, Madam He also understood the necessity for the Mohists to go to the capital. If they wanted to live safely and steadily here, they had to resolve potential crises.","\"Ran Ran, your elder brother is right. As a woman, it's not appropriate for you to get involved in such matters,\" she said.","He Zhiran knew there would be opposition when she talked about going to the capital.","For things like this, she had learned to be smart—don't try to argue. She had already expressed what she wanted to say clearly. She would just secretly follow Mo Jiuye when the time came anyway.","\"Mother, let's continue talking about whether Father should resign from his official post.\"","Madam He thought her daughter had already listened to her and her son's advice.","\"That's good too. It will be better to clearly tell your father my and your elder brother's thoughts face-to-face rather than writing letters that could be used against us.\"","\"Since that's the case, Mother and elder brother should stay here at ease. I'll talk to my husband later and buy land nearby to build you two a courtyard similar to the Mohists'.\"","Upon hearing they would build a courtyard similar to the Mohists, He Ziming immediately took out several silver notes from his sleeve and gave them to her."]},{"number":497,"title":"Chapter 497: Do you Know What You Mean","paragraphs":["\"These silver notes are what elder brother has saved from his years of practicing medicine, the amount is not very much, only eight thousand taels. If building such an estate costs too much, many details can be reduced.\"","He Ziming was not completely ignorant. Not to mention building houses in such a barren place as the northwest, even in the Capital city, eight thousand taels could buy a three-courtyard residence.","It was just that he and Madam He both felt that stained glass windows were very valuable, so they thought the silver might not be enough.","\"Elder brother, building an estate like ours wouldn't require so much silver,\" Lan Er pushed the silver notes back.","\"I'll take care of the building, just consider it filial piety from your younger sister to father and mother.\" He Zhiran, as the eldest son, certainly could not let his younger sister pay for building a house for their parents.","He offered the silver notes again. \"Are you looking down on elder brother for not having the ability? Not even having the capacity to build a house for father and mother.\"","\"Elder brother, I didn't mean that. You are father and mother's child, and so am I. Whoever contributes the silver makes no difference. Besides, you're planning to open a medical clinic here, and will need silver to operate it. I earned some silver in the northwest, so just grant me this once to fulfill my filial heart, alright?\" Lan Er firmly refused to take He Ziming's silver notes.","Madam He saw the silver notes going back and forth between the siblings and felt very comforted.","Brotherly love and sisterly deference were fully embodied in them.","In the Capital city, many prominent families had siblings who fought and schemed against each other over more benefits.","Yet her children were both considerate of each other, having such children was her greatest honor in life.","\"Alright, stop arguing, you two. Your father and I have also saved up some silver over the years. We'll pay for the building ourselves.","If you really want to be filial, just live your own lives well and cause your father and I less worry. That would be more practical than giving us a mountain of gold and silver.\"","Madam He's words were already very down-to-earth. What mother doesn't hope for a smooth life for her children to live at ease?","Lan Er was also not melodramatic. Anyway, building a house wouldn't require that much silver, it didn't matter who paid for it.","\"Then listen to mother. I'll have father find Master Hu to help starting tomorrow.\"","To get the house built before winter.","Although they had digressed a bit, Lan Er had not forgotten about elder brother He Ziming's intentions.","\"Elder brother, does Lan Er know your feelings?\"","\"She doesn't seem to know.\" He Ziming had never spoken with such little confidence before, clearly he had been thinking it was one-sided all along.","He Zhiran knew Lan Er's personality, and also knew her purpose for coming to the northwest.","If it hadn't been for her and Mo Jiuye stopping her, Lan Er probably wouldn't exist in this world anymore.","After more contact over time, she knew Lan Er's mindset was very firm. Even if Lan Er had feelings for elder brother He, she probably wouldn't agree and would keep the promise she made initially.","\"Elder brother, don't rush to confess for now. Let me try to probe Lan Er's thoughts.","A relationship needs mutual affection. If Lan Er is unwilling, let's not force it.\"","She didn't want He Ziming to have too much hope. The greater the hope, the greater the disappointment.","\"I understand. If Miss Lan Er is unwilling, I promise not to pester her.\" He Ziming quickly stated his stance.","Madam He listened to her children's conversation, at a loss for what to say.","It turned out these siblings had directly ignored her, not caring whether she agreed to her son marrying Lan Er or not, they wouldn't listen to her opinion anyway.","Oh well, she didn't have much opposition to her son's feelings anyway, just let nature take its course.","Seeing that mother had nothing to say, He Zhiran stood up.","\"I've been out for a while, going back to check on the children.\"","\"I'll go with you.\" Madam He also stood up, wanting to see her two little grandchildren again after a while.","If she went back to the Capital city and couldn't see those two treasures, she probably wouldn't enjoy her meals anymore.","When He Zhiran and Madam He returned, Lan Er was still there. But the mother and daughter tacitly showed no abnormalities.","Not until the sky darkened and everyone dispersed, did Lan Er bring a basin of clean water into He Zhiran's room, and He Zhiran called for her to stay.","\"Lan Er, when I first brought you and Yu Er to the northwest, I never asked your ages.\"","Lan Er was very perceptive, and the young madam would often chat with her, but never asked such questions.","Still, she politely answered, \"Young Madam, Lan Er and Yu Er are the same age, just turned eighteen this year.\"","In the Da Shun Dynasty, girls generally started betrothal discussions at fifteen. As long as they had no physical defects, they would basically marry by sixteen.","Lan Er and Yu Er were eighteen this year, quite old maids by now.","\"You and Yu Er are so fair, if not for saying so, I wouldn't have known you were already eighteen.\" He Zhiran didn't immediately get to the point, but saw Lan Er's evasive eyes, seeming preoccupied.","She wanted to keep the conversation light.","\"Look at me, not even eighteen yet and already mother to two babies.\"","\"That is the young madam's fortune, to bear twins in one birth, and both sons too.\" Lan Er thought He Zhiran was lamenting something, and her nervousness dissipated.","He Zhiran chatted casually with her for a bit longer before finally saying, \"Have you and Yu Er thought about how to spend the rest of your days? You can't do menial chores at the Mo house forever, right? Besides, you don't have any indenture contracts and are free persons.\"","Hearing this, Lan Er fell to her knees with a thud.","\"Young Madam, when Yu Er and I followed you back to the northwest, it was just hoping that on the day the princess' revenge is accomplished, we can go pay respects at her grave and tell her the news. I had no other thoughts originally. I was already indifferent to the world, but grateful for the Mo family's kindness, I reignited my desire to live.","Now, Lan Er is willing to stay at the Mo family forever, even as an ox or horse if need be.\"","Lan Er was clever and immediately grasped He Zhiran's implication.","Moreover, when she encountered young master He earlier, Madam He was also there. Her blushing might have revealed something to Madam He. What if because of this, the young madam wanted to marry her off to that family?","So she had to state her stance before the young madam brought it up.","Since He Zhiran had started the topic, she had no intention of stopping halfway."]},{"number":498,"title":"Chapter 498: Marriage is the happiest when love exists.","paragraphs":["\"A person can't dedicate their whole life to a bit of longing in their heart. Even if you get married, you can still live in Xiling Village and be able to walk around with Mo Family often, hearing about the news of Princess Si getting her revenge at the first moment,\" He Zhiran said.","Lan Er was more and more puzzled.","\"Noble Consort, even if Lan Er lives in Xiling Village, she won't marry.\" She didn't look down on the peasant men in Xiling Village, she just simply didn't want to marry, and the longing in her heart didn't allow it either.","He Zhiran was really surprised that she had never seen such a stubborn person before.","\"What's wrong with getting married? Look at me, my husband dotes on me, my in-laws rely on me, and I can also have two lovely babies.","You are an outstanding woman. I think outstanding women should have all this.\"","\"Noble Consort's blessings are not something everyone can expect. Lan Er doesn't dare to extravagantly hope for these.\"","While He Zhiran was talking, she kept observing Lan Er's changes in expression. She could see a momentary bright light in her eyes, which showed that deep down she yearned for this kind of life.","\"Although you used to have the status of a maid, I can see it very clearly that your temperament and etiquette are no worse than those prestigious ladies in the capital city. The villagers here in Xiling Village definitely don't match you.\"","After thinking about it, He Zhiran felt that the previous preamble was adequate enough and there was no need to beat around the bush anymore.","\"My eldest brother He Ziming has been with my father to be personally taught by him since he was young. Not only are his literary talents outstanding, his appearance is also remarkable. Today when I talked with him, I knew that he doesn't like the deceitful ways of the court.\"","\"Noble Consort, did you say Master He doesn't want to go back to the capital city?\" Lan Er widened her eyes and looked at He Zhiran, full of disbelief.","Just now when she refused to get married, it was partly because of her previous promise, and also because of He Ziming.","She had to admit that her whole heart and eyes were full of Master He now, it was just that she knew more clearly that her status simply didn't match his.","Especially since she still had the promise to Princess Si first, she just wanted to hide this feeling in her heart to let time slowly help her digest it.","But now, why did Noble Consort mention Master He to her, could it be...?","From Lan Er's expression, He Zhiran could be completely certain of her thoughts.","\"My eldest brother said that he likes the lifestyle in the northwest, and also that there is a girl here who he can't stop thinking about.\"","This was direct enough. If Lan Er still didn't understand, then she could only pretend to be muddled.","Lan Er's face reddened all of a sudden.","\"Noble Consort, in this lifetime Lan Er will...\" She didn't get the chance to say the words not marry before He Zhiran interrupted her.","\"In this world, many things will change along with changes in the environment. I also understand your original intention. Whether you marry or not will not affect the oath you once made.","Besides, you can also see that everyone in the Mo Family is self-reliant. We completely don't need any kind of master-servant differences. You have been with the Mo Family for so long, has anyone here treated you as a servant?\"","This was indeed true, Lan Er had to admit this point.","She and Yu Er never lacked food, clothing, or anything else. Not only were these the same as the Mo Family's women, but the Mo Family's women also didn't do less work than them when working.","\"This is...\" She hesitated indeed.","Which woman doesn't yearn for a love that belongs to herself?","By now Noble Consort's words were already very obvious. She also indicated that the He Family didn't despise her status.","\"It's just...just...\" Lan Er hemmed and hawed for a long time but still couldn't find any reason to refuse. Of course, she was also reluctant to refuse.","\"No more 'just', I won't rush you for an answer on this matter. Think carefully about it after you go back tonight when you inevitably lose sleep. You can tell me your decision tomorrow morning.\"","When Lan Er came out with her head lowered, Mo Jiuye, who had been busy outside all day, came back. At first he was stunned when he saw Lan Er kneeling in front of He Zhiran.","\"Ranran, what on earth happened?\"","In his understanding, his wife had never liked other people kneeling to her. Could Lan Er have committed some unforgivable mistake?","Seeing Mo Jiuye come back, He Zhiran also didn't talk about what happened just now since Lan Er was a young lady who would be shy easily.","\"Lan Er you can get up. I won't rush you for an answer on this matter either. Think about it carefully tonight when you inevitably lose sleep, then tell me your decision tomorrow morning.\"","After Lan Er went out, Mo Jiuye closed the door. He Zhiran took the initiative to tell Mo Jiuye what happened earlier.","Mo Jiuye was also an aristocrat in the capital city before, so he must have his own subjective opinion on this kind of marriage with unequal status. He Zhiran told him carefully because she wanted to hear his thoughts.","\"Husband, tell me the truth. If you fall in love with a girl whose status has a huge disparity from yours, what would you do?\"","Mo Jiuye had never thought about something like this before. When he was a teenager, his family had already engaged him to He Zhiran. Besides, after all these years away from home, he had never met a girl he admired either.","However, since his wife asked, he still thought about it carefully before answering.","\"Before marrying you, I had never had feelings for any other girl. In my mindset, marriage was completely up to my elders to decide. I also believed in my parents' judgement, and the facts verified this point too. Marrying you is the biggest blessing in my life.","Also, through interacting with you more and more, I like you even more now. I can even devote my life for your sake.\"","Although the couple had always been affectionate with each other and He Zhiran also knew that she had a place in Mo Jiuye's heart, it was still the first time for him to say such things openly between them. Not only Mo Jiuye, even He Zhiran the listener couldn't help blushing.","\"Husband, I'm asking your opinion on this matter, not asking you to talk about our feelings.\"","Mo Jiuye went forward to embrace He Zhiran in his arms and lovingly planted a kiss on her forehead.","\"It's because I don't know what other people think. I only know that a marriage with love existing, regardless of rich or poor origins, or whether the families match, is the happiest kind.\"","Although he didn't answer the question directly, He Zhiran had already found the answer she wanted from it.","But she still wanted to hear Mo Jiuye say it from his own mouth.","\"What if I wasn't the daughter of the Minister of Revenue's family and was just an ordinary commoner or even a maid, but happened to also fall in love with you, what would you do?\"","When it came to love, Mo Jiuye was absolutely single-minded. In the past when he didn't understand the taste of love, perhaps this question would have been hard to answer, but it was different now. He now loved He Zhiran to the bone.","\"If it really was like this, I would tell my mother that I want to marry you. No matter what your status is, you are the person I, Mo Jiuye, want to spend my life with.\"","\"What if your mother didn't agree then what?\" He Zhiran became more and more interested in this topic and asked persistently.","\"You understand my mother's character too. Although she was more stern when she was in the capital city, she is also very reasonable and understanding. For any girl I come to like, as long as she has good moral character and disposition, my mother would not oppose.\""]},{"number":499,"title":"Chapter 499: Is Yamen Busy Today","paragraphs":["He Zhiran understood that her mother-in-law was indeed reasonable and never looked down on others like the noble matriarchs in the Capital city.","Thinking of her own mother, though a bit more homely compared to her mother-in-law, she was also a kind and open-minded person.","It seemed that as long as Lan Er agreed, she and her brother could explain the situation to their mother, and this marriage wouldn't be as difficult as imagined.","Of course, the head of the He Family in the Capital city might have a different opinion, but as long as her mother didn't object, things would be easier.","First, she needed to resolve the current predicament.","While He Zhiran pondered over the situation between He Ziming and Lan Er, Mo Jiuye's body had undergone a fundamental change.","His normal body temperature gradually increased after intimately interacting with his wife, and the primal desire arising from his heart made him instinctively seek her cherry lips.","This was the first time the couple had been so intimate since He Zhiran became pregnant.","It wasn't that He Zhiran was unwilling before; she had even taken the initiative to hint to Mo Jiuye that after three months of pregnancy, the situation would generally stabilize, and as long as they were careful, there wouldn't be any problems.","But Mo Jiuye was afraid of harming his wife and children, and no matter how difficult it was for him, he had always restrained himself.","It wasn't until several days after the twins' full moon that Mo Jiuye's urge reignited, reaching an uncontrollable level.","He was also worried that his wife might become pregnant again. The pain she had endured during childbirth was still vivid in his mind, and he had sworn never to let his wife go through that again.","Therefore, since He Zhiran's postpartum recovery period ended, he had been enduring with willpower.","As the saying goes, \"Forbearance has its limits,\" which described Mo Jiuye's current psychological state.","His large hands roamed over He Zhiran's back, and his fierce kisses never stopped...","That night, Mo Jiuye could no longer control his primal physical desires. Nevertheless, he was still very gentle with He Zhiran's body, and no matter how intense his desire burned, he would always ask about her feelings.","Especially towards the end, he was afraid of releasing his seed inside his wife's womb, so he summoned all his willpower to quickly withdraw.","He then tightly embraced He Zhiran, savoring her every breath.","Although He Zhiran had no experience in this area, as a soul from the modern world, she understood Mo Jiuye's reasons for doing so.","Moreover, she also enjoyed the intimacy with Mo Jiuye, and if this situation continued, it would undoubtedly affect their marital dynamics.","With a thought, she entered her space and purchased a box of condoms from Taobao, shyly explaining the usage to Mo Jiuye.","Mo Jiuye had some understanding, as there were contraceptives in the medical academy, but he was worried that frequent use would harm his wife's health, so he had never considered that idea.","To his surprise, his wife's Taobao space actually sold such a good product. Did this mean that from now on, he wouldn't have to worry about anything and could be intimate whenever he wanted?","Mo Jiuye opened a condom package, revealing a naughty smile.","\"Ran Ran, I want to try this thing now...\"","He Zhiran...","She had just been exhausted from their previous activities and had informed Mo Jiuye about the existence of condoms for his sake.","Who knew this hungry wolf would be so impatient...","A night of passion, and the couple slept more soundly than usual.","The two little ones were also very well-behaved, knowing that their father and mother hadn't played for a long time, and they didn't cry all night, sleeping until daybreak.","In the courtyard, Madam Mo and the other women of the Mo Family were waiting.","Usually, at this time every day, they would come to see the babies, and Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran would have already gotten up. But today was exceptionally unusual; not only were the two adults silent, but the two babies hadn't cried either.","Since the birth of the twins, these people had become accustomed to waking up early every day as their first task to visit the little siblings in Mo Jiuye's courtyard.","In fact, it seemed that only by doing this could they start their day full of energy.","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran had already woken up, but after last night's exertion, neither of them felt like moving, so they indulged themselves for once.","It wasn't until the sound of Mingzhu crying for food woke up that the couple reluctantly got up.","Mo Jiuye was used to this pattern of family members waking up early to see the children, so he opened the door and walked out, leaving the room to the women.","He Zhiran didn't need to do anything; the women didn't require her to feed the children herself. The two elderly ladies and sisters-in-law would fight over serving the two little ones, and some would even be unhappy if they couldn't assist the babies...","With the children in the care of the family's women, He Zhiran became idle. She would check on the breeding farm, inspect the crops in the fields, and appropriately provide key input when Mo Jiuye was building greenhouses these days.","It wasn't until the afternoon that He Zhiran walked towards her own courtyard. As she approached the corner, she saw Meng Huaining riding back on a horse.","Seeing He Zhiran, Meng Huaining dismounted.","\"Sister-in-law, aren't you busy at the Government Office today? Why are you back so early?\"","He Zhiran knew that Meng Huaining must have had something to do, returning at this hour, and she hadn't seen her brother-in-law today, even though they usually went together.","Meng Huaining knew that Sister-in-law He was the matriarch of the Mo Family and had the right to voice her opinion on matters discussed by the men.","\"Sister-in-law, let's go to Second Uncle first. A letter has arrived from the Capital city.\"","The mention of a letter from the Capital city was a matter of great concern for He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye. After Xiaobai returned, he had been recovering from his injuries in the space, and although they were worried about the situation in the Capital city, they couldn't ask the injured Xiaobai to deliver messages.","Finally, a letter had arrived from the Capital city, but Meng Huaining's expression suggested that the content was not very optimistic.","\"I'll go call your Brother-in-law first.\" At the moment, the other Mo brothers were mostly on the mountain, and it would take some time to call them back. He Zhiran was eager to learn the contents of the letter, so she decided to call Mo Jiuye to Second Uncle's place first.","He Zhiran returned to the greenhouse area and took Mo Jiuye with her.","There was no need to find Mo Qing and Fourth Brother, as the two immobile ones were left in the main courtyard making bamboo tubes for bombs.","Currently, the room only had Mo Qing, Fourth Brother, Mo Jiuye, He Zhiran, and Meng Huaining.","Meng Huaining cautiously looked towards the entrance before taking out the letter from the Capital city and handing it to Mo Qing.","\"Father-in-law, this is the letter I just received from the Capital city. The situation is not very optimistic. Please review it first.\""]},{"number":500,"title":"Chapter 500: I'll give them a bloody death.","paragraphs":["Mo Qing had also been keeping an eye on the news from the Capital city, and immediately opened the letter to read it.","He saw that his gaze while reading the letter became increasingly profound.","\"Father, what on earth happened?\" Seeing him put down the letter, Mo Jiuye hurriedly asked.","\"The letter said that Emperor Shunwu had not held morning court for ten days. The court is now divided into three factions, with half supporting Nan Heng, and the rest supporting Prince Rui and the Fourth Prince.","There is also the matter of us killing those assassins sent by the Empress to kill the Empress that the magistrate reported to the court. At that time, Emperor Shunwu, not knowing who had instigated him, handed the matter to Xue Prime Minister to deal with.","Xue Prime Minister didn't even investigate, and after a few days he reported the matter to Emperor Shunwu, saying that the more than two hundred people who died in the northwest were all local commoners, because the Mo Family wanted to occupy their land, Jiuye brutally killed them.","As soon as this was reported to Emperor Shunwu, it aroused his thunderous anger. If it weren't for Prince Rui and Mr. Fei persuading him that there might be hidden facts in it, Emperor Shunwu would have sent troops to the northwest to arrest Jiuye.","For this reason, Prince Rui also had a very unpleasant quarrel with the Empress's party. The current situation is also increasingly dangerous.\"","Mo Jiuye clenched his fists: \"What a good Empress, what a good Xue family, I will make sure they do not die well.\"","He Zhiran was also very angry at this moment. If it were in the past, she would only listen to such things, and if Mo Qing did not ask her, she would not take the initiative to express her opinion. But today was different. The Xue family was simply too bullying.","\"Father, the greenhouse will be built in two days. I plan to go to the Capital city with my husband. Since they won't let the Mo Family have a good life, let's take the initiative and get rid of all those who don't mean well to the Mo Family.\"","\"We must go to the Capital city. The Mo Family men are not cowards. It is not your turn as a woman to stand up for this.\" Mo Qing was the first to object.","In his opinion, although his ninth daughter-in-law was a little smarter, it was impossible for him to let a powerless weak woman rush into battle.","He Zhiran was also impatient at first, so she directly said what was on her mind.","Since the words had already been said, there was absolutely no reason to take them back, not to mention that she and Mo Jiuye had planned this in advance.","Mo Jiuye also disagreed with her going at first, partly because he was worried that she would be in danger, and partly because of their two newborn children.","But no one understood He Zhiran's temper better than him. She would not change her mind no matter how much persuasion was made to make her give up on something she wanted to do.","Having no alternative, Mo Jiuye had to compromise.","However, he had already reached an agreement with He Zhiran that she could go to the Capital city with him, but once she was in danger, she should not care about anything else and escape into the space to save her life first. If He Zhiran did not agree, he would not compromise either.","In order to be able to go to the Capital city, let alone such a simple condition, even if it was more harsh she would agree.","Therefore, the husband and wife had planned it out long ago that after the greenhouse was built, they would set off for the Capital city, regardless of whether they could receive news from the Capital city or not.","Since he had already agreed to take his wife with him, when Mo Jiuye faced opposition from his family, he naturally had to speak up to help.","\"Father, Zhiran wants to go to the Capital city with me, mainly because she wants to see her father-in-law. After all, they haven't seen each other for more than a year, and she must miss her father as a daughter. \"","Mo Jiuye knew his father and brothers' temperament. As people who were born and raised on the battlefield, how could they possibly let a woman participate in these struggles?","The best way was to use the excuse that his daughter-in-law missed her father.","He Zhiran also realized at this moment that she was too impatient just now and forgot about the bloody nature of the Mo men.","\"Father, I was just too impatient just now. I'm actually going to the Capital city mainly to see my father.\"","After thinking about it, she continued.","\"My mother and eldest brother both fell in love with the northwest, and plan to settle here for the long term. My trip to the Capital city this time is to try to persuade my father to resign from office and leave that vortex of struggle as soon as possible.","My father dotes on me the most, I'm afraid only I can convince him to listen, so I decided to go to the Capital city with my husband. Then my husband will go about his business, while I stay at the military minister’s residence to persuade my father.\"","When Mo Qing heard He Zhiran say this, although he was still doubtful in his heart, he could not stop his daughter-in-law from visiting her parents because of his own subjective ideas.","He took a deep breath and said, \"Since this is the case, you husband and wife should discuss this matter yourselves. However, successfully resolving the crisis the Mo Family is facing in the Capital city this time is not an easy task. Let me discuss specific countermeasures with you brothers later. Our Mo Family is not without talent. It is impossible to let you shoulder the danger alone.\"","In Mo Qing's view, it would not be easy to resolve the crisis in the Capital city, although his ninth son was capable, such things could not be done alone by one person.","Moreover, his Mo Family now had nine sons, all of whom could participate except for the fourth son whose actions were hindered.","If that didn’t work out, there were still good friends like Liang Hao and Tao Ran’s group. Any one of them would be a great help to Mo Jiuye if they went along.","If it were in the past, Mo Jiuye would have had similar ideas to take several capable elder brothers to go together.","But this time was different. His wife was going with him. She had space. If necessary, she would take some special items from space to use.","Although Mo Jiuye had been a scapegoat for more than a year, those things still had reasonable ways to see the light of day.","It would be different when he went to the Capital city. If he wanted to get rid of those ill-intentioned people to the Mo Family in the simplest way, his wife would certainly take out many unexpected things. At that time, even if someone else saw it, he would really have no reason to explain.","Moreover, his wife's space was a huge secret that he would never allow one more person to know about.","\"Father, have you ever thought that in the Emperor's eyes now, everyone in the Mo Family is a criminal. If our goal is too big when we go to the Capital city this time, it will be easy to expose our whereabouts. What's more, we can't guarantee that the northwest will definitely be safe.","I'll take Zhiran with me and send her to her father-in-law first. I can go alone first to check out the general situation. After knowing ourselves and knowing our enemies, I can have Little White send a message back, and then have someone come over to help.\"","Mo Qing agreed with Mo Jiuye's words in his heart, but he was still a little worried, so he did not respond immediately.","Instead, the fourth elder brother sitting aside spoke up.","\"Father, I agree with Ninth Brother's idea. The situation in the Capital city now is also only what we understand from the letter. We can only analyze the general circumstances of how things actually are.","Instead of going with so many people ostentatiously, we might as well just do as Ninth Brother said, let him scout out the situation first before making a decision.","The little white raised by Ninth Brother is indeed extraordinary. It takes at most four days for a round trip between the Capital city and the northwest. As long as we follow Ninth Brother's arrangements and take action after receiving his message, it won't be too late.\""]}]);
